          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The declaration and blind reconstruction agree on μ, both L² spaces, exact graph witnesses and D.closure. In the supplied module, hsub uses the given D.graph and hmem uses hD.graph_closure_eq_closure_graph; no replacement operator is introduced."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
          "original": "The pinned prerequisite is explicitly full-space and finite-dimensional, not the compact weighted-manifold spectral theory cited as background.",
          "reconstructed": "E is any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure. Integration is over E without a boundary. Dimension zero is not excluded. Tests belong to C¹ with compact support; u and G are L² equivalence classes.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The theorem's typeclasses and quantified tests match the candidate assumptions. The private helper integrates over unrestricted volume on E. Compactness is required of the test support, not the ambient space. No manifold or boundary theorem is transferred to E."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
          "original": "The weighted identity holds for pairs in the completed smooth gradient graph and for compact tests and constant directions.",
          "reconstructed": "For every admissible W, every D satisfying closability and the exact graph characterization, every (u,G) in D.closure.graph, every compactly supported C¹ scalar φ and every v in E, both integrabilities and the identity hold.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "These are the quantifiers in the declaration. The graph characterization is an equivalence for all scalar/vector L² pairs. The result is not restricted to the original smooth core. It neither constructs D in this theorem nor proves the converse characterization of closure membership by tests."
        },
        {
          "slot": "assumptions",
          "original": "The route paraphrase leaves analytic regularity, normalization and the precise completed-gradient interface implicit; the candidate publication explicitly supplies them.",
          "reconstructed": "W is C¹ and exp(-W) is volume-integrable. D is closable and has exactly the smooth compact gradient graph. The selected pair belongs to the closure graph, and φ is C¹ with compact support. No curvature, global score bound or differentiability of arbitrary L² representatives is assumed.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "All these hypotheses occur in the Lean statement and authored assumptions. The private helper genuinely uses only C¹ W, f and φ plus compact support of φ. Continuity and compact support establish its three volume-integrability obligations. Positivity and integrability of the exponential density justify the finite positive normalization, including in dimension zero."
        },
        {
          "slot": "conclusion",
          "original": "Integral φ⟨G,v⟩ dμ equals minus integral u(D_vφ−φD_vW) dμ for completed-gradient pairs.",
