s the one-step parameter estimates appearing in lemma 6.6(ii). a scalar update estimate after schedule selection. same the binding credits only finite updated variance and finite-variance contraction. branch persistence, iterative termination, sampler construction, error and cost are explicitly excluded. no completion of the entire recursive argument is asserted. constant dependencies the bound 2c₀ and contraction factor 2c₀/(1+2c₀). exactly 2c and rho=2c/(1+2c). same writing t=h+c and d=1+r+rt gives aplus=t/d. d≥1 proves aplus≤2c. the contraction residual is exactly 2cd−rt(1+2c)=2c+r(2c−t)≥0. domains informational the restriction c<1/4 is removed. this is a disclosed, valid generalization of the scalar inequality, not equivalence of unrestricted parameter domains or permission to enlarge the algorithm's admissible schedule. scopes informational the formal result handles an already selected single update rather than the stage-selection machinery. the source restatement, lesson and binding consistently restrict their claim to this component. conclusion informational initial infinity is represented by zero precision, with a guarded finite-previous-variance comparison. the unconditional updated bound remains valid at r=0; no real inverse of zero is interpreted as infinity.",
