          "reconstructed": "α=κ⁻¹+r, β=1+r, r⁺=r+a⁻¹, w=(r⁺)⁻¹(ru+a⁻¹y), and K⁺=(aβ+1)K/(aβ+K).",
          "relation": "same",
          "evidence": "The factors 1/2 and a⁻¹ are preserved. Positivity of a,α,β and K makes all relevant denominators nonzero. At r=0 the update gives r⁺=a⁻¹ and w=y. K denotes the ratio of supplied bounds, not an optimal spectral condition number."
        }
