    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260910-GaussianConditionalKernel",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260910-GaussianConditionalKernel",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:gaussian-rgo-conditional-kernel · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianConditionalKernel.exists_tilted_isCondKernel.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S2.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "PBPS v1 §2.2, (2.7)-(2.8), takes X with normalized Gibbs law μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, an independent standard Gaussian G, and Y=X+sqrt(η)G. The selected backward conditional-law clause gives X conditional on Y=y density proportional to exp(−V(x)−‖x−y‖²/(2η)). ASTIS formalizes its normalized conditional-kernel mechanism: for any probability μ on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space E and any η>0, the everywhere-defined normalized tilt R(y,dx)=exp(−‖x−y‖²/(2η))μ(dx)/∫exp(−‖z−y‖²/(2η))μ(dz) is a measurable Markov kernel satisfying L(Y,X)=L(Y)⊗R. The source's Gibbs, C² curvature and η≤1/β restrictions are not needed for this identity; this generalization is explicit, and the source Gibbs probability certificate is a separate compiled parent. This is an ASTIS mathematical restatement and standard expansion, not an original quotation. Equality with other conditional versions is only marginal-almost-everywhere. No RGO implementation, PBPS process invariance or quantitative sampling bound is asserted.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its induced norm and Borel σ-algebra, every probability measure μ on E, and every real η > 0, let γ_E be the centered standard Gaussian probability measure with identity covariance and let J be the pushforward of μ ⊗ γ_E by (x,z) ↦ (x, x+√η·z). There exists a measurable Markov kernel R from E to E such that, for every y ∈ E, R(y) is exactly μ tilted by x ↦ −‖x−y‖²/(2η), and R is a conditional kernel for the swapped joint measure J_swap, the pushforward of J by (x,y) ↦ (y,x). Explicitly, define w_y(x)=exp(−‖x−y‖²/(2η)) and Z_y=∫_E w_y(x) dμ(x). The pointwise formula is R(y)=μ.withDensity(x ↦ ENNReal.ofReal(w_y(x)/Z_y)); its reference measure is μ, not Lebesgue measure. The denominator uses the prescribed totalized real integral, and no additional integrability premise is assumed. Markov means R(y) has total mass one for every y. Kernel measurability means y ↦ R(y,B) is measurable for each measurable output event B. If ν is the first marginal of J_swap, equivalently the second marginal of J, the conditional-kernel assertion is the equality of measures ν ⊗ₘ R = J_swap. On every measurable rectangle A×B this composition has mass given by the nonnegative integral ∫_A R(y,B) dν(y). Thus R provides a measurable version of the conditional law of the original first coordinate given the noisy second coordinate. The tilted formula is asserted for all y, including values in ν-null sets; no pointwise uniqueness among all conditional kernels or uniqueness of values on such null sets is asserted. The sole scale parameter is η>0, with the forward scaling √η and the exponent denominator exactly 2η. No density or moment assumption on μ is imposed. Dimension zero is allowed, using the unique standard Gaussian probability law there.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
          "slot": "objects",
          "original": "Independent Gibbs input X and standard Gaussian G, with Y=X+√η G and the backward conditional law of X.",
          "reconstructed": "The actual product-law pushforward J, a measurable probability kernel R, and the disintegration of J.map Prod.swap.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The product measure encodes independence. Swapping coordinates correctly makes Y the conditioning coordinate and X the returned coordinate."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
          "original": "Euclidean state space with a normalized Gibbs input.",
          "reconstructed": "Any finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space and any probability input μ, including singular laws.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The disclosed generalization is valid: the Gaussian likelihood is integrated against μ itself, not against an assumed density of μ. Finite-dimensional canonical volume appears only in the observation density. Dimension zero causes no exceptional normalization."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
          "original": "The backward conditional distribution given Y=y.",
          "reconstructed": "For every probability μ and η>0, there exists one measurable Markov kernel whose specified tilted formula holds for every y.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Strict positivity of the likelihood gives a positive normalizer at every y. This selects an everywhere-defined version; the publication correctly restricts agreement with other conditional versions to observation-marginal almost everywhere."
        },
        {
          "slot": "assumptions",
          "original": "The source Gibbs and curvature setting, with η∈(0,1/β] in the augmentation discussion.",
          "reconstructed": "Only probability μ, finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel structure and η>0.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "For every y, 0<w(y,x)≤1 gives integrability and 0<Z(y)≤1 without moments or curvature. Joint measurability and measurable parameter integration establish the normalized density kernel. Neither normalization nor an assumed conditional kernel is supplied."
        },
