ed measurable conditional-kernel construction for the actual gaussian augmentation. same the binding supports only measurable-normalized-conditional. implementation, process construction, nonexplosion, invariance and quantitative guarantees remain separate obligations. backward marginal recovery is a consequence of disintegration, not a pbps invariance certificate. constant dependencies forward noise scaling √η and quadratic exponent denominator 2η. exactly √η and 2η, with gaussian density constant (√(2πη))^(−dim e). same the common gaussian density constant remains in the joint and observation densities and cancels from the posterior. cancellation uses the proved z(y)>0. no dimension factor, variance rescaling or positive-variance restriction is lost. domains informational arbitrary probability inputs replace the source gibbs input. this extension is explicitly disclosed and justified by the bounded, strictly positive likelihood. it does not claim that a singular input has a volume density. assumptions informational curvature and η≤1/β are omitted for the conditional-law identity. neither is needed for normalization or disintegration; η>0 remains essential. this omission does not relax the conditions of the source algorithms or their quantitative estimates. quantifiers informational an explicit all-y version elaborates conditional-law notation. the positive normalizer and measurable kernel construction justify this version. no all-y uniqueness claim is made.",
