w is (m+r)-strongly convex on e. precisely, e is convex and, for every x,y ∈ e and all real a,b ≥ 0 with a+b = 1, w(a x+b y) ≤ a w(x)+b w(y) − ((m+r)/2) a b ‖x−y‖². second, the canonical gradient of w is globally lipschitz with constant l+r: for every x,y ∈ e, ‖∇w(x)−∇w(y)‖ ≤ (l+r)‖x−y‖. here d²u(x)[v,v] is obtained by differentiating the continuous-linear-map-valued first derivative, applying the resulting derivative to v, and then applying the resulting linear functional to v again. the fréchet derivative api is totalized to zero where differentiability fails, but the assumed c² regularity supplies genuine first and second derivatives of u. the canonical gradient ∇w(x) is the riesz vector representing the totalized fréchet derivative of w at x; its inner product with each direction v equals that derivative applied to v. completeness supplies the inverse riesz map, and no independently chosen gradient field is an input. the nonnegative parameters may be zero; their sums are coerced to ordinary real numbers in the strong-convexity and norm inequalities. division by 2 is ordinary real division with nonzero denominator. the function w is the specified let-bound construction, not an extra assumption. no finite-dimensionality, measurable structure, or measure is assumed, and all bounds are global and pointwise. accepted sphmc v1 section 6.2.2 lemma 6.4 curvature/smoothness clause; shared pbps v1 (2.9)-(2.10) analytic prerequisite only autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.quadraticregularization.strongconvexon_and_lipschitzwith_gradient_add_quadratic autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/quadraticregularization.lean true publication_gate_review heatbath_exposition_research 2b63de59d9eddde06dbbadfff6fc384e0003b5fd1ccdf04c8729f3082067edf1 accepted rgo_independent_verifier objects the selected sphmc clause concerns the actual potential u_a,u=u+norm(x-u)^2/(2a), its strong convexity and gradient smoothness. the selected expansion uses w=u+(r/2)norm(x-u)^2. w is 