          "reconstructed": "E has NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances. Its volume is the canonical inner-product volume; the density is on E × E with product volume. No positive-dimension hypothesis appears.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Independent direct elaboration printed exactly those five typeclasses and no additional ambient assumptions. Canonical volume matches Euclidean Lebesgue normalization through orthonormal coordinates. The focused zero-dimensional test proves the entire triple for E=EuclideanSpace R (Fin 0), V=0 and alpha=1. This is the stated formal generalization, not a claim that the paper separately discusses dimension zero."
