          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "The independently elaborated #check agrees with the pinned statement and anonymous reconstruction. There is no assumed minimizer, preselected normalizer, almost-everywhere weakening, local-domain restriction, integrability witness or desired law identity among the theorem's inputs."
        },
        {
          "slot": "assumptions",
          "original": "PBPS (1.1) assumes C² regularity and a positive lower/upper Hessian sandwich, while Section 2.2 restricts the scale above as well. The selected certificate explicitly keeps genuine C², the positive lower Hessian bound and eta>0, omitting unused upper restrictions.",
          "reconstructed": "ContDiff R 2 V, alpha>0, eta>0, and alpha*norm(v)^2 ≤ D²V(x)[v,v] for every x,v suffice. The derivative is the derivative of the continuous-linear-map-valued first derivative, evaluated twice at v.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
