          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Integrability is established internally before integral_exp_pos and isProbabilityMeasure_tilted are used. Thus the real integral is an actual finite integral and its strict positivity excludes the zero nonintegrable-tilt fallback. Measurable pushforward proves probability. The density equality is equality of whole measures, not merely mass equality; the explicitly proved Gibbs density is substituted into the previously established mu×volume Gaussian density. The paper's proportionality is resolved by this proof, not treated as an assumed normalization fact."
