          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "The module and elaborated signature have FiniteDimensional ℝ E and BorelSpace E, not an arbitrary MeasureSpace parameter. Completeness needed by the gradient API follows from finite dimension. The whole-space convexity condition imposes no hidden boundary condition. In dimension zero, canonical volume is unit mass and the positive finite Gibbs weight is integrable."
        },
        {
