          "evidence": "For m>0 the code's b equals V(0)−‖g‖²/m. Cauchy–Schwarz and Young with ε=m/2 give ‖g‖‖x‖≤(m/4)‖x‖²+‖g‖²/m, so the signs and coefficient loss are correct. The lesson's envelope integral exp(−b)(4π/m)^(dim(E)/2) is mathematically correct and explicitly explanatory rather than a claimed new Lean equality. No bound on V(0) or g is required; they contribute only a finite multiplicative factor."
