    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260910-PBPSGaussianAugmentation",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260910-PBPSGaussianAugmentation",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "pbps-v1:joint-density-relative-input · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.GaussianAugmentation.augmentation_eq_withDensity.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S2.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "ASTIS expanded intermediate calculation between (2.7) and (2.6), not a quotation or full Gibbs-density identification. Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space with canonical volume, mu any probability measure, eta>0, and gamma its standard Gaussian law. Define Phi(x,z)=(x,x+sqrt(eta)*z). Then Phi_#(mu tensor gamma) equals (mu tensor volume).withDensity of the function (x,y) -> ((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-1))^dim(E) * exp(-||y-x||^2/(2*eta)), interpreted as a nonnegative density. Measurability and sigma-finiteness for product-density transport are derived from the displayed objects. This explicitly allows singular mu and zero-dimensional E and uses no sampler step-size upper bound. Instantiating mu with the source's normalized Gibbs density to produce a density relative to volume tensor volume remains a separate obligation. No reflection, conditional representative, PBPS dynamics, convergence or cost is asserted.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its induced norm and with the Borel σ-algebra of its norm topology. Write d = finrank_ℝ(E) ∈ ℕ, let γ_E be the centered standard Gaussian probability measure with identity covariance, and let λ_E be the canonical Lebesgue measure normalized by orthonormal coordinates. For every probability measure μ on E and every real η > 0, define Φ_η : E × E → E × E by Φ_η(x,z) = (x, x + √η · z). Then the following equality of measures on E × E holds:\n\n(Φ_η)_*(μ ⊗ γ_E) = (μ ⊗ λ_E).withDensity((x,y) ↦ ENNReal.ofReal(((√(2πη))⁻¹)^d · exp(−‖y−x‖²/(2η)))).\n\nThe reference measure on the right is μ in the first coordinate and canonical Lebesgue measure λ_E in the second coordinate; it is not Lebesgue measure in both coordinates. The input μ is arbitrary apart from being a Borel probability measure: no density, moment, or smoothness hypothesis on μ is imposed. The left side is the pushforward of the product probability measure, so it describes the joint law of (X, X + √η · Z) when X has law μ and Z has law γ_E independently. For every Borel set A ⊆ E × E, the right side assigns to A the nonnegative integral of the displayed extended-nonnegative density over A with respect to μ ⊗ λ_E.\n\nThe dimension d is a natural number and zero dimension is allowed; canonical volume in that case is unit mass on the one-point space. The power in the prefactor is ordinary natural-number exponentiation. All scalar operations are real, √ is the nonnegative real square root, π is the circle constant, and the norm is the inner-product norm. ENNReal.ofReal embeds nonnegative real numbers into extended nonnegative reals and sends negative real numbers to zero. Real division and reciprocal are totalized at zero, with 0⁻¹ = 0, but η > 0 makes the displayed denominators positive, so these expressions use their ordinary nonzero-denominator values. No arbitrary choice of a measure-space volume, separate completeness hypothesis, or nontriviality hypothesis is present.",
