      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S2.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "ASTIS mathematical expansion of the standard Gaussian-noise density used in the passage from the independent augmentation (2.7) to the density (2.6), not a quotation or the complete joint-law claim. For a finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its Borel sigma algebra and canonical inner-product volume, any eta>0, and standard Gaussian G on E, the law of sqrt(eta)*G has volume density ((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-1))^dim(E) * exp(-||z||^2/(2*eta)). The natural-power expression also includes dimension zero. This explicitly extends the noise calculation beyond the paper's positive-dimensional Euclidean notation and does not need the sampler's upper bound eta<=1/beta. No potential, input distribution, Gibbs normalizer, conditional law or process conclusion is part of this selected prerequisite. The actual joint augmentation and source Gibbs-density instantiation remain separate proof obligations.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, with the norm induced by its inner product and with measurable sets equal to the Borel sets of its norm topology. Write d = finrank_ℝ(E) ∈ ℕ. Let γ_E be the centered standard Gaussian probability measure on E with identity covariance, and let λ_E be the canonical Lebesgue measure normalized by orthonormal coordinates. For every real η > 0, the pushforward of γ_E under S_η(z) = √η · z is the following measure on E:\n\n(S_η)_*γ_E = λ_E.withDensity(z ↦ ENNReal.ofReal(((√(2πη))⁻¹)^d · exp(−‖z‖²/(2η)))).\n\nHere pushforward means assigning to a Borel set A the γ_E-measure of S_η⁻¹(A). The measure on the right assigns to A the nonnegative integral of the displayed extended-nonnegative density over A with respect to λ_E. The measure λ_E is the canonical inner-product-space volume, not an arbitrarily chosen measure. Dimension zero is allowed; in that case canonical volume is unit mass on the one-point space, and the exponent d is zero. The exponentiation is natural-number power. The square root is the nonnegative real square root, π is the circle constant, and scalar multiplication is over ℝ. ENNReal.ofReal embeds nonnegative real values and sends negative real values to zero. Real reciprocal and division are totalized at zero, with 0⁻¹ = 0; the assumption η > 0 ensures that the displayed denominators are positive. No separate completeness or nontriviality assumption is imposed.",
