    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260910-PBPSGaussianReflection",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260910-PBPSGaussianReflection",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "pbps-v1:prop-2.1-iii-generative-component · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.GaussianReflection.reflection_preserves_augmentation.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#S2.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "ASTIS extraction of the generative-law symmetry calculation supporting Proposition 2.1(iii), not a quotation or the full Gibbs-density proposition. Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel sigma algebra, mu any probability measure, and eta>0. Let gamma be the standard Gaussian, Phi(x,z)=(x,x+sqrt(eta) z), and R(x,y)=(x,2x-y). Then R(R(p))=p for every p and R_#(Phi_#(mu tensor gamma))=Phi_#(mu tensor gamma). The calculation uses Gaussian sign symmetry, independence, and measurable pushforward composition. Generality beyond the source Gibbs law and eta<=1/beta is explicit; identifying the normalized density (2.6) with the generative law (2.7), and all process/algorithm guarantees, are separate unproved obligations.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product space E equipped with its Borel measurable structure, every probability measure μ on E, and every real parameter η > 0, define R : E × E → E × E by R(x,y) = (x, 2x − y). Let X have law μ and let Z independently have the centered standard Gaussian law on E with identity covariance. Then R is an involution on all of E × E, meaning R(R(x,y)) = (x,y) for every x,y ∈ E, and R preserves the joint law ν of (X, X + √η Z): R₊ν = ν, where R₊ denotes pushforward. Equivalently, (X, X − √η Z) and (X, X + √η Z) have the same joint distribution. No restriction on μ beyond being a probability measure is assumed; in particular no density or moment assumption is present. The coefficient 2 is fixed, and the Gaussian displacement scale is the nonnegative square root √η; there are no additional constants. The asserted scope is η > 0. All pushforward maps involved are measurable, so Measure.map uses ordinary pushforward and its totalized nonmeasurable fallback is not invoked.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
          "slot": "objects",
          "original": "Selected extraction: μ, standard Gaussian γ, Φ(x,z)=(x,x+√η z), R(x,y)=(x,2x−y).",
          "reconstructed": "The same measures and maps, with ν=Φ₊(μ⊗γ).",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "The production declaration and blind reconstruction use the same two-coordinate law; no kernel or conditional representative is substituted."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
          "original": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product E with Borel measurable structure; state space E×E.",
          "reconstructed": "NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace ℝ, FiniteDimensional ℝ, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace on E.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "These typeclasses express the selected domain. Every map actually used in the proof is globally measurable."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
          "original": "Every eligible E, every probability μ, every η>0, and every state for involution.",
          "reconstructed": "Universal E, μ and η with 0<η; Function.Involutive quantifies over all states.",
          "relation": "same",
          "evidence": "The checked fully elaborated declaration has exactly these quantifiers; no almost-everywhere weakening."
        },
        {
          "slot": "assumptions",
          "original": "Probability μ, standard Gaussian noise independent of X, η>0.",
          "reconstructed": "IsProbabilityMeasure μ; μ.prod(stdGaussian E); 0<η.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Product law encodes independence. BorelSpace and finite dimension make stdGaussian a genuine probability measure; both product factors supply SFinite instances. No invariance hypothesis is supplied."
        },
        {
          "slot": "conclusion",
          "original": "Pointwise involution and preservation of the complete generative joint law.",
          "reconstructed": "R∘R=id pointwise and Measure.map R (Measure.map Φ (μ.prod γ))=Measure.map Φ (μ.prod γ).",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "Both conjunction branches are proved. This is equality of measures, not merely matching moments, marginals or normalization constants."
        },
