      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260910-pbpsgaussianreflection semantic-audit astis-rt-20260910-pbpsgaussianreflection pbps-v1:prop-2.1-iii-generative-component · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.gaussianreflection.reflection_preserves_augmentation. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder astis extraction of the generative-law symmetry calculation supporting proposition 2.1(iii), not a quotation or the full gibbs-density proposition. let e be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its borel sigma algebra, mu any probability measure, and eta>0. let gamma be the standard gaussian, phi(x,z)=(x,x+sqrt(eta) z), and r(x,y)=(x,2x-y). then r(r(p))=p for every p and r_#(phi_#(mu tensor gamma))=phi_#(mu tensor gamma). the calculation uses gaussian sign symmetry, independence, and measurable pushforward composition. generality beyond the source gibbs law and eta<=1/beta is explicit; identifying the normalized density (2.6) with the generative law (2.7), and all process/algorithm guarantees, are separate unproved obligations. for every finite-dimensional real inner-product space e equipped with its borel measurable structure, every probability measure μ on e, and every real parameter η > 0, define r : e × e → e × e by r(x,y) = (x, 2x − y). let x have law μ and let z independently have the centered standard gaussian law on e with identity covariance. then r is an involution on all of e × e, meaning r(r(x,y)) = (x,y) for every x,y ∈ e, and r preserves the joint law ν of (x, x + √η z): r₊ν = ν, where r₊ denotes pushforward. equivalently, (x, x − √η z) and (x, x + √η z) have the same joint distribution. no restriction on μ beyond being a probability measure is assumed; in particular no density or moment assumption is present. the coefficient 2 is fixed, and the gaussian displacement scale is the nonnegative square root √η; there are no additional constants. the asserted scope is η > 0. all pushforward maps involved are measurable, so measure.map uses ordinary pushforward and its totalized nonmeasurable fallback is not invoked. accepted arxiv:2609.06905v1, section 2.2, proposition 2.1(iii), (2.7), (2.14) autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.gaussianreflection.reflection_preserves_augmentation autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/gaussianreflection.lean true pbps_reflection_worker gaussian_blind_decoder 5d59223c41747ec4ec0aaa13e603e43ec3de00e9c7283752b50d49bff76d1766 accepted gaussian_independent_verifier objects selected extraction: μ, standard gaussian γ, φ(x,z)=(x,x+√η z), r(x,y)=(x,2x−y). the same measures and maps, with ν=φ₊(μ⊗γ). equivalent the production declaration and blind reconstruction use the same two-coordinate law; no kernel or conditional representative is substituted. domains finite-dimensional real inner-product e with borel measurable structure; state space e×e. normedaddcommgroup, innerproductspace ℝ, finitedimensional ℝ, measurablespace and borelspace on e. explicit-elaboration these typeclasses express the selected domain. every map actually used in the proof is globally measurable. quantifiers every eligible e, every probability μ, every η>0, and every state for involution. universal e, μ and η with 0<η; function.involutive quantifies over all states. same the checked fully elaborated declaration has exactly these quantifiers; no almost-everywhere weakening. assumptions probability μ, standard gaussian noise independent of x, η>0. isprobabilitymeasure μ; μ.prod(stdgaussian e); 0<η. explicit-elaboration product law encodes independence. borelspace and finite dimension make stdgaussian a genuine probability measure; both product factors supply sfinite instances. no invariance hypothesis is supplied. conclusion pointwise involution and preservation of the complete generative joint law. r∘r=id pointwise and measure.map r (measure.map φ (μ.prod γ))=measure.map φ (μ.prod γ). equivalent both conjunction branches are proved. this is equality of measures, not merely matching moments, marginals or normalization constants. scopes only the extracted generative-reflection component; density identification and downstream adapters excluded. exactly that component, under the broader μ/e/η scope stated in the lesson. same module comments, lesson assumptions, candidate assumptions and proof-edge support all disclose this scope. the density-generative-identification obligation is separate; no full-process or l² theorem is claimed. constant dependencies fixed reflection coefficient 2 and gaussian scale √η; no additional constants. the same 2 and real.sqrt η, with η>0 and no α or β. same positivity is retained but unused by the algebra. no hidden division, curvature assumption, dimension factor or bound is introduced. domains informational compared with the full paper setting, the selected result allows arbitrary finite-dimensional real inner-product spaces. explicitly disclosed in extraction, module and lesson; a valid broader calculation. assumptions informational the actual theorem allows any probability μ and all η>0, without gibbs, smoothness, curvature or upper-step-size assumptions. explicit in lesson and candidate assumptions; not presented as proving those source assumptions. scopes informational the source proposition concerns its density-defined joint law; the lean law is a generative pushforward. the missing density-to-generative identification is expressly a separate obligation. acceptance covers only generative-reflection. scopes informational the generative proof route does not formalize the source's direct density proof or its operator/process consequences. no such closure is claimed. l² and algorithmic adapters remain outside this declaration.",
