      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260908-positivefiberupdate semantic-audit astis-rt-20260908-positivefiberupdate discrete-sampling:2307.13826v4 · possible-source-error blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.probability.coordinateheatbath.heatbath_eq_cond. possible-source-error source hidden from decoder x_{t+1}(w) = x_t(v). choose x_{t+1}(v) from the conditional gibbs distribution μ(σ(v) = · | σ(w) = x_t(w) for all w ≠ v). let n be any natural number, let (x_j) indexed by fin(n+1) be measurable spaces, and let μ be a finite measure on their dependent product ω = ∏_j x_j. fix i ∈ fin(n+1). assume x_i is a nonempty standard borel space and the complementary product ω_{-i} = ∏_{j∈fin(n)} x_{i.succabove(j)} has measurable singletons. write r_i(x) = (x_{i.succabove(j)})_j and e_i(x) = (r_i(x), x_i). let κ be the selected regular conditional-distribution kernel of the second coordinate given the first under (e_i)_#μ, and define h_i(x) = (e_i^{-1})_#(δ_{r_i(x)} × κ(r_i(x))). then, for every x ∈ ω whose complementary-coordinate fiber f_x = {y ∈ ω : r_i(y) = r_i(x)} has nonzero μ-measure, h_i(x) = (μ(f_x))^{-1} • (μ restricted to f_x). thus the coordinate heat-bath measure at every such x equals μ conditioned on that fiber. source-reviewed section 1.3, printed/pdf page 5, general glauber update steps 2–3; https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.13826v4#page=5. two short formula/instruction excerpts below. astis context paraphrase (not source quotation): the source uses a distribution on omega subset of {0,1}^v, a finite site set v and a starting configuration x_t in omega; step 2 applies to every w != v. the preceding uniform-site selection step is outside this fixed-site comparison. autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.probability.coordinateheatbath.heatbath_eq_cond autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/probability/coordinateheatbathconditional.lean true positive_fiber_worker math_decoder ac527c3ca65e38837e9289657ab78b22792fb7