      "subtitle": "companion:pbps-conditional-score · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalScore.reflected_conditional_covariance.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "The paper works on R^d, d>=1, with C2 potential V and genuine Hessian bounds 0<alpha I<=D2V<=beta I, and 0<eta<=1/beta.\nLet X have normalized density proportional to exp(-V), and let Y_+=X+sqrt(eta)Z and Y_-=X-sqrt(eta)Z for independent standard Gaussian Z. The selected differentiation step uses smooth compactly supported real f.\nThe conditional density of Y_- given Y_+=y is proportional to exp(-V((y+u)/2)-norm(y-u)^2/(8eta)). Differentiating the conditional expectation of f gives its covariance with the unnormalized logarithmic derivative -grad V((y+u)/2)/2-(y-u)/(4eta). This is the differentiation input to Appendix C.1; the subsequent conditional variance estimate and extension to general L2 inputs are separate obligations.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its norm and Borel measurable structure, and let V:E→ℝ, α,β∈[0,∞), and η∈ℝ. Assume α>0, η>0, V is twice continuously Fréchet differentiable, and for every x,v∈E, α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖². Define μ to be normalized exponential weighting of Lebesgue measure by −V. Let J be the pushforward of μ⊗γ under (x,g)↦(x,x+√η g), where γ is the standard centered Gaussian on E. Define the continuous-linear-functional-valued function s by s(y,u)=−(1/2)DV((y+u)/2)−(1/(4η))⟨y−u,·⟩. There exist Markov kernels R and S from E to E with the following simultaneous properties. First, R disintegrates the swapped joint measure swap₍*₎J conditional on its first coordinate; thus, in the joint-coordinate notation (X,Y) for J, R is a conditional distribution of X given Y. Second, for every y∈E, S(y) is the pushforward of R(y) under x↦2x−y. Third, for every y∈E, S(y) is normalized exponential weighting of Lebesgue measure in u by −V((y+u)/2)−‖y−u‖²/(8η). Finally, for every smooth compactly supported real-valued function f on E and every y∈E, both u↦s(y,u) and u↦f(u)s(y,u) are Bochner integrable under S(y), and F(z)=∫f(u)S(z)(du) has a Fréchet derivative at y equal to ∫f(u)s(y,u)S(y)(du)−(∫f(u)S(y)(du))(∫s(y,u)S(y)(du)). Equivalently, its derivative applied to h∈E is ∫f(u)s(y,u)[h]S(y)(du)−(∫f(u)S(y)(du))(∫s(y,u)[h]S(y)(du)).\nThe same R,S work for every f,y. The explicit fiber identities hold everywhere, although disintegration itself identifies a conditional version relative to the marginal. This is existence of a suitable version, not a statement about every conditional version. Local μ,J,s are definitions rather than hypotheses. No positive-dimension or separate α≤β premise occurs. There is no asserted uniqueness, measure-valued or operator-norm differentiability, continuous derivative, higher derivative, arbitrary measurable test extension or quantitative derivative bound. The unnormalized score need not have zero mean; the formula centers it. The exact coefficients are √η, 2, 1/2, 1/(8η) and 1/(4η), with kernels selected before the tests.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "domain-mismatch",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
          "slot": "objects",
          "original": "Reflected conditional density and differentiation of its test expectation.",
          "reconstructed": "Actual Gibbs Gaussian augmentation J; R disintegrates swapped J; S is the reflected pushforward with explicit tilt and dual-valued score.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "actual_reflected_density and reflected_kernel construct actual Markov kernels using GaussianConditionalKernel and a jointly measurable product-kernel map."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
          "original": "Positive-dimensional Euclidean space in the source scale regime.",
          "reconstructed": "Any finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including zero dimension, with eta>0 and real C∞ compactly supported tests.",
          "relation": "stronger-in-lean",
          "evidence": "The broader ambient and scale domains are disclosed in the lesson and candidate assumptions; public test class matches the selected source input."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
