      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260911-pbpsconditionalbochner semantic-audit astis-rt-20260911-pbpsconditionalbochner companion:pbps-conditional-bochner · domain-mismatch blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalbochner.conditional_bochner_energy. domain-mismatch source hidden from decoder paper setting: euclidean d>=1, v c2, 0<alpha<=beta and actual hessian bounds alpha i<=d2v<=beta i, eta>0 with beta eta<=1. the gibbs-gaussian augmentation is (x,x+sqrt(eta)z) with independent gibbs x and standard gaussian z; s_y is the actual reflected conditional law. the bochner prerequisite uses smooth compactly supported f; extending to the noncompact score test remains separate. pbps appendix c.1 applies a conditional poincare inequality to the reflected conditional potential w_y(u)=v((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8 eta), whose lower curvature is (alpha+eta inverse)/4. the selected astis prerequisite expands the missing analytic curvature route using the separately proved compact-test weighted bochner identity: for the actual conditional law s_y, the square-generator integral equals the coordinate hessian-square integral plus the d2w_y quadratic-form integral, and is at least (alpha+eta inverse)/4 times gradient energy. global normalization and all tested integrability are established under the actual conditional law. this is a prerequisite expansion, not the poincare or variance conclusion stated in c.1. for every finite-dimensional real inner-product space e with its borel measurable structure, v:e->r, nonnegative real alpha,beta and real eta, assume 0<alpha<=beta, v c2, eta>0, beta eta<=1, and alpha norm(v)^2<=d2v(x)[v,v]<=beta norm(v)^2 for every x,v. define mu as canonical volume tilted by -v, with the supplied totalized normalized exponential definition; define gamma as standard gaussian and j as the pushforward of mu tensor gamma under (x,z)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)z). thus j has coordinates (x,y). for all y,u define w_y(u)=v((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta). there exist markov kernels r,s:e->e such that r disintegrates the swapped joint (y,x), conditional on its first coordinate, and for every y, s(y) is the pushforward of r(y) under x->2x-y. for every y, w_y is c2, exp(-w_y) is volume-integrable with strictly positive normalizer z_y=integral exp(-w_y), and s(y)(du)=z_y inverse exp(-w_y(u))du. these equalities hold for every y, not only almost everywhere. for every smooth compactly supported f, define l_y(u)=delta f(u)-inner(gradient w_y(u),gradient f(u)), h(u)=sum_i norm(gradient(z->df(z)[e_i])(u))^2, c_y(u)=d2w_y(u)[gradient f(u),gradient f(u)]. all four l_y^2, norm(gradient f)^2, h and c_y are integrable under s(y), including absolute integrability of c_y. their integrals satisfy integral l_y^2 = integral h + integral c_y, and ((alpha+1/eta)/4) integral norm(gradient f)^2 <= integral l_y^2 under s(y). kernels are chosen before y and f and do not depend on the test. the inequality constant depends only on alpha,eta; beta enters hypotheses. zero dimension is allowed. disintegration does not assert a uniquely determined conditional law at every y; the universal statements specify the selected kernels' pointwise properties. accepted appendix c.1 conditional poincare analytic prerequisite autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalbochner.conditional_bochner_energy autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalbochner.lean true root-samplinglib-writer bochner_blind_decoder bff1feee3c38b819961ce190dea1903d317e8f520a0ac1b47f510d72226fdc41 accepted log_depth_source_review objects actual reflected gibbs-gaussian conditional potential and law in c.1. common r,s, swapped disintegration, reflection, actual tilted w_y and differential expression. explicit-elaboration consumer retains r,s,hcond,hsr,hsy,hcurv for the same law. domains positive-dimensional euclidean paper setting. finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space including zero dimension. str