rator d_y from a dense linear subspace of scalar l2(s(y)) into vector l2(s(y);e). d_y is closable and its closure is closed. for every scalar class a and vector class b, graph membership (a,b) in d_y is equivalent to existence of smooth compactly supported scalar f with a=f and b=gradient f s(y)-almost everywhere. r,s are selected before all y. d_y is selected after y and before a,b; f may depend on y,a,b. there is no asserted measurability or continuity of y->d_y and no uniform operator bound. conditional disintegration does not assert a uniquely determined version at every y; by contrast both s(y) measure equalities and all fiber analytic conclusions are explicitly for every y. mu,j,w are displayed definitions, not extra premises or freely chosen objects. no separate exp(-v) integrability assumption is added. the coefficients 1/2,2,8 are fixed. approved definitions determine the reconstruction; iscondkernel is interpreted only as the supplied disintegration on the first coordinate, without extra pointwise density convention or uniqueness requirement. accepted appendix c.1 weighted-space analytic prerequisite autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalgradient.conditional_gradient_closable autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalgradient.lean true root-samplinglib-writer gradient_blind_decoder 8fa693243008088e11a8b1891be5801a1a15c88f81509d79a180d3c9e8097601 accepted log_depth_source_review objects actual gibbs-gaussian reflected conditional law in pbps c.1. common r,s retaining disintegration and reflection; exact conditional gibbs gradient on scalar/vector l2(s_y). explicit-elaboration one conditional_bochner_energy witness is retained, then rewritten by hsy. domains positive-dimensional euclidean paper setting. every finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space including dimension zero. stronger-in-lean public domain and lesson explicitly allow zero dimension. quantifiers analytic prerequisite on actual conditional fibers. one r,s 