    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCProxyReverseTransport",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCProxyReverseTransport",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-proxy-reverse-transport · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.ProxyReverseTransport.proxy_reverse_transport.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS2.SSS1",
      "original_theorem": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel E, including zero dimension; P,Q probability measures.\nReal p>=2 inherited from the source Lemma6.2 proof route. Lemma6.3(ii) does not independently restate this range; the formal statement makes it explicit.\nr>=0 and0<delta<1, including zero radius. The genuine infimum p-displacement transportCost(P,Q)<=ofReal(r^p) is the input, not a supplied optimal coupling or proxy.\nFinite marginal p-moments are not assumed or concluded; this raw-budget theorem is an explicit generalization of the source Pp presentation. Its relation to a full Wp metric API remains separate.\nThe same proxy and coupling precede all tau>0,q>1. Their independence from tau is justified by the actual truncation construction, strengthening the source fixed-time presentation.\nLet P,Q be probability measures on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space. Let real p>=2,r>=0 and 0<delta<1. Suppose the actual infimum over couplings of the pth displacement integral is at most ofReal(r^p). There exist one probability proxy Pdag and one probability coupling Gamma of Pdag,Q such that every measurable event B satisfies |P.real B-Pdag.real B|<=delta and norm(x-y)<=r delta^(-1/p) Gamma-a.e. For this same Pdag and Gamma, every tau>0 and real q>1 satisfy: Htau Pdag is absolutely continuous with respect to Htau Q; its actual ENNReal RN qth-power integral is at most ofReal exp(q(q-1)r^2/(2tau delta^(2/p))); the real RN qth power is integrable under Htau Q, its integral has the same exponential bound, and its logarithm divided by q-1 is at most q r^2/(2tau delta^(2/p)). Htau is the existing actual GaussianSmoothing operator with scale sqrt(tau).",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, including dimension zero. Let P,Q be probability measures and real p,r,delta satisfy p>=2,r>=0,0<delta<1. Assume the actual extended-nonnegative infimum over measures gamma whose first/second marginals are P,Q of the nonnegative integral of ofReal(norm(x-y)^p) is at most ofReal(r^p). This hypothesis does not supply an attaining coupling. There exist measures Pdag on E and Gamma on E times E such that both are probability measures, Gamma has first marginal Pdag and second marginal Q, every Borel measurable event B satisfies abs(P(B).toReal-Pdag(B).toReal)<=delta, and norm(x-y)<=r delta^(-1/p) Gamma-almost everywhere. For every real tau>0 and q>1, let Htau(mu) be the actual law of X+sqrt(tau)Z using the product of mu and the centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian on E, and f_tau=dHtau(Pdag)/dHtau(Q) the extended nonnegative RN derivative. Then Htau(Pdag) is absolutely continuous with respect to Htau(Q); the extended nonnegative integral of f_tau^q under Htau(Q) is at most ofReal(exp(q(q-1)r^2/(2tau delta^(2/p)))); the real function (f_tau.toReal)^q is integrable under Htau(Q); its real Bochner integral is at most exp(q(q-1)r^2/(2tau delta^(2/p))); and the real logarithm of that same integral divided by q-1 is at most q r^2/(2tau delta^(2/p)). The witnesses Pdag,Gamma precede the universal quantifiers over tau,q and are the same for every smoothing conclusion; they may depend on E,P,Q,p,r,delta. The displayed constants have no explicit dimension dependence. The approved context supplies actual coupling, transport-infimum, Gaussian, product/pushforward, RN and integral definitions. No individual moment, density or regularity assumption on P,Q, or transport optimizer, is displayed. Integrability is explicit. Extended powers, ofReal, toReal and real log retain their specified totalized conventions; no pointwise finiteness premise is inserted. No source text was visible and no source-fidelity judgment is made.",
