      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCGaussianKL",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCGaussianKL",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-gaussian-kl · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.GaussianKL.gaussian_kl_reverse_transport.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS2.SSS1",
      "original_theorem": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel E, including zero dimension; P,Q probability measures.\nr>=0 and tau>0. Zero radius is included; nonnegative radius is retained for its geometric meaning although the algebra uses only r^2.\nThe actual extended nonnegative infimum quadratic displacement transportCost(P,Q)<=ofReal(r^2) is the input; no optimizer or supplied coupling premise.\nSource Lemma6.3(i) uses Euclidean marginal P2 membership and W2. The proved raw-cost formulation and finite-dimensional inner-product domain are explicit generalizations; finite displacement cost does not imply marginal moments.\nInformationTheory.klDiv is the actual ENNReal divergence, with absolute continuity and LLR integrability proved before using its real integral formula. No exponential displacement moment is required.\nLet P,Q be probability measures on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space E, including dimension zero. Let r>=0 and tau>0. Suppose the actual infimum over couplings gamma of the extended nonnegative integral of ofReal(norm(x-y)^2) is at most ofReal(r^2). Then the actual extended-nonnegative InformationTheory.klDiv of GaussianSmoothing P sqrt(tau) relative to GaussianSmoothing Q sqrt(tau) is at most ofReal(r^2/(2tau)). GaussianSmoothing is the product-noise addition pushforward with centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian, scaled by sqrt(tau). No marginal second moments, optimizer, Gaussian KL formula or target LLR integrability are assumed.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its Borel measurable structure, every pair of probability measures P,Q, and every real r,tau, assume r>=0,tau>0 and the actual extended-nonnegative infimum over all measures gamma on E times E whose first/second marginals are P,Q of the nonnegative integral of ofReal(norm(x-y)^2) is at most ofReal(r^2). Then klDiv(gaussianSmoothing(P,sqrt(tau)),gaussianSmoothing(Q,sqrt(tau)))<=ofReal(r^2/(2tau)). No attaining coupling is assumed. Gaussian smoothing is the addition pushforward of mu product kappa_sqrt(tau), where kappa_sqrt(tau) is the pushforward of the centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian by multiplication by sqrt(tau). Dimension zero is allowed. The conclusion concerns the actual extended-nonnegative divergence in the direction smoothed P relative to smoothed Q. For these probability laws mu,nu it equals ofReal(integral log((dmu/dnu).toReal) dmu) when mu is absolutely continuous with respect to nu and that log likelihood ratio is integrable under mu; otherwise it equals infinity. Absolute continuity and log-likelihood integrability are not additional hypotheses. The finite bound concerns the divergence itself, not its totalized real conversion. All space, measure and parameter quantifiers are universal. There are no additional dimension, moment, density or regularity assumptions in the printed statement. The constant is exactly 1/(2tau), without a dimension factor. The reconstruction uses only the printed statement and approved definitions; it makes no source-fidelity judgment and does not independently verify compilation or hashes.",
