      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-rgo-backward · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.RGOBackward.rgo_backward_recovery.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS2.SSS1",
      "original_theorem": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including dimension zero; mu is a probability measure.\nb>=0, a>0 and arbitrary u. Precision b=0 retains the source A=infinity case.\nThe kernel is selected before all probability inputs nu and radii r>=0. The budget is transportCost(nu,rho), in that direction.\nGeneral probability base abstracts the source Gibbs presentation; no concrete potential identification is included.\nActual raw infimum cost is used, without inferring marginal P2 membership or claiming full W2 API correspondence.\nLet mu be a probability measure on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, b>=0, a>0 and u a point. Define rho as mu tilted by -b*norm(x-u)^2/2. Then rho is a probability measure and there exists one Markov kernel K, chosen before every input law and radius, with K(y)=rho.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2a)) at every y, equivalently mu tilted with precision b+a^-1 and center (b+a^-1)^-1 times (b*u+a^-1*y). The actual composition K with GaussianSmoothing rho sqrt(a) equals rho. For all probability nu and r>=0 with actual infimum quadratic displacement cost from nu to rho at most ofReal(r^2), the actual KL of K composed with GaussianSmoothing nu sqrt(a) relative to rho is at most ofReal(r^2/(2a)).",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure; dimension zero is permitted. Let mu be any probability measure. For every real b,a with b>=0 and a>0, and every u in E, define rho=tilted(mu,x maps to -(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2). Tilt is normalized exponential reweighting with the supplied totalized normalization convention. Then rho is a probability measure and there exists a measurable Markov kernel K:E to E such that: (1) For every y, equality of measures K(y)=tilted(rho,x maps to -norm(x-y)^2/(2*a)). (2) For every y the same kernel equals tilted(mu,x maps to -((b+a^-1)/2)*norm(x-(b+a^-1)^-1 scalar-multiplied by (b scalar-multiplied by u+a^-1 scalar-multiplied by y))^2). (3) Let G_sqrt(a)(P) be the law of X+sqrt(a)*Z under the actual product P times centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian. Exact recovery holds: K composed with G_sqrt(a)(rho)=rho. Kernel composition with eta assigns every measurable event B the integral of K(y,B) against eta. (4) For every probability nu and real r>=0, if the actual extended-nonnegative infimum over measures gamma on E times E with first marginal nu and second marginal rho of the extended-nonnegative integral of ofReal(norm(x-z)^2) is at most ofReal(r^2), then actual klDiv(K composed with G_sqrt(a)(nu),rho)<=ofReal(r^2/(2*a)). No optimizing coupling is assumed. The existential K is chosen after E,mu,b,a,u but before nu,r; the same K satisfies both pointwise fibers, recovery and all divergence bounds. Neither fiber equality is only almost everywhere. The divergence is extended nonnegative: infinity unless the first measure is absolutely continuous relative to the second and their log RN derivative is integrable under the first; otherwise ofReal of that log-density integral plus second total real mass minus first total real mass. The conclusion bounds the actual divergence in that direction, not its totalized real conversion. Absolute continuity and log-density integrability are not extra hypotheses. No density, moment, smoothness or nondegeneracy assumption on mu or nu is stated beyond probability and the displayed transport budget. The exact constant is 1/(2*a). Only the anonymous packet and approved definitions were used; no source-fidelity verdict or compilation claim.",
