      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS2.SSS1",
      "original_theorem": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space including zero dimension; mu probability; b>=0 and arbitrary u.\neta>=0 and tau>0, so total eta+tau>0. Zero existing smoothing time is allowed.\nThe kernel may depend on mu,b,eta,tau,u but is chosen before nu,r. No joint measurable choice across these parameters is asserted.\nThe proposal input is the actual ENNReal W2(nu,H_eta rho)<=ofReal(r), r>=0. Its exact square identity gives the internal quadratic coupling budget; no toReal fallback, optimizer or marginal moments are supplied.\nGeneral probability base and absence of marginal P2 assumptions explicitly generalize the source Gibbs/P2 setting. This packet uses the existing actual W2 interface; concrete normalized source times and full recursion remain separate.\nLet mu be a probability measure on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, b>=0, eta>=0, tau>0 and u a point. Put rho=mu.tilted(-b*norm(x-u)^2/2). Then rho is probability and H_tau(H_eta rho)=H_(eta+tau)rho as actual measures, where H_s is GaussianSmoothing at standard deviation sqrt(s). There exists one Markov kernel K, selected before all proposal laws nu and radii r, with every-point fiber rho.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2*(eta+tau))), and K composed with H_tau(H_eta rho)=rho. For every probability nu and r>=0 with actual extended-nonnegative WassersteinSpace.wassersteinDistance(nu,H_eta rho)<=ofReal(r), the actual ENNReal KL(K composed with H_tau nu,rho)<=ofReal(r^2/(2*tau)).",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel structure; zero dimension is permitted. Let mu be any probability measure. For any real b,eta,tau with b>=0,eta>=0,tau>0 and any u, let rho be mu reweighted by exp(-(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2) and normalized by its integral. Let S_s(P) be the actual law of X+sZ under P times the centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian. Then rho is probability and S_sqrt(tau)(S_sqrt(eta)(rho))=S_sqrt(eta+tau)(rho). There exists one measurable Markov kernel K such that for every y, K(y) is rho reweighted by exp(-norm(x-y)^2/(2*(eta+tau))) and normalized by its rho integral. The exact measure identity K composed with S_sqrt(tau)(S_sqrt(eta)(rho))=rho holds. Kernel composition with P assigns each measurable B the integral K(y,B) dP(y), and each fiber is probability. The same K simultaneously satisfies for every probability nu and real r>=0: if W2(nu,S_sqrt(eta)(rho))<=ofReal(r), then actual KL(K composed with S_sqrt(tau)(nu),rho)<=ofReal(r^2/(2*tau)). W2(P,Q) is the extended-nonnegative square root of the actual infimum over measures Gamma whose first marginal is P and second is Q of the extended-nonnegative integral of ofReal(norm(x-y)^2). No separate second-moment hypothesis on either marginal is imposed. The divergence direction is reconstructed output relative to rho. Actual ENNReal KL for probability laws equals ofReal(integral log((dP/dQ).toReal) dP) when P is absolutely continuous relative to Q and that logarithm is P-integrable, and infinity otherwise. Neither absolute continuity nor log-integrability is an extra premise. K may depend on E,mu,b,eta,tau,u but is chosen before nu,r. Its fiber formula is everywhere, not only almost everywhere. Its tilt uses total eta+tau, while the bound uses added tau exactly, coefficient1/(2*tau). Only the anonymous statement and approved definitions were used; no source-fidelity or compilation judgment.",
