ula, including m=0. explicit-elaboration the lean name strongconvexon does not silently exclude m=0: hm is nonnegative, and the decoded/lesson chord formula is the governing meaning. on the source domain fréchet and classical hessian senses agree. constant dependencies chord correction m/2 and hessian lower bound m, with no dimension-dependent factor. the same m/2 and m, with the norm from the same euclidean inner product. same neither joining the two iff statements nor identifying the hessian rescales the modulus. no unspecified constants or dependencies are introduced. scopes informational strongconvexon at m=0 expresses ordinary convexity despite the theorem name. the actual nonnegativity hypothesis and published chord formula explicitly include zero and preserve definition 1.5. quantifiers informational the natural-number dimension includes zero, a harmless explicit boundary case. the lesson says d=0 is allowed; source imposes no d>0 assumption. there are no nonzero directions in that case, and both chord and hessian conditions reduce to identities.",
