      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.AdaptiveKLError.adaptive_center_kl_error.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS3",
      "original_theorem": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space including dimension zero; arbitrary probability base mu; b>=0,a>0.\nT,H,B are constructed before every center law nu, input P and approximate Markov L; fiber formulas are everywhere.\nP is any actual probability joint input law. Its divergence from the ideal nu compProd H is explicitly charged.\nL is an actual measurable Markov kernel. It need not retain the center; relative conditional KL may then be infinite.\nNo AC, finite KL, LLR integrability or separately assumed fiber-KL measurability. General probability-base joint semantics explicitly extend the source setting.\nLet mu be a probability measure on a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space E,b>=0,a>0. Construct Markov kernels T,H:E to E and B:E times E to E times E. Every T(u) is mu tilted by -b*norm(x-u)^2/2, and H(u) is its actual Gaussian smoothing at standard-deviation sqrt(a). Every B(u,y) retains u and draws from T(u) tilted by -norm(x-y)^2/(2a), equivalently from mu tilted at precision b+a^-1 and center (b+a^-1)^-1*(b*u+a^-1*y). For every probability center law nu, B composed with nu compProd H equals nu compProd T. The same T,H,B satisfy for every probability center law nu, every probability input law P on E times E and every Markov kernel L on E times E: s to actual ENNReal KL(L(s),B(s)) is measurable, and actual KL(L composed with P,nu compProd T) is at most KL(P,nu compProd H) plus the nonnegative integral of KL(L(s),B(s)) against P. All KL terms and the integral may be infinite.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, mu any probability measure, b>=0 and a>0. There exist Markov kernels T,H:E to E and B:E times E to E times E. For every u,T(u) is mu reweighted by exp(-(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2) and normalized by its mu integral. H(u) is the law of X+sqrt(a)*Z with X of law T(u) and independent centered identity-covariance Gaussian Z; sqrt(a) is the standard-deviation scale. For every u,y, B(u,y) is the pushforward by x to (u,x) of T(u) tilted by -norm(x-y)^2/(2a), equivalently of mu tilted by -(c/2)*norm(x-m(u,y))^2, with c=b+a^-1 and m(u,y)=c^-1*(b*u+a^-1*y). Both normalized fiber identities hold everywhere, and B retains the first coordinate u. For every probability nu, B composed with nu compProd H equals nu compProd T as full joint laws: sample u from nu and y from H(u), then apply B, to obtain the joint law of u and x with x drawn from T(u). Furthermore for every probability nu on E, probability P on E times E and Markov L:E times E to E times E, s to KL(L(s),B(s)) is measurable, and KL(L composed with P,nu compProd T)<=KL(P,nu compProd H)+the nonnegative integral of KL(L(s),B(s)) against P. T,H,B are chosen after E,mu,b,a and before nu,P,L; the same choice works simultaneously for all later inputs. No additional moment,density,AC,integrability or finite-KL hypotheses. Kernel measurability belongs to the kernel structure; fiber-KL measurability is an additional conclusion. B is the specified ideal kernel whereas L is arbitrary and need not preserve first coordinate; P need not have first marginal nu. The bound concerns full joint laws, with the integral against P. All KL values, addition, inequality and nonnegative integral are extended nonnegative real-valued with infinity permitted. Under the supplied definition probability KL is infinite if AC or required log-density integrability fails. No finiteness is asserted and infinite RHS is permitted. Only the anonymous packet was read; no compilation or source-fidelity judgment.",
