      "original_theorem": "Let f be a convex C1 beta-smooth real-valued function on all Euclidean d-space, with beta>=0 as in Definition1.12. Smoothness means f(y)<=f(x)+<grad f(x),y-x>+(beta/2)||y-x||^2 for every x,y. Exercise3.1 explicitly says second differentiability is not required. Equation (3.5) asserts ||grad f(y)-grad f(x)||^2<=beta<grad f(y)-grad f(x),y-x> for all x,y, obtained by exchanging endpoints in (3.4).",
