    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCStoppedRGODepth",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCStoppedRGODepth",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-stopped-rgo-depth · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StoppedRGODepth.stopped_rgo_depth.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1",
      "original_theorem": "E is finite-dimensional over the reals with its Borel measurable structure, and d=finrank_R(E)>0. mu is any probability measure; no density or moment assumption is added.\nkappa>=1, 0<c<1/4, q>=2, 0<Delta<=1/2, 0<gamma<=1 and C>=8 are explicit scalar conditions.\neta is measurable and lies in (0,c] at every state. It may depend on precision, center, count and full padded history; there is no common predetermined sequence across all paths.\ns0 is fixed before the terminal variance B, its inverse precision threshold and J are computed. These remain fixed throughout the entire execution.\nQ and Lterm are arbitrary Markov kernels. The actual absorbed update and all finite output kernels are constructed using FiniteRGOProgram.\nSource formulas correspond to baseline smoothness one. Initial precision may be zero or already beyond the threshold. Arbitrary starting count/history is not asserted to be a valid record of previous calls.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space of dimension d=finrank_R(E)>0 and mu a probability measure. Use states s=(b,u,k,h) in NNReal times E times Nat times E^Nat. Fix kappa>=1, 0<c<1/4, q>=2, 0<Delta<=1/2, 0<gamma<=1 and C>=8. Let eta be measurable on the full state and satisfy 0<eta(s)<=c everywhere. Fix initial s0 and arbitrary Markov observation and terminal kernels Q,Lterm. Define K(r)=(1+r)/(1/kappa+r), tau(r)=K(r) when K(r)>=2 and c otherwise, and a(s)=(eta(s)+tau(b))/(1+b). Compute ell=q+log(K(b0)*d*q/Delta), B=gamma/(sqrt(d*ell)+ell) and J=ceil(C*log(e*K(b0)/B)) once from s0. There exist an update F, a Markov state kernel P and Markov output kernels R_n. F adds 1/a(s) to precision, updates the center to (b*u+y/a(s))/(b+1/a(s)), increments the count and prepends y to history. P(s)=dirac s when 1/B<=b and is the F(s,.) pushforward of Q(s) otherwise. For all n, R_n=Lterm composed with P^n. B is positive, P^J(s0) assigns mass one to the terminal set {s:1/B<=b(s)}, and for every m, R_(J+m)(s0)=R_J(s0). Finally J<=(3*C+(C/2)*log(1/gamma))*ell.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space with actual real dimension d>0, mu any probability measure on E, and S=NNReal times E times Nat times E^Nat. Write s=(b,u,k,h), casting b to a real in arithmetic. For any measurable eta:S to R, parameters kappa,c,q,Delta,gamma,C satisfying kappa>=1,0<c<1/4,0<eta(s)<=c for every state,q>=2,0<Delta<=1/2,0<gamma<=1,C>=8, any initial s0=(b0,u0,k0,h0) and any Markov kernels Q,Lterm:S to E, define K(r)=(1+r)/(kappa^-1+r), tau(r)=K(r) if K(r)>=2 and c otherwise, and a(s)=(eta(s)+tau(b))/(1+b). Put ell=q+log(K(b0)*d*q/Delta), B=gamma/(sqrt(d*ell)+ell) and J=Nat.ceil(C*log(e*K(b0)/B)).\nThere exist a function F:S times E to S, a kernel P:S to S and a sequence R_n:S to E. For all s,y, the real cast of the first coordinate of F(s,y) is b_new=b+1/a(s), and its other coordinates are exactly b_new^-1*(b*u+y/a(s)),k+1,h_new, where h_new(0)=y and h_new(n+1)=h(n). Vector products mean scalar multiplication. P and every R_n are Markov. For every state s, P(s)=dirac s if b>=1/B, and otherwise P(s) is the pushforward of Q(s) by y to F(s,y). For every n, the entire kernel R_n equals Lterm composed with P^n, applying P^n first; P^0 is identity.\nB>0. The J-step state law from the specified s0 assigns mass one to states with precision at least 1/B. For every m, R_(J+m)(s0)=R_J(s0) as output measures at that initial state only, not necessarily as entire kernels. Finally J, cast to a real, is at most (3*C+(C/2)*log(1/gamma))*ell.\nK depends on kappa; tau on kappa,c; a on eta,kappa,c and current state. ell depends on q,kappa,b0,d,Delta; B additionally on gamma; J additionally on C. These constants do not depend on Q,Lterm,mu or the other initial coordinates. The stopping threshold is fixed using s0 although the fiber formula for P holds globally. The existential witnesses follow all supplied data. mu is supplied as a probability measure but does not otherwise occur in the displayed conditions or conclusion; no relation between mu,Q,Lterm beyond probability/Markov assumptions is stated. eta needs only measurability and the global bounds. Measurability of F is not a separate asserted conclusion.",
