    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCFiniteRGOKLError",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCFiniteRGOKLError",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-finite-rgo-kl-error · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.FiniteRGOKLError.finite_rgo_kl_error.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS3",
      "original_theorem": "E is finite-dimensional over the reals with its Borel measurable structure; zero dimension is permitted. mu is a probability measure.\na is measurable and strictly positive at every state. theta is fixed and nonnegative. Initial precision can be zero or already stopped.\nQ and L are measurable Markov kernels on the complete precision-center-count-history state. No probability density or moment assumption is added.\nT,H are constructed before arbitrary Q,L. F, P and all R_n have their displayed actual program semantics.\nNo finite KL, absolute continuity, assumed error measurability, common observation-error budget or terminal-error bound is a premise.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, and mu any probability measure. States are s=(b,u,k,h) in NNReal times E times Nat times E^Nat. Let a(s)>0 be measurable and theta a fixed nonnegative precision threshold. Define F(s,y) by b_new=b+1/a(s), u_new=(b*u+y/a(s))/(b+1/a(s)), count k+1 and history with y prepended. There exist Markov kernels T,H, constructed before all actual kernels, with T(s) the normalized tilt of mu by -b*norm(x-u)^2/2 and H(s) its Gaussian smoothing with standard deviation sqrt(a(s)). For every Markov observation kernel Q and terminal kernel L there exist Markov P and R_n: P(s)=dirac s if theta<=b and otherwise the pushforward of Q(s) under F(s,.); R_0=L; R_(n+1)(s)=L(s) if stopped and otherwise the bind of Q(s) with y mapped to R_n(F(s,y)). Define e(s)=0 if stopped and KL(Q(s)||H(s)) otherwise, and t(s)=KL(L(s)||T(s)). Both e and t are measurable. For every n and initial s, KL(R_n(s)||T(s)) is at most the sum over j<n of the integral of e under P^j(s), plus the integral of t under P^n(s).",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, mu any probability measure on E, and S=NNReal times E times Nat times E^Nat. Let a:S to R be measurable and positive at every state, and let B be any nonnegative threshold. For s=(b,u,k,h), define F(s,y)=(b+1/a(s),(b*u+y/a(s))/(b+1/a(s)),k+1,h_y), with h_y(0)=y and h_y(m+1)=h(m). Vector division means reciprocal scalar multiplication and the first coordinate remains NNReal.\nThere exist Markov kernels T,H:S to E with T(s) equal to mu normalized by the density exp(-b*norm(x-u)^2/2) and H(s) equal to its convolution with the centered isotropic Gaussian of standard deviation sqrt(a(s)). After these same T,H are fixed, for every Markov Q,L:S to E there exist Markov P:S to S and Markov R_n:S to E, with P(s)=dirac s if B<=b and the F(s,.) pushforward of Q(s) otherwise. R_0=L, and R_(n+1)(s)=L(s) if B<=b and the bind of Q(s) with y mapped to R_n(F(s,y)) otherwise. Equality with the threshold belongs to the stopped branch.\nDefine e(s)=0 if B<=b and KL(Q(s)||H(s)) otherwise, and t(s)=KL(L(s)||T(s)). Both are measurable extended-nonnegative-real functions. For every n and every initial s, KL(R_n(s)||T(s)) <= sum over 0<=j<n of integral e(x) under P^j(s), plus integral t(x) under P^n(s). P^0 is the identity kernel. The terminal term is integrated under the time-n state law, not evaluated at the initial state. The left reference law is T(s) at the initial state. All KL values, sums and nonnegative integrals may be infinity; no absolute continuity or finite entropy assumption is present. For n=0 the sum is empty and the conclusion is KL(L(s)||T(s))<=t(s).\nQuantifiers are all E,mu,a with the displayed structures and assumptions, then all B, then existence of T,H, then all Markov Q,L, then existence of P and the entire sequence R_n, then all n,s. P,R may depend on Q,L; T,H are chosen before them. No approximation quality of Q,L, bounded stopping time or threshold-hitting conclusion is stated.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "domain-mismatch",
