    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCStoppedGaussianRGOError",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCStoppedGaussianRGOError",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-stopped-gaussian-rgo-error · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StoppedGaussianRGOError.stopped_gaussian_rgo_error.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S6.SS3",
      "original_theorem": "E has its Borel structure and actual dimension d=finrank_R(E)>0; mu is any probability measure.\nkappa>=1,0<c<1/4,0<Delta<=1/2,0<gamma<=1,C>=8; eta is measurable and in (0,c] at every state.\nq=2 is fixed. B and J are computed once from the fixed initial state s0 and used throughout execution.\nM,L are Markov kernels. Only states outside D require the displayed source-scaled squared-W2 premise for M.\nTerminal KL is unrestricted for the residual inequality. Only the final total-error implication assumes its bound on D; no condition is imposed outside D.\nLet E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space of positive real dimension d, and mu a probability measure. States s=(b,u,k,h) belong to NNReal times E times Nat times E^Nat. Let eta be measurable with 0<eta(s)<=c at every state. Assume kappa>=1, 0<c<1/4, 0<Delta<=1/2, 0<gamma<=1 and C>=8. Fix s0. Define K(r)=(1+r)/(1/kappa+r), tau(r)=K(r) if K(r)>=2 and c otherwise, a(s)=(eta(s)+tau(b))/(1+b), ell=2+log(K(b0)*d*2/Delta), B=gamma/(sqrt(d*ell)+ell), J=ceil(C*log(e*K(b0)/B)), and D={s:1/B<=b}. There exist Markov T,H with T(s) the normalized quadratic tilt of mu at precision b and center u, and H(s) its Gaussian smoothing at standard deviation sqrt(a(s)). After T,H are fixed, take any Markov M,L such that at each s outside D, squared W2(M(s),GaussianSmoothing(T(s),sqrt(eta(s)/(1+b))))<=ofReal(K(b)*[2*tau(b)*Delta^2/(K(b)*(J+1))]/(1+b)). There exist F,Q,P,R: F updates precision to b+1/a(s), center to (b*u+y/a(s))/(b+1/a(s)), count to k+1 and prepends y to history; Q(s) is M(s) with independent Gaussian variance tau(b)/(1+b) added; P(s)=dirac s on D and otherwise the F(s,.) pushforward of Q(s). Q,P and all R_n are Markov and R_n=L composed with P^n. B>0, P^J(s0)(D)=1, and R_(J+m)(s0)=R_J(s0) for all m. Without terminal accuracy assumptions, KL(R_J(s0)||T(s0))<=J*ofReal(Delta^2/(J+1))+integral over D of KL(L(x)||T(x)) under P^J(s0). If KL(L(s)||T(s))<=ofReal(Delta^2/(J+1)) holds for every s in D, then KL(R_(J+m)(s0)||T(s0))<=ofReal(Delta^2) for every natural m.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, of positive dimension d, and mu any probability measure. Set S=NNReal times E times Nat times (Nat to E), writing s=(b,u,k,h). Let eta:S to Real be measurable. For any real kappa,c,Delta,gamma,C satisfying kappa>=1,0<c<1/4,0<eta(s)<=c for every s,0<Delta<=1/2,0<gamma<=1,C>=8, and any initial state s0=(b0,u0,k0,h0), define K(r)=(1+r)/(kappa^-1+r), tau(r)=K(r) if K(r)>=2 and c otherwise, a(s)=(eta(s)+tau(b))/(1+b). Define ell=2+log(2*K(b0)*d/Delta), B=gamma/(sqrt(d*ell)+ell), J=Nat.ceil(C*log(e*K(b0)/B)), and D={s:b>=B^-1}.\nThere exist Markov kernels T,H:S to E such that T(s) is mu tilted by x mapped to -(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2, meaning probability proportional to exp(-(b/2)*norm(x-u)^2) mu(dx), and H(s) is T(s) convolved with centered isotropic Gaussian covariance a(s)I.\nFor every pair of Markov M,L:S to E satisfying for every s outside D, squared W2(M(s),G_sqrt(eta(s)/(1+b))(T(s)))<=ofReal(K(b)*[2*tau(b)*Delta^2/(K(b)*(J+1))]/(1+b)), there exist F:S times E to S, Markov Q:S to E,P:S to S, and Markov R_n:S to E. For every s,y, F(s,y)=(b+a(s)^-1,(b+a(s)^-1)^-1*(b*u+a(s)^-1*y),k+1,y::h), with real scalar-vector products and history (y::h)(0)=y,(y::h)(n+1)=h(n). Q(s)=G_sqrt(tau(b)/(1+b))(M(s)). P(s)=dirac s on D and the pushforward of Q(s) by F(s,.) off D. For every n, R_n=L composed with P^n: n state transitions then L.\nThen B>0, P^J(s0)(D)=1, and R_(J+m)(s0)=R_J(s0) for every natural m. Moreover KL(R_J(s0)||T(s0))<=J*ofReal(Delta^2/(J+1))+integral over D of KL(L(x)||T(x)) under P^J(s0). If additionally KL(L(s)||T(s))<=ofReal(Delta^2/(J+1)) for every s in D, then KL(R_(J+m)(s0)||T(s0))<=ofReal(Delta^2) for every natural m.\nG_sigma adds independent centered isotropic Gaussian standard deviation sigma. Wasserstein distance and KL are extended-nonnegative; the nonnegative residual integral may be infinite. No density, moment, convexity or smoothness of mu is assumed. The arbitrary initial counter and history are unrestricted and eta can depend on all coordinates. T,H precede the universal M,L; F,Q,P,R follow them and their approximation assumption. The update and smoothing formulas hold everywhere, the transport premise only off D, and the optional terminal premise throughout D. Stopping, stabilization and final KL concern fixed s0; the reference is T(s0), whereas the residual reference varies as T(x). F measurability is not a separate public conjunct. H does not appear in the later transport premise or entropy conclusions.",
