      "repair_proposals": [
        {
          "id": "ASTIS-REPAIR-ANDI-GD-NONNEGATIVE-STEP",
          "class": "assumption-addition",
          "status": "accepted",
          "necessity": "mathematically-necessary",
          "proposed_change": "In Theorem3.3 replace the printed step restriction h<=1/beta with 0<=h<=1/beta. Retain the pinned source statement separately; do not overwrite it.",
          "reconstructed_statement": "In the source C2 Euclidean setting, let f be alpha-convex and beta-smooth. For every x,y and step size 0 <= h <= 1/beta, with T(z)=z-h grad f(z), ||T(y)-T(x)|| <= sqrt(1-alpha h)||y-x||. The source positive reciprocal and ordinary square-root domains remain unchanged; this proposal only makes the missing nonnegative-step restriction explicit.",
          "statement_sha256": "8a047dafe3d5c1e8605ca06c74c3f9817afa64874f9eab0afc6ebeb75c5f34de",
          "justification": "The literal all-real-step statement fails for every negative h on f(t)=t^2/2 with alpha=beta=1. The proof needs h>=0 when multiplying the curvature and step bounds.",
          "minimality_evidence": "Only add h>=0; include h=0 because T is then identity and the factor is 1. No strict positivity of h, no additional smoothness, and no dimension restriction is proposed. Existing reciprocal/square-root source domains are not redefined. Removing h>=0 admits the explicit quadratic counterexample.",
          "reference_or_counterexample": "{\"counterexample\": \"f(t)=t^2/2 on R, alpha=beta=1, h=-1, x=0,y=1: h<=1/beta but 2>sqrt(2). For every h<0, (1-h)^2-(1-h)=h(h-1)>0.\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3\"}",
          "review": {
            "state": "accepted",
            "reviewer": "complexity_repair_9729",
            "independent_from_formalizer": true,
            "independent_from_decoder": true,
            "evidence": "Independently checked the exact proposal against https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3, Section 3 opening, Definition 3.2, Theorem 3.3 and its proof. The printed theorem supplies only h <= 1/beta. Its setting and displayed estimate agree with the proposal; the proposal preserves the pinned statement and adds only a step-domain restriction. Necessity is mathematical: for f(t)=t^2/2 on R, alpha=beta=1 and x=0,y=1, T(y)-T(x)=1-h. Every h<0 satisfies the printed upper bound, but 1-h>1 and hence 1-h>sqrt(1-h). Equivalently, the positive difference of squares is h(h-1)>0. At h=-1 the failed bound is 2 <= sqrt(2). This counterexample has positive moduli, ordinary real square roots, and C-infinity regularity, so no denominator, smoothness or representation issue causes failure. Sufficiency can be checked directly: writing v=y-x, d=grad f(y)-grad f(x), p=<d,v>, curvature and cocoercivity give p>=alpha||v||^2>=0 and ||d||^2<=beta p. For 0<=h and beta h<=1, ||v-hd||^2<=||v||^2-2hp+beta h^2 p<=||v||^2-hp<=(1-alpha h)||v||^2. Thus the proposed source-domain estimate follows. Minimality holds for the uniform theorem class: any retained negative step is refuted by the same quadratic, while h=0 gives equality and must remain allowed. No stronger positivity or extra regularity is required. Acceptance covers this precise repair only; the Hilbert/C1 extension, zero-modulus interpretation and subsequent complexity obligation are separate boundaries and are not certified by this verdict. No prior review or repair verdict was read; no repository edits or builds were performed.",
            "review_run_sha256": "790b93593839be533260f927c94a8d2a82b8423edc01be3951838e054f6db233",
            "reviewer_packet_sha256": "e279d92f0a10dc3fab0cb0fa3289c297a01df657795edb1daec78f06c9197482",
            "proposal_sha256": "605e0d27935fc270ca0a51aa0780b62154443a56935bc35649cd3722687862a6",
            "run_artifact": "runs/semantic-roundtrip/andi-opt-gd-distance-complexity/repair-review-current-0.json"
          },
          "proposal_author": "coco_source"
        }
