      "label": "In Theorem3.3 replace the printed step restriction h<=1/beta with 0<=h<=1/beta. Retain the pinned source statement separately; do not overwrite it.",
      "status": "fidelity-repaired",
      "subtitle": "assumption-addition · mathematically-necessary",
      "summary": "The literal all-real-step statement fails for every negative h on f(t)=t^2/2 with alpha=beta=1. The proof needs h>=0 when multiplying the curvature and step bounds.",
      "column": 8,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "repaired_theorem": "In the source C2 Euclidean setting, let f be alpha-convex and beta-smooth. For every x,y and step size 0 <= h <= 1/beta, with T(z)=z-h grad f(z), ||T(y)-T(x)|| <= sqrt(1-alpha h)||y-x||. The source positive reciprocal and ordinary square-root domains remain unchanged; this proposal only makes the missing nonnegative-step restriction explicit.",
      "details": [
        {
          "label": "Repair ID",
          "value": "ASTIS-REPAIR-ANDI-GD-NONNEGATIVE-STEP"
        },
        {
          "label": "Status",
          "value": "accepted"
        },
        {
          "label": "Minimality evidence",
          "value": "Only add h>=0; include h=0 because T is then identity and the factor is 1. No strict positivity of h, no additional smoothness, and no dimension restriction is proposed. Existing reciprocal/square-root source domains are not redefined. Removing h>=0 admits the explicit quadratic counterexample."
        },
        {
          "label": "Repaired statement hash",
          "value": "8a047dafe3d5c1e8605ca06c74c3f9817afa64874f9eab0afc6ebeb75c5f34de"
        },
        {
          "label": "Reference / counterexample",
          "value": "{\"counterexample\": \"f(t)=t^2/2 on R, alpha=beta=1, h=-1, x=0,y=1: h<=1/beta but 2>sqrt(2). For every h<0, (1-h)^2-(1-h)=h(h-1)>0.\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3\"}"
        },
        {
          "label": "Source mutation",
          "value": "forbidden; proposal remains separate"
        }
