      "search": "repair:astis-repair-andi-gd-nonnegative-step repair-proposal in theorem3.3 replace the printed step restriction h<=1/beta with 0<=h<=1/beta. retain the pinned source statement separately; do not overwrite it. assumption-addition · mathematically-necessary the literal all-real-step statement fails for every negative h on f(t)=t^2/2 with alpha=beta=1. the proof needs h>=0 when multiplying the curvature and step bounds. in the source c2 euclidean setting, let f be alpha-convex and beta-smooth. for every x,y and step size 0 <= h <= 1/beta, with t(z)=z-h grad f(z), ||t(y)-t(x)|| <= sqrt(1-alpha h)||y-x||. the source positive reciprocal and ordinary square-root domains remain unchanged; this proposal only makes the missing nonnegative-step restriction explicit. astis-repair-andi-gd-nonnegative-step accepted only add h>=0; include h=0 because t is then identity and the factor is 1. no strict positivity of h, no additional smoothness, and no dimension restriction is proposed. existing reciprocal/square-root source domains are not redefined. removing h>=0 admits the explicit quadratic counterexample. 8a047dafe3d5c1e8605ca06c74c3f9817afa64874f9eab0afc6ebeb75c5f34de {\"counterexample\": \"f(t)=t^2/2 on r, alpha=beta=1, h=-1, x=0,y=1: h<=1/beta but 2>sqrt(2). for every h<0, (1-h)^2-(1-h)=h(h-1)>0.\", \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#s3\"} forbidden; proposal remains separate",
