convention and global β/2 quadratic upper model. explicit-elaboration definition1.5 and definition1.12 match these normalizations. the actual gradient, global quantifiers, and regularity are displayed. c1 instead of c2 is a disclosed generalization. conclusion geometric and exponential distance chain. actual iterate distance ≤ sqrt(1-αh)^n r ≤ exp(-αhn/2)r. explicit-elaboration for positive source moduli and h=1/β, substitution gives its exact two bounds. natural powers remove endpoint ambiguity at κ=1,n=0. fermat gives the fixed point; iterated lipschitz control and 1-a≤exp(-a) justify the lesson. scopes the selected component of theorem3.3 and its following paragraph. the declaration supports only iterated-distance. explicit-elaboration checked the exact binding, complete module, and authored lesson. the refreshed item says complexity has its own declaration binding; historical uncovered/outside-this-unit prose is removed. separate source obligations are not silently credited to one declaration. constant dependencies κ=β/α and initial distance r. αh, natural n, and r; no hidden constant. explicit-elaboration at reciprocal step αh=1/κ, preserving the exponent factor 1/2 exactly. the extension permits zero moduli without division or a condition-number claim. domains informational disclosed extension from euclidean c2 objectives to complete real hilbert c1 objectives. the formal hypotheses retain the global curvature and upper model; the original setting is a specialization. quantifiers informational uniform admissible-step extension with natural-power endpoint convention. the source reciprocal-step instance is recovered for β>0; n=0 yields r≤r. the supplied global minimizer follows the source convention. assumptions informational nonnegative-step condition remains explicit in the reused one-step parent. the rate paragraph itself selects h=1/β>0 in its positive-modulus domain. no new source repair is required for this rate binding.",
