    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCPoissonRejection",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260911-SPHMCPoissonRejection",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-poisson-rejection · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PoissonRejection.poisson_rejection_output.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A1.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "S, X and A are arbitrary measurable spaces; Q:S->X is a Markov kernel.\nnu is a fixed probability measure on A, and B is a fixed real number with B>0.\nW:((S times X) times A)->Real is jointly measurable and satisfies |W((s,x),z)|<=B for every s,x,z.\nA fixed x0 in X defines the output on the never-success event.\nEach attempt draws independently from the displayed proposal/Poisson/infinite auxiliary/uniform product. Each retry is an independent whole attempt. Cost is the full N estimator calls for every attempt reached.\nLet Q be a Markov proposal kernel from a measurable parameter space S to a measurable space X, let nu be a fixed probability measure on auxiliary space A, and let W((s,x),z) be jointly measurable with |W|<=B for a fixed B>0. Fix a default x0. An attempt independently draws x from Q(s), N from Poisson(2B), an infinite iid nu sequence z, and U uniform on [0,1], and accepts when U is at most the product over i<N of (B+W((s,x),z_i))/(2B). Let Lambda_s be this actual product law, E_s its acceptance event, and p_s=Lambda_s(E_s). On an iid sequence of whole attempts, return the proposal at the first success, using x0 only on never-success, and charge N for every attempt whose predecessors all failed. There is a measurable Markov kernel R whose fiber is both the actual output law and Q(s) exponentially tilted by w(s,x)=integral W((s,x),z) nu(dz). Conditional acceptance is exp(w-B), the projected accepted submeasure is exp(w-B)Q(s), and p_s is its total mass with p_s>=exp(-2B). Never-success has measure zero; the first n attempts all fail with probability (1-p_s)^n. The expected total full-batch charge equals 2B/p_s and is at most 2B exp(2B).",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let S, X and A be arbitrary measurable spaces, Q a Markov probability kernel from S to X, and nu a probability measure on A. Let W:((S x X) x A)->R be jointly measurable. For every real B>0 satisfying |W((s,x),z)|<=B for all s,x,z, and every default x0 in X, define m_s(x)=integral W((s,x),z) dnu(z). At parameter s one attempt p=(x,k,z,u) has law Lambda_s=Q(s) x Poisson(2B) x nu^N x Uniform[0,1], with all displayed coordinates independent. Accept p precisely when u<=product_{i=0}^{k-1}(B+W((s,x),z_i))/(2B); the empty product is 1. Denote this event E_s and let a_s=Lambda_s(E_s). Let rho_s=Lambda_s^N be the law of an infinite independent sequence of attempts. Define out_s(omega) as the X coordinate of the least-index accepted attempt if one exists, and x0 otherwise. There exists a Markov kernel R from S to X such that, for every s, out_s is measurable and its rho_s pushforward is R(s), where R(s) is the exponential tilt of Q(s) by m_s, namely its density relative to Q(s) is exp(m_s(x))/integral exp(m_s(y)) dQ(s)(y). For every x the acceptance probability over the Poisson, auxiliary-sequence and uniform coordinates is exp(m_s(x)-B). The X marginal of Lambda_s restricted to E_s equals Q(s) with density exp(m_s(x)-B), and a_s=integral exp(m_s(x)-B) dQ(s)(x). The rho_s probability of no accepted attempt at any natural index is zero. For every natural n the probability that all attempts with index i<n fail is (1-a_s)^n. Moreover a_s>=exp(-2B). Define C_s(omega)=sum_{n=0}^infinity k_n times the indicator that every attempt i<n fails, where k_n is the Poisson coordinate of attempt n. This sum includes the first successful attempt; if no attempt succeeds, it sums every k_n. Its extended-nonnegative expectation is exactly a_s^(-1)*(2B) and is at most 2B*exp(2B). Probability, density and nonnegative-expectation equalities are interpreted in the extended nonnegative reals with ofReal embeddings as in the Lean statement. The output is a total function, including on the null event of endless rejection.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "domain-mismatch",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
