      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260911-sphmcpoissonrejection semantic-audit astis-rt-20260911-sphmcpoissonrejection companion:sphmc-poisson-rejection · domain-mismatch blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.poissonrejection.poisson_rejection_output. domain-mismatch source hidden from decoder s, x and a are arbitrary measurable spaces; q:s->x is a markov kernel. nu is a fixed probability measure on a, and b is a fixed real number with b>0. w:((s times x) times a)->real is jointly measurable and satisfies |w((s,x),z)|<=b for every s,x,z. a fixed x0 in x defines the output on the never-success event. each attempt draws independently from the displayed proposal/poisson/infinite auxiliary/uniform product. each retry is an independent whole attempt. cost is the full n estimator calls for every attempt reached. let q be a markov proposal kernel from a measurable parameter space s to a measurable space x, let nu be a fixed probability measure on auxiliary space a, and let w((s,x),z) be jointly measurable with |w|<=b for a fixed b>0. fix a default x0. an attempt independently draws x from q(s), n from poisson(2b), an infinite iid nu sequence z, and u uniform on [0,1], and accepts when u is at most the product over i<n of (b+w((s,x),z_i))/(2b). let lambda_s be this actual product law, e_s its acceptance event, and p_s=lambda_s(e_s). on an iid sequence of whole attempts, return the proposal at the first success, using x0 only on never-success, and charge n for every attempt whose predecessors all failed. there is a measurable markov kernel r whose fiber is both the actual output law and q(s) exponentially tilted by w(s,x)=integral w((s,x),z) nu(dz). conditional acceptance is exp(w-b), the projected accepted submeasure is exp(w-b)q(s), and p_s is its total mass with p_s>=exp(-2b). never-success has measure zero; the first n attempts all fail with probability (1-p_s)^n. the expected total full-batch charge equals 2b/p_s and is at most 2b exp(2b). let s, x and a be arbitrary measurable spaces, q a markov probability kernel from s to x, and nu a probability measure on a. let w:((s x x) x a)->r be jointly measurable. for every real b>0 satisfying |w((s,x),z)|<=b for all s,x,z, and every default x0 in x, define m_s(x)=integral w((s,x),z) dnu(z). at parameter s one attempt p=(x,k,z,u) has law lambda_s=q(s) x poisson(2b) x nu^n x uniform[0,1], with all displayed coordinates independent. accept p precisely when u<=product_{i=0}^{k-1}(b+w((s,x),z_i))/(2b); the empty product is 1. denote this event e_s and let a_s=lambda_s(e_s). let rho_s=lambda_s^n be the law of an infinite independent sequence of attempts. define out_s(omega) as the x coordinate of the least-index accepted attempt if one exists, and x0 otherwise. there exists a markov kernel r from s to x such that, for every s, out_s is measurable and its rho_s pushforward is r(s), where r(s) is the exponential tilt of q(s) by m_s, namely its density relative to q(s) is exp(m_s(x))/integral exp(m_s(y)) dq(s)(y). for every x the acceptance probability over the poisson, auxiliary-sequence and uniform coordinates is exp(m_s(x)-b). the x marginal of lambda_s restricted to e_s equals q(s) with density exp(m_s(x)-b), and a_s=integral exp(m_s(x)-b) dq(s)(x). the rho_s probability of no accepted attempt at any natural index is zero. for every natural n the probability that all attempts with index i<n fail is (1-a_s)^n. moreover a_s>=exp(-2b). define c_s(omega)=sum_{n=0}^infinity k_n times the indicator that every attempt i<n fails, where k_n is the poisson coordinate of attempt n. this sum includes the first successful attempt; if no attempt succeeds, it sums every k_n. its extended-nonnegative expectation is exactly a_s^(-1)*(2b) and is at most 2b*exp(2b). probability, density and nonnegative-expectation equalities are interpreted in the extended nonnegative reals with ofreal embeddings as in the lean statement. the output is a total function, including on the null event of endless rejection. accepted appendix a.1 lemma a.2; bounded poisson rejection mechanism and explicit actual retry costs autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.poissonrejection.poisson_rejection_output autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/poissonrejection.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_f 365bbf974b6fb4076b5350ca113a4fab6a2464dd83589203e6f7606f5f133236 accepted log_depth_source_review objects proposal, bounded conditional estimator, independent poisson batch and repeated product acceptance. actual independent four-coordinate attempts, iid whole-attempt stream, total first-success output and accumulated count. explicit-elaboration expanded products, finite acceptance, nat.find default and preceding-failure cost are explicit. domains a fixed proposal and conditional estimator; general fors may use path proposal and endpoint. arbitrary measurable parameter/proposal/auxiliary spaces, markov q, fixed auxiliary probability and jointly measurable w. different explicit parameterized extension, not representation of every abstract conditional estimator or path-endpoint simulator. quantifiers fixed proposal and bound determine the accepted law. for every admissible w,b,x0 there is one common r before all s; conditional acceptance for all x and tails for all n. explicit-elaboration no measurable selection from separate fiberwise existence; only fiberwise out measurability claimed. assumptions bounded estimator realizations and independent copies with rate 2b. fixed b>0, fixed probability nu, pointwise bound, joint measurability, explicit product draws and default. explicit-elaboration boundedness yields probability factors and integrability; no current count/acceptance independence. conclusion accepted exponential tilt and acceptance at least exp(-2b). public conditional acceptance, accepted submeasure, exact p, actual tilt, termination, failure tail and exact full-batch expecte