t, (2h ∑_{k=0}^{n−1} q^k)(f(x_n)−f(z)) ≤ q^n ‖x₀−z‖². the empty sum for n=0 is zero, t^[0] is the identity, and q^0=1 even when q=0. source-reviewed https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#s3; theorem3.4 weighted proof after lemma3.5 autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gradientdescentvalue.gradient_descent_weighted_value_bound autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/gradientdescentvalue.lean true andi-gdv-worker value_blind f99f4619eed1462a5863d14aace3260697dddd10bef2b3f30eeb611dd614e645 accepted coco_source objects a scalar objective, its euclidean gradient, actual gd update and iterated gaps to a minimizer. c1 function with genuine riesz gradient, actual update and function.iterate, signed scalar gaps to arbitrary z. explicit-elaboration c1 in the callers provides derivative meaning despite the shared helper having a more general totalized-gradient interface. the recurrence is derived from actual iterates, not assumed. domains euclidean c2, nonnegative source moduli and ordinary reciprocal step domain. c1 on any complete real inner-product space; signed real alpha,beta, division-free beta h<=1. different infinite-dimensional spaces, signed curvature and zero beta are genuinely broader mathematical domains, explicitly disclosed in current lessons; not source equivalence. quantifiers weighted proof for actual iterates relative to a minimizer, all iteration counts in its positive-coefficient domain. every x0,z and natural n including zero at one fixed admitted step. different global upper/chord models use one f,alpha,beta,h. arbitrary-comparator weighted statement follows the (3.3) extension, with no gap sign assumed. assumptions section c2, alpha-convex and beta-smooth, printed h<=1/beta; lemma3.5 coefficient a>0. c1, signed alpha chord inequality, signed beta upper model, h>=0,beta h<=1; alpha h<=1 so q>=0. different the extra lower bound on h exposes an essential source domain omission. the source regularity and parameter-sign assumptions are weakened tran