          "evidence": "The two new declarations intentionally omit C1/C2. The gradient is Lean totalized fderiv passed through the Riesz map. It is not a freely supplied vector field, but one must not identify it with an existing classical derivative at arbitrary points. Lessons explicitly state this and the global model premise. Source smooth functions are a specialization; this is not source-equivalent regularity."
