          "necessity": "mathematically-necessary",
          "proposed_change": "Add h>=0 to the printed h<=1/beta restriction in Lemma3.1. Retain the original pinned source separately and preserve the local algebraic generalization.",
          "reconstructed_statement": "Let f:R^d->R be C2 and beta-smooth with beta>0. For every step 0<=h<=1/beta and every x, define T(x)=x-h grad f(x). Then f(T(x))-f(x)<=-(h/2)||grad f(x)||^2.",
          "statement_sha256": "1c1f243a974a44bd02e19373aa69b3db5a9279fa87c5e5f041aface939939949",
          "justification": "f(t)=t^2/2 on R, beta=1,h=-1,x=1 satisfies h<=1/beta. T(1)=2; f(2)-f(1)=3/2 but -(h/2)|f prime(1)|^2=1/2, so descent fails. More generally h<0 gives discrepancy h(h-1)/2>0.",
          "minimality_evidence": "Only the lower bound h>=0 is added to the source step domain; h=0 remains valid. Source positive modulus/regularity premises are retained. No convexity or strong convexity assumption is added. Omitting the new lower bound admits the explicit quadratic counterexample.",
          "reference_or_counterexample": "Primary source https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3, Lemma3.1. Exact counterexample: f(t)=t^2/2 on R, beta=1,h=-1,x=1 satisfies h<=1/beta. T(1)=2; f(2)-f(1)=3/2 but -(h/2)|f prime(1)|^2=1/2, so descent fails. More generally h<0 gives discrepancy h(h-1)/2>0.",
          "review": {
            "state": "accepted",
            "reviewer": "converse_source_review",
            "independent_from_formalizer": true,
            "independent_from_decoder": true,
            "evidence": "Independent exact-proposal review of the complete current descent repair packet, with no registry or prior verdict/source-review files read. I am distinct from andi-pl-worker and pl_blind. The source was checked directly at https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3, Lemma 3.1: the section uses C² Euclidean objectives and prints h≤1/β. The proposal preserves positive β and that regularity while adding h≥0 only.\n\nThe reference is a nonempty plain string, with a complete self-contained quadratic counterexample. f(t)=t²/2 has derivative t and Hessian 1, hence is C² and 1-smooth. For h=−1,x=1 the actual step is 2, the function increment is 3/2, and the claimed upper bound is 1/2. For any h<0 the excess is (h²−h)/2>0. Thus all negative steps must be excluded for a guarantee uniform over the unchanged smooth objective class. This is not a compiler-motivated assumption.\n\nSufficiency: set g=∇f(x). Substituting x−hg in the smooth upper model yields f(x−hg)−f(x)≤(−h+βh²/2)‖g‖². Since β>0 and 0≤h≤1/β, multiplying βh≤1 by h‖g‖²≥0 gives βh²‖g‖²≤h‖g‖² and proves the exact coefficient −h/2. No convexity, strong convexity, minimum or PL hypothesis is needed. At h=0 both sides vanish. Keeping h=0 and the original upper endpoint shows minimality; h>0 would be stronger than necessary.\n\nCurrent code and lesson match this algebra: the module imports only Mathlib and applies the supplied upper model at the actual totalized gradient step; it uses real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq, norm_smul and a nonnegative multiplication before polynomial arithmetic. astis_dependencies is correctly empty. The formal result has no differentiability premise and allows signed β in complete inner-product spaces; the lesson explicitly labels this an algebraic consequence of the supplied global model. These are separate local generalizations, not part of the accepted source repair. An unused α is mentioned in the shared lesson assumptions but expressly declared unused and is not an added source condition or Lean premise.\n\nAccept this exact h≥0 overlay with β>0 reciprocal scope and original C² Euclidean setting retained. No further assumption or conclusion modification is warranted. This review does not certify unrelated PL/weighted rates or infer full repository build status from the packet.",
            "review_run_sha256": "a0735dae7a9d2b3e179bf51bc9aa25805f7c205ba4eb799bb5d899151c25eef5",
            "reviewer_packet_sha256": "4c29fa80c2d9bc72093473354090da5213eaf5b3e74eae6593c91304bb38f7af",
            "proposal_sha256": "01c96d7e5fa04295516f9724c0d98fc93f0d9e08c9f97fb17c9d288a6b703034",
            "run_artifact": "runs/semantic-roundtrip/andi-opt-gd-pl/repair-review-result-0.json"
          },
          "proposal_author": "coco_source"
        }
