          "reference_or_counterexample": "Primary source https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#S3, Theorem3.6. Exact counterexample: For f(t)=t^2/2 on R, with alpha=beta=1, z=0,x0=1,N=1,h=-1 satisfies exact PL and all printed source premises. The new gap is f(2)=2, but (1-alpha h)(f(1)-f(0))=1. Thus 2<=1 is false. For every h<0, (1-h)^2>(1-h).",
          "review": {
            "state": "accepted",
