rt(eta) z, define u as real lebesgue measure restricted to (0,1], and define c = integral_e f(h+z) dp(z) - <gradient f(xp),h>. these definitions are made before quantifying x: p depends on e and eta, u is fixed, and c depends on f,h,xp,p but not on x. then (sqrt(eta))^2=eta, u has total mass one, and z |-> f(h+z) is bochner integrable with respect to p. moreover, for every x in e, define, for every r in r and z in e, k_x(r,z) = <(pi/2)(cos((pi/2)r)(x-h) - sin((pi/2)r)z), gradient f(xp) - gradient f(h + sin((pi/2)r)(x-h) + cos((pi/2)r)z)>, where angle brackets denote the real inner product and real multiplication of vectors denotes scalar multiplication. the function k_x on the entire product r x e is measurable and is bochner integrable with respect to the product measure u x p. for every z in e, its oriented real interval integral satisfies integral_0^1 k_x(r,z) dr = <gradient f(xp), x-(h+z)> - f(x) + f(h+z). finally, integral_(r x e) k_x(r,z) d(u x p)(r,z) = <gradient f(xp),x> - f(x) + c. the interval integral uses real lebesgue measure, while the last integral uses exactly u x p. accepted appendix d.1 actual unclipped mean before eq18; consumed by sphmc appendix a.4(2) autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.gradientarcmean.gradient_arc_mean autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/gradientarcmean.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_k 17393b2685c5aba14092382890d2cf2b980384127d345053f9f43fa77a6af589 accepted log_depth_source_review objects actual gradient-arc estimator with independent gaussian noise and uniform time. explicit arc, velocity and gradient difference under u.prod p. explicit-elaboration all three definitions expanded; exact same input and estimator used by ftc and mean. domains euclidean smooth setting. finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space, including dimension zero, with second countability. different disclosed coordinate-free and zero-dimensional extension; second countability automatic, no dimension division. quantifiers constructed source center; an additive constant independent of x. arbitrary h,xp; p,u,c before forall x; path identity for every z. stronger-in-lean c contains no x; later source-center substitution remains separate. assumptions smooth potential and positive variance in the source sampler setting. differentiable f, actual beta-lipschitz gradient, eta>0, beta>=0; no convexity/residual/clipping restriction. different quadratic growth and gaussian moments prove integrability; beta0 and omitted downstream restrictions valid for selected identity. conclusion mean supplies the log weight up to an x-independent constant. exact ftc and common-c mean plus potential l1, joint measurability/l1, sqrt variance identity and uniform probability. explicit-elaboration all public conclusions matched; positive f(h+z), negative f(x), c=e f(h+z)-inner(g,h). scopes mean identification before normalized comparison. actual auxiliary integration for each fixed x. same no random-x or joint parameter-kernel, normalization, clipped law, renyi or cost claimed. constant dependencies an x-independent additive constant and unit time interval. c depends on f,h,xp,eta,p, not x; u has mass one. explicit-elaboration c fixed before x; actual gaussian zero mean removes linear auxiliary term; no missing normalization factor. domains informational coordinate-free and zero-dimensional cases; second countability automatic. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference. assumptions informational beta zero valid without division; zero-lipschitz gradient makes w vanish. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference. quantifiers informational arbitrary center; common c independent of x; source substitution deferred. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference. objects informational uniform ioc equals source icc after removing a null singleton; ftc endpoints retained. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference. conclusion informational potential and joint estimator integrability, measurability, ftc and actual zero mean explicitly supplied. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference. scopes informational selected fixed-x mean dependency only; no extra random-x or normalized sampler conclusion. independent formal reviewer accepted this disclosed difference.",
