 equality of that distribution with the tilt by <g,x>-f(x)+c, no distributional error bound for that latter tilt, and no explicit beta- or dimension-dependent estimate for the displayed clipping-tail integral are stated. the integral defining c is a typed signed integral; integrability of z->f(h+z) under p is not separately asserted in the displayed conclusion. accepted appendix d.1 eq18 and clipping mean comparison; consumed by sphmc a.4(2), actual poisson mechanism a.1 lemma a.2 autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.clippedgradientprogram.clipped_gradient_program autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/clippedgradientprogram.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_l 5286a9bc2c8639eb71453501e86be83341dbdd4c5aa08d3cd707be530d7de513 accepted log_depth_source_review objects actual source-centered gradient arc, clipped estimator, gaussian proposal and independent poisson retry program. explicit source h,w,wc,gaussian maps,two distinct uniforms,iid auxiliary and attempt streams,least-success output and stopped batch count. explicit-elaboration expanded statement exposes actual program definitions; production change aligns parent output/count. domains euclidean smooth setting. finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space including zero dimension and explicit second countability. different disclosed coordinate-free/zero-dimensional extensions; no dimension division, second countability automatic. quantifiers fixed call with source center and an additive log-weight constant independent of proposal point. fixed eta,beta,b,x0,xp; all definitions including c precede forall x. same source-center substitution present; c has no x dependence; no global adaptive-parameter family. assumptions surrounding accuracy theorem uses residual, step and parameter restrictions. differentiable f with actual beta-lipschitz gradient,beta>=0,eta>0,b>0 suffice for selected construction. different beta0 supported; omitted restrictions are unnecessary for c