      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1",
      "original_theorem": "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space with d=finrank(E)>0. f:E->R is differentiable everywhere and its actual gradient is globally beta-Lipschitz. eta,beta>0, ell>=2 and 0<eps<=1/2. Convexity is not used in this fixed smooth dependency.\nGiven x0 and supplied x_plus, cache g=grad f(x_plus) and set h=x0-eta*g. Assume norm(h-x_plus)<=sqrt(d*eta). Let L=ell+log(1/eps), and assume 64*beta*(sqrt(d*L)+L)<=1/eta. The reference-point construction and its cost are outside this fixed-call input contract.\nLet P=(z->sqrt(eta)*z)_*stdGaussian(E), nu=Lebesgue restricted to (0,1] product P, and q=(z->h+sqrt(eta)*z)_*stdGaussian(E). For theta=pi*r/2 define W0(x,r,z)=<(pi/2)*(cos(theta)*(x-h)-sin(theta)*z),g-grad f(h+sin(theta)*(x-h)+cos(theta)*z)>. Set W=min(1,max(-1,W0)), m(x)=integral W(x,a) dnu(a), and qhat=q.tilted(m). First form G=(z->x0+sqrt(eta)*z)_*stdGaussian(E), then pi=G.tilted(-f). The mean m describes a law; the algorithm does not calculate that integral.\nOne attempt is (x,N,a,u), with independent laws q,Poisson(2),nu^Nat and uniform[0,1]. Accept when u<=product over i<N of (1+W(x,a_i))/2. The full attempt sequence has iid law rho. Output the x-coordinate of the least accepted index, or x0 if no index is accepted. C(omega) sums each batch size N_n whenever all earlier attempts failed, including the successful batch. The specified cached gradient count is G_cost=1+C: one initial evaluation of g and one new gradient evaluation in each W0 call. Random-number generation is not counted as a gradient query.\nThe output map is measurable and its rho-pushforward equals qhat; the never-accepted event has rho-measure zero. rho,qhat,pi are probability measures, and pi and qhat are mutually absolutely continuous. Both actual real RN ell-power functions are integrable under their denominator measures, and both integrals are strictly positive and at most 1+eps^2. Each explicit logarithmic RN moment divided by ell-1 is at most eps^2. The actual cached gradient count has expected value at most 1+2*exp(2). For every 0<p<=1/2, rho{G_cost>K_G*log(2/p)}<=p, where K_G=2*(exp(1)-1)*(exp(2)+1/log(2))+1+1/log(2). The cost expectation and tail are stated in extended nonnegative reals.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space E with d=dim_R(E)>0, every everywhere differentiable f:E->R, real eta,beta,ell,eps and points x0,xp, assume eta,beta>0,ell>=2,0<eps<=1/2,actual gradient beta-Lipschitz, norm(x0-eta grad f(xp)-xp)<=sqrt(d eta), and64 beta(sqrt(d(ell+log(1/eps)))+ell+log(1/eps))<=1/eta. No convexity is assumed. Set g=grad f(xp),h=x0-eta g,P=(z->sqrt(eta)z)_*stdGaussian(E),nu=Lebesgue restricted to(0,1] product P,q=(z->h+sqrt(eta)z)_*stdGaussian(E). Define W(x,(t,v))=min(1,max(-1,< (pi/2)(cos(pi*t/2)(x-h)-sin(pi*t/2)v),g-grad f(h+sin(pi*t/2)(x-h)+cos(pi*t/2)v)>)), with circular pi. Set m(x)=integral W(x,a) dnu(a),qhat=q.tilted(m). First form q0=(z->x0+sqrt(eta)z)_*stdGaussian(E), then target pi=q0.tilted(-f). The input omega is an iid sequence of attempts(X_n,K_n,(Z_ni)_i,U_n), with independent q,Poisson2,nu^Nat,and uniform[0,1] components. Acceptance B_n means U_n<=product over i in Fin K_n of(1+W(X_n,Z_ni))/2; division is inside each factor and empty product=1. Output Y is X at the least accepting index,or x0 if none accepts. The ENNReal count C=1+sum_n K_n*indicator(all i<n reject) includes all counts through the successful batch, with one initial unit rather than one per trial. The eighteen conclusions are: Y measurable; Y_*rho=qhat;rho(all trials reject)=0;rho,qhat,pi probability;pi<<qhat andqhat<<pi;the actual real RN ell-powers are Bochner integrable under their denominator measures;their corresponding real integrals I=integral((dpi/dqhat).toReal)^ell dqhat andJ=integral((dqhat/dpi).toReal)^ell dpi are both strictly positive;I,J<=1+eps^2;log(I)/(ell-1),log(J)/(ell-1)<=eps^2;the nonnegative expectation of C<=ofReal(1+2exp2);and for every real0<p<=1/2,rho{ofReal([2(exp1-1)(exp2+1/log2)+1+1/log2]*log(2/p))<C}<=ofReal(p). ell is real,not necessarily integer. The cost threshold inequality is strict; cost and probability bounds use ENNReal.",
