      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260912-gibbsgradientmoment semantic-audit astis-rt-20260912-gibbsgradientmoment companion:sphmc-gibbs-gradient-moment · domain-mismatch blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_gradient_moment. domain-mismatch source hidden from decoder e is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its borel sigma-algebra and canonical lebesgue volume. dimension zero is included. u:e->r is twice continuously differentiable. the nonnegative real parameters alpha,beta satisfy 0<alpha and alpha<=beta. at every x,v the genuine hessian obeys alpha*norm(v)^2<=d2u(x)[v,v]<=beta*norm(v)^2. the alpha<=beta assumption remains in the public statement, despite its unused binder name. define mu=volume.tilted(-u), the actual normalized exponential gibbs measure. for the standard orthonormal basis (e_i), define h(x)=sum_i d2u(x)[e_i,e_i]. no minimizer, normalizing constant, weighted integrability or moment bound is supplied as an assumption. the actual measure mu is a probability measure. both norm(grad u)^2 and h are integrable under mu. their expectations are equal, and the expected squared gradient is at most beta*finrank(e). these are five public conclusions; bare exponential integrability, weighted linear integrability and directional integration by parts are proved internally. for every finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space e with its borel structure and canonical lebesgue volume, let d=dim_r e, with no assumption d>0. for every u:e->r and nonnegative real alpha,beta, assume 0<alpha, alpha<=beta, u is globally c2, and alpha||v||^2<=d2u(x)[v,v]<=beta||v||^2 for all x,v. put z=integral exp(-u) against volume, a real bochner integral with value zero if not integrable. define mu=volume.withdensity(x -> ennreal.ofreal(exp(-u(x))/z)), with real division by zero equal to zero and ofreal truncating negative values to zero. this is precisely the given tilted measure. for the full standard orthonormal basis e_i indexed by fin(d), set h(x)=sum_i d2u(x)[e_i,e_i]. then five conclusions hold under the same mu: mu is probability; x->||grad u(x)||^2 is bochner integrable; h is bochner integrable; integral ||grad u||^2 dmu=integral h dmu; and this integral<=beta*d. all derivatives and gradients are actual. the numeric upper bound explicitly depends only on beta,d; alpha remains a strictly positive assumption parameter. dimension zero uses the empty basis sum. accepted section6.3 reference-point construction: ideal gibbs gradient-moment proof component autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_gradient_moment autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/gibbsgradientmoment.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_r d8d893cf7c266e83aff4c19553407aa37fe0c704c73a360f3ba8e68fd7c7695b accepted log_depth_source_review objects ideal gibbs gradient moment used in the reference-point estimate. actual canonical-volume exponential tilt, actual gradient and standard-basis hessian diagonal sum. explicit-elaboration total tilted definition reconstructed correctly; actual integrability and probability exclude degenerate zero-normalizer branch. domains positive-dimensional euclidean setting. complete finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space, including dimension zero. different disclosed extension; empty sums and canonical nonzero volume validate zero dimension. quantifiers ideal-law estimate under source curvature assumptions. every admissible space, potential and alpha/beta pair; five conclusions for the same determined tilted measure. same no supplied minimizer, normalizer, weighted integrability or desired moment. assumptions normalized smooth potential with positive lower curvature in section6.3. actual c2 hessian bounds, nnreal alpha/beta, alpha>0 and alpha<=beta. different general beta extends beta1; alpha<=beta remains despite unused binder. conclusion ideal gibbs gradient moment supplies dimension-scale input to initialization. probability, two gibbs l1 statements, gradient-square/hessian-diagonal expectation equality and beta*finrank upper bound. explicit-elaboration exactly five public conjuncts; internal weighted integrability and ibp are not extra public conclusions. scopes ideal-law component in reference-point construction. ideal gibbs moment only; no approximate output, gaussian perturbation, history or total reference cost. same attribution, module header and reader preserve limitation. constant dependencies normalized smoothness gives dimension-scale ideal control. final beta*finrank bound; alpha and local u/gradient values occur only in integrability proof. explicit-elaboration same weighted identity normalized; no envelope constants survive. domains informational coordinate-free and zero-dimensional extensions explicit and proved. independent reviewer accepted: coordinate-free and zero-dimensional extensions explicit and proved. assumptions informational general beta specializes to normalized beta1; alpha<=beta retained. independent reviewer accepted: general beta specializes to normalized beta1; alpha<=beta retained. conclusion informational normalization, noncompact l1 and moment identity proved rather than assumed. independent reviewer accepted: normalization, noncompact l1 and moment identity proved rather than assumed. objects informational h is explicit standard-basis diagonal sum; no separate trace/laplacian/basis-invariance api theorem. independent reviewer accepted: h is explicit standard-basis diagonal sum; no separate trace/laplacian/basis-invariance api theorem. scopes informational only ideal-law input to larger initialization and cost argument. independent reviewer accepted: only ideal-law input to larger initialization and cost argument.",
