      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260912-sphmcreferencecarryingcost semantic-audit astis-rt-20260912-sphmcreferencecarryingcost companion:sphmc-reference-carrying-cost · domain-mismatch blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.referencecarryingcost.reference_carrying_cost. domain-mismatch source hidden from decoder e is a finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space with d=dim(e)>0. v is c2 and its genuine hessian satisfies alpha*norm(w)^2<=d2v(x)[w,w]<=beta*norm(w)^2, with 0<alpha<=beta. the retained state s=(b,u,xref,k,h) belongs to nnreal x e x e x nat x (nat->e). eta,tau are measurable strictly positive functions of the full state. epsilon is any real-valued function; no sign or measurability is assumed globally. m is an actual markov kernel to original-coordinate points. theta is a supplied nonnegative precision cutoff. set beta_s=beta+b, a_s=alpha+b, kappa_s=beta_s/a_s, v=(eta+tau)/beta_s and v_s(w)=v(w)+b/2*norm(w-u)^2. only at active states b<theta assume w2(m(s),h_(eta/beta_s) pi_(v_s))^2<=ofreal(kappa_s*epsilon(s)^2/beta_s), where pi_(v_s) is the volume tilt by -v_s and h_t adds independent gaussian variance t. this is the current-call accuracy input, not a supplied moment or cost bound. for p=(s,(x,z)), set y=x+sqrt(tau/beta_s)*z, bplus=b+tonnreal(1/v), uplus=(bplus)^(-1)*(b*u+v^(-1)*y), f_p(w)=v(w)+bplus/2*norm(w-uplus)^2 and t_p(w)=w-(beta+bplus)^(-1)*grad f_p(w). n(p) is the least n with norm(grad f_p(t_p^n(x)))^2<=(alpha+bplus)*d, or zero if no such n exists. the reused parent proves finite attainment; this is its same actual program from the pre-noise x. define c(p)=0 if theta<=b, otherwise n(p)+1. set kappa_plus=(beta+bplus)/(alpha+bplus) and b(s)=0 if theta<=b, otherwise 2+kappa_plus*log(1+4*(eta+tau)*(1+eta)+2*(eta+tau)*kappa_s*epsilon(s)^2/d+tau/(eta+tau)). k(s)=m(s) product g, with g the standard gaussian probability. for integration, mu is any sfinite measure on the full state and mu compprod k is the actual kernel composition-product integration measure. the real global bound additionally assumes integrable b mu. a probability state law gives an expectation interpretation; the theorem does not establish that an arbitrary mu was generated by the recursive algorithm. the actual reference count c is jointly measurable and nonnegative. measurability of epsilon implies measurability of b. for every state, c(s,.) is integrable under k(s) and its integral is at most b(s). for every sfinite state measure mu, the extended nonnegative integral of ofreal(c) under mu compprod k is at most the extended integral of ofreal(b) under mu. if b is mu-integrable, c is integrable under mu compprod k and its real integral is at most the real integral of b. absorbed states have exactly zero count; the active count is the same actual n+1 used in the enhanced reference update. let \\(e\\) be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its borel measurable structure, and let \\[ d=\\dim_{\\mathbb r}e>0. \\] let \\(\\alpha,\\beta\\in[0,\\infty)\\) satisfy \\(0<\\alpha\\le\\beta\\). suppose \\(v:e\\to\\mathbb r\\) is \\(c^2\\) and, for every \\(x,w\\in e\\), \\[ \\alpha\\|w\\|^2\\le d^2v(x)[w,w]\\le\\beta\\|w\\|^2. \\] define the state space \\[ s=[0,\\infty)\\times e\\times e\\times\\mathbb n\\times e^{\\mathbb n}, \\] with its product measurable structure. write a state as \\(s=(b,c,u,j,\\xi)\\). the formulas below explicitly use \\(b,c\\); the remaining coordinates may influence all state-dependent functions and kernels. let \\(\\eta,\\tau,\\varepsilon:s\\to\\mathbb r\\). assume \\(\\eta,\\tau\\) are measurable and strictly positive at every state. no measurability or sign condition on \\(\\varepsilon\\) is imposed initially. let \\(m:s\\rightsquigarrow e\\) be a markov kernel, so every \\(m(s)\\) is a probability measure, and fix a threshold \\(\\theta\\in[0,\\infty)\\). for each state define \\[ \\beta_s=\\beta+b,\\qquad a_s=\\alpha+b, \\] and the measure \\[ \\nu_s(dx)= \\bigl(\\mathrm{volume}.\\mathrm{tilted} [-v(\\,\\cdot\\,)-\\tfrac b2\\|\\cdot-c\\|^2]\\bigr)(dx). \\] here “tilted” means exponential weighting followed by normalization under the supplied total-inverse convention. let \\(g\\) denote the standard gaussian probability measure on \\(e\\), and define \\[ q_s=(x,z\\mapsto x+z)_\\# \\left(\\nu_s\\otimes (z\\mapsto\\sqrt{\\eta(s)/\\beta_s}\\,z)_\\#g\\right). \\] assume that for every \\(s\\) with \\(b<\\theta\\), \\[ \\left[ \\left( \\inf_{\\substack{\\gamma\\text{ a measure on }e\\times e\\\\ (\\pi_1)_\\#\\gamma=m(s),\\;(\\pi_2)_\\#\\gamma=q_s}} \\int_{e\\times e}^{-} \\operatorname{ofreal}\\!\\left(\\|x-y\\|^2\\right)\\,d\\gamma(x,y) \\right)^{1/2} \\right]^2 \\le \\operatorname{ofreal}\\!\\left( \\frac{\\beta_s}{a_s}\\frac{\\varepsilon(s)^2}{\\beta_s} \\right). \\] this is an inequality in the extended nonnegative reals. the inner power is the real \\(1/2\\) power and the outer square is the natural-number power. an empty coupling set has infimum \\(+\\infty\\). there is no corresponding approximation assumption for \\(b\\ge\\theta\\). define \\[ v_s=\\frac{\\eta(s)+\\tau(s)}{\\beta_s}, \\qquad b_s'=b+\\operatorname{tonnreal}(v_s^{-1}). \\] here \\(v_s>0\\), so the real value of \\(b_s'\\) equals \\(b+1/v_s\\). for an outcome \\(p=(s,y,z)\\in s\\times e\\times e\\), define \\[ o_p=y+\\sqrt{\\tau(s)/\\beta_s}\\,z,\\qquad m_p=(b_s')^{-1}\\bigl(bc+v_s^{-1}o_p\\bigr), \\] \\[ f_p(x)=v(x)+\\frac{b_s'}2\\|x-m_p\\|^2, \\qquad t_p(x)=x-\\frac1{\\beta+b_s'}\\nabla f_p(x). \\] all gradients here differentiate only \\(x\\), holding \\(p\\) fixed. starting at \\(y\\), set \\(x_n(p)=t_p^{[n]}(y)\\), with \\(x_0(p)=y\\), and \\[ q_n(p)=\\|\\nabla f_p(x_n(p))\\|^2. \\] define the natural number \\[ n(p)= \\begin{cases} \\min\\{n\\in\\mathbb n:q_n(p)\\le(\\alpha+b_s')d\\}, &\\text{if this set is nonempty},\\\\ 0,&\\text{otherwise}. \\end{cases} \\] thus the fallback value is explicitly zero if no qualifying iterate exists. define the real-valued cost \\[ c(p)= \\begin{cases} 0,&b\\ge\\theta,\\\\ n(p)+1,&b<\\theta, \\end{cases} \\] and the real-valued bound \\[ b(s)= \\begin{cases} 0,&b\\ge\\theta,\\\\[2mm] 2+\\dfrac{\\beta+b_s'}{\\alpha+b_s'} \\log\\!\\left( 1+4(\\eta(s)+\\tau(s))(1+\\eta(s)) +\\dfrac{2(\\eta(s)+\\tau(s))(\\beta_s/a_s)\\varepsilon(s)^2}{d} +\\dfrac{\\tau(s)}{\\eta(s)+\\tau(s)} \\right),&b<\\theta. \\end{cases} \\] let \\[ k(s)=m(s)\\otimes g. \\] thus conditional on a fixed state, the outcome coordinates are independently distributed as \\(y\\sim m(s)\\) and \\(z\\sim g\\). the theorem concludes all of the following: 1. \\(c:s\\times e\\times e\\to\\mathbb r\\) is measurable. 2. if \\(\\varepsilon\\) is measurable, then \\(b:s\\to\\mathbb r\\) is measurable. 3. \\(c(p)\\ge0\\) for every \\(p\\). 4. for every state \\(s\\), \\(c(s,\\cdot,\\cdot)\\) is bochner integrable with respect to \\(k(s)\\), and \\[ \\int_{e\\times e}c(s,y,z)\\,dk(s)(y,z)\\le b(s). \\] 5. for every s-finite measure \\(\\mu\\) on \\(s\\), let \\(\\mu\\ltimes k\\) be the measure obtained by integrating \\(k(s)\\) against \\(\\mu\\). then \\[ \\int_{s\\times e\\times e}^{-}\\operatorname{ofreal}(c(p))\\, d(\\mu\\ltimes k)(p) \\le \\int_s^{-}\\operatorname{ofreal}(b(s))\\,d\\mu(s). \\] furthermore, if \\(b\\) is bochner integrable with respect to \\(\\mu\\), then \\(c\\) is bochner integrable with respect to \\(\\mu\\ltimes k\\), and \\[ \\int c\\,d(\\mu\\ltimes k)\\le\\int b\\,d\\mu. \\] scope notes: - the outer measure \\(\\mu\\) need not be finite or a probability measure. only the pointwise kernels \\(m(s)\\) and \\(k(s)\\) are stipulated probability measures. - the unconditional extended-integral inequality does not assume measurability of \\(\\varepsilon\\) or \\(b\\). under the supplied library conventions, that inequality alone does not certify measurability or integrability of its integrands. - the statement does not explicitly conclude that the stopping predicate has a witness, that \\(n\\) is measurable separately, or that the returned iterate satisfies the gradient threshold. its definition retains the no-witness fallback. - the cost is exactly \\(n+1\\) on the active branch. no supplied definition identifies it with a specific implementation’s number of oracle calls. - no sample-output distribution, total variation guarantee, or convergence guarantee for an output iterate is asserted. - the tilted measure has a supplied total definition; normalization-integral finiteness or strict positivity is not a separate displayed assumption or conclusion. - the numerical constants are exactly \\(2,4,2\\) in the displayed bound. all remaining dependencies are explicit through \\(\\alpha,\\beta,d,b,\\eta,\\tau,\\varepsilon\\) and the threshold branch. - this reconstruction uses only the anonymous statement and approved definition context. it makes no source-identity inference or source-fidelity judgment. accepted algorithm3.3 and section6.3: actual reference-point gradient query cost autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.referencecarryingcost.reference_carrying_cost autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/referencecarryingcost.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_w 97c6c8a86a01856d1d433d3c3b9e6ecb7cdca15339369893f36333487da2ee27 accepted log_depth_source_review objects actual current input,reference gd and count. full state,pre-noise start,same completed-square first hit,actual m product g and compprod. explicit-elaboration hq,hn identify indices from genuine gradients and all trajectories. domains normalized euclidean execution states and probability expectations. general beta,coordinate-free positive dimension,arbitrary retained states and sfinite outer measure. different extensions disclosed; expectation interpretation only for probability outer measure. quantifiers cost of current active call. w2 required active; all states fiberl1; all sfinite outer measures integral bounds.