    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260912-SPHMCEnhancedTerminalExecution",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260912-SPHMCEnhancedTerminalExecution",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-enhanced-terminal-execution · domain-mismatch",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.EnhancedTerminalExecution.enhanced_terminal_execution.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1",
      "original_theorem": "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space with positive dimension d. V:E->R is fixed and C2, with genuine Hessian between kappa^(-1)*norm(w)^2 and norm(w)^2, where kappa is a nonnegative real with kappa>=1. The baseline smoothness is one.\nThe full state space is S=NNReal x E x E x Nat x (Nat->E), with s=(b,u,xref,k,history). Fix any initial state s0. M is an actual Markov kernel S->E. eta:S->R is measurable and satisfies0<eta(s)<=c with0<c<1/4. M and eta may depend on all state coordinates. Fix q>=2 and0<Delta<=1/2. Delta is the current recursive-call accuracy; no source accuracy, moment, reference-admissibility or history-validity premise is imposed on M or s0.\nDefine K(r)=(1+r)/(1/kappa+r), tau(s)=K(b) if K(b)>=2 and c otherwise, v(s)=(eta(s)+tau(s))/(1+b). Put L=q+log(K(b0)*d*q/Delta), B=(1/1024)/(sqrt(d*L)+L), J=ceil(8*log(exp(1)*K(b0)/B)), and eps=Delta/sqrt(J+1). These parameters remain fixed after choosing s0. The numerical8 and1/1024 are local sufficient constants, not quoted source constants.\nFor z=(x,zeta), obs(s,z)=x+sqrt(tau(s)/(1+b))*zeta, bplus=b+toNNReal(1/v(s)) and uplus=bplus^(-1)*(b*u+v(s)^(-1)*obs). Define F(s,z)(w)=V(w)+bplus/2*norm(w-uplus)^2 and T(s,z)(w)=w-(1+bplus)^(-1)*grad F(s,z)(w). N(s,z) is the least n whose true gradient square at T^n(x) is at most(1/kappa+bplus)*d, with fallback zero if no index exists. update(s,z)=(bplus,uplus,T^N(x),k+1,prepend(obs,history)). The pre-noise sample x initializes this actual inner first hit.\nFor the terminal extension put bbar(s)=max(b,B^(-1)), A(s)=1/bbar(s), TF_s(w)=V(w)+bbar(s)/2*norm(w-u)^2, TT_s(w)=w-(1+bbar(s))^(-1)*grad TF_s(w). TN(s) is the least n with norm(grad TF_s(TT_s^n(xref)))^2<=d*bbar(s), with fallback zero. Set txp=TT^TN(xref), tg=grad V(txp), th=u-A*tg. This terminal threshold is distinct from the inner threshold.\nLet nu be Lebesgue measure restricted to(0,1] product standardGaussian. The proposal tproposal_s is the law of th+sqrt(A)*Z. For p=(x,(t,Z)), put zeta=sqrt(A)*Z and w=inner((pi/2)*(cos(pi*t/2)*(x-th)-sin(pi*t/2)*zeta),tg-grad V(th+sin(pi*t/2)*(x-th)+cos(pi*t/2)*zeta)). tW_s(p)=min(1,max(-1,w)). Each attempt consists of a proposal, an independent Poisson(2) batch size, an independent infinite nu sequence and an independent acceptance uniform on[0,1]. It accepts iff that uniform is at most the product over i:Fin batchSize of(1+tW_s(proposal,aux_i))/2.\ntrho_s is the infinite independent attempt law. output_s is the proposal at the first accepting attempt, or zero if there is no success. queryCount is the sum of every batch size whose earlier attempts all failed, including the successful batch. The sampling-only charged count is1+queryCount. tpi_s is the Gaussian law u+sqrt(A)*Z exponentially tilted by -V. Kernel multiplication/powers use the actual full-state transition; Lt composed with P^n is the resulting output law.\nB>0 and0<eps<=1/2. On D={s:b>=1/B}, bbar(s)=b. TN and txp are measurable; the true terminal gradient threshold is attained, every earlier iterate fails it, and norm(th-txp)<=sqrt(d*A). There exist Markov kernels Lt:S->E and P:S->S. P(s) is dirac(s) on D and otherwise the pushforward of M(s) product standardGaussian by update(s,·). (P^J)(s0)(D)=1, and for every natural m, (Lt composed with P^(J+m))(s0)=(Lt composed with P^J)(s0). For every state s, output_s is measurable, trho_s mapped by output_s equals this same Lt(s), never-success has trho_s measure zero, and the nonnegative integral of1+queryCount is at most1+2*exp(2). tpi_s is a probability mutually absolutely continuous with Lt(s); both RN q-powers are integrable under their respective denominator laws, with strictly positive integrals at most1+eps^2, and their logarithms divided by q-1 are at most eps^2.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Packet SHA-256: `f0ba78fb133847d01b0d1b756cd7091d44eb106355d47d4e80af73287abef62b`  \nExpanded-statement SHA-256: `fec9ed0bd1777b77c64f297ed7a09967f1a2094cede1eb251059464c60add721`\n\nThe following reconstruction uses only the packet’s expanded type and approved notation context.\n\n**Quantified objects and hypotheses.** Let \\(E\\) be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, and let\n\\[\nd=\\dim_{\\mathbb R}E>0.\n\\]\nLet \\(V:E\\to\\mathbb R\\) be \\(C^2\\), and let \\(\\kappa\\) be a nonnegative real satisfying \\(\\kappa\\ge1\\). Assume, for every \\(x,w\\in E\\),\n\\[\n\\kappa^{-1}\\|w\\|^2\n\\le D^2V(x)[w,w]\n\\le \\|w\\|^2.\n\\]\n\nDefine the state space\n\\[\nS=\\mathbb R_{\\ge0}\\times E\\times E\\times\\mathbb N\\times E^{\\mathbb N},\n\\]\nand write \\(s=(b,a,u,k,h)\\). Let \\(\\eta:S\\to\\mathbb R\\) be measurable. Let \\(c,q,\\Delta\\in\\mathbb R\\) satisfy\n\\[\n0<c<\\tfrac14,\\qquad\n0<\\eta(s)\\le c\\quad(s\\in S),\\qquad\nq\\ge2,\\qquad\n0<\\Delta\\le\\tfrac12.\n\\]\nFix an arbitrary initial state \\(s_0=(b_0,a_0,u_0,k_0,h_0)\\) and an arbitrary Markov kernel \\(M:S\\rightsquigarrow E\\). In particular, no approximation, invariance, or accuracy hypothesis on \\(M\\) appears.\n\n**Definitions depending on these inputs.** For real \\(r\\), set\n\\[\nK(r)=\\frac{1+r}{\\kappa^{-1}+r},\\qquad\n\\tau(s)=\n\\begin{cases}\nK(b),&2\\le K(b),\\\\\nc,&K(b)<2.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nDefine\n\\[\nL=q+\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{K(b_0)dq}{\\Delta}\\right),\\qquad\nB=\\frac{1/1024}{\\sqrt{dL}+L},\n\\]\n\\[\nJ=\\left\\lceil 8\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{eK(b_0)}B\\right)\\right\\rceil_{\\mathbb N},\n\\qquad\n\\varepsilon=\\frac{\\Delta}{\\sqrt{J+1}}.\n\\]\nHere the ceiling is a natural-number ceiling.\n\nThe following definitions specify a state update. For \\(s=(b,a,u,k,h)\\), put\n\\[\nv(s)=\\frac{\\eta(s)+\\tau(s)}{1+b},\\qquad\nb^+(s)=b+\\operatorname{toNNReal}(v(s)^{-1}).\n\\]\nFor a pair \\((x,z)\\in E\\times E\\), define\n\\[\ny(s,x,z)=x+\\sqrt{\\frac{\\tau(s)}{1+b}}\\,z,\n\\]\n\\[\na^+(s,x,z)=b^+(s)^{-1}\n\\left(ba+v(s)^{-1}y(s,x,z)\\right),\n\\]\n\\[\nF_{s,x,z}(w)=V(w)+\\frac{b^+(s)}2\n \\|w-a^+(s,x,z)\\|^2,\n\\]\n\\[\nT_{s,x,z}(w)=w-\\frac{1}{1+b^+(s)}\\nabla F_{s,x,z}(w).\n\\]\nLet\n\\[\nQ_n(s,x,z)=\n\\left\\|\\nabla F_{s,x,z}\\!\\left(T_{s,x,z}^{\\,n}(x)\\right)\\right\\|^2.\n\\]\nDefine \\(N(s,x,z)\\) by an explicit existence branch:\n\\[\nN(s,x,z)=\n\\begin{cases}\n\\min\\{n\\in\\mathbb N:\n Q_n(s,x,z)\\le(\\kappa^{-1}+b^+(s))d\\},\n &\\text{if this set is nonempty},\\\\\n0,&\\text{otherwise}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nIteration with exponent zero is the identity. Set\n\\[\nU(s,x,z)=\n\\left(\n b^+(s),\\\n a^+(s,x,z),\\\n T_{s,x,z}^{\\,N(s,x,z)}(x),\\\n k+1,\\\n h^+\n\\right),\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\nh^+(0)=y(s,x,z),\\qquad h^+(n+1)=h(n).\n\\]\n\nFor the terminal construction, define, for every state \\(s=(b,a,u,k,h)\\),\n\\[\n\\bar b(s)=\\max\\{b,B^{-1}\\},\\qquad\nF_s^{\\mathrm t}(w)=V(w)+\\frac{\\bar b(s)}2\\|w-a\\|^2,\n\\]\n\\[\nT_s^{\\mathrm t}(w)\n=w-\\frac{1}{1+\\bar b(s)}\\nabla F_s^{\\mathrm t}(w),\n\\qquad\nQ_n^{\\mathrm t}(s)\n=\\left\\|\\nabla F_s^{\\mathrm t}\n  \\left((T_s^{\\mathrm t})^n(u)\\right)\\right\\|^2.\n\\]\nDefine\n\\[\nN_{\\mathrm t}(s)=\n\\begin{cases}\n\\min\\{n\\in\\mathbb N:Q_n^{\\mathrm t}(s)\\le d\\bar b(s)\\},\n &\\text{if this set is nonempty},\\\\\n0,&\\text{otherwise}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nThen put\n\\[\nx_{\\mathrm t}(s)=(T_s^{\\mathrm t})^{N_{\\mathrm t}(s)}(u),\\quad\nA(s)=\\bar b(s)^{-1},\\quad\ng(s)=\\nabla V(x_{\\mathrm t}(s)),\\quad\nm(s)=a-A(s)g(s).\n\\]\n\nLet \\(\\gamma_E\\) denote the standard Gaussian probability on \\(E\\), and let\n\\[\n\\nu=\\lambda|_{(0,1]}\\otimes\\gamma_E,\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\lambda\\) is real Lebesgue measure. For \\(x\\in E\\) and \\((t,z)\\in\\mathbb R\\times E\\), write\n\\[\n\\theta=\\frac{\\pi t}{2},\\qquad z_A=\\sqrt{A(s)}\\,z,\n\\]\nand define\n\\[\nW_s(x,t,z)=\n\\min\\!\\left\\{1,\\max\\!\\left\\{-1,\\\n\\left\\langle\n \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\bigl(\\cos\\theta(x-m(s))-\\sin\\theta\\,z_A\\bigr),\n \\ g(s)-\\nabla V\\bigl(m(s)+\\sin\\theta(x-m(s))+\\cos\\theta\\,z_A\\bigr)\n\\right\\rangle\n\\right\\}\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThus the displayed inner product is clipped to \\([-1,1]\\).\n\nDefine the proposal probability\n\\[\nG_s=(z\\mapsto m(s)+\\sqrt{A(s)}z)_\\#\\gamma_E.\n\\]\nOne rejection-sampling attempt is a tuple\n\\[\np=(X,H,\\xi,R)\\in\nE\\times\\mathbb N\\times(\\mathbb R\\times E)^{\\mathbb N}\\times\\mathbb R\n\\]\nwith independent coordinates having laws\n\\[\nX\\sim G_s,\\qquad H\\sim\\operatorname{Poisson}(2),\\qquad\n\\xi\\sim\\nu^{\\otimes\\mathbb N},\\qquad\nR\\sim\\lambda|_{[0,1]}.\n\\]\nLet \\(\\rho_s\\) be the countable product law of independent attempts with this distribution. An attempt is accepted exactly when\n\\[\nR\\le \\prod_{i=0}^{H-1}\\frac{1+W_s(X,\\xi_i)}2.\n\\]\nThe product is over \\(\\operatorname{Fin}(H)\\), and equals \\(1\\) when \\(H=0\\). Denote this acceptance set by \\(\\mathcal A_s\\).\n\nFor an attempt sequence \\(\\omega\\), define the returned point\n\\[\n\\Phi_s(\\omega)=\n\\begin{cases}\nX_{n_*},&\n n_*=\\min\\{n\\in\\mathbb N:\\omega_n\\in\\mathcal A_s\\}\n \\text{ exists},\\\\\n0_E,&\\text{no attempt is accepted}.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nFinally define the target measure\n\\[\n\\pi_s=\n\\left((z\\mapsto a+\\sqrt{A(s)}z)_\\#\\gamma_E\\right)\n       \\text{ exponentially tilted by }-V.\n\\]\nThis is the normalized exponential-tilting measure defined with total inverse conventions. Its being a probability is a conclusion below, rather than an additional premise.\n\n**Asserted conclusions.** All of the following hold:\n\n1. The constants satisfy\n   \\[\n   B>0,\\qquad 0<\\varepsilon\\le\\tfrac12.\n   \\]\n   For every state \\(s=(b,a,u,k,h)\\),\n   \\[\n   b\\ge B^{-1}\\Longrightarrow \\bar b(s)=b.\n   \\]\n\n2. The maps \\(N_{\\mathrm t}:S\\to\\mathbb N\\) and \\(x_{\\mathrm t}:S\\to E\\) are measurable. For every \\(s\\),\n   \\[\n   Q_{N_{\\mathrm t}(s)}^{\\mathrm t}(s)\\le d\\bar b(s),\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   j<N_{\\mathrm t}(s)\n   \\Longrightarrow d\\bar b(s)<Q_j^{\\mathrm t}(s),\n   \\]\n   and\n   \\[\n   \\|m(s)-x_{\\mathrm t}(s)\\|\\le\\sqrt{dA(s)}.\n   \\]\n   These conclusions establish that the terminal stopping index attains its criterion and is its first attaining index, despite the fallback branch in its definition.\n\n3. There exist Markov kernels \\(L_{\\mathrm t}:S\\rightsquigarrow E\\) and \\(P:S\\rightsquigarrow S\\) such that, for every state \\(s=(b,a,u,k,h)\\),\n   \\[\n   P(s)=\n   \\begin{cases}\n   \\delta_s,&b\\ge B^{-1},\\\\[1mm]\n   \\bigl((x,z)\\mapsto U(s,x,z)\\bigr)_\\#\n       \\bigl(M(s)\\otimes\\gamma_E\\bigr),&b<B^{-1}.\n   \\end{cases}\n   \\]\n   Thus the specified threshold states are absorbing. Moreover,\n   \\[\n   P^J(s_0)\\{s=(b,a,u,k,h):b\\ge B^{-1}\\}=1.\n   \\]\n   For every \\(m\\in\\mathbb N\\), equality of output measures holds:\n   \\[\n   (L_{\\mathrm t}\\circ P^{J+m})(s_0)\n     =(L_{\\mathrm t}\\circ P^J)(s_0).\n   \\]\n   Composition here first applies the state kernel and then \\(L_{\\mathrm t}\\).\n\n4. For every state \\(s\\), the function \\(\\Phi_s\\) is measurable, and\n   \\[\n   (\\Phi_s)_\\#\\rho_s=L_{\\mathrm t}(s).\n   \\]\n   Nontermination has measure zero:\n   \\[\n   \\rho_s\\{\\omega:\\forall n,\\ \\omega_n\\notin\\mathcal A_s\\}=0.\n   \\]\n   There is also the precise extended nonnegative integral bound\n   \\[\n   \\int\n   \\left[\n      1+\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}\n      \\mathbf1_{\\{\\forall i<n:\\omega_i\\notin\\mathcal A_s\\}}H_n\n   \\right]\\,d\\rho_s(\\omega)\n   \\le\n   \\operatorname{ofReal}(1+2e^2).\n   \\]\n   The count adds one, then the complete Poisson batch sizes of every attempted batch through and including the first accepted attempt. It is not a count of attempts, and does not count just an inspected prefix of a batch. For \\(n=0\\), the preceding-failures condition is vacuous.\n\n5. For every state \\(s\\), \\(\\pi_s\\) is a probability measure, and it is mutually absolutely continuous with \\(L_{\\mathrm t}(s)\\):\n   \\[\n   \\pi_s\\ll L_{\\mathrm t}(s),\\qquad L_{\\mathrm t}(s)\\ll\\pi_s.\n   \\]\n   Define the real-valued functions\n   \\[\n   f_s(x)=\\operatorname{toReal}\n      \\left(\\frac{d\\pi_s}{dL_{\\mathrm t}(s)}(x)\\right),\n   \\qquad\n   r_s(x)=\\operatorname{toReal}\n      \\left(\\frac{dL_{\\mathrm t}(s)}{d\\pi_s}(x)\\right).\n   \\]\n   The conversion sends an infinite extended nonnegative value to zero. Both \\(f_s^q\\) and \\(r_s^q\\) are Bochner integrable with respect to their respective denominator measures:\n   \\[\n   f_s^q\\in L^1(L_{\\mathrm t}(s)),\\qquad\n   r_s^q\\in L^1(\\pi_s).\n   \\]\n   Their integrals satisfy\n   \\[\n   0<\\int_E f_s(x)^q\\,dL_{\\mathrm t}(s)(x)\n       \\le1+\\varepsilon^2,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   0<\\int_E r_s(x)^q\\,d\\pi_s(x)\n       \\le1+\\varepsilon^2,\n   \\]\n   and\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log\\!\\left(\\int_E f_s(x)^q\\,dL_{\\mathrm t}(s)(x)\\right)}\n        {q-1}\\le\\varepsilon^2,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\log\\!\\left(\\int_E r_s(x)^q\\,d\\pi_s(x)\\right)}\n        {q-1}\\le\\varepsilon^2.\n   \\]\n\nThe constants \\(B,J,\\varepsilon\\) are fixed using \\(s_0\\) only through its first coordinate \\(b_0\\), together with \\(\\kappa,d,q,\\Delta\\). The terminal conclusions hold for every state using those same constants, including states below the threshold, where \\(\\bar b(s)\\) replaces \\(b\\) by \\(B^{-1}\\).\n\nThe proposition does not assert that \\(L_{\\mathrm t}(s)=\\pi_s\\), does not identify the composed output measure with a single global target, and does not give an expected total cost including the state-update iterations or terminal gradient-descent iterations. The explicit work bound concerns the displayed rejection-sampling count only.",
