l disintegration. r composed with p means first draw a state from p and then an output from r. there exist a markov joint kernel j:s->(e x s) and a markov absorbed transition p:s->s. for every s, j_s is the pushforward of m_s product gamma_e by (x,z) -> (obs(s,(x,z)),u(s,(x,z))). its first marginal is exactly g(m_s,sqrt(tau_s/(beta+b))). the kernel identity j.fst compprod j.condkernel=j holds. for each s, for j.fst_s-almost every y, for j.condkernel(s,y)-almost every t, t.precision=bp_s and t.center=bp_s^(-1)*(b*u+v_s^(-1)*y). for every actual markov r:s->e, every s and every measurable a, the nonnegative integral of r(u(s,(x,z)),a) under m_s product gamma_e equals the iterated nonnegative integral of r(t,a) first under j.condkernel(s,y), then under j.fst_s. p_s is dirac_s when threshold<=b and the pushforward by u otherwise. if b<threshold, (r composed with p)(s,a) equals the same conditional iterated integral. packet id: `astis-blind-b97f548aa346d3c3` packet sha-256 recorded in the packet: `549c3fb5aa2db39058c8373ba545c3bb32dcafe1198d9449d0f21c14d069ffb9` lean statement sha-256 recorded in the packet: `b97f548aa346d3c3e98ddaf00086c08c90b44462cc5f4931f165afebfc9c8bc8` these are the packet-supplied hashes; i have not independently recomputed them. i read only the designated anonymous packet. no source text was visible. the reconstruction below identifies no source theorem or intended application. **objects, assumptions, and definitions** let \\(e\\) be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its borel measurable structure, and let \\[ d=\\dim_{\\mathbb r}e\\in\\mathbb r. \\] let \\(v:e\\to\\mathbb r\\) and \\(\\alpha,\\beta\\in\\mathbb r_{\\ge0}\\). assume: 1. \\(0<\\alpha\\) and \\(\\alpha\\le\\beta\\). 2. \\(v\\) is twice continuously fréchet differentiable. 3. for every \\(x,w\\in e\\), \\[ \\alpha\\|w\\|^2 \\le (d(dv)(x)[w])[w] \\le \\beta\\|w\\|^2. \\] 4. \\(0<d\\). nonnegative real parameters are coerced to real numbers wherever real arithmetic is displayed below. define the state space \\[ s=\\mathbb r_{\\ge0}\\times e\\times e\\times\\mathbb n\\times e^{\\mathbb n}. \\] its products are right-associated. write a state as \\(s=(a,m,b,k,h)\\), with \\(h:\\mathbb n\\to e\\) a full infinite sequence. equip this space with the product measurable structure. for every pair of measurable functions \\(\\eta,\\tau:s\\to\\mathbb r\\) satisfying \\[ \\forall s\\in s,\\quad \\eta(s)>0,\\qquad \\tau(s)>0, \\] every markov kernel \\(m:s\\rightsquigarrow e\\), and every threshold \\(\\theta\\in\\mathbb r_{\\ge0}\\), make the following definitions. for \\(s=(a,m,b,k,h)\\), put \\[ v(s)=\\frac{\\eta(s)+\\tau(s)}{\\beta+a}, \\qquad a^+(s)=a+\\operatorname{tonnreal}(v(s)^{-1}). \\] here \\(\\operatorname{tonnreal}\\) truncates a real number below at zero. in these hypotheses \\(v(s)>0\\), so this truncation does not change the positive inverse. for \\(p=(s,(x,g))\\in s\\times(e\\times e)\\), define \\[ \\begin{aligned} o(p)&=x+\\sqrt{\\frac{\\tau(s)}{\\beta+a}}\\,g,\\\\ c(p)&=(a^+(s))^{-1}\\bigl(a\\,m+v(s)^{-1}o(p)\\bigr),\\\\ f_p(u)&=v(u)+\\frac{a^+(s)}2\\|u-c(p)\\|^2,\\\\ t_p(u)&=u-(\\beta+a^+(s))^{-1}\\nabla f_p(u),\\\\ q(n,p)&=\\left\\|\\nabla f_p\\bigl(t_p^{[n]}(x)\\bigr)\\right\\|^2. \\end{aligned} \\] all scalar-vector products use the real vector-space structure. \\(t_p^{[n]}\\) denotes \\(n\\)-fold iteration, including the identity for \\(n=0\\). the starting point is the newly drawn \\(x\\), not either stored state coordinate \\(m\\) or \\(b\\). define \\[ n(p)= \\begin{cases} \\min\\{n\\in\\mathbb n:q(n,p)\\le(\\alpha+a^+(s))d\\}, &\\text{if this set is nonempty},\\\\ 0,&\\text{otherwise}, \\end{cases} \\qquad u(p)=t_p^{[n(p)]}(x). \\] define an updated sequence by \\[ h_p^+(0)=o(p),\\qquad h_p^+(n+1)=h(n) \\quad(n\\in\\mathbb n), \\] and the state update \\[ u(p)=\\bigl(a^+(s),c(p),u(p),k+1,h_p^+\\bigr). \\] thus the observation is prepended to the stored infinite sequence. let \\(\\gamma_e\\) be standar