      "repaired_theorem": "For every natural dimension d, let f:R^d→R be twice continuously differentiable and let beta>0. Assume f(y)≤f(x)+<grad f(x),y-x>+(beta/2)||y-x||² for all x,y∈R^d, and let z be a global minimizer of f, with f_star=f(z). For every h with 0<h≤1/beta, every x₀∈R^d and every natural N≥1, define x_(k+1)=x_k-h grad f(x_k) for all natural k starting from x₀. Then min_{0≤k<N}||grad f(x_k)||≤sqrt(2(f(x₀)-f_star)/(N*h)).",
