      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "Chewi arXiv:2605.07006v1 Exercise3.2. In the Section3 C2 Euclidean setting, assume f is alpha-convex and beta-smooth. Write T_h(x)=x-h grad f(x). The fundamental theorem of calculus gives ||T_h(y)-T_h(x)|| <= integral_0^1 ||DT_h((1-t)x+t y)||op ||y-x|| dt. Bound the eigenvalues of DT_h and show that h=2/(alpha+beta) minimizes the resulting bound. The resulting factor is (kappa-1)/(kappa+1), with kappa=beta/alpha, improving the preceding convergence bound. The condition-number contraction interpretation uses positive strong convexity and smoothness. ASTIS-authored faithful paraphrase; no source wording is silently replaced by a Lean extension.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any complete real inner-product space, with its induced norm (no finite-dimensionality assumption), and let f:E→ℝ be twice continuously Fréchet differentiable. Write ∇f(x) for the Riesz vector representing its Fréchet derivative. The global α-strong-convexity assumption means: for every u,v∈E and every s,t∈ℝ with s≥0, t≥0 and s+t=1, f(su+tv)≤s f(u)+t f(v)−(α/2)st‖u−v‖². The global quadratic upper bound means: for every u,v∈E, f(v)≤f(u)+⟨∇f(u),v−u⟩+(β/2)‖v−u‖². For every real α,β satisfying 0≤α, 0<β and α≤β, if these two global assumptions hold, then for every x,y∈E the following conjunction holds: (i) ‖(y−[2/(α+β)]∇f(y))−(x−[2/(α+β)]∇f(x))‖≤[(β−α)/(α+β)]‖y−x‖; and (ii) for every real h, (β−α)/(α+β)≤max{|1−hα|,|1−hβ|}. Thus the second conjunct compares the stated factor with the scalar expression at all real h, including negative h, and does not assert that it is a lower bound on the actual Lipschitz constant of this particular f. In the written quantifier scope both conjuncts are under ∀x,y, although (ii) does not depend on x,y. The denominator α+β is strictly positive by the premises. The factor and selected step depend only on α,β. The allowed case α=0 gives factor 1 and step 2/β, so strict contraction is not always asserted. The allowed case α=β>0 gives factor 0 and step 1/α. The cases x=y and the zero space are included.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "domain-mismatch",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
