      "subtitle": "chewi-opt-v1-exercise-3-3 · lean-weakened-conclusion",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.QuadraticGradientDescent.quadratic_gradient_iterate.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "Chewi arXiv:2605.07006v1 Exercise3.3. Let f(x)=inner(x,A*x)/2 for a positive-definite symmetric matrix A on Euclidean space. Derive the gradient-descent iterates explicitly and check how sharp the results of this section are. The actual update is x_(n+1)=x_n-h gradient f(x_n). The exercise prints no solution. ASTIS-authored faithful paraphrase. The operator-power and eigenmode identities are selected proof components; full assessment of every Section3 rate remains an uncovered source obligation.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every complete real inner product space E and every continuous real-linear endomorphism H:E→E satisfying ⟨Hu,v⟩=⟨u,Hv⟩ for all u,v∈E, define f:E→ℝ by f(z)=⟨z,Hz⟩/2. Then for every real h, every natural number N (including zero), and every x∈E, the N-fold iterate starting at x of T(z)=z−h∇f(z) equals (I−hH)^N x. The power of an endomorphism means repeated composition, and the zeroth iterate and zeroth endomorphism power are both the identity. The gradient is taken in the real inner product structure; the displayed quadratic is differentiable under these assumptions. There are no positivity, spectral, finite-dimensionality, or step-size restrictions. In particular h=0 and N=0 are included, and no convergence or contraction conclusion is asserted.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "lean-weakened-conclusion",
