          "reconstructed": "Explicit f(x)=mu*x^2/2, mu=beta/[2(N+1)], true gradient map T, minimizer 0 and iterate T^[N](1).",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "In one dimension the matrix [mu] is positive definite because mu>0. The reconstruction identifies the actual gradient and iteration, not an assumed recurrence."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
