          "original": "Convex beta-smooth objectives, positive beta, step 1/beta and attained minimum.",
          "reconstructed": "Only beta>0 is assumed; positivity of mu, C2 regularity, mu-strong convexity, global beta upper model and minimum at 0 are conclusions.",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "The chosen witness proves admissibility rather than assuming the desired lower bound. Since 0<mu=beta/[2(N+1)]<=beta, its Hessian and gradient satisfy the beta smoothness bound; beta need not be its least possible smoothness constant. No regularity, attainment or trajectory assumption is smuggled into the statement."
        },
        {
          "slot": "conclusion",
          "original": "Selected component tests sharpness in order of the convex function-value rate, without a printed witness or numerical lower constant.",
          "reconstructed": "An exact objective gap beta/[4(N+1)]*(1-1/[2(N+1)])^(2N) and lower bound beta/[16(N+1)].",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The supplied formula is an authored solution to the selected exercise component. For N>=1, N+1<=2N gives gap>=beta/(32N), a uniform reciprocal-order obstruction at R=1. The theorem does not purport to reproduce the general upper theorem inside this declaration."
