    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-ANDI-OPT-GDRatesConvex",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-ANDI-OPT-GDRatesConvex",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "chewi-opt-v1-theorem-3-4 · implicit-assumption-exposed",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GradientDescentRates.convex_value_le.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "In the section C² Euclidean setting, strong convexity and smoothness give a distance-plus-function decrement for the gradient update. Remark (3.3) allows any comparator z. Applying the forced recurrence and monotonic function values gives the weighted final-gap estimate, then the printed inverse-power closed form and the convex limiting rate. The source prints only h≤1/β; the missing nonnegative-step condition and singular reciprocal endpoints remain visible in separate binding deltas.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every complete real inner-product space E (with its normed additive commutative group structure), every function f:E→ℝ, and every real β and h, assume: f is continuously Fréchet differentiable on all of E; f is convex on all of E, meaning f((1-t)x+t y)≤(1-t)f(x)+t f(y) for all x,y∈E and t∈[0,1]; h>0; βh≤1; and for every x,y∈E,\nf(y)≤f(x)+⟨∇f(x),y-x⟩+(β/2)‖y-x‖².\nHere ∇f is the Riesz gradient. Then for every initial point x₀∈E, every comparator z∈E, and every natural number N>0, define the actual iterates by xₖ₊₁=xₖ-h∇f(xₖ). The theorem gives the last-iterate bound\nf(x_N)-f(z)≤‖x₀-z‖²/(2hN).\nThe same fixed step h is used at each iteration, and the norm and inner product are those of E. There is no finite-dimensionality assumption, explicit positive or nonnegative sign assumption on β, or assumption that z is a minimizer, stationary point, or selected comparator; both x₀ and z are universally quantified. No existence of a minimizer, gradient Lipschitz condition, or additional convergence conclusion is asserted. N=0 and h=0 are excluded, so the displayed denominator is strictly positive. If x₀=z, the displayed right side is zero. There are no conditional conclusion branches.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "implicit-assumption-exposed",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
