          "evidence": "Arbitrary z is a disclosed extension of the displayed final rate supported by the general-comparator energy argument. Monotonicity of f(X_n), nonnegative weights, and nonnegativity of squared distance suffice even when f(X_N)-f(z)<0. No minimizer existence or optimality assumption is hidden."
        },
        {
