          "evidence": "The quadratic upper model is the source definition (1.7), not an extra replacement for a source Lipschitz hypothesis. C1 weakens the section C² convention. Explicit positive-step and positive-iteration hypotheses exclude genuine singular or invalid cases. Convexity is zero strong convexity with the same normalization."
        },
        {
          "slot": "conclusion",
          "original": "Theorem 3.4 has one-step energy and normalized value bounds, with convex specialization.",
          "reconstructed": "f(X_N)-f(z)≤‖x₀-z‖²/(2hN).",
