on supplies no bound at this endpoint. under its strict hypothesis 0<q<1, the second denominator is positive and the two displayed right sides agree. lean's inverse is totalized at zero, but this does not extend the conditional second conclusion to q=0. n=0, α=0, and h=0 are excluded. if x₀=z, the right side of the first bound is zero, as is that of the second whenever its condition holds. no explicit sign assumption on β is present. no finite-dimensionality, optimizer or stationary-point condition on z, existence of a minimizer, or gradient lipschitz assumption is stated. the quantified comparator z is arbitrary in e. these are last-iterate function-value inequalities, with no additional distance-contraction or limit claim. accepted https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#s3; theorem3.4 (3.1)-(3.3), lemma3.1, weighted calculation after lemma3.5 autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gradientdescentrates.strongly_convex_value_le autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/gradientdescentrates.lean true andi-gd-rates-worker gdrates_blind_96104 33fda466080073b41c4f174482256e6885e6d2162304d1966867c8cf272462ca accepted gdrates_source_96104 objects euclidean objective, its gradient, fixed-step gd and objective gap. actual riesz gradient and n-fold iteration of x ↦ x-h∇f(x). explicit-elaboration the printed lean statement, entire supplied module and blind reconstruction agree; no arbitrary vector field or assumed sequence replaces actual gradient descent. domains euclidean space; iteration count; source denominators impose unstated restrictions. complete real inner-product space; real parameters; h>0 and natural n>0. also α>0, 0≤q=1-αh<1; inverse-power branch requires q>0. different space is generalized. positive h and n are substantive explicit domain restrictions, not a literal match to printed h≤1/β. βh≤1 agrees with that upper restriction when β>0. lean omits β≥0, and also handles β=0 without division by β. quantifiers displayed rate compares to a minimizer; equation