      "subtitle": "chewi-opt-v1-theorem-3-3 · implicit-assumption-exposed",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GradientDescentComplexity.distance_le_of_log_bound.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "In the section’s C² Euclidean setting, an α-strongly convex β-smooth objective gives the displayed contraction of the gradient update x⁺=x−h∇f(x), for all x,y and h≤1/β. Taking y to be a global minimizer x⋆, using h=1/β, κ=β/α and R=‖x₀−x⋆‖, iteration yields the geometric and exponential distance estimates. The following logarithmic complexity conclusion is a separate proof obligation with its own declaration binding. The printed step restriction omits h≥0; its necessary domain is exposed in the bindings without rewriting the source.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any complete real inner-product space, with its normed additive commutative group structure, and let f:E→ℝ be continuously Fréchet differentiable. Let α, β, ε be real numbers with α>0, β>0, and ε>0. Assume that f is α-strongly convex on all of E, in the precise convention f((1−t)x+ty)≤(1−t)f(x)+tf(y)−(α/2)t(1−t)‖x−y‖² for every x,y∈E and t∈[0,1]. Assume also the global quadratic upper bound f(y)≤f(x)+⟨∇f(x),y−x⟩+(β/2)‖y−x‖² for every x,y∈E, where ∇f(x) is the Riesz representative of the Fréchet derivative. For every global minimizer x⋆∈E (meaning f(x⋆)≤f(x) for all x∈E), every initial point x₀∈E, and every natural number N including zero, suppose the conditional iteration bound holds: if ‖x₀−x⋆‖>0, then 2(β/α)log(‖x₀−x⋆‖/ε)≤N, with N regarded as a real number. Define xₖ₊₁=xₖ−β⁻¹∇f(xₖ), starting at x₀. Then ‖x_N−x⋆‖≤ε. The logarithm is the real natural logarithm, with Lean's totalized convention log(0)=0. The iteration hypothesis imposes no restriction on N when x₀=x⋆. Zero iterations returns x₀. No finite-dimensionality or separate relation α≤β is assumed.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "implicit-assumption-exposed",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
