          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Definition1.5 and Definition1.12 match these normalizations. The actual gradient, global quantifiers, and regularity are displayed. C1 instead of C2 is a disclosed generalization. Positive α and β expose the condition-number and reciprocal-step domain, while positive ε and R justify inversion of log. No added α≤β premise is needed; on a nontrivial space it follows from curvature compatibility, and on a singleton R=0."
