is needed; on a nontrivial space it follows from curvature compatibility, and on a singleton r=0. conclusion n≥2κ log(r/ε) suffices for distance ≤ε. n≥2(β/α)log(r/ε), when r>0, implies actual final distance ≤ε. explicit-elaboration the coefficient 2 is unchanged. multiplication by α/β>0 gives log(r/ε)≤αn/(2β); exponentiating and canceling the positive exponentials yields exp(-αn/(2β))r≤ε. composing the parent bound proves the stated conclusion. scopes the selected component of theorem3.3 and its following paragraph. the declaration supports only logarithmic-complexity. explicit-elaboration checked the exact binding, complete module, and authored lesson. the refreshed item says complexity has its own declaration binding; historical uncovered/outside-this-unit prose is removed. separate source obligations are not silently credited to one declaration. constant dependencies κ=β/α, r and ε. exactly 2(β/α)log(r/ε); no dimension or unspecified constant. same the current lesson uses distance, not squared distance or objective error. its reciprocal step and exponent αn/(2β) invert to precisely the source count. domains informational disclosed extension from euclidean c2 objectives to complete real hilbert c1 objectives. the formal hypotheses retain the global curvature and upper model; the original setting is a specialization. assumptions informational positive denominator and logarithm domains are explicit. the rate uses finite positive κ and positive accuracy. conditional r>0 handling adds the stationary-start case without changing the source positive-r formula. quantifiers informational zero iterations and already accurate initial points are explicitly included. if r≤ε the exponential estimate and nonnegative iteration count already suffice. no positive iteration-count assumption or logarithm at zero is needed.",
