          "evidence": "The opening Section 4.1 convention admits an upper radius certificate. At every stage the passed radius equals the scheduled radius; the final radius equals sqrt(epsilon/alpha). Therefore evaluating phi at 8*kappa and kappa needs no monotonicity. Positive parameters give valid calls. The algebraic horizon premise supplies exactly the radius needed for the final call."
