c fixed-objective certified-cost component. weaker-in-lean binding supports restart-radius, finite-accuracy-cost only. the updated obligation asymptotic-oracle-reduction is explicitly not closed. the finite parent gains no new logarithmic coverage merely because that obligation appears in the common source context. constant dependencies halving follows from alpha/2 quadratic growth with tolerance alpha*r^2/8; per-call budget uses kappa=beta/alpha. exactly the same factors 1/2, 1/8 and 8*kappa, with a separate phi(kappa) final term. the stage multiplier is the supplied n and the last cost is included even when n=0. explicit-elaboration the authored algebra matches the packet proof. quadratic growth bounds the next squared distance by r_k^2/4; positivity gives halving. exact cancellation in each passed radius/tolerance ratio avoids a hidden comparison of different phi arguments. domains informational hilbert/c1 finite-component generalization; beta is a budget parameter in the formal theorem. current module assumptions and lesson describe the actual domain. euclidean beta-smooth objectives fit the intended application, but that class-to-contract adapter is outside this declaration. quantifiers informational full source class-uniform first-order solver realization remains uncovered. a is an unconstrained point/cost map apart from ha for fixed f,z. publication keeps asymptotic-oracle-reduction separate and explicitly not closed. conclusion informational finite radius/accuracy/cost component accepted; adequate horizon remains an input. the binding supports only restart-radius and finite-accuracy-cost; the shared new logarithmic obligation does not alter the finite theorem statement or lesson.",
