          "evidence": "The packet module implements each call as A y r delta and propagates its returned point and cost; no radius invariant or final answer is substituted for execution. The map has no oracle restriction."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
          "original": "Euclidean objective with smoothness parameter beta and positive strong-convexity modulus.",
          "reconstructed": "A complete real inner-product space with C1, alpha-strongly convex f on all E; beta occurs only in the cost contract.",
          "relation": "different",
          "evidence": "Euclidean spaces specialize the stated Hilbert domain. The proof needs differentiability for the gradient lower bound; Lipschitz-gradient smoothness is not inferred from beta. This is a disclosed generalization of the finite composition component, not equivalence of function classes."
        },
