      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-andi-opt-restartlogcomplexity semantic-audit astis-rt-andi-opt-restartlogcomplexity chewi-opt-v1-lemma-4-1 · lean-weakened-conclusion blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.restartlogcomplexity.logarithmic_accuracy_and_cost. lean-weakened-conclusion source hidden from decoder assume an algorithm optimizes every convex beta-smooth euclidean objective from a point within radius r of a minimizer to objective error epsilon in phi(beta r²/epsilon) first-order queries. for an alpha-strongly convex beta-smooth objective, lemma4.1 constructs a restarted method with stated order o(phi(8kappa) log(alpha r²/epsilon)), kappa=beta/alpha. its proof calls the base method at radii r/2^k and tolerances alpha(r/2^k)²/8; quadratic growth halves the radius after each call. after reaching radius at most sqrt(epsilon/alpha), one final call at tolerance epsilon gives the desired objective accuracy. the proof records per-stage phi(8kappa) and final phi(kappa) costs. the finite construction, final call and full asymptotic/oracle conclusion are distinct obligations. let e be any complete real inner-product space with its normed additive commutative group structure, and let f:e→ℝ be continuously fréchet differentiable on all of e. let α, β, r, ε be strictly positive real numbers. assume f is α-strongly convex on e with the normalization f((1−t)x+ty) ≤ (1−t)f(x)+tf(y)−(α/2)t(1−t)‖x−y‖² for every x,y∈e and t∈[0,1]. for every z,x₀∈e such that f(z)≤f(x) for all x∈e and ‖x₀−z‖≤r, consider any map a:e×ℝ×ℝ→e×ℕ and any map φ:ℝ→ℕ. suppose that for every y∈e and every real r,δ, if r>0, δ>0, and ‖y−z‖≤r, then, writing a(y,r,δ)=(v,c), both f(v)−f(z)≤δ and c≤φ(βr²/δ) hold. the same fixed minimizer z is used in every such call guarantee. no condition on a for other inputs, no smoothness bound involving β, and no monotonicity assumption on φ is asserted. define l=ln(αr²/ε)/ln(4), n=⌈l⌉₊∈ℕ (the natural-number ceiling, equal to zero for l≤0 and otherwise the least natural number at least l), and r_k=r/2^k for every k∈ℕ. define a state-and-cost sequence (x_k,c_k) by (x_0,c_0)=(x₀,0), and for each k∈ℕ define (v_k,d_k)=a(x_k,r_k,αr_k²/8) and (x_{k+1},c_{k+1})=(v_k,c_k+d_k). after these n recursive calls, define (x_*,d_*)=a(x_n,√(ε/α),ε) and the natural-number total cost c=c_n+d_*. the square root is the nonnegative real square root; its argument here is positive. then all of the following conclusions hold simultaneously: (1) n≤max{0,l}+1, interpreting n as a real number; (2) n=0 if and only if αr²≤ε; (3) ‖x_n−z‖≤r_n; (4) f(x_*)−f(z)≤ε; (5) c≤n·φ(8(β/α))+φ(β/α), an inequality in ℕ; and (6) c≤(max{0,l}+1)·φ(8(β/α))+φ(β/α), an inequality in ℝ with c and the values of φ coerced to real numbers. in addition, the single extra hypothesis φ(β/α)≤φ(8(β/α)) implies the conjunction of both (7) c≤(max{0,l}+2)·φ(8(β/α)) and (8) if 4≤αr²/ε, then c≤3l·φ(8(β/α)); these latter bounds are real inequalities. thus the bound in (8) is nested under both the comparison of the two φ values and the ratio condition 4≤αr²/ε; the ratio condition alone is not stated to imply that bound. when αr²≤ε, n=0 and the recursion contributes the initial pair (x₀,0); the final call a(x₀,√(ε/α),ε) is still made and contributes its cost. in this case the natural-number bound (5) reduces to c≤φ(β/α). equality αr²=ε is included in this zero-recursion case. costs and φ values may themselves be zero: they are only required to be natural numbers, and the stated inequalities remain valid without any positivity assumption on them. accepted https://arxiv.org/html/2605.07006v1#s4.ss1; section4.1 opening radius-certified optimization convention; lemma4.1 statement and proof (4.1) autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.restartlogcomplexity.logarithmic_accuracy_and_cost autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/restartlogcomplexity.lean true andi-restart-log-worker restart_log_blind_2700 3f99af6fa440b5b2e1865c2010c