lid calls. only the stronger absorbed bounds require phi(kappa)<=phi(8*kappa), and the 3l bound additionally requires q>=4. conclusion radius halving and final accuracy support the full logarithmic first-order-query reduction. actual radius and final error, with certified finite cumulative cost. n=ceil_nat(log(q)/log(4)), n<=max(0,l)+1, n=0 iff q<=1; c<=n*phi(8*kappa)+phi(kappa), the global real bound, and conditional absorbed bounds. weaker-in-lean each displayed conjunction agrees with the elaborated lean statement and blind reconstruction. the final 3l inequality is nested under both conditions, as the authored formula and proof correctly state. no first-order-query theorem follows without realizing the certified solver contract in the oracle/class model. scopes an algorithmic reduction, whose proof contains finite call composition and asymptotic counting. a deterministic fixed-objective certified-cost component. weaker-in-lean binding supports logarithmic-certified-cost only. the updated obligation asymptotic-oracle-reduction is explicitly not closed. the finite parent gains no new logarithmic coverage merely because that obligation appears in the common source context. constant dependencies halving follows from alpha/2 quadratic growth with tolerance alpha*r^2/8; per-call budget uses kappa=beta/alpha. exactly the same factors 1/2, 1/8 and 8*kappa, with a separate phi(kappa) final term. the logarithmic base is 4; the global +1 rounding and conditional +2 absorption give 3/log(4) under q>=4. explicit-elaboration the authored algebra matches the packet proof. q>0 and log(4)>0 justify log monotonicity; q<=4^n gives the finite horizon. natural-valued phi is nonnegative. under q>=4, l>=1 and l+2<=3l. no dependence on dimension or hidden positivity of phi is introduced. domains informational hilbert/c1 finite-component generalization; beta is a budget parameter in the formal theorem. current module assumptions and lesson describe the actual domain. euclidean beta-smooth objectives fit the intended application, but that class-to-contract adapter is outside this declaration. quantifiers informational full source class-uniform first-order solver realization remains uncovered. a is an unconstrained point/cost map apart from ha for fixed f,z. publication keeps asymptotic-oracle-reduction separate and explicitly not closed. conclusion informational finite logarithmic certified-cost component accepted; unconditional absorption is not claimed. the exact statement retains the final phi(kappa) globally and nests the 3l bound under phi comparison and q>=4. no claim of a globally valid untruncated logarithm is made.",
