          "original": "A given algorithm works over the strongly convex class and induces an algorithm working over the convex class.",
          "reconstructed": "For each fixed parameter tuple and phi, next,update,s0 are fixed before the all-g hypothesis and before the all-f conclusion.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "hs quantifies every eligible g and every qualifying minimizer w; its witnesses must equal execution of the same callbacks and s0. The correction is defined before f is quantified and depends only on original callbacks and known u,delta. Neither z nor w is passed into execution. Thus this is actual class-uniformity at the fixed parameter tuple, not selection of a new solver per objective."
