      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "Let E be a real inner-product space, ι a finite index type, w a unit vector, and directions z_i tangent to the unit sphere at w. If f has a global minimum on that sphere at w, each scalar curve t ↦ f(Exp_w(t z_i)) is continuous at zero, diagonal_i is its Mathlib total double derivative at zero, and laplacian is the finite sum of the diagonal_i, then laplacian is nonnegative.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let ι be a finite type and E a real inner-product space. For every function f : E → ℝ, point w : E, finite family of directions directions : ι → E, family diagonal : ι → ℝ, and scalar laplacian : ℝ, assume that ‖w‖ = 1; every directions(i) is orthogonal to w; w is a global minimizer of f on the unit sphere {z ∈ E : ‖z‖ = 1}; for every i, the curve t ↦ f(unitSphereExp w (t • directions(i))) is continuous at t = 0; diagonal(i) equals deriv (deriv (t ↦ f(unitSphereExp w (t • directions(i))))) 0; and laplacian = ∑_i diagonal(i). Then 0 ≤ laplacian.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
