      "source_url": "https://chewisinho.github.io/st_flour.pdf#page=215",
      "original_theorem": "Let μ₀, μ₁ ∈ P₂(ℝᵈ), let γ ∈ Γ(μ₀, μ₁) be an optimal quadratic coupling, define π_t(x,y)=(1-t)x+ty and μ_t=(π_t)♯γ. Then for 0≤s≤t≤1, W₂(μ_s,μ_t)=(t-s)W₂(μ₀,μ₁). This is the ordered metric-identity component of Theorem 7.6; existence of γ and the full geodesic-space conclusion are outside this formal target.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a nonempty finite-dimensional real inner product space equipped with its Borel measurable structure, assumed second countable and standard Borel. Let μ₀ and μ₁ be probability measures on E with finite second moments, and let γ be a quadratic optimal coupling of μ₀ and μ₁. For each real r, define the displacement interpolation μᵣ as the pushforward of γ under (x,y) ↦ (1-r)x+ry. Then, for every pair of real numbers s and t satisfying 0 ≤ s ≤ t ≤ 1, the extended-nonnegative-real Wasserstein distance obeys W₂(μₛ, μₜ) = ENNReal.ofReal(t-s) · W₂(μ₀, μ₁).",
