      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260918-proximalexecution semantic-audit astis-rt-20260918-proximalexecution companion:sphmc-algorithm-d2-lemma-d3 · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.approximateproximalexecution.approximate_proximal_execution. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder for a c² potential with kappa-inverse and unit hessian bounds, the iteration x₀=y, xₙ₊₁=y−eta∇v(xₙ) stops at its first residual at most (1−eta)eps. it returns the current iterate, within eps of the unique proximal minimum. its gradient-query count, including the successful test, is bounded by c_c[1+log(1+‖∇v(y)‖/eps)], uniformly in y, for fixed 0<eta≤c<1. samplinglib additionally establishes measurable first-hit/output, quantitative unique minimum and the exact finite-fuel execution equation. assumptions: the source uses euclidean space; the formal statement uses a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its borel measurable structure. v is c², kappa≥1 and kappa⁻¹‖v‖²≤d²v(x)[v,v]≤‖v‖² for every x,v. 0<eta≤c<1 and eps>0. exact arithmetic and exact gradient queries are the cost model, not floating-point arithmetic. let e be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space equipped with its borel measurable structure. let v:e→ℝ be c², and let κ∈ℝ≥0 satisfy κ≥1 and κ⁻¹‖v‖²≤d²v(x)[v,v]≤‖v‖² for every x,v∈e. for every η,c,ε∈ℝ with 0<η≤c<1 and ε>0, define t_y(x)=y−η∇v(x), f_y(x)=v(x)+(η⁻¹/2)‖x−y‖², and x_j(y)=t_y^[j](y). there exist measurable p:e→e and n:e→ℕ such that y↦x_{n(y)}(y) is measurable and, for every y∈e: (1) p(y)+η∇v(p(y))=y; (2) for every z∈e, f_y(p(y))+((κ⁻¹+η⁻¹)/2)‖z−p(y)‖²≤f_y(z), and f_y(z)≤f_y(p(y)) iff z=p(y); (3) ‖x_{n(y)+1}(y)−x_{n(y)}(y)‖≤(1−η)ε, whereas this inequality fails for every natural j<n(y); (4) ‖x_{n(y)}(y)−p(y)‖≤ε; (5) n(y)+1≤[2+(1+log((1−c)⁻¹))/(−log c)] [1+log(1+‖∇v(y)‖/ε)]; and (6) q(∇v,η,ε,y,n(y)+1,y)=some(x_{n(y)}(y),n(y)+1). source-reviewed appendix d.2, algorithm d.2 and lemma d.3, equations d.5–d.6 autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.approximateproximalexecution.approximate_proximal_execution autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/approximateproximalexecution.lean true root blind_20260918_d d886709d6bad308be7c5b6b79971bd8dd0bff76c28b36ad34fb9e6d0f41461ea accepted source_review_20260918_d objects the pinned attributed contract specifies the potential, unique proximal minimum, residual-stopped iteration, measurable first-hit/output and exact finite-fuel execution. v, f_y, t_y, p(y), first-hit n(y), returned x_n and proximalquery. explicit-elaboration the quadratic-growth inequality and minimizer equivalence identify p as a genuine unique minimum. q in the reconstruction denotes the module's proximalquery interpreter. domains the pinned contract explicitly distinguishes the article's euclidean setting from the formal finite-dimensional complete real inner-product borel space. finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its borel measurable structure. same the reconstructed typeclasses match the disclosed domain. dimension zero is included. euclidean instances remain covered. quantifiers for an admissible potential and fixed admissible parameters, the claims hold uniformly in the center y. for every admissible v, κ, eta, c, eps, measurable p and n exist and all conclusions hold for every y. explicit-elaboration the existential maps occur after parameter hypotheses and before forall y. neither c nor the complexity coefficient may vary with y. assumptions c² potential, κ ≥ 1, normalized genuine hessian bounds, 0 < eta ≤ c < 1, positive tolerance, and exact arithmetic/query semantics. contdiff ℝ 2 v, κ ≥ 1, second-derivative bounds, 0 < eta ≤ c < 1 and eps > 0; proximalquery uses exact-real operations. equivalent the article's section 2 supplies c² regularity and d.2 explicitly supplies the full step-size range. contdiff justifies