    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20260929-PicardCenterMoment",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20260929-PicardCenterMoment",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-d7-two-layer-moment-propagation · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.PicardCenterMoment.picard_center_gradient_moment.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A4.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed expanded proof component, not the full equation D.7 or Lemma D.4. Work in the paper's normalized Euclidean setting: V is C2, kappa>=1, kappa^(-1)I<=Hess V<=I, 0<eta<=c<1, eps>0, and xstar is a minimizer. For one Algorithm 3.1 phase, let X be the current position and P0 the refreshed momentum. Samplinglib freezes their required input as the explicit combined bound E[||X-xstar||^2+||P0||^2]<=M with integrability; deriving this M from the paper's run-wide state estimate and refresh remains a separate adapter. For nodes satisfying |t_i|<=1, the first Picard centers are Y0_i=X+t_i P0. Measurable innovations are here abstracted by the only facts used in this calculation, integrable E||G_j||^2<=d; their actual standard-Gaussian joint law remains separate. Approximate proximal nonexpansiveness, the proximal error and one-smoothness control Z0_j=gradient V(q(Y0_j)+sqrt(eta)G_j). For finite weights with sum_j |omega_ij|<=S, the second centers are Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j. Samplinglib formalizes this conditional propagation with explicit sufficient constants: E||gradient V(Y0_i)||^2<=2M; with B=6M+3 eps^2+3 eta d, E||Z0_j||^2<=B; and E||gradient V(Y1_i)||^2<=4M+2 S^2 B. It constructs the actual stopped approximate-proximal output and exposes measurability and integrability. The repeated Algorithm 3.1 law, run-wide state estimate, momentum-refresh adapter, actual Gaussian/joint law, Chebyshev-Lobatto node and weight instantiation, parameter substitutions yielding C kappa d Lq^18, D.8 and Theorem 5.1 remain separate.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure, let (Omega,mu) be a probability space, and let iota be a finite type of nodes. Let V:E->R be twice continuously Frechet differentiable and let kappa>=1 satisfy (1/kappa)||v||^2 <= D^2V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for every x,v in E. Let 0<eta<=c<1 and eps>0. Let X,P:Omega->E be measurable, let xstar in E satisfy grad V(xstar)=0, and suppose w |-> ||X(w)-xstar||^2+||P(w)||^2 is integrable with expectation at most M. For each i in iota let t_i be real with |t_i|<=1, set Y0_i=X+t_i P, and let G_j:Omega->E be measurable innovations such that ||G_j||^2 is integrable with expectation at most dim_R(E) for every j. Let real weights omega_ij satisfy sum_j |omega_ij|<=S for every i, and define B=6M+3eps^2+3eta dim_R(E). Then there exist measurable functions p:E->E, N:E->N, and q:E->E such that, for every y in E, p(y)+eta grad V(p(y))=y, ||q(y)-p(y)||<=eps, and the finite exact-real proximalQuery run on y with fuel N(y)+1 returns some(q(y),N(y)+1), where the recorded natural number counts all gradient tests including the successful one. Define Z0_j=grad V(q(Y0_j)+sqrt(eta)G_j) and Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j, pointwise on Omega. Then, for every applicable node index, each of ||grad V(Y0_i)||^2, ||Z0_j||^2, and ||grad V(Y1_i)||^2 is integrable, and their expectations satisfy E_mu||grad V(Y0_i)||^2<=2M, E_mu||Z0_j||^2<=B, and E_mu||grad V(Y1_i)||^2<=4M+2S^2B.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
          "slot": "objects",
          "original": "Position X, refreshed momentum P0, first centers Y0_i=X+t_i P0, approximate proximal output q, innovations G_j, queries Z0_j=gradient V(q(Y0_j)+sqrt(eta)G_j), and second centers Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j.",
          "reconstructed": "The same objects, with P denoting P0, together with measurable exact proximal map p, stopping index N, and actual returned iterate q.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "The attributed contract, embedded module and lesson define the same Y0, Z0 and Y1; Lean additionally exposes the stopped execution witnesses."
        },
        {
          "slot": "domains",
