          "reconstructed": "A finite-dimensional complete real inner-product Borel space, probability measure, finite node type, and measurable inputs and innovations with the same moment bounds; no Gaussian law or independence is assumed.",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "Finite-dimensional real inner-product space is the coordinate-free Euclidean setting for these invariant expressions, and the attributed contract explicitly adopts the same innovation-moment abstraction."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
          "original": "For one realized phase, the estimates apply to every first-layer query and second-layer center; the stopped approximate-proximal output is constructed.",
          "reconstructed": "For every admissible data set there exist measurable p,N,q with pointwise execution facts for every y and moment conclusions for every node.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
