      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20260929-picardcentermoment semantic-audit astis-rt-20260929-picardcentermoment companion:sphmc-d7-two-layer-moment-propagation · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.picardcentermoment.picard_center_gradient_moment. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder attributed expanded proof component, not the full equation d.7 or lemma d.4. work in the paper's normalized euclidean setting: v is c2, kappa>=1, kappa^(-1)i<=hess v<=i, 0<eta<=c<1, eps>0, and xstar is a minimizer. for one algorithm 3.1 phase, let x be the current position and p0 the refreshed momentum. samplinglib freezes their required input as the explicit combined bound e[||x-xstar||^2+||p0||^2]<=m with integrability; deriving this m from the paper's run-wide state estimate and refresh remains a separate adapter. for nodes satisfying |t_i|<=1, the first picard centers are y0_i=x+t_i p0. measurable innovations are here abstracted by the only facts used in this calculation, integrable e||g_j||^2<=d; their actual standard-gaussian joint law remains separate. approximate proximal nonexpansiveness, the proximal error and one-smoothness control z0_j=gradient v(q(y0_j)+sqrt(eta)g_j). for finite weights with sum_j |omega_ij|<=s, the second centers are y1_i=y0_i-sum_j omega_ij z0_j. samplinglib formalizes this conditional propagation with explicit sufficient constants: e||gradient v(y0_i)||^2<=2m; with b=6m+3 eps^2+3 eta d, e||z0_j||^2<=b; and e||gradient v(y1_i)||^2<=4m+2 s^2 b. it constructs the actual stopped approximate-proximal output and exposes measurability and integrability. the repeated algorithm 3.1 law, run-wide state estimate, momentum-refresh adapter, actual gaussian/joint law, chebyshev-lobatto node and weight instantiation, parameter substitutions yielding c kappa d lq^18, d.8 and theorem 5.1 remain separate. let e be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space with its borel measurable structure, let (omega,mu) be a probability space, and let iota be a finite type of nodes. let v:e->r be twice continuously frechet differentiable and let kappa>=1 satisfy (1/kappa)||v||^2 <= d^2v(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for every x,v in e. let 0<eta<=c<1 and eps>0. let x,p:omega->e be measurable, let xstar in e satisfy grad v(xstar)=0, and suppose w |-> ||x(w)-xstar||^2+||p(w)||^2 is integrable with expectation at most m. for each i in iota let t_i be real with |t_i|<=1, set y0_i=x+t_i p, and let g_j:omega->e be measurable innovations such that ||g_j||^2 is integrable with expectation at most dim_r(e) for every j. let real weights omega_ij satisfy sum_j |omega_ij|<=s for every i, and define b=6m+3eps^2+3eta dim_r(e). then there exist measurable functions p:e->e, n:e->n, and q:e->e such that, for every y in e, p(y)+eta grad v(p(y))=y, ||q(y)-p(y)||<=eps, and the finite exact-real proximalquery run on y with fuel n(y)+1 returns some(q(y),n(y)+1), where the recorded natural number counts all gradient tests including the successful one. define z0_j=grad v(q(y0_j)+sqrt(eta)g_j) and y1_i=y0_i-sum_j omega_ij z0_j, pointwise on omega. then, for every applicable node index, each of ||grad v(y0_i)||^2, ||z0_j||^2, and ||grad v(y1_i)||^2 is integrable, and their expectations satisfy e_mu||grad v(y0_i)||^2<=2m, e_mu||z0_j||^2<=b, and e_mu||grad v(y1_i)||^2<=4m+2s^2b. source-reviewed appendix d.2, proof of lemma d.4 equation d.7, html lines 2177–2181; algorithm 3.1 lines 282–307 autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.picardcentermoment.picard_center_gradient_moment autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/picardcentermoment.lean true root blind_picard_center_decoder 4fb23c58198b49cf9dbf14e6e35c458b7aaaa6481e192e487882e557e29ff552 accepted analytic_picard_source_reviewer objects position x, refreshed momentum p0, first centers y0_i=x+t_i p0, approximate proximal output q, innovations g_j, queries z0_j=gradient v(q