a vacuous-edge technical premise for an empty node type. conclusion with b=6m+3eps^2+3eta d, the three squared-gradient fields are integrable and bounded by 2m, b and 4m+2s^2b; measurable stopped approximate-proximal outputs are constructed. exactly these integrability and numerical bounds, plus the explicit proximal identity, eps-accuracy and finite interpreter return for measurable p,n,q. explicit-elaboration the theorem conjunction and five-step lesson agree term by term; center moments remain internal dominators rather than extra public conclusions. scopes a conditional two-layer propagation component, not full d.7 or lemma d.4; repeated law, state estimate, refresh adapter, gaussian joint law, concrete nodes/weights, parameter substitution, d.8 and theorem 5.1 remain separate. only the conditional propagation and actual local proximal execution; state/noise/weight facts are premises. same the source contract, module header, publication boundary and obligation ledger all preserve these exclusions. constant dependencies the constants are 2m, b=6m+3eps^2+3eta d and 4m+2s^2b; the c kappa d lq^18 substitution remains separate. identical coefficients and dependencies, with d=finrank(e). same the embedded proof derives 2 from the first-center square bound, 6/3/3 from the three-term query estimate, and 2s^2 from weighted cauchy-schwarz, without independence. assumptions informational lean explicitly assumes m>=0 and s>=0; m is redundant and s only restricts the vacuous empty-node edge beyond the nonempty source phase. independent source review classification: explicit-elaboration; nonblocking. domains informational the euclidean gaussian phase is factored into a coordinate-free finite-dimensional space and marginal innovation moments; the actual gaussian joint law remains a visible separate obligation. independent source review classification: explicit-elaboration; nonblocking. quantifiers informational lean exposes globally measurable proximal/stopping witnesses and t