      "original_theorem": "Algorithm 3.1 draws a fresh standard Gaussian Z independently of the incoming phase state (X,Pinit) and forms P0=exp(-h/2)Pinit+sqrt(1-exp(-h))Z. For h>=0 and any incoming probability law with integrable combined squared state bounded by M, the refreshed combined moment equals the incoming position plus exp(-h) times incoming momentum moment, plus (1-exp(-h))d, and is at most M+(1-exp(-h))d. This is only the first half-refresh; the repeated history and D.7 remain separate.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space equipped with its Borel σ-algebra, let ν be a probability measure on E × E, let x⋆ ∈ E, let h ∈ ℝ satisfy h ≥ 0, and let M ∈ ℝ. Assume the incoming energy (x,p) ↦ ‖x − x⋆‖² + ‖p‖² is ν-integrable and\n∫_{E×E} (‖x − x⋆‖² + ‖p‖²) dν(x,p) ≤ M.\nLet γ_E = stdGaussian(E), set μ = ν ⊗ γ_E, and for ((x,p),z) ∈ (E × E) × E define\nX((x,p),z) = x,  P₀((x,p),z) = e^(−h/2)p + √(1 − e^(−h)) z.\nThen X and P₀ are measurable, the function ((x,p),z) ↦ ‖X((x,p),z) − x⋆‖² + ‖P₀((x,p),z)‖² is μ-integrable, and\n∫_{(E×E)×E} (‖X((x,p),z) − x⋆‖² + ‖P₀((x,p),z)‖²) dμ((x,p),z)\n= ∫_{E×E} (‖x − x⋆‖² + e^(−h)‖p‖²) dν(x,p) + (1 − e^(−h)) finrank_ℝ(E)\n≤ M + (1 − e^(−h)) finrank_ℝ(E).",
