      "original_theorem": "Faithful scoped paraphrase: the paper defines Pi_eta=pi_eta tensor N(0,I) and uses its stationary-reference position and momentum moments in the Lemma D.4 argument following equation (D.3). This bounded prerequisite constructs the actual product probability law from a Gaussian-smoothed base and independent standard momentum, proves coordinate integrability and exact coordinate moments, and bounds total phase energy by M+(sigma^2+1)d when the base position moment is at most M. The paper convention is sigma=sqrt eta for eta nonnegative. It does not establish stationarity, invariance, contraction, equation (D.3), the history supremum, (D.7), or (D.8).",
