      "original_theorem": "ASTIS mathematical statement (not a quotation): a finite squared Wasserstein radius transfers the second moment of any Lipschitz observable, with the explicit estimate E_mu ||g||^2 <= 2 E_nu ||g||^2 + 2 b^2 r^2.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any normed additive group with a second-countable topology and its Borel measurable structure, let F be any normed additive group, and let mu and nu be any measures on E. Let g : E → F, let b be a nonnegative real number, and let r be any real number. Assume that g is Lipschitz with constant b, that x ↦ ‖g(x)‖² is integrable with respect to nu, and that W₂(mu,nu)² ≤ ENNReal.ofReal(r²), where W₂ is the extended nonnegative quadratic Wasserstein distance defined as the square root of the infimum of quadratic coupling costs. Then x ↦ ‖g(x)‖² is integrable with respect to mu, and ∫ ‖g(x)‖² dmu(x) ≤ 2 ∫ ‖g(x)‖² dnu(x) + 2 b² r².",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
