      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261002-SPHMCInitialGibbsQ2",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261002-SPHMCInitialGibbsQ2",
      "status": "fidelity-mismatch",
      "subtitle": "arxiv:2609.06906v1:lemma-4.16-q2-gibbs-initialization-edge · lean-strengthened-assumptions",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.InitialGibbsPhaseTransport.initial_gibbs_phase_transport_q2.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "",
      "original_theorem": "Faithful scoped paraphrase of Chen–Chewi–Lu–Zhang, arXiv:2609.06906v1, Lemma 4.16 proof: under normalized Hessian bounds alpha I <= Hessian U <= I, an admissible reference point satisfies squared gradient norm at most alpha times dimension. The proof selects a critical minimizer p, obtains its reference-point distance from strong monotonicity, bounds the Gibbs position second moment, adds independent Gaussian smoothing of variance eta <= 1, and couples the two phase momenta identically. For q=2, these steps give squared M_kappa transport cost at most 5 kappa d when kappa=1/alpha. This ASTIS component supplies p explicitly and does not prove its existence or the source lemma for every q>=2.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product Borel space, U:E→ℝ be C², and alpha,eta be nonnegative reals with 0<alpha<=1 and eta<=1. Assume alpha‖v‖² <= D²U(x)[v,v] <= ‖v‖² for every x,v. Given p and xref with gradient U(p)=0 and ‖gradient U(xref)‖² <= alpha dim_R E, set μ=volume.tilted(-U) and piEta=gaussianSmoothing μ (sqrt eta). Then the squared phase quadratic Kantorovich infimum at parameter 1/alpha between (dirac xref)⊗standardGaussian and piEta⊗standardGaussian is at most ENNReal.ofReal(5 dim_R E/alpha). The theorem assumes p and xref; it does not establish their existence. Eta=0 is permitted. The constant is exactly 5 dim_R E/alpha and has no further eta or U dependence.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "lean-strengthened-assumptions",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
