      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261002-sphmcinitialgibbsq2 semantic-audit astis-rt-20261002-sphmcinitialgibbsq2 arxiv:2609.06906v1:lemma-4.16-q2-gibbs-initialization-edge · lean-strengthened-assumptions blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.initialgibbsphasetransport.initial_gibbs_phase_transport_q2. lean-strengthened-assumptions source hidden from decoder faithful scoped paraphrase of chen–chewi–lu–zhang, arxiv:2609.06906v1, lemma 4.16 proof: under normalized hessian bounds alpha i <= hessian u <= i, an admissible reference point satisfies squared gradient norm at most alpha times dimension. the proof selects a critical minimizer p, obtains its reference-point distance from strong monotonicity, bounds the gibbs position second moment, adds independent gaussian smoothing of variance eta <= 1, and couples the two phase momenta identically. for q=2, these steps give squared m_kappa transport cost at most 5 kappa d when kappa=1/alpha. this astis component supplies p explicitly and does not prove its existence or the source lemma for every q>=2. let e be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product borel space, u:e→ℝ be c², and alpha,eta be nonnegative reals with 0<alpha<=1 and eta<=1. assume alpha‖v‖² <= d²u(x)[v,v] <= ‖v‖² for every x,v. given p and xref with gradient u(p)=0 and ‖gradient u(xref)‖² <= alpha dim_r e, set μ=volume.tilted(-u) and pieta=gaussiansmoothing μ (sqrt eta). then the squared phase quadratic kantorovich infimum at parameter 1/alpha between (dirac xref)⊗standardgaussian and pieta⊗standardgaussian is at most ennreal.ofreal(5 dim_r e/alpha). the theorem assumes p and xref; it does not establish their existence. eta=0 is permitted. the constant is exactly 5 dim_r e/alpha and has no further eta or u dependence. source-reviewed lemma 4.16 proof, pdf p.22 autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.initialgibbsphasetransport.initial_gibbs_phase_transport_q2 auto