      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CanonicalLogSobolev.finite_klDiv_and_toReal_le_half_mul_information.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://chewisinho.github.io/main.pdf",
      "original_theorem": "Chewi Definition 1.2.25 gives Ent_pi(rho) <= (C/2) E_pi(rho, log rho). Specializing to the canonical Radon--Nikodym density rho=dmu/dpi and identifying the Dirichlet form with relative Fisher information yields finite KL(mu||pi) and KL(mu||pi) <= (C/2) FI(mu||pi), provided the density, entropy, generator-domain, score and integration-by-parts hypotheses are genuine. For Lee--Shen--Tian curvature rate lambda, C=lambda^{-1}. No Bakry--Emery, Talagrand T2 or Wasserstein statement is included.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let iota be finite and let State be its real Euclidean space. Let mu be a probability measure and pi a reference measure, with mu sigma-finite and with the Radon--Nikodym/Lebesgue-decomposition interface. Let L be a real-linear generator and C a real constant. Assume pi satisfies the density-form generator log-Sobolev inequality with multiplier C. Assume the canonical density rho=dmu/dpi is admissible for that LSI, the canonical log-density has an almost-everywhere differentiable score of finite squared integral under mu, the density/log-density pair lies in the required generator integration-by-parts domain, and the carre-du-champ equals rho times the squared score almost everywhere. Then the ENNReal Kullback--Leibler divergence klDiv(mu||pi) is not infinity and its real value is at most (C/2) times the canonical relative Fisher information. The statement does not assert that any concrete pi satisfies LSI or any transport inequality.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
