          "original": "A finite-dimensional Euclidean probability setting in which the density, entropy, generator-domain, score, and integration-by-parts expressions are genuine.",
          "reconstructed": "The theorem quantifies over EuclideanSpace real iota with finite iota; mu is a probability and sigma-finite, pi is a probability through hLSI, and Lebesgue decomposition, density admissibility, smooth finite score, Dirichlet-pair domain, and Fisher-gamma identification are explicit.",
          "relation": "explicit-elaboration",
          "evidence": "Every analytic domain named in the source packet is represented by a hypothesis in the displayed Lean signature; the full proof uses those hypotheses rather than totalized expressions alone."
        },
        {
          "slot": "quantifiers",
          "original": "For every canonical density specialization satisfying the stated LSI and genuine analytic side conditions.",
