          "original": "The final event discrepancy after shared continuation is at most the ideal-history expected local error.",
          "reconstructed": "For every measurable t, the absolute real-event difference between ((S composed with K) applied to mu) and ((S composed with L) applied to mu) is at most integral epsilon dmu.",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "hKL bounds the intermediate laws; KernelTotalVariation.abs_real_comp_sub_le applies common-kernel contraction; Measure.comp_assoc gives the displayed composition order. This is the correct first-K-or-L-then-S order."
        },
        {
          "slot": "scopes",
          "original": "The common-continuation component only; a separate construction establishes that actual adaptive histories admit this representation.",
          "reconstructed": "A generic common-suffix theorem bound only to common-adaptive-suffix, without constructing histories or asserting a complete capped-algorithm comparison.",
          "relation": "same",
          "evidence": "The source contract, lesson and binding agree on this boundary. Neither the complete module nor this declaration constructs dummy histories, identifies delta_t, performs the cap comparison, or derives complexity. The broader publication target remains conditional on those separate obligations."
        },
        {
          "slot": "constant dependencies",
