an theorem's probability, markov, integrability and almost-everywhere assumptions, plus ismarkovkernel s. explicit-elaboration the theorem calls the mean result with exactly mu,k,l,epsilon and hbound, then uses s without altering it between branches. constructing this common continuation from an adaptive algorithm is not derived from these assumptions. conclusion the final event discrepancy after shared continuation is at most the ideal-history expected local error. for every measurable t, the absolute real-event difference between ((s composed with k) applied to mu) and ((s composed with l) applied to mu) is at most integral epsilon dmu. equivalent hkl bounds the intermediate laws; kerneltotalvariation.abs_real_comp_sub_le applies common-kernel contraction; measure.comp_assoc gives the displayed composition order. this is the correct first-k-or-l-then-s order. scopes the common-continuation component only; a separate construction establishes that actual adaptive histories admit this representation. a generic common-suffix theorem bound only to common-adaptive-suffix, without constructing histories or asserting a complete capped-algorithm comparison. same the source contract, lesson and binding agree on this boundary. neither the complete module nor this declaration constructs dummy histories, identifies delta_t, performs the cap comparison, or derives complexity. the broader publication target remains conditional on those separate obligations. constant dependencies data processing adds no factor and leaves the original expected local budget unchanged. the bound remains exactly integral epsilon dmu, independently of s and the sizes of the state spaces. same the composed intermediate measures are both probabilities, so the eventwise total-variation convention has factor-one markov contraction. the proof forwards hkl unchanged; associativity introduces neither a factor two nor an additional error term. scopes informational the informal shared adaptive continuation becomes an explicit single markov kernel s. constructing that kernel on a sufficiently rich retained-history state remains a separate source adapter, as the packet expressly states. independent source review classification: explicit-elaboration; nonblocking. conclusion informational this component preserves a supplied conditional eventwise budget; it neither identifies the paper's delta_t nor certifies the full dummy-history, cap or complexity argument. independent source review classification: scope-clarification; nonblocking.",
