      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every pair of real sequences a, delta : N -> R and every natural number n, if |a(i+1) - a(i)| <= delta(i) for every natural number i with i < n, then |a(n) - a(0)| <= sum_(i=0)^(n-1) delta(i). The sum is finite and ranges over precisely the indices 0 through n-1; for n = 0 it is the empty sum 0 and the conclusion is 0 <= 0. No condition is imposed on delta outside this index range, and no separate nonnegativity assumption is required.",
