      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.06906v1",
      "original_theorem": "Faithful scoped paraphrase of Chen–Chewi–Lu–Zhang, arXiv:2609.06906v1, Lemma 4.16 proof, PDF p.22: under 0<alpha<=1 and normalized C2 Hessian bounds alpha I <= Hessian U <= I, an admissible reference point has squared gradient norm at most alpha times dimension. The proof internally chooses a minimizer x-star. Combining that existence step with the previously verified q=2 Gibbs moment, Gaussian smoothing, and identical-momentum coupling gives squared M_kappa transport cost at most 5 kappa d for kappa=1/alpha. This is only the q=2 component; the source all-q concentration claim remains open.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional complete real inner-product Borel space E, every potential U : E -> R, every alpha and eta in NNReal, and every reference point xref in E, assume 0 < alpha <= 1, eta <= 1, U is C^2, alpha * ||v||^2 <= D^2 U(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for every x,v in E, and ||gradient U(xref)||^2 <= alpha * finrank_R(E). Let mu be the normalized exponential tilt of volume by -U (when its normalizing integral is finite), and let piEta be the Gaussian smoothing of mu with standard deviation sqrt(eta). Then phaseWassersteinSq at parameter 1/alpha between (dirac xref) product (standard Gaussian on E) and piEta product (standard Gaussian on E) is at most ENNReal.ofReal(5 * (1/alpha) * finrank_R(E)).",
