      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every finite-dimensional real inner-product space E, every function V : E -> R, and every real m > 0, if V is Frechet differentiable on all of E and m-strongly convex on all of E, then there exists p in E such that V(p) <= V(x) for every x in E and the real inner-product gradient of V at p is zero.",
