      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.03106v4",
      "original_theorem": "ASTIS supporting expansion for Lee--Shen--Tian Lemma 2, used by SPHMC Lemma 4.17: when two normalized restricted-Gaussian fibers are written as exponential tilts of a common base, their relative entropy is the integral under the left fiber of the explicit normalized log-density ratio, provided that representative is integrable. This is the value-level KL-to-explicit-ratio step before the source differentiates its smooth ratio; it does not itself assert ratio integrability, a score identity, LSI, Fisher, T2, or W2 contraction.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let X be a measurable space, let mu be a nonzero sigma-finite measure on X, and let f,g : X -> R. Assume that f is measurable, x |-> exp(f(x)) and x |-> exp(g(x)) are mu-integrable, and r : X -> R defined by r(x) = f(x) - log(integral_X exp(f) dmu) - g(x) + log(integral_X exp(g) dmu) is integrable with respect to mu.tilted f. Then klDiv(mu.tilted f, mu.tilted g) != infinity, and toReal(klDiv(mu.tilted f, mu.tilted g)) = integral_X r d(mu.tilted f).",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
