lue equals the left-tilt integral of the displayed ratio. explicit-elaboration the separate ennreal finiteness certificate makes the real-valued equality faithful and prevents toreal from masking infinite kl. scopes only the value-level kl-to-explicit-ratio step; no assertion of ratio integrability, score identity, lsi, fisher information, t2, or w2 contraction. only probability normalization, absolute continuity, value-level a.e. representative transfer, kl finiteness, and the integral identity. same the module contains no differentiability, gradient, lsi, fisher, transport, or contraction conclusion, and the candidate exposition explicitly preserves this boundary. constant dependencies the representative depends on f, g, their common base, and the normalizers z_f and z_g. the representative uses integral exp(f) dmu and integral exp(g) dmu, with both tilted measures and kl determined by the same mu, f, and g. same no extra parameter or source-independent constant is introduced; the displayed signs and normalizer dependencies agree. domains informational lean proves the bridge for arbitrary normalized exponential tilts over a nonzero sigma-finite base rather than only restricted-gaussian fibers. independent source review classification: domain-generalization; nonblocking.",
