      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261005-chebyshevlobattomomentum semantic-audit astis-rt-20261005-chebyshevlobattomomentum companion:sphmc-chebyshev-lobatto-momentum-norm · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.chebyshevlobattomomentum.momentum_absolute_sum_le. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder faithful scoped source restatement: j is a natural number>=2 and h is a positive real. fin j uses indices i=0,...,j-1 corresponding to source j=i+1. t_i=h/2[1-cos(i*pi/(j-1))]; ell_j is the real mathlib lagrange cardinal polynomial at those nodes; lambda is the actual supremum of sum_j|ell_j(s)| on the compact interval[0,h]; b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s) ds using real lebesgue measure. for these actual source nodes and integral coefficients, sum_j |b_j| <= h*lambda. the finite compact supremum and every needed interval integrability are derived from polynomial continuity. no b_j>=0 or supplied coefficient envelope is assumed. derived absolute-integral prerequisite for appendix d1/d2 using the actual b1 coefficients. this does not prove individual clenshaw-curtis weight nonnegativity, logarithmic lambda, complete b1, interpolation remainder b2 or either main theorem. for every natural j>=2 and every real h>0, index nodes by fin(j)={0,...,j-1} and define t_i=(h/2)(1-cos((i/(j-1))pi)), ell_j(x)=product_{k in fin(j),k!=j} ((t_j-t_k)^(-1))(x-t_k), lambda=sup_{s in [0,h]} sum_{j in fin(j)} |ell_j(s)|. the quotient in the node definition uses real coercions, so its denominator is the real number j-1. the ell_j are real lagrange basis polynomials evaluated at real arguments, and lambda is the real supremum of the indicated interval image. then sum_{j in fin(j)} |integral_0^h ell_j(s) ds| <= h lambda. the integrals use real lebesgue measure with oriented endpoints; h>0 makes the interval order increasing. the absolute value is applied separately to each integral, followed by a finite sum. this theorem asserts precisely this total absolute integrated-weight bound, without adding signed normalization, individual positivity, an upper growth bound on lambda, or quadrature exactness conclusions. accepted d1/d2 html2099-2124; source algorithm3.1, b1 actual coefficient definitions1684-1713; proximal nonexpansiveness lemma4.2(4.4) autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.chebyshevlobattomomentum.momentum_absolute_sum_le autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/chebyshevlobattomomentum.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261005 e30ea003dec64441a8bc20ff89a6af54e68cc78ad474a8d185786a50aecba9c5 accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual source nodes,lagrange polynomials,lambda supremum,momentum integrals. identical product polynomials and actual integrated weights. explicit-elaboration no free envelope; finj i maps sourcej=i+1. domains j>=2,h>0,real lebesgue oriented0h integral. same domain and exactlyj indices. explicit-elaboration polynomial continuity yields finite compact-supremum image and interval integrability. quantifiers everyj,h as above, fixed constructed arrays. same universal parameters and finite sum. explicit-elaboration no positivity quantified as premise. assumptions j>=2,h>0 only; actual coefficient definitions. same; no supplied lambda/weight bound. explicit-elaboration current proof derives continuous absolute sum,f-image bounded above and pointwise le_cssup; finite integration hypotheses explicit. conclusion sum|integral ell_j|<=hlambda. exact absolute-integral sum bound. explicit-elaboration norm-integral inequality, derived interval integrability, finite-sum integration, monotone integral off<=lambda,constant integralhlambda. scopes derived absolute-integral prerequisite ford.1 comparison,not completeb.1. same; no signed normalization,positivity,loglambda,b.2/main. explicit-elaboration binding role prerequisite. this substitutes a proved absolute budget in comparison but does no