      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261005-monotoneproximalmap semantic-audit astis-rt-20261005-monotoneproximalmap companion:sphmc-monotone-proximal-nonexpansive · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.monotoneproximalmap.nonexpansive_of_monotone_optimality. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder faithful scoped source restatement: e is any real inner-product normed additive group; g,p:e→e, eta>=0. for every x,y, inner(g(x)-g(y),x-y)>=0, and for every y, p(y)+eta*g(p(y))=y. no differentiability, probability, finite dimension, existence or measurability is assumed or concluded by this abstract leaf. the given exact optimality solution p is 1-lipschitz. this abstract implication is extracted verbatim from the existing private proof and is consumed by both the existing input-estimator theorem and the actual proximal-phase comparison. it carries no new mathematical-completion credit. shared abstract prerequisite for source proximal nonexpansiveness; not an existence, algorithm, stochastic estimator or paper theorem. actual paper consumers derive monotonicity and construct p themselves. for every real inner-product space e with its normed additive-group structure, any functions g,p:e->e and any real eta>=0, suppose that g is monotone in the precise sense <g(x)-g(y),x-y> >= 0 for every x,y in e, and that p(y)+eta g(p(y))=y for every y in e. then p is nonexpansive: for every u,v in e, ||p(u)-p(v)|| <= ||u-v||. the conclusion is lipschitzwith 1 p in the norm-induced metric on e. the theorem assumes that a global p satisfying the equation has been supplied; it does not assert existence of such a p. it imposes no completeness, finite-dimensionality, measurable-space, smoothness, gradient, strong-monotonicity, or strictly positive eta requirement. accepted d1/d2 html2099-2124; source algorithm3.1, b1 actual coefficient definitions1684-1713; proximal nonexpansiveness lemma4.2(4.4) autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.monotoneproximalmap.nonexpansive_of_monotone_optimality autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/monotoneproximalmap.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261005 90f7d486ec43de3b1219e3b57b09df85c15777bc9c3fcf918f538be3748de50a accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects supplied g,p and exact monotone optimality solution. same g,p equation and monotonicity. explicit-elaboration no gradient or proximal existence silently supplied; all hypotheses explicit. domains any real inner-product normed additive group e,eta>=0. same domain, without completeness/finite dimension/measurability. explicit-elaboration abstract shared implication valid even eta=0 and dimension0. quantifiers for every supplied g,p,eta with global two-point monotonicity and global equation. same quantifiers, output nonexpansiveness for every input pair. explicit-elaboration given global p is premise, never existence conclusion. assumptions eta>=0,monotonicity,genuine supplied equation. all three retained. explicit-elaboration shared proof forms exact difference and nonnegative monotone term; no strong convexity or eta>0 needed. conclusion p is1-lipschitz. exact lipschitzwith1 in induced metric. explicit-elaboration pair difference with p-displacement; cauchy-schwarz; zero-norm case separate, positive-norm cancellation valid. scopes extracted existing abstract prerequisite, no mathematical completion credit. same explicit prerequisite without algorithm/oracle/probability results. explicit-elaboration binding role prerequisite; lesson scope identifies only source nonexpansiveness mechanism. generic boilerplate as-applicable does not introduce unused probability/phase claims. constant dependencies exactly1,eta nonnegative. exactly1, independent of dimension/regularity. explicit-elaboration no inversion by eta; positive displacement only when nonzero.",
