      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A4.SS2",
      "original_theorem": "E is an arbitrary real normed vector space; g, parameters, supplied finite nodes/weights and fuel are arbitrary. The input contains one state pair, two refresh noises and two Fin-m noise arrays; no probability or success assumption.\nFor arbitrary real normed E, gradient oracle g, eta,eps,h, Fin m nodes and weights, input w and fuel:E->Nat, phaseQuery returns Option((E*E)*Nat). It first refreshes P0 and builds Y0. It sequentially executes every proximalQuery at Y0_i from Y0_i using fuel(Y0_i), and if successful evaluates g at returned point plus sqrt(eta)G0_i and adds one query to that returned count. It builds Y1 from these actual returned gradients, sequentially executes every second proximal/noisy-gradient call similarly using G1, then returns the complete phase output and the sum of both arrays actual counts. Any failed call returns none, with no successful cost certificate.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "This packet supplies a function definition, rather than a theorem proposition. For any real normed vector space E, natural m, arbitrary g:E->E, eta,epsilon,h in R, arrays t,b,d:Fin(m)->R and omega:Fin(m) x Fin(m)->R, fuel:E->N, and input w=((X,P),((zeta0,zeta1),(G0,G1))), the defined function returns an element of Option((E x E) x N). The input vectors belong to E and G0,G1:Fin(m)->E; b,d denote positionWeight,momentumWeight.\nSet a=exp(-h/2), sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)), P0=a P+sigma zeta0 and Y0_i=X+t_i P0. In increasing Fin(m) order, collect calls run(g,eta,epsilon,Y0_i,fuel(Y0_i),Y0_i), mapping each success (x0_i,k0_i) to (Z0_i,k0_i+1) with Z0_i=g(x0_i+sqrt(eta)G0_i). Any failure propagates none. A successful collection returns the array Z0 and Q0=sum_i(k0_i+1). Set Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j. Similarly collect run(g,eta,epsilon,Y1_i,fuel(Y1_i),Y1_i), mapping each success (x1_i,k1_i) to (Z1_i,k1_i+1) with Z1_i=g(x1_i+sqrt(eta)G1_i). Failure propagates none. A successful second collection returns Z1 and Q1=sum_i(k1_i+1). Return\n  some((X+h P0-sum_j b_j Z1_j,\n        a(P0-sum_j d_j Z1_j)+sigma zeta1),Q0+Q1).\nThe finite exact-real interpreter returns none at zero fuel. At positive fuel it evaluates g(x), sets next=y-eta g(x), and returns (x,1) when ||next-x||<=(1-eta)epsilon. Otherwise it recurses from next with one less fuel and adds one to a successful returned count. collectQueries on zero nodes returns an empty array and count zero; on m+1 nodes it executes the first call, then the recursively collected tail, adding counts and propagating failure.\nAll sums use all m actual nodes. On success the returned count equals 2m+sum_i(k0_i+k1_i), counting all interpreter evaluations including terminal tests and one additional shifted-point g evaluation per node in each stage. This is an exact-real operational definition with arbitrary supplied vectors, without positivity, regularity, probability-law, sufficient-fuel, measurability, complexity-bound or successful-termination assumptions or conclusions. For m=0 both collections succeed empty with total count zero.",
