ity consumer is supplied. the source h producer from positive momentum weights remains a separate obligation. conclusion a_h^t m_kappa+m_kappa a_h <= -(1/(8kappa))m_kappa, source(4.15), obtained from each source(4.14) block. q_kappa(x,p)/(8kappa)<=<x,hx>+2<p,hx>-(1/kappa)<x,p>+||p||^2 for all x,p. equivalent the rhs is d_h=-2<m_kappa z,a_h z>_sum. the matrix lhs quadratic form is +2<m_kappa z,a_h z>_sum=-d_h. q has one <x,p> cross term and off-diagonal coefficients1/2. multiplying the public inequality by -1 gives the source full matrix quadratic order. scopes scoped drift component(4.14)-(4.15) within proposition4.7; lemma4.6, the remainder and step absorption are needed separately for kernel contraction. deterministic full-space pointwise dissipation only; no dynamics or kernel theorem. explicit-elaboration source html556-589 constructs the actual h using positive weights and bounds the remainder; html613-620 applies those facts to contraction. module heading, lesson sources/statement and assumption differences retain that boundary. k/khat/kbar contraction, invariance, positivity/loglambda, repeated-phase/main and unrelated run-wide guarantees receive no admission. constant dependencies lower spectral alpha=1/(2kappa), alpha<=1/2, d_lambda>=alpha/2*(u^2+v^2), m^(2)<=2i, yielding1/(8kappa). identical lower bound and exact factor1/(8kappa), independent of dimension, h beyond its prescribed bounds, and x,p. same scalar helper derives lambda-(lambda-alpha)^2>=alpha, shifted determinant>=0, completes the square and proves q<=2(u^2+v^2). summation introduces no factor of finrank. public field identities alpha/4=1/(8kappa),2alpha=1/kappa preserve the exact source constant.",
