          "evidence": "Independently checked private phase_displacement_le: S=h^2Lambda/2, B=hLambda; first-gradient error<=delta, first-node error<=Sdelta, second-gradient error<=(1+S)delta. Position<=S(1+S)delta, momentum<=aB(1+S)delta. Lambda>=1 and h^2Lambda<=1 imply h<=1,S<=1/2,S<=B/2; a<=1. Therefore Euclidean norm<=sum of coordinate norms<=(S+aB)(1+S)delta<=9Bdelta/4<=3Bdelta. Source momentum positivity would give a sharper intermediate estimate; this independently derived absolute-integral route proves the same universal final D.2 conclusion without an added premise."
