    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261005-SPHMCSourceQuadratureWork",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261005-SPHMCSourceQuadratureWork",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-source-quadrature-work · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.SourceQuadratureWork.source_quadrature_phase_work.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#A2.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "E is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with Borel sigma-algebra; the source node count is natural J>=2 and index Fin J.\nV is C2, kappa>=1, and kappa^(-1)||v||^2 <= D2V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2 for all x,v. Its actual gradient vanishes at the supplied xstar.\n0<eta<=c<1, eps>0, 0<h<=1 and M>=0. The incoming probability law nu on(X,P) has integrable ||X-xstar||^2+||P||^2 with mean<=M. No source node, coefficient, Lambda or row-budget hypothesis.\nUsing exactly the source t,ell,Lambda,omega,b arrays above, set positionWeight_j=omega_{J-1,j} (the final node is h), momentumWeight_j=b_j and S=h^2 Lambda/2. Under mu=nu product ((Gaussian product Gaussian) product (Gaussian Fin-J array product Gaussian Fin-J array)), set d=finrank(E), a=exp(-h/2), sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)), MR=M+(1-exp(-h))*d, B=6MR+3eps^2+3eta*d, C=2+(1+log((1-c)^(-1)))/(-log c), L0=C[1+log(1+sqrt(2MR)/eps)], L1=C[1+log(1+sqrt(4MR+2S^2B)/eps)]. There exist measurable p,q,N with exact proximal equation, ||q(y)-p(y)||<=eps and successful proximalQuery from y with fuel N(y)+1 returning (q(y),N(y)+1) for every y. P0=aP+sigma zeta0, Y0_i=X+t_i P0, Z0_j=grad V(q(Y0_j)+sqrt(eta)G0_j), Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j, Z1_j=grad V(q(Y1_j)+sqrt(eta)G1_j), Phi=(X+hP0-sum_j positionWeight_j Z1_j, a(P0-sum_j momentumWeight_j Z1_j)+sigma zeta1). The same Phi is measurable and defines the Gaussian pushforward Markov kernel. The count T=2*J+sum_i[(N(Y0_i)+1)+(N(Y1_i)+1)] is measurable. For every driving input w, phaseQuery with fuel(y)=N(y)+1 returns exactly some(Phi(w),T(w)); the real cast of T is integrable under mu and E_mu T<=J*(2+L0+L1). The node range and row budget needed by the compiled producer are derived from the coefficient certificate; the Fin J cardinal count is exactly J.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space equipped with its Borel measurable structure, and let J be any natural number with J>=2. Let V:E->R be C^2 and let kappa be a nonnegative real with 1<=kappa. Suppose, for every x,v in E,\n  kappa^(-1)||v||^2 <= D^2 V(x)[v,v] <= ||v||^2.\nLet eta,c,epsilon be real with 0<eta<=c<1 and epsilon>0. Let nu be a probability measure on E x E, and let xstar in E satisfy grad V(xstar)=0. Fix real h,M with 0<h<=1 and M>=0. Assume (X,P)->||X-xstar||^2+||P||^2 is Bochner integrable under nu with integral at most M.\nFor i,j in Fin(J)={0,...,J-1}, define exactly\n  t_i=(h/2)(1-cos((i/(J-1))pi)),\n  ell_j(X)=product_{k in Fin(J), k!=j} (X-t_k)/(t_j-t_k),\n  Lambda=sup_{s in [0,h]} sum_j |ell_j(s)|,\n  omega_ij=integral_0^{t_i} (t_i-s)ell_j(s) ds,\n  b_j=omega_{J-1,j},\n  d_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s) ds,\n  S=(h^2/2)Lambda.\nHere i,J are cast to reals in the quotient, ell denotes the real Lagrange polynomial product using inverse denominators, b denotes positionWeight and d momentumWeight; the supremum is the conditionally complete real supremum and integrals are oriented Lebesgue interval integrals. These arrays and S are fixed by J,h, rather than supplied freely.\nPut D=dim_R E, a=exp(-h/2), sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)). Let G be the centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability law on E, gi=product_{Fin(J)} G, gamma=(G x G) x (gi x gi), and mu=nu x gamma. Thus an incoming state of law nu is independent of all noise coordinates; the two Gaussian vectors and two finite Gaussian arrays are mutually independent, with independent coordinates within each array. Define the exact constants\n  MR=M+(1-exp(-h))D,\n  B=6 MR+3 epsilon^2+3 eta D,\n  C=2+(1+log((1-c)^(-1)))/(-log c),\n  L0=C[1+log(1+sqrt(2 MR)/epsilon)],\n  L1=C[1+log(1+sqrt(4 MR+2 S^2 B)/epsilon)].\nThen there exist single global measurable functions p,q:E->E and N:E->N such that for every y in E,\n  p(y)+eta grad V(p(y))=y,\n  ||q(y)-p(y)||<=epsilon,\n  proximalQuery(grad V,eta,epsilon,y,N(y)+1,y)=some(q(y),N(y)+1).\nThe approved definition identifies proximalQuery with run. This exact-real recursive interpreter returns none at zero fuel. With positive fuel it evaluates g(x), sets next=y-eta g(x), returns (x,1) if ||next-x||<=(1-eta)epsilon, and otherwise recurses from next with one less fuel, adding one to a successful returned count. Counts include the final successful test.\nFor these witnesses and full input w=((X,P),((zeta0,zeta1),(G0,G1))) in (E x E) x ((E x E) x ((Fin(J)->E) x (Fin(J)->E))), define\n  P0(w)=a P+sigma zeta0,\n  Y0_i(w)=X+t_i P0(w),\n  Z0_j(w)=grad V(q(Y0_j(w))+sqrt(eta)G0_j),\n  Y1_i(w)=Y0_i(w)-sum_j omega_ij Z0_j(w),\n  Z1_j(w)=grad V(q(Y1_j(w))+sqrt(eta)G1_j),\n  Phi(w)=(X+h P0(w)-sum_j b_j Z1_j(w),\n          a(P0(w)-sum_j d_j Z1_j(w))+sigma zeta1),\n  T(w)=2J+sum_i[(N(Y0_i(w))+1)+(N(Y1_i(w))+1)] in N.\nBoth Phi and T are measurable. There exists a Markov kernel K from E x E to E x E satisfying, for every incoming state s,\n  K(s)=(z -> Phi(s,z))_* gamma.\nFor every full input w one also has the exact successful execution identity\n  phaseQuery(grad V,eta,epsilon,h,t,omega,b,d,(y -> N(y)+1),w)\n    =some(Phi(w),T(w)).\nHere phaseQuery is explicitly defined in the approved context: form P0,Y0; sequentially collect J calls to the same proximalQuery at Y0_i with anchor and initial iterate Y0_i and supplied fuel; map each successful returned point/count (r,k) to (g(r+sqrt(eta)G0_i),k+1). Form Y1 with that first collected array. Sequentially collect the corresponding J second-stage calls, mapping each success to (g(r+sqrt(eta)G1_i),k+1). Return the displayed two-stage final state and sum of collected counts. The collector orders the actual Fin(J) nodes, adds their counts, and propagates any failure as none. Thus T counts every interpreter gradient evaluation including terminal tests, plus one shifted-gradient evaluation per actual node in each of two stages, with overhead exactly 2J. The success identity is pointwise for every w, not only almost surely.\nFinally w->(T(w):R) is Bochner integrable under mu and\n  integral (T(w):R) dmu(w) <= (J:R)(2+L0+L1).\nAll sums use the J actual nodes. The theorem asserts these witnesses, approximation and measurability conditions, a probability transition kernel, successful counted exact-real execution with the fixed coefficient arrays, and the displayed expected count bound. It does not assert an invariant law, sampler convergence, final-state moment bound, numerical bias, machine-precision behavior, a quantitative growth bound for Lambda, or elapsed-time complexity.",
