lobal measurable functions p,q:e->e and n:e->n such that for every y in e, p(y)+eta grad v(p(y))=y, ||q(y)-p(y)||<=epsilon, proximalquery(grad v,eta,epsilon,y,n(y)+1,y)=some(q(y),n(y)+1). the approved definition identifies proximalquery with run. this exact-real recursive interpreter returns none at zero fuel. with positive fuel it evaluates g(x), sets next=y-eta g(x), returns (x,1) if ||next-x||<=(1-eta)epsilon, and otherwise recurses from next with one less fuel, adding one to a successful returned count. counts include the final successful test. for these witnesses and full input w=((x,p),((zeta0,zeta1),(g0,g1))) in (e x e) x ((e x e) x ((fin(j)->e) x (fin(j)->e))), define p0(w)=a p+sigma zeta0, y0_i(w)=x+t_i p0(w), z0_j(w)=grad v(q(y0_j(w))+sqrt(eta)g0_j), y1_i(w)=y0_i(w)-sum_j omega_ij z0_j(w), z1_j(w)=grad v(q(y1_j(w))+sqrt(eta)g1_j), phi(w)=(x+h p0(w)-sum_j b_j z1_j(w), a(p0(w)-sum_j d_j z1_j(w))+sigma zeta1), t(w)=2j+sum_i[(n(y0_i(w))+1)+(n(y1_i(w))+1)] in n. both phi and t are measurable. there exists a markov kernel k from e x e to e x e satisfying, for every incoming state s, k(s)=(z -> phi(s,z))_* gamma. for every full input w one also has the exact successful execution identity phasequery(grad v,eta,epsilon,h,t,omega,b,d,(y -> n(y)+1),w) =some(phi(w),t(w)). here phasequery is explicitly defined in the approved context: form p0,y0; sequentially collect j calls to the same proximalquery at y0_i with anchor and initial iterate y0_i and supplied fuel; map each successful returned point/count (r,k) to (g(r+sqrt(eta)g0_i),k+1). form y1 with that first collected array. sequentially collect the corresponding j second-stage calls, mapping each success to (g(r+sqrt(eta)g1_i),k+1). return the displayed two-stage final state and sum of collected counts. the collector orders the actual fin(j) nodes, adds their counts, and propagates any failure as none. thus t counts every interpreter gradient evaluation including terminal tests, plus one shifted-gradient evaluation per actual node in each of two stages, with overhead exactly 2j. the success identity is pointwise for every w, not only almost surely. finally w->(t(w):r) is bochner integrable under mu and integral (t(w):r) dmu(w) <= (j:r)(2+l0+l1). all sums use the j actual nodes. the theorem asserts these witnesses, approximation and measurability conditions, a probability transition kernel, successful counted exact-real execution with the fixed coefficient arrays, and the displayed expected count bound. it does not assert an invariant law, sampler convergence, final-state moment bound, numerical bias, machine-precision behavior, a quantitative growth bound for lambda, or elapsed-time complexity. source-reviewed 3.6, b1/b2 coefficient definitions and row/constant proof, html1684-1713; actual algorithm3.1 consumer autosamplingtheory.examplecases.smoothedpicardhmc.sourcequadraturework.source_quadrature_phase_work autosamplingtheory/examplecases/smoothedpicardhmc/sourcequadraturework.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261005 72e82d804674cbf58cf5f93d95be0684021274e62c8c89b99c7eaefaf244b14d accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual source nodes and coefficients feeding the counted phase, same measurable p,q,n, full gaussian law/phi/k and terminal-inclusive natural count t. blind theorem fixes arrays from j,h and reconstructs full phase output, successful program identity and actual expected count. explicit-elaboration positionweight is omega at fin indexj-1, whose node is h by coefficient certificate; momentum weights are integral0h ell_j. no free coefficient or terminal array remains. domains complete finite-dimensional real inner-product e with borel structure; sourcej>=2 indicesfinj; incoming probability state law and full gaussian driving law. same e,indices and gamma=(gxg)x(gi xgi), mu=nu xgamma. explicit-elaboration both refresh vectors and both finj gaussian arrays retained, each array with independent coordinates. source euclidean setting is r