      "original_theorem": "Exact bounded statement:\nFinite real Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; any function F:E->R, any translation p:E and a real scale s!=0.\nNo continuity, measurability of F, exponential integrability, probability or moment premise. Equality is of Mathlib totalized normalized tilted measures; probability is a separate obligation for every consumer.\nThe actual pushforward of the normalized Lebesgue Gibbs tilt under x->p+s*x is the normalized Lebesgue tilt with inverse-affine potential x->F(s^-1*(x-p)). The nonzero actual Lebesgue Jacobian cancels between partition and set numerator. This canonical identity alone makes no probability assertion.\nSource realκ>=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0<eta<=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta<=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every type E equipped with exactly the ambient structures\n  NormedAddCommGroup E, InnerProductSpace R E, FiniteDimensional R E,\n  MeasurableSpace E, BorelSpace E,\nlet volume be its actual finite-dimensional real Hilbert Lebesgue/Haar measure. There is no separate CompleteSpace E or Nontrivial E binder; zero-dimensional E is allowed. Let F:E->R be an arbitrary function, p:E an arbitrary point, and s:R an arbitrary real scalar satisfying s!=0.\nDefine the genuine affine map phi(x)=p+s scalar-multiplied x, whose inverse is psi(x)=s^(-1) scalar-multiplied (x-p). Then the exact measure equality is\n  Measure.map(phi)(volume.tilted(x -> -F(x)))\n    = volume.tilted(x -> -F(psi(x))).\nFor every measure nu, the supplied definition is\n  nu.tilted(h)=nu.withDensity(x -> ENNReal.ofReal(exp(h(x))/integral exp(h) dnu)).\nThe real Bochner integral normalization is totalized outside exponential integrability; a zero denominator gives zero density by real division by zero. The statement has no measurability, continuity, C2, exponential-integrability, positive-normalizer, curvature or moment premise on F. The only explicit nonstructural premise is s!=0, allowing both positive and negative scales. There is no probability premise on either measure and no probability conclusion. In particular the equality of these actual possibly totalized measures must not be promoted into a claim that the measures are probability laws.\nThe right-hand side is exactly the normalized tilt by -F composed with the inverse affine map, with no residual scalar Jacobian multiplier displayed. Dimension zero remains in scope, with no dimension-positive hypothesis. No parameter space, measurable selector, posterior family, kernel, gradient, second moment, covariance, score estimate or algorithm conclusion appears. The newly approved ambient context supplies the exact missing instance list, so there is no remaining definition or ambient-binder ambiguity. No CompleteSpace premise or hypotheses of another declaration are inserted.",
