)/4 and source-derived upper M=(beta+eta^-1)/4. Auxiliary normalized density equality only; no R2=R/alternateD identification/jointselector or normalized conditional density derivative. BOTH-curvature generic statement is narrower than lower-only source D6 and is disclosed; source companion models supply the upper bound. Anisotropic BL, unreflected linear moments/covariance-upper and SPHMC Hessian lower, outer-y/marginal Poincare, PBPS sampler/reflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation/cost, SPHMC complete algorithm/Wp/proxywarmness, main results/composition/expectedcost remainopen. TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace instances and canonical full-space volume,including dimension zero. Let W:E->R be C2 and assume exp(-W) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. Let m,M:R satisfy m>0 and m<=M. Assume for EVERY x,a:E BOTH genuine all-point/all-vector bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nDefine mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)),the actual normalized exp(-W)/positive partition measure.\nFor EVERY original real-linear partial operator D:Lp R 2 mu->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 mu,assume D.IsClosable and the exact graph iff: for every scalar L2 class b and vector L2 class G,(b,G) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi with b=phi mu-AE and G=gradient(phi) mu-AE. D.closure is the actual closure of this same original graph on its submodule domain.\nThen for EVERY z:D.closure.domain satisfying the actual centered condition integral (z as scalar L2 representative)(x) dmu(x)=0,\n  m*||z as Lp R 2 mu||^2 <= ||D.closure(z)||^2.\nThese are genuine weighted scalar/vector quotient L2 norms. D is fixed before all centered z,not selected anew per input. Mean zero is with respect to actual mu;no assumed Poincare/coercivity/limit certificate or resolvent witness is an input. The original graph's smooth test functions have compact support,but z is a general actual closure-domain element without a compact-support condition. Both lower and upper C2 curvature assumptions are retained;this is not a lower-only contract. The inequality is output for every such centered z,not a premise. No probability-law change,pointwise rough Hessian,anisotropic Hessian-inverse inequality,joint measurable operator choice,normalized-score derivative,marginal inequality or main/cost composition statement is asserted.",
