      "subtitle": "companion:centered-gibbs-resolvent-limit · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CenteredGibbsResolventLimit.gibbs_centered_resolvent_sequence.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel fullspace E including0, genuine C1 W and integrable exp(-W) against volume. Actual normalized probability mu=volume.tilted(-W), positive normalizer and finite-measure scalarL2 separability are derived. SAME exact original compact-smooth gradient D is closable before ALL f/epsilon.\nGenuine f in L2(mu) with actual mean integral0; f integrability is derived from true probability/L2 and returned. Every positive epsilon sequence tends0; actual variational solutions are constructed rather than supplied.\nFor every genuinely centered weighted L2 forcing and positive epsilon sequence->0, derive true f integrability and construct u_n in SAME original Gibbs D.closure.domain, retaining actual variational and ordinary local weak-gradient integrability facts; epsilon_n*u_n tends0 strongly.\nFix real complete Hilbert H,K and SAME actual closed partial linear D before forcing f, positive epsilon sequence->0 and actual variational solutions u_n. H separable explicitly; actual finite-dimensional Borel Gibbs E gives genuine scalar L2 separability by countably generated finite measure, not finite-dimensional L2. Actual energy/scaled domain, Riesz WeakDual sequential compactness, WithLp2 genuine graph double-orthogonal and forcing orthogonal to EVERY kernel give strong epsilon*u_n->0 and epsilon*D(u_n)->0 without Poincare or uniform unscaled u. True C1 Gibbs W/positive exponential normalizer/actual normalized probability and SAME exact original compact-smooth closable gradient beforeALLf; genuine mean-zero L2 forcing is integrable and kernel-orthogonal via actual AEconstant. Construct actual positive-epsilon variational solutions, retaining ordinary localL1/weakC1 test integrabilities. Actual common PBPS J/R/S/reflected law/sourceC2 alpha-beta/eta cap/positive partitions and originalD_y beforeALLf/epsilon; fiberwise only. No epsilon0 solution/range/unscaled uniform bound/extra spatial moment/supplied weak-limit or graph or residual certificate/Poincare/BL/core/adjoint/jointselector/normalized conditional-score derivative/both main/composition; TV never transfers unbounded expectedcost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances and canonical ordinary volume, including dimension zero. Let W:E->R be C1 and assume exp(-W) volume-integrable. Define mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), the actual normalized Gibbs probability exp(-W)/partition described in the approved full-space context. A separate positive-partition binder is not a displayed additional assumption.\nFor EVERY original real-linear partial operator D:Lp R 2 mu->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 mu, assume D.IsClosable and exact original graph: for every scalar L2 a and vector L2 G, (a,G) is in D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi with a=phi mu-AE and G=gradient(phi) mu-AE. D.closure is the genuine same-graph closure operator on its actual submodule domain.\nFor EVERY actual scalar f:Lp R 2 mu satisfying integral f(x) dmu(x)=0, and EVERY epsilon:N->R with all epsilon_n>0 and Tendsto epsilon atTop0, both following conclusions hold:\n(1) The actual standard representative x->f(x) is Integrable under mu.\n(2) There exists ONE actual family u:N->D.closure.domain. For every n, this family satisfies ALL the following:\n  for every v:D.closure.domain,\n    epsilon_n*<u_n,v>_{L2(mu;R)}+<D.closure(u_n),D.closure(v)>_{L2(mu;E)}=<f,v>_{L2(mu;R)};\n  the standard scalar representative of u_n and actual standard vector representative of D.closure(u_n) are each locally integrable with respect to ordinary volume;\n  for every real C1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:E, BOTH x->psi(x)*<D.closure(u_n)(x),a>_E and x->u_n(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable, and\n    integral psi(x)*<D.closure(u_n)(x),a>_E dx = - integral u_n(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor this SAME family, epsilon_n scalar-multiplied by (u_n as scalar L2(mu)) tends atTop to the zero quotient strongly in genuine weighted L2 norm topology.\nD precedes all centered forcing and all sequences. One family is selected after f/epsilon and before every n and every test. Forcing L1 and mean, all variational inner products and limit use actual mu; local integrability and ordinary weak-gradient products/integrals use volume. Actual L2 quotients and standard measurable representatives are retained. There is no monotonicity or centered-u assumption. Only scaled-function convergence is explicitly concluded here, not scaled-gradient convergence, C2 PDE/cutoff facts or an unscaled/range/epsilon=0/further inequality/core/main/cost composition theorem. There is no joint measurable selector.",
