      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with Borel measurable structure and canonical volume, including dimension zero. mu is any finite measure; no absolute-continuity or Gibbs hypothesis on mu is required.\nD is the same closable real-linear partial operator, with original graph iff actual C-infinity compact scalar representatives and their genuine gradients, both classes identified mu-a.e. This semantics comes from the existing gradient producer in the paper consumer.\nThe tested scalar f is only C1 and compactly supported. Its gradient, L2 integrability and actual closure membership are conclusions, not inputs.\nFor every finite Borel measure mu, every closable partial gradient D whose original graph is exactly compact smooth scalar representatives and their genuine gradients, and every C1 compact scalar f, derive MemLp f 2 mu and MemLp (gradient f) 2 mu and prove the actual pair of their L2 classes lies in D.closure.graph. No graph-membership or approximation certificate is supplied.\nSame actual compact-gradient graph closure admits C1 compact function/gradient pairs; actual positive-epsilon weak resolvent has all C1 compact weighted volume tests and genuine ordinary weak gradient. Actual PBPS reflected conditional R/S law and original fixed D precede epsilon/input. No local H2, global operator-core/Bochner, conditional Poincare/BL, centered epsilon limit, noncompact constant/linear domains, measurable y-selection, SPHMC Hessian lower/full4.1, PBPS hypocoercivity or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure,including dimension zero. Let mu be any finite measure on E. Write X=L2(mu;R) and Y=L2(mu;E) for the actual quotient spaces. Let D:X partial-linear[R]->Y be a real linear partial operator on a submodule domain,and assume D is closable. Assume its graph is exactly the smooth compactly supported gradient graph:for every a in X and H in Y,\n  (a,H) in graph(D) if and only if there exists phi:E->R such that\n    phi is globally smooth,\n    phi has compact support,\n    the representative of a equals phi mu-almost everywhere,\n    the representative of H equals grad phi mu-almost everywhere.\nThe gradient is the actual Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative. For every real-valued f:E->R that is globally C1 and has compact support,there exist proofs hp of MemLp(f,2,mu) and hq of MemLp(grad f,2,mu) such that\n  (hp.toLp(f),hq.toLp(grad f)) in graph(closure(D)).\nMemLp asserts suitable measurability and finite L2 norm of the actual functions;toLp is their actual quotient embedding,agreeing almost everywhere with its input. Closability means the topological closure of graph(D) is single-valued,and closure(D) is that closed partial operator. Thus the graph membership relates the L2 class of the actual C1 function to the L2 class of its actual gradient. No membership is built into the operator definition.\nThe theorem supplies both function/gradient L2 membership and closure-graph membership. It does not construct D,assume the finite measure is a probability or absolutely continuous measure,assume D has dense domain,upgrade f to smoothness,choose a different output gradient,or assert a pointwise identity of all possible representatives.",
