    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactPoissonSmoothGraph",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactPoissonSmoothGraph",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:compact-poisson-smooth-graph · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CompactPoissonSmoothGraph.compact_weak_poisson_smooth_graph_approximation.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel space E with canonical ordinary full-space volume, including dimension zero. Real pointwise v,F and vector G are genuinely global volumeL2; their topological supports lie in the same compact K.\nEvery real C1 compact test psi and every a satisfies both L1 products and integral psi*inner(G,a)=-integral v*D_a psi. Every real C2 compact psi has both L1 products and integral v*Delta psi=integral F*psi. These actual weak equations, measurability/L2 and supports are inputs; graph density, Sobolev membership, smooth sequence, real mixed Hessian and weighted core are not supplied.\nThe rough v/G/F representatives are differentiated only in the actual weak/distributional sense. Classical gradients and Laplacians in the conclusion belong to actual smooth approximants. SchwartzMap E real is genuinely C-infinity/rapidly decaying; common compact support is additionally derived. No positive dimension, jointly measurable selector, source C-infinity potential or normalized plateau is assumed.\nFrom the exact compact-supported volumeL2 and original weak-gradient/PDE inputs, Derive one real Schwartz sequence phi_n with one common outer compact Kprime containing every tsupport(phi_n), chosen before all n and all three limits. Actual volumeL2 classes of phi_n converge to v; actual classical gradient(phi_n) is MemLp2 and its class converges to the original G; actual Laplacian(phi_n) classes converge to F. Every phi_n is C-infinity and compactly supported. The same sequence realizes all limits. Kprime need not equal K. No classical derivatives of rough v, real Hessian family, quantitative source complexity constant or weighted operator core is claimed.\nDerive one real smooth sequence with common outer compact support and simultaneous actual ordinary-volume L2 function/gradient/Laplacian limits for v=chi*u, g=chi*G+u*gradientchi, F=chi*r+2inner(gradientchi,G)+u*laplacianchi. Same original D before epsilon/f, same u before ALL cutoffs. No supplied graph-density/approximation/mixedHessian/core certificate, no classical rough derivatives, no weighted-domain/operator-core/globalcutoff/Bochner/BL/Poincare/jointmeasurablechoice/main/composition claim. Reflected/RGO quarter Hessian and fourfold energy kept distinct; TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume; dimension zero is allowed and all approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. Let v,F:E->R, G:E->E and K:Set E. Assume K is compact and each of tsupport(v), tsupport(F), tsupport(G) is contained in K. Assume actual MemLp v 2 volume, MemLp F 2 volume and MemLp G 2 volume; these include volume-a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm.\nAssume that for every real C1 compactly supported psi:E->R and every a:E, both x->psi(x)*<G(x),a>_E and x->v(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G(x),a>_E dx = - integral v(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nAssume also that for every real C2 compactly supported psi:E->R, both x->v(x)*Delta(psi)(x) and x->F(x)*psi(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral v(x)*Delta(psi)(x) dx = integral F(x)*psi(x) dx.\nThe test Laplacian is the actual finite-basis trace. No pointwise classical derivatives of v or G or F, Sobolev certificate, core theorem, or sequence certificate are premises.\nThen there exist a compact set Kprime in E and one sequence phi:N->SchwartzMap E R such that, for every n, tsupport(phi_n) is contained in Kprime, and the actual scalar quotient classes (phi_n).toLp 2 volume converge as n tends to infinity to hv2.toLp(v) in the norm topology of scalar L2(volume). There further exists a family hphiG of actual MemLp witnesses, one for each n, for gradient(phi_n):E->E at exponent 2 with respect to volume, such that the same sequence's actual vector quotient classes (hphiG_n).toLp(gradient(phi_n)) converge in vector L2(volume) norm to hG2.toLp(G), and the same sequence's scalar quotient classes (Delta(phi_n)).toLp 2 volume converge in scalar L2(volume) norm to hF2.toLp(F).\nAll three limits are Filter.Tendsto atTop (nhds the displayed actual quotient target). The MemLp.toLp targets are volume-a.e. linked to the original pointwise inputs. The Schwartz functions are genuine smooth rapidly decreasing real functions on real E, and their classical gradients and Laplacians are actual operators on these smooth approximants. This is one common compact Kprime and one sequence for all n and for all three limits, not three separate sequences or moving n-dependent support sets. There is no containment relation asserted between Kprime and K, no rate, no pointwise convergence, no support equality for chosen quotient representatives, and no weighted-domain/core or further inequality/composition conclusion.",
