    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactWeakPoissonSobolev",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactWeakPoissonSobolev",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:compact-weak-poisson-sobolev · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CompactWeakPoissonSobolev.compact_weak_poisson_sobolev.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. v and F are real pointwise functions with genuine global volume MemLp2; K is compact and tsupport v and tsupport F are contained in K.\nFor every real C2 compact phi, v*Delta phi and F*phi are integrable for volume and integral v*Delta phi=integral F*phi. This generic analytic interface is consumed with these inputs actually derived by the same-D localized resolvent; no all-Schwartz, TD equation or final Sobolev certificate is supplied.\nAll rough functions/class representatives are differentiated only as distributions. Complex test derivatives are real Frechet derivatives on E, real/imaginary projections are real-linear CLMs, and the complex TD pairing is bilinear integral psi*v without conjugation. No Nontrivial or positive-dimensional assumption is added.\nUnder the exact ordinary-volume global L2/support and real compact-C2 PDE assumptions, Construct actual vc,Fc in complex L2(volume), with vc=volume-a.e. ofReal(v) and Fc=volume-a.e. ofReal(F). For every complex Schwartz psi, both (Delta psi)*ofReal(v) and psi*ofReal(F) are L1 and their integrals equal. For T_v=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc) and T_F=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc), derive Delta T_v=T_F and MemSobolev 2 2 T_v. The latter uses B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T and a genuine complex L2 witness, not a supplied regularity result.\nDerive actual all-complex-Schwartz tested PDE with both products L1, genuine complex volume-L2 classes/AE embeddings, actual TD Laplacian and MemSobolev2 using B2=I-(2pi)^-2 Delta. Genuine conditional same originalD before epsilon/f, one actualu before allC2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. No real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/Bochner, BL/Poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/scales distinct; TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. All approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. Let v,F:E->R and K a subset of E. Assume K is compact, tsupport(v) is contained in K and tsupport(F) is contained in K. Assume both v and F satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to volume, including volume-a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm.\nAssume that for every real C2 compactly supported phi:E->R, both functions x->v(x)*Delta(phi)(x) and x->F(x)*phi(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral v(x)*Delta(phi)(x) dx = integral F(x)*phi(x) dx.\nHere Delta(phi) is the actual test-function finite-basis Laplacian. No classical derivatives of v or F are assumed.\nThen there exist vc,Fc in Lp C 2 volume such that vc=(x->(v(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere and Fc=(x->(F(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere. For these same vc,Fc all of the following conclusions hold simultaneously:\n(1) For every psi in SchwartzMap E C, both x->Delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):C) and x->psi(x)*(F(x):C) are volume-integrable and\n  integral Delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):C) dx = integral psi(x)*(F(x):C) dx.\n(2) Delta(Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)) = Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc).\n(3) MemSobolev 2 2 (Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)).\nThe classes are selected before all Schwartz tests and the complex test integrals use the original pointwise v and F casts, not newly selected functions per test. The real weak PDE and its two L1 products are premises; the two complex Schwartz L1 products, the complex test equation, the genuine distribution equation and Sobolev membership are conclusions.\nLp C 2 volume is the genuine complex L2 quotient with its standard measurable representative. These volume-a.e. identities bind the chosen classes to the actual pointwise real functions cast into C; they do not assert pointwise support identities for the chosen complex representatives. Every Schwartz test is a genuine smooth rapidly decreasing complex function on the real space E, and no compact-support restriction is imposed on it. Its derivatives are real Frechet derivatives. Pairings and displayed integrals use ordinary complex multiplication with no complex conjugation. Lp.toTemperedDistribution is the genuine complex-linear distribution embedding whose value at psi is integral psi(x)*the L2 representative(x) dx. The distribution Laplacian is the true tempered-distribution operator. MemSobolev 2 2 means there exists an actual fprime in Lp C 2 volume with besselPotential E C 2 of the displayed distribution equal to Lp.toTemperedDistribution(fprime); its multiplier is (1+||xi||^2)^(2/2). The approved Fourier convention is Delta T=-(2*pi)^2 FM(||xi||^2)T. This order-2 Bessel-Sobolev assertion is not a pointwise classical Laplacian, a real Hessian representative, or a weighted-core conclusion.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
