ex volume-l2 classes/ae embeddings, actual td laplacian and memsobolev2 using b2=i-(2pi)^-2 delta. genuine conditional same originald before epsilon/f, one actualu before allc2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. no real mixed-second representatives/hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/bochner, bl/poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. reflected/rgo laws/operators/scales distinct; tv does not transfer unbounded cost. let e be a finite-dimensional real hilbert space with its borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. all approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. let v,f:e->r and k a subset of e. assume k is compact, tsupport(v) is contained in k and tsupport(f) is contained in k. assume both v and f satisfy actual memlp at exponent 2 with respect to volume, including volume-a.e. strong measurability and finite l2 norm. assume that for every real c2 compactly supported phi:e->r, both functions x->v(x)*delta(phi)(x) and x->f(x)*phi(x) are volume-integrable and integral v(x)*delta(phi)(x) dx = integral f(x)*phi(x) dx. here delta(phi) is the actual test-function finite-basis laplacian. no classical derivatives of v or f are assumed. then there exist vc,fc in lp c 2 volume such that vc=(x->(v(x):c)) volume-almost everywhere and fc=(x->(f(x):c)) volume-almost everywhere. for these same vc,fc all of the following conclusions hold simultaneously: (1) for every psi in schwartzmap e c, both x->delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):c) and x->psi(x)*(f(x):c) are volume-integrable and integral delta(psi)(x)*(v(x):c) dx = integral psi(x)*(f(x):c) dx. (2) delta(lp.totempereddistribution(vc)) = lp.totempereddistribution(fc). (3) memsobolev 2 2 (lp.totempereddistribution(vc)). the classes are selected before all schwartz tests and the complex test integrals use the original pointwise v and f casts, not newly selected functions per test. the real weak pde and its two l1 products are premises; the two complex schwartz l1 products, the complex test equation, the genuine distribution equation and sobolev membership are conclusions. lp c 2 volume is the genuine complex l2 quotient with its standard measurable representative. these volume-a.e. identities bind the chosen classes to the actual pointwise real functions cast into c; they do not assert pointwise support identities for the chosen complex representatives. every schwartz test is a genuine smooth rapidly decreasing complex function on the real space e, and no compact-support restriction is imposed on it. its derivatives are real frechet derivatives. pairings and displayed integrals use ordinary complex multiplication with no complex conjugation. lp.totempereddistribution is the genuine complex-linear distribution embedding whose value at psi is integral psi(x)*the l2 representative(x) dx. the distribution laplacian is the true tempered-distribution operator. memsobolev 2 2 means there exists an actual fprime in lp c 2 volume with besselpotential e c 2 of the displayed distribution equal to lp.totempereddistribution(fprime); its multiplier is (1+||xi||^2)^(2/2). the approved fourier convention is delta t=-(2*pi)^2 fm(||xi||^2)t. this order-2 bessel-sobolev assertion is not a pointwise classical laplacian, a real hessian representative, or a weighted-core conclusion. accepted pbps arxiv:2609.06905v1 section2.2 actual reflected conditional law and appendixc.1 compact-gradient density/closedness analytic prerequisite; sphmc arxiv:2609.06906v1 section4.1 covariance-upper/bl dependency only. this authored compact-schwartz-sobolev prerequisite is not a quoted numbered source theorem. autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.functionalinequalities.compactweakpoissonsobolev.compact_weak_poisson_sobolev autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/functionalinequalities/compactweakpoissonsobolev.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 acf43d2a935f3ebbfc0bb470aa1f53f610a8e5f08b5f3a0dbbd81a