only; no weighted domain/core or classical hessian. equivalent source original restatement and both six-step lessons expressly retain omitted analytic boundaries. primary source motivates prerequisite rather than states this exact theorem. constant dependencies deltat=-(2pi)^2 fm(norm²)t; b2=i-(2pi)^-2delta. no dimension-dependent bound. same fourier convention and bessel order2 multiplier (1+norm²)^(2/2). equivalent private122-139 uses exact inverse((2pi)^2), not coefficient1; sobolev simp197 has r+s=2+0. no hidden scaling.",
