    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactWeightedPoissonCoercivity",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-CompactWeightedPoissonCoercivity",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:compact-weighted-poisson-coercivity · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CompactWeightedPoissonCoercivity.compact_weak_poisson_weighted_coercivity.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E, canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. W is C2, exp(-W) genuinely integrable with positive Z. The actual given measure mu equals volume.tilted(-W), hence is the normalized Gibbs law. The Hessian quadratic form is bounded below by m times squared norm for every point/vector; m is any real number, not necessarily positive.\nThe original partial real-linear gradient D on actual weighted L2 is closable. Its graph consists exactly of AE classes of C-infinity compact functions and their genuine classical gradients. This is an original structural interface, not a supplied final closure-domain, coercivity, adjoint or core certificate.\nPointwise real v,F and vector G are global ordinary-volume MemLp2 with topological supports in the same compact K. Every real C1 compact psi/every direction a has both legal L1 products and integral psi*inner(G,a)=-integral v*D_a psi. Every real C2 compact psi has both legal L1 products and integral v*Delta psi=integral F*psi. No approximation, weighted class/convergence, domain membership or scalar inequality is an input.\nFrom the stated genuine compact weak data and original gradient interface, Derive actual weighted MemLp2 of v,G,A=inner(gradientW,G)-F. Return actual vW,AW,GW L2 classes with all three mu-AE links, (vW,GW) in the SAME D.closure graph, and m*norm(GW)^2<=norm(AW)^2. The actual ordinary smooth sequence, common compact weighted transfer and generator-gradient limits are produced internally. This is compact scalar coercivity, not a rough Hessian, full Bochner/adjoint/operator-core identity, global cutoff result, epsilon-zero/Poincare/BL or complete main theorem.\nDerive genuine compact weighted L2/AE classes vW/GW/AW for actual v/G/(innergradWG-F), same original D.closure graph membership and lambda*normGW^2<=normAW^2 via actual same ordinary-to-weighted smooth sequence. Source fixes originalD before epsilon/f and ONEu before ALLC2chi. No supplied weighted domain/core/convergence/coercivity certificate; no rough classical Hessian or full adjoint/generator-core identity, globalcutoff/tail/Bochner,epsilon0/kernel/range/noncompactlinear/Poincare/BL/jointmeasurablechoice/main/composition. Reflected quarter/fourfold constants exact. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume; dimension zero is permitted and all approved section instances belong to the contract. Let W:E->R be C2. Assume exp(-W) is volume-integrable and its volume integral is strictly positive. Let m be any real number and assume that for every x,a in E,\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a.\nThere is no positivity or nonnegativity assumption on m. Let mu:Measure E be supplied with the exact law equality mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), namely exp(-W)/integral exp(-W) times volume.\nLet D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E) be a real-linear partial operator on its actual submodule domain. Assume D is closable and has exactly the following graph: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H, (a,H) belongs to graph(D) iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real function psi with a=psi mu-almost everywhere and H=gradient(psi) mu-almost everywhere. The closure is the genuine operator obtained from that same graph closure.\nLet v,F:E->R, G:E->E and K:Set E. Assume K compact and each of tsupport(v),tsupport(F),tsupport(G) is contained in K. Assume actual MemLp v 2 volume, MemLp F 2 volume and MemLp G 2 volume. For every real C1 compactly supported psi and every a:E, assume both x->psi(x)*<G(x),a>_E and x->v(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G(x),a>_E dx = - integral v(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor every real C2 compactly supported psi, assume both x->v(x)*Delta(psi)(x) and x->F(x)*psi(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral v(x)*Delta(psi)(x) dx = integral F(x)*psi(x) dx.\nHere gradient and fderiv are actual operators and Delta on tests is the actual finite-basis Laplacian; no classical gradient/Hessian of rough v or G is assumed.\nDefine the actual scalar function A(x)=<gradient(W)(x),G(x)>_E-F(x), with exactly this minus sign. Then v,G,A each satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to mu. Furthermore there exist actual scalar classes vW,AW in Lp R 2 mu and a vector class GW in Lp E 2 mu such that vW=v mu-almost everywhere, AW=A mu-almost everywhere and GW=G mu-almost everywhere, and simultaneously\n  (vW,GW) belongs to D.closure.graph,\n  m*||GW||_{L2(mu;E)}^2 <= ||AW||_{L2(mu;R)}^2.\nEach MemLp includes actual a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm. The norms in the coercivity conclusion are genuine weighted quotient L2 norms. The supplied mu equality and original smooth-test graph are premises, whereas weighted L2, these returned quotient/AE links, same-operator closure membership, and the scalar inequality are outputs. No dense-domain premise or existence of D is added. This is a compact-supported ordinary weak-data to weighted-domain/coercivity result; it does not state a classical rough-function Laplacian, cutoff removal, global tail/global coercivity theorem, generator-adjoint/core equality, or further functional inequality/composition conclusion.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
