      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including dimension0. Fix SAME original real weighted-L2 partial-linear gradient D with exact compact-C-infinity genuine gradient graph and closability BEFORE all queried functions or classes.\nActual finite mu and EVERY real constant c; scalar constant and genuine zero vector gradient are L2 by finite measure. No global ordinary-volume integrability or spatial moment is required.\nFor EVERY real c, produce u in SAME original D.closure.domain whose actual representative is mu-AE constant c and whose actual vector output is0.\nActual finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0. Fix actual finite mu and SAME original closable exact compact-C-infinity gradient D BEFORE ALL C1 f with actual MemLp f2mu and MemLp gradientf2mu. Genuine smooth cutoff exhaustion/derivative-product/weighted L2 limits put actual class pair into SAME closure graph, without compact support or extra spatial moment. Finite mu constants are genuinely in original closure domain with outputzero. For actual C1 Gibbs W/exp(-W) integrable, combine actual constants-domain with accepted one-way implication for full zero-output iff AEconstant on SAME D. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/Sdensity/positive partitions/sourceC2 alpha beta eta cap and original D_y beforeALL constants/u/directions; real unnormalized y-score C1/L2/boundedgradient from accepted score producer transfers along ONLY explicit reflected density equality S2_y=S_y and enters SAME original closed graph. No R2=R or alternateD equality, global ordinary L1, C-infinity potential, gradient of rough representative, Nontrivial E, spatial moment, supplied domain/fullkernel/spectralgap/Poincare certificate, epsilon0/range/centering/measurablejointselector/core/BL/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary volume, including dimension zero. All approved section instances belong to the contract. Let mu:Measure E be any finite measure. Let D:Lp R 2 mu ->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 mu be supplied and closable, with exactly this original graph: For every scalar class a and vector class H in these actual quotient spaces, (a,H) belongs to D.graph if and only if there exists a smooth compactly supported real function phi:E->R with a=phi almost everywhere for the stated measure and H=gradient(phi) almost everywhere for that same measure. D is the genuine real-linear partial gradient on its submodule domain; D.closure is its actual same-graph closure operator. For every supplied real c there exists u in this SAME D.closure.domain such that the standard representative of the scalar quotient u equals the actual constant function x->c mu-almost everywhere, and D.closure(u)=0 as the actual vector L2(mu) quotient.\nD is fixed before c, and u may depend on c. Both domain membership and zero output are produced rather than assumed for constants. No probability/positive density/absolute continuity is required of finite mu, and zero measure is not excluded. This is an existential constant-domain witness for each c, not a uniqueness or arbitrary-u kernel characterization by itself. It adds no spectral-gap or further inequality, measurable simultaneous selection, core/adjoint or composition conclusion.",
