          "reconstructed": "The identity L2 conclusion is vector-valued under each actual normalized tilt,not L2 of a density or finite second moment of the original mu. Covariance is the centered real covariance of scalar projections under R(y),using its proven probability/L2 properties. The first derivative is a continuous linear functional and the nested derivative differentiates that functional-valued map before applying v,w. C is an arbitrary fixed positive scalar;its derivative contribution is absent,without requiring a Gaussian prefactor. No separate ContDiff conclusion or smoothness hypothesis is supplied in the statement. Zero dimension is allowed,and all y/v/w formulas are pointwise. No Gaussian law equality,convexity or further Hessian/moment bound is added. No material ambiguity or definition gap is present.",
