      "original_theorem": "Attributed analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space equipped with its Borel measurable space, including dimension zero. eta is a strictly positive real. mu is an arbitrary probability measure on E, possibly singular and without finite moments.\nC_eta=((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^-1)^dim E and Z_eta(y)=integral exp(-norm(y-x)^2/(2*eta)) dmu(x). The actual smoothed law is the measurable pushforward of mu×standard Gaussian by (x,g)->x+sqrt(eta)g. The potential is exactly -log(C_eta Z_eta), not Gaussian averaging of an input potential.\nAll first/second Gaussian derivative domination, Bochner integrability, measurability and strictly positive normalizers are derived. The local CLM dual instances choose existing canonical normed structures and add no mathematical premises. No input density, moment, curvature or supplied regularity certificate is assumed.\nSource Section3.1 defines the unnormalized convolution exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*Gaussian. This theorem constructs the exact normalized density potential U_eta=-log(C_eta Z_mu). For Gibbs mu=exp(-V) volume/Z_V, U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V; formalizing that Gibbs specialization and constant-shift adapter remains separate. This normalization difference does not change derivatives, but the two chosen potentials are not asserted literally identical.\nThe actual Gaussian add-noise probability law equals volume.withDensity(ofReal(C_eta Z_eta)). Its density is strictly positive at every y, Z_eta is globally C2, and the exact negative-log density U_eta=-log(C_eta Z_eta) is globally C2. The input law may be singular and may lack moments.\nCloses the genuine Gaussian-smoothed density and global C2 normalizer/negative-log potential prerequisite, for arbitrary probability input and eta>0. It does not yet prove the score/posterior-covariance identities (4.1), Lemma4.1 curvature via Brascamp-Lieb/Cramer-Rao, higher derivative/cumulant estimates, target invariance, numerical bias/history/expected costs, PBPS process, either complete main result or composition. TV proximity does not transfer unbounded cost. Source Section3.1 defines the unnormalized convolution exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*Gaussian. This theorem constructs the exact normalized density potential U_eta=-log(C_eta Z_mu). For Gibbs mu=exp(-V) volume/Z_V, U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V; formalizing that Gibbs specialization and constant-shift adapter remains separate. This normalization difference does not change derivatives, but the two chosen potentials are not asserted literally identical.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure,let mu be any probability measure on E,and let eta be any real number with eta>0. Put d=dim_R E,allowing d=0,and define the actual scalar and real-valued function\n  C=((sqrt(2 pi eta))^(-1))^d,\n  Z(y)=integral_E exp(-||y-x||^2/(2 eta)) dmu(x).\nThe integral is the real Bochner integral. Let G be the standard centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure on E,and let volume be canonical Lebesgue measure on this inner-product space. Then the following four conclusions hold simultaneously:\n  (mu x G)_*( (x,g) -> x+sqrt(eta)g )\n    = volume.withDensity(y -> ENNReal.ofReal(C Z(y)));\n  C Z(y)>0 for every y in E;\n  Z:E->R is globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable;\n  y -> -log(C Z(y)) is globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable.\nThe product mu x G is independent,and the pushforward is the law of X+sqrt(eta)G when X has law mu and the Gaussian vector is independent of X. The right side is the actual Lebesgue-density measure using the displayed normalizer and convolution integral. The positivity conclusion holds everywhere,not merely almost everywhere,and the negative-log function is defined from that exact normalized density. Real exponential,logarithm and square root have the stated real meanings.\nNo density,absolute continuity or finite-moment assumption is imposed on the input probability measure mu. There is no upper bound or small-step assumption on eta and no exclusion of zero dimension. The theorem asserts the exact measure equality,pointwise positive density and the two global C2 statements;it does not assert higher smoothness,analyticity,convexity,Hessian bounds,gradient Lipschitz constants,a diffusion evolution or a sampling algorithm.",
