tion retains actual defined density and potential. domains scoped finite-dimensional real inner-product borel space including0, canonical volume/stdgaussian and bochner integral. e is finite-dimensional real-inner-product with its borel measurable structure. mu is measure e with isprobabilitymeasure;eta in r with eta>0;d=module.finrank r e in n and may be zero. c in r;z:e->r. g and volume are measures on e;the independent product law lies on e x e and its pushforward lies on e. density is embedded into ennreal via ofreal;z and negative-log density are real-valued functions on all e. norm is induced by the given inner product. no separately supplied input density or vector-valued potential appears. explicit-elaboration three canonical local instances and all private proofs inspected. actual gaussian prefactor includes empty-product dimension0. fresh zero-dimensional specialization and singular dirac test pass with no density premise. quantifiers every probability mu, eta>0; exact pushforward equality, everywhere positivity and global c2 of z/u simultaneously. for every e with the stated structures,every probability mu on e,and every eta>0,define exactly c and z;then the four displayed conclusions hold simultaneously. density positivity is for every y in e. both contdiff r 2 conclusions are global over all e. the measure equality identifies the full measures,not only values on a selected set or almost-everywhere representatives. c and z are fixed definitions,not existentially selected functions. equivalent old statement is byte-identical in current source packet/code and unchanged anonymous reconstruction. private regularity now returns additionally proved derivative witnesses; public c2 uses only original conclusions and adds no premise. assumptions only arbitrary probability, eta>0 and finite-dimensional borel real-hilbert structure; no density/moment/curvature/suppliedc2. only the finite-dimensional real-inner-product/borel structure,the probability normalization of mu,and eta>0. no finite moment,input lebesgue density,absolute continuity,regularity of mu,eta upper bound,nonzero dimension,integrability certificate or supplied smoothness/density identity is assumed. the approved definitions specify the real bochner integral,standard gaussian,canonical volume and density measure. explicit-elaboration explicit first/second gaussian domination is integrated against probability constants; common-neighborhood dominated differentiation and continuity derive z c2. log applied only after true positivity. no added hidden hypotheses in extended private interface. conclusion actual gaussian pushforward density, c_eta z positive at every y, z globalc2 and exact normalized -log(c_eta z) globalc2. the pushforward of mu.prod g under (x,g)->x+sqrt(eta)g equals volume.withdensity(ofreal(c z)). for every y,c z(y)>0. z is globally contdiff r 2,and the actual function y->-real.log(c z(y)) is globally contdiff r 2. these four assertions are simultaneous and use the displayed exact c,z. equivalent all four outputs freshly rechecked through gaussiannormalizerregularity and gaussiandensity. full40-line prior test exercises singular input and genuine backward kernel/c2 combination; no previous verdict used. scopes declaration-local analytic prerequisite, with normalized u versus source unnormalized v explicitly separated; no further credit for unchanged c2 theorem. measure equality concerns the actual independent-noise pushforward and the actual volume-density measure. positivity is everywhere;the negative logarithm uses exactly that normalized density. the smoothness conclusions are c2,not an asserted c-infinity or analytic result. the input mu is unrestricted apart from being a probability measure,so no input density or finite-moment condition is added. dimension zero is permitted. no hessian,convexity,gradient bound,diffusion semigroup or numerical algorithm is asserted. no material ambiguity or definition gap is present. explicit-elaboration five authored c2 proof steps checked. this selected declaration does not itself state score/covariance; current sibling and new source test do, as corrected whole-module header explains. separate gibbs constant adapter exists outside this statement; no literal u=v and no lemma4.1/curvature/main claim. constant dependencies c_eta=((sqrt(2pi eta))^-1)^dime; kernel denominator2eta, noise sqrteta; source gibbs potential shift+logzv. exact normalizer c=((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-1))^d with natural exponent d=finrank_r e. exact kernel exponent -||y-x||^2/(2*eta),and noise scale sqrt(eta). the logarithm is -log(c z(y)) including the normalizer,not -log z alone. c depends only on eta,d;z depends on eta,mu and y. there is no omitted volume factor,unspecified constant,moment parameter or smoothness-bound coefficient. equivalent actual gaussian prefactor and variance retained in full current code/parents; no generic new c substituted into this probability density theorem. hc positive including0 and real logarithm positivity justify exact normalized potential.",
