      "original_theorem": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nSame actual C2 normalized Gibbs law, positive integrable partition and BOTH global positive m/M curvature bounds; finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E including0.\nALL actual C1 scalar functions f with true scalar and gradient MemLp2. No supplied centering, Poincare, Admissible, variance or extra spatial moments. Original compact-smooth D is constructed before all f.\nFor every genuine C1 scalar/gradient weightedL2 observable, derive real Admissible integrability and m*Var_mu(f)<=DirichletEnergy_mu(f) on the actual normalized Gibbs law, using actual centered graph membership and AE quotient identities.\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel full E including0, genuine C2 W with actual exponential integrability/positive partition, normalized tilted probability, BOTH global mI<=HessW<=MI and0<m<=M. SAME original exact compact-smooth closable weighted gradient D BEFORE all truly mean-zero domain z. Actual positiveepsilon variational solutions from residual/globalcoercivity producers are identified by SAME D/epsilon/forcing uniqueness, then tested against z; strong scaled residual limit and genuine scalar Cauchy-Schwarz/zero-norm branch give m*normz^2<=normDclosurez^2. No uniform unscaled solution bound, centered resolvent, epsilon0 solution, core/range/adjoint certificate or input Poincare. Actual C1 scalar/gradientL2 pairs and centered function are admitted to a genuine original graph, actual probability/AE quotient identities and real integrability produce Admissible and m*Var<=DirichletEnergy. Actual common Gaussian J/R/S, sourceC2 alpha-beta eta cap, reflected W_y, positive partitions and one original D_y precede allcentered z/score directions; actual unnormalized parameter-y score variance <=(eta^-1-alpha)^2*norma^2/(4*(alpha+eta^-1)), with exact reflected m=(alpha+eta^-1)/4 and source-derived upper M=(beta+eta^-1)/4. Auxiliary normalized density equality only; no R2=R/alternateD identification/jointselector or normalized conditional density derivative. BOTH-curvature generic statement is narrower than lower-only source D6 and is disclosed; source companion models supply the upper bound. Anisotropic BL, unreflected linear moments/covariance-upper and SPHMC Hessian lower, outer-y/marginal Poincare, PBPS sampler/reflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation/cost, SPHMC complete algorithm/Wp/proxywarmness, main results/composition/expectedcost remainopen. TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances and canonical full-space volume,including dimension zero. Let W:E->R be C2 and assume exp(-W) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. Let m,M:R satisfy m>0,m<=M. Assume for EVERY x,a:E BOTH bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nDefine mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)),the actual normalized exp(-W)/positive partition Gibbs measure.\nFor EVERY actual real function f:E->R,assume f C1,actual MemLp f 2 mu,and actual MemLp (gradient f) 2 mu. No compact support or mean-zero condition is required of f;these are genuine scalar/vector AE strong-measurability and finite-L2 hypotheses,not inferred from finite probability alone.\nThen ALL of the following actual integrability assertions hold:\n  Integrable f mu,\n  Integrable (x->(f(x)-integral f(y) dmu(y))^2) mu,\n  Integrable (x->||gradient(f)(x)||^2) mu.\nThese three and only these conjuncts are the approved Admissible(mu,f) predicate. Moreover,\n  m*integral (f(x)-integral f(y) dmu(y))^2 dmu(x)\n  <= integral ||gradient(f)(x)||^2 dmu(x).\nThe left integral is exactly variance(mu,f);the right is exactly dirichletEnergy(mu,f),with NO extra prefactor. All integrals use the SAME actual mu,including the inner mean;there is no division by mass in the API's mean formula (mu here is normalized). The gradient is exactly (InnerProductSpace.toDual R E).symm(fderiv R f x),the genuine real Riesz representative,with actual C1 derivatives ensured by the input.\nThis statement has no D parameter or graph/domain premise;the operator mentioned in background context is not added as a theorem assumption. Both lower and upper global C2 curvature controls,integrability and positive partition remain explicit. Admissible and the inequality are outputs,not supplied certificates. The result applies to every C1 scalar-and-gradient L2 function,not just already-centered or compact functions. No rough Hessian,Hessian-inverse anisotropic inequality,normalized-score differentiation,marginal-law inequality,measurable selector or main/expected-cost composition is asserted.",
