    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-GibbsCovarianceLower",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-GibbsCovarianceLower",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:gibbs-covariance-lower · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Analysis.GibbsGradientMoment.gibbs_covariance_lower.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed Cramer-Rao half restatement:\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable space and canonical volume, including dimension zero. alpha,beta are NNReal, 0<alpha<=beta. U or V is genuinely C2; actual Hessian at every point and direction lies between alpha*norm(v)^2 and beta*norm(v)^2.\nEvery Gibbs law is the actual volume.tilted(-potential). Probability, finite second moments, score integrability, centered score pairing and covariance bounds are derived. No minimizer, finite input moments, partition constant, derivative/score/covariance or well-behaved certificate is supplied.\nThe actual Gibbs mu=volume.tilted(-U) is probability and id belongs to L2(mu). For every direction v, covarianceBilin(mu)(v,v)>=norm(v)^2/beta. This is the linear-observable covariance corollary of Cramer-Rao, not the full nonlinear-observable theorem or a matrix-inverse result.\nActual Gibbs all-direction covariance lower bound and its actual RGO/source V_eta Hessian upper consumer only. No Brascamp-Lieb covariance upper/Hessian lower, full Lemma4.1, general nonlinear Cramer-Rao, higher regularity, exact stationarity, approximate/stochastic/history work, PBPS process or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical Lebesgue volume,including dimension zero. Let U:E->R be globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable,and let alpha,beta be nonnegative real parameters (NNReal). Assume alpha>0,alpha<=beta,and for every x,v in E,\n  (alpha:R)||v||^2<=D^2 U(x)[v,v]<=(beta:R)||v||^2.\nThe Hessian is the actual nested Frechet derivative,applied successively to v twice. Define the actual tilt\n  mu=volume.tilted(x -> -U(x)),\nmeaning the measure with density exp(-U(x))/integral_E exp(-U) dvolume relative to volume,with ENNReal.ofReal density coercion. The normalization integral is the actual real Bochner integral;the tilt definition alone does not include a probability or nonzero-normalization certificate.\nThen these three conclusions hold simultaneously:\n  mu is a probability measure;\n  the E-valued identity x->x belongs to MemLp exponent 2 under mu;\n  for every v in E,\n    ||v||^2/(beta:R)<=CovBilin(mu)(v,v).\nMemLp here means identity measurability modulo mu and finite second moment. The covariance term is the real centered covariance of the scalar projection <v,X> with itself under mu;the probability and L2 conclusions supply its stated moment regime. Equivalently,with the vector Bochner mean m=integral_E x dmu(x),the covariance is integral_E(<v,x>-<v,m>)^2 dmu(x).\nThe measure mu is fixed by its displayed exponential tilt,not an arbitrary input measure assumed to be probability or L2. Both probability normalization and L2 are conclusions. beta is strictly positive as a consequence of alpha>0 and alpha<=beta. No upper covariance bound,gradient integration-by-parts premise,provided matrix,critical point,positive-dimension restriction or numerical sampling statement is included.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
