      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261006-gibbscovariancelower semantic-audit astis-rt-20261006-gibbscovariancelower companion:gibbs-covariance-lower · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_covariance_lower. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder attributed cramer-rao half restatement: e is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its borel measurable space and canonical volume, including dimension zero. alpha,beta are nnreal, 0<alpha<=beta. u or v is genuinely c2; actual hessian at every point and direction lies between alpha*norm(v)^2 and beta*norm(v)^2. every gibbs law is the actual volume.tilted(-potential). probability, finite second moments, score integrability, centered score pairing and covariance bounds are derived. no minimizer, finite input moments, partition constant, derivative/score/covariance or well-behaved certificate is supplied. the actual gibbs mu=volume.tilted(-u) is probability and id belongs to l2(mu). for every direction v, covariancebilin(mu)(v,v)>=norm(v)^2/beta. this is the linear-observable covariance corollary of cramer-rao, not the full nonlinear-observable theorem or a matrix-inverse result. actual gibbs all-direction covariance lower bound and its actual rgo/source v_eta hessian upper consumer only. no brascamp-lieb covariance upper/hessian lower, full lemma4.1, general nonlinear cramer-rao, higher regularity, exact stationarity, approximate/stochastic/history work, pbps process or either complete main/composition. tv never transfers unbounded expected cost. let e be any complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its borel measurable structure and canonical lebesgue volume,including dimension zero. let u:e->r be globally twice continuously frechet differentiable,and let alpha,beta be nonnegative real parameters (nnreal). assume alpha>0,alpha<=beta,and for every x,v in e, (alpha:r)||v||^2<=d^2 u(x)[v,v]<=(beta:r)||v||^2. the hessian is the actual nested frechet derivative,applied successively to v twice. define the actual tilt mu=volume.tilted(x -> -u(x)), meaning the measure with density exp(-u(x))/integral_e exp(-u) dvolume relative to volume,with ennreal.ofreal density coercion. the normalization integral is the actual real bochner integral;the tilt definition alone does not include a probability or nonzero-normalization certificate. then these three conclusions hold simultaneously: mu is a probability measure; the e-valued identity x->x belongs to memlp exponent 2 under mu; for every v in e, ||v||^2/(beta:r)<=covbilin(mu)(v,v). memlp here means identity measurability modulo mu and finite second moment. the covariance term is the real centered covariance of the scalar projection <v,x> with itself under mu;the probability and l2 conclusions supply its stated moment regime. equivalently,with the vector bochner mean m=integral_e x dmu(x),the covariance is integral_e(<v,x>-<v,m>)^2 dmu(x). the measure mu is fixed by its displayed exponential tilt,not an arbitrary input measure assumed to be probability or l2. both probability normalization and l2 are conclusions. beta is strictly positive as a consequence of alpha>0 and alpha<=beta. no upper covariance bound,gradient integration-by-parts premise,provided matrix,critical point,positive-dimension restriction or numerical sampling statement is included. accepted sphmc arxiv:2609.06906v1 section4.1 lemma4.1 cramer-rao half; equation4.1; chewi auxiliary 20261006 main.pdf theorem3.5.8/corollary3.5.9 zero-based pages124-125 autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_covariance_lower autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/gibbsgradientmoment.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 68423dd177f97c0a5ba75ce69e6f36749618520ae63244d3b040437274241e42 accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual gibbs probability of a c2 strongly convex potential; linear-observable reverse covariance component. u, canonical volume, actual exponential tilt mu, id l2 and covariancebilin are reconstructed correctly. equivalent normalization is derived; covariance is evaluated with proven id l2, never a supplied matrix. domains scoped interface extends source finite real euclidean space to complete finite-dimensional real hilbert borel spaces, including dimension zero. exactly that domain; alpha,beta are nnreal and hessian is the actual nested frechet derivative. explicit-elaboration finite hilbert haar/orthonormal-basis apis cover euclidean source; zero case checked separately. quantifiers for every u,alpha,beta satisfying global bounds, simultaneous probability/l2 and all-directions covariance conclusions. no arbitrary supplied law, normalizer, moment or covariance certificate; every v quantified. equivalent unit-to-all-vector scaling retains v=0 and no measurable-selection claim. assumptions global c2, 0<alpha<=beta, alpha norm(v)^2 <= hess(u)[v,v] <= beta norm(v)^2 for every x,v. these and only the declared ambient instances/binders are assumed. equivalent analytic regularity hidden in book well-behaved is derived from these curvature hypotheses; no input moment/ibp certificate. conclusion actual tilt is probability, id in l2, and covariance(v,v)>=norm(v)^2/beta. all three conclusions retained with actual covariance and exact divisor. equivalent proof covers position l2, centered ibp, score bound, square expansion and true covariance api. scopes only the linear covariance cr corollary needed by lemma 4.1 reverse inequality. no covariance upper, nonlinear cr, bl, smoothing curvature pair or main result asserted. equivalent authored six-step proof and ledger disclose the narrower component and unfinished consumers. constant dependencies sharp dimension-free final constant beta^-1; alpha>0 supplies integrability and beta positivity. same beta denominator, no eta/dimension/u-dependent final factor. equiva