      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261006-gibbsgradientmoment semantic-audit astis-rt-20261006-gibbsgradientmoment companion:sphmc-gibbs-gradient-moment · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_gradient_moment. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder e is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its borel sigma-algebra and canonical lebesgue volume. dimension zero is included. u:e->r is twice continuously differentiable. the nonnegative real parameters alpha,beta satisfy 0<alpha and alpha<=beta. at every x,v the genuine hessian obeys alpha*norm(v)^2<=d2u(x)[v,v]<=beta*norm(v)^2. the alpha<=beta assumption remains in the public statement, despite its unused binder name. define mu=volume.tilted(-u), the actual normalized exponential gibbs measure. for the standard orthonormal basis (e_i), define h(x)=sum_i d2u(x)[e_i,e_i]. no minimizer, normalizing constant, weighted integrability or moment bound is supplied as an assumption. the actual measure mu is a probability measure. both norm(grad u)^2 and h are integrable under mu. their expectations are equal, and the expected squared gradient is at most beta*finrank(e). these are five public conclusions; bare exponential integrability, weighted linear integrability and directional integration by parts are proved internally. for every finite-dimensional complete real inner-product space e with its borel structure and canonical lebesgue volume, let d=dim_r e, with no assumption d>0. for every u:e->r and nonnegative real alpha,beta, assume 0<alpha, alpha<=beta, u is globally c2, and alpha||v||^2<=d2u(x)[v,v]<=beta||v||^2 for all x,v. put z=integral exp(-u) against volume, a real bochner integral with value zero if not integrable. define mu=volume.withdensity(x -> ennreal.ofreal(exp(-u(x))/z)), with real division by zero equal to zero and ofreal truncating negative values to zero. this is precisely the given tilted measure. for the full standard orthonormal basis e_i indexed by fin(d), set h(x)=sum_i d2u(x)[e_i,e_i]. then five conclusions hold under the same mu: mu is probability; x->||grad u(x)||^2 is bochner integrable; h is bochner integrable; integral ||grad u||^2 dmu=integral h dmu; and this integral<=beta*d. all derivatives and gradients are actual. the numeric upper bound explicitly depends only on beta,d; alpha remains a strictly positive assumption parameter. dimension zero uses the empty basis sum. accepted section6.3 reference-point construction: ideal gibbs gradient-moment proof component autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.analysis.gibbsgradientmoment.gibbs_gradient_moment autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/analysis/gibbsgradientmoment.lean true root-samplinglib-writer blind_reconstruction_r d8d893cf7c266e83aff4c19553407aa37fe0c704c73a360f3ba8e68fd7c7695b accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual gibbs law, actual gradient and full hessian diagonal trace in a genuine finite orthonormal basis. mu=volume.tilted(-u), h is exactly the finite sum, with actual gradient/integrals. equivalent old helper proof is independently included in current full-module review. domains disclosed complete finite-dimensional real hilbert/borel extension of finite euclidean ideal gibbs background; zero dimension allowed. same instances, nnreal alpha,beta and empty full basis in dimension zero. explicit-elaboration no coordinate-only approximation or supplied trace. quantifiers every c2 u and 0<alpha<=beta with global all-x,v curvature bounds. the unchanged fully expanded public type retains all premises and all five conjunctions. equivalent fresh #check/test elaboration confirms exact expanded type, including alpha<=beta. assumptions only ambient instances, positive lower curvature, ordered nonnegative bounds, c2 and actual hessian inequalities. no supplied probability/integrability/minimizer, score ibp or final integral certificate. equivalent gaussian domination and directional haar ibp prove those requirements. conclusion probability; integrability of gradient-square and h; equality of their actual gibbs expectations; expectation<=beta*finrank. all five conclusions reconstructed accurately. equivalent parseval and finite integral sum prove equality and beta*d, not a trace surrogate for directional covariance. scopes expanded ideal gibbs gradient-moment proof component used in section 6.3, not the entire reference-point/history/cost theorem. only this component, without stochastic-history or summed-cost guarantees. equivalent fresh current module/binding review grants no new mathematical credit to the unchanged old public theorem. constant dependencies exact upper bound beta*d; alpha positivity and u(0)/gradient(0) used only for domination. same beta*finrank and exact equality, zero-dimension sum handled. equivalent no hidden kappa/eta/noise/history constant in this standalone interface.",
