      "subtitle": "companion:gibbs-gradient-zero-kernel · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.GibbsGradientKernel.closed_gradient_zero_ae_constant.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0; W is C1 and exp(-W) is genuinely integrable. mu is exactly the normalized volume.tilted(-W) Gibbs probability, whose density is positive. No curvature or spectral gap is assumed.\nFix SAME original weighted-L2 real partial-linear gradient D with exact compact-C-infinity genuine gradient graph and closability before ALL u in D.closure.domain. Each queried u satisfies D.closure u=0 as an actual vector L2 class, not a pointwise derivative assertion or final kernel certificate.\nFor the SAME original Gibbs compact-gradient closure, EVERY domain element u with D.closure u=0 is weighted-AE ONE real constant. This is only one direction; constant-domain membership and full kernel equality are not asserted.\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0 and actual full-space volume. Genuine locally-volume-L1 u, all C1 compact directional tests with legal integrable products and zero weak derivative imply ONE real constant volume-AE. Actual normalized Gibbs W C1/exp(-W) integrable, SAME original exact compact-smooth graph D and closability give closed-gradient-zero implies weighted-AE constant. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S and original dense D_y precede ALL closure-domain u; source C2 curvature/eta cap/positive partitions retained but no additional curvature is needed by the generic kernel leaf. Only one direction; constants-domain converse, full kernel equality, centered residual/epsilon0/range/Poincare/BL/core and both main/composition remain open. No global-volume integrability of constants, classical differentiability of rough u, Nontrivial E, final kernel certificate, spectral gap or joint fiber selector. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel space with its canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero and all approved ambient instances. Let W:E->R be C1 and assume exp(-W) is integrable against volume. Define mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), the actual normalized Gibbs measure exp(-W)/integral exp(-W) times volume. In this full-space setting the approved context gives the positive normalized density; no separate positive-partition hypothesis is a displayed binder in this statement.\nFor every real-linear partial operator D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E), assume D is closable and its graph is characterized exactly as follows: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H, (a,H) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real function phi:E->R with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) mu-almost everywhere. D.closure is the genuine single-valued operator from that same graph closure, with its actual submodule domain.\nThen for every u in this SAME D.closure.domain, if D.closure(u)=0 as an actual vector L2(mu) class, there exists a real c with (u as a scalar L2(mu) representative)(x)=c for mu-almost every x.\nD is fixed before every u. The constant c is selected after u and may depend on u; no universal common constant for all zero-output elements is claimed. The premise is equality of the true closed-gradient output to the zero vector quotient, not a claim that the rough representative's totalized derivative vanishes pointwise. C1 regularity of W suffices here and no curvature, positive spectral gap, dense-domain condition or mean-zero assumption is added. This is a universal implication for a supplied closable exact-gradient D, not an existential construction of D. It is one direction only: zero output implies weighted-AE constancy. It does not produce constant-function domain membership or prove full kernel equality, nor a centered/epsilon-zero/range/Poincare or further inequality/core/composition theorem. There is no joint measurable choice of constants.",
