      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Thmtheorem1",
      "original_theorem": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nFinite real Hilbert/Borel full E including0, actual C2 W, true exp(-W) volume integrability and positive partition, BOTH global mI<=HessW<=MI with0<m<=M.\nGenuine vector id in L2 of normalized tilted Gibbs law. This canonical node keeps the moment premise explicit to rule out totalized covariance outside its integrable domain; the actual paper consumer produces it internally. No covariance/Poincare certificate input.\nFor each direction a, the genuine covariance bilinear form of the normalized BOTH-curvature Gibbs law satisfies Cov_mu(a,a)<=norma^2/m, using the actual linear observable, constant gradient and proven C1 Poincare.\nCanonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1<=kappa, 0<eta<=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace and CompleteSpace instances,with canonical ordinary full-space volume;dimension zero is included and no Nontrivial premise is imposed. Let W:E->R be C2 and assume actual volume Integrable exp(-W) and strictly positive volume partition Z=integral exp(-W). Let m,M:R satisfy 0<m<=M. For EVERY x,a:E assume BOTH actual diagonal Frechet-Hessian bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nAdditionally assume actual MemLp id 2 (volume.tilted(-W)):the position-vector identity function is genuinely AE strongly measurable with finite vector L2 norm for this law.\nDefine mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)),the actual normalized Gibbs measure exp(-W)/Z against volume. Then for EVERY a:E,\n  ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin(mu)(a,a) <= ||a||^2/m.\nThe covariance bilinear is the actual dual covariance composed with both Riesz/toDual maps. With the supplied genuine vector second moment and the normalized finite probability law,its diagonal is the true centered projection variance\n  integral <a,x-meanX>^2 dmu(x),where meanX=integral x dmu(x).\nThe explicit position MemLp hypothesis is retained;finite probability alone is not substituted for it. In the API the covariance bilinear outside vector L2 is defined as zero;that fallback is NOT the meaning of this estimate because this premise gives genuine moments. Measure.tilted is the actual withDensity ENNReal.ofReal(exp(h)/integral exp(h)) construction;it is totalized outside normalizable cases,with denominator zero yielding zero density.The explicit integrable positive partition here avoids that normalization fallback.\nThis theorem outputs the single all-direction covariance estimate for this law.It does not output additional operator/kernel/normalized-score identities,anisotropic Hessian-inverse bounds,Hessian regularity of another potential or a whole-paper theorem.Both m/M curvature controls and CompleteSpace are explicit,and all statements retain dimension zero.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
