nded expected cost. let e be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with normedaddcommgroup,innerproductspace r,finitedimensional r,measurablespace,borelspace and completespace instances,with canonical ordinary full-space volume;dimension zero is included and no nontrivial premise is imposed. let w:e->r be c2 and assume actual volume integrable exp(-w) and strictly positive volume partition z=integral exp(-w). let m,m:r satisfy 0<m<=m. for every x,a:e assume both actual diagonal frechet-hessian bounds m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv r (fderiv r w) x a) a, (fderiv r (fderiv r w) x a) a <= m*||a||^2. additionally assume actual memlp id 2 (volume.tilted(-w)):the position-vector identity function is genuinely ae strongly measurable with finite vector l2 norm for this law. define mu=volume.tilted(x->-w(x)),the actual normalized gibbs measure exp(-w)/z against volume. then for every a:e, probabilitytheory.covariancebilin(mu)(a,a) <= ||a||^2/m. the covariance bilinear is the actual dual covariance composed with both riesz/todual maps. with the supplied genuine vector second moment and the normalized finite probability law,its diagonal is the true centered projection variance integral <a,x-meanx>^2 dmu(x),where meanx=integral x dmu(x). the explicit position memlp hypothesis is retained;finite probability alone is not substituted for it. in the api the covariance bilinear outside vector l2 is defined as zero;that fallback is not the meaning of this estimate because this premise gives genuine moments. measure.tilted is the actual withdensity ennreal.ofreal(exp(h)/integral exp(h)) construction;it is totalized outside normalizable cases,with denominator zero yielding zero density.the explicit integrable positive partition here avoids that normalization fallback. this theorem outputs the single all-direction covariance estimate for this law.it does not output additional operator/kernel/normalized-score identities,anisotropic hessian-inverse bounds,hessian regularity of another poten