ctor memlp id2. all premises retained; true finite normalized probability derived. same canonical b standing conditions are explicit, not imported to source a. c1 linear projection l2 from hx.const_inner, gradient constanta and its l2 from actual probability. no poincare/covariance certificate. conclusion true cov_mu(a,a)<=norma^2/m for all a. exactly the all-direction scalar covariance estimate. equivalent actual c1 curvature poincare gives mvar<=energy; constant-gradient probability energy=norma^2, genuine covariance/variance bridge and division by positivem. scopes source-linked canonical isotropic sufficient prerequisite; full anisotropic bl, source main results and reflected pbps law separate. single isotropic all-direction covariance conclusion; no kernel/hessian/main extras. equivalent authored c1-poincare or route honestly replaces only the sufficient scalar covariance invocation. no book/external full bl theorem is admitted. constant dependencies exact coefficient1/m, dimension independent; m remains premise but is absent from scalar constant. exact1/m, no prefactor1/2 or trace/dimension factor. same integral constant gradient against actual probability is norma^2. upper curvature belongs to actual poincare proof premises; it is not erased merely because m disappears from result.",
