      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. W is C1, exp(-W) is integrable, and mu is exactly volume.tilted(-W).\nD is the original closable partial gradient on L2(mu), with graph exactly compact smooth scalar representatives and their genuine gradients modulo mu-a.e. D is fixed before epsilon>0 and forcing f in L2(mu). The genuine solution u/G/r and all local volume facts are derived, not supplied.\nFor every C2 real cutoff chi with compact topological support, the same u chosen before all chi yields explicit v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*G+u*grad chi and Fchi=chi*r+2 inner(grad chi,G)+u Delta chi. Neither sign, normalized mass, compact derivative bounds nor localized PDE/H2 certificate is assumed. All localized L2 and test integrals use volume; variational identities use L2(mu).\nFor the exact normalized Gibbs mu, original closable D fixed before epsilon/forcing, construct the actual resolvent u in D.closure.domain. Retain the actual all-domain variational equation, ordinary locally integrable u/G, all C1 compact directional weak-gradient tests, squared local integrability of r=epsilon*u+inner(grad W,G)-f, compact-volume L2 of u/G/r and every C2 original distribution test. For every C2 compact chi define v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*G+u*grad chi, Fchi=chi*r+2 inner(grad chi,G)+u Delta chi. Prove genuine global-volume L2 of v/Gchi/Fchi and each topological support contained in tsupport chi. For every C1 compact psi/direction a both weak-gradient products are L1 with integral psi inner(Gchi,a)=-integral v Dpsi[a]. For every C2 compact phi both PDE products are L1 with integral v Delta phi=integral Fchi phi. The same u is chosen before all cutoffs; only smooth test/cutoff functions have classical derivatives.\nSame actual original D/u/G/r, one u before all C2 compact chi: derive actual compact support/global volume L2 of chi*u, chi*G+u*gradchi, chi*r+2<gradchi,G>+u*Delta chi, all C1 compact weak-gradient and C2 compact distribution PDE with every L1 term legal. No localized weighted closure-domain membership, H2, Schwartz/tempered adapter, global core/Bochner, BL/Poincare, epsilon0, noncompact domain, measurable y-selector or either main/composition. Reflected/RGO law/scale remain distinct; TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with Borel measurable structure and canonical Lebesgue volume, permitting dimension zero. The approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. Let W:E->R be C1 and assume exp(-W) is Lebesgue integrable. Define mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)), i.e. the measure with density exp(-W)/integral exp(-W) relative to volume; positive normalization is not built into that definition.\nFor every real-linear partial operator D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E), assume D is closable and its graph is exactly characterized as follows: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H,\n  (a,H) belongs to graph(D) if and only if there exists a smooth compactly supported phi:E->R with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) mu-almost everywhere.\nD.closure is the operator with that same topological graph closure, on its submodule domain. This D is fixed before epsilon and the forcing f.\nFor every real epsilon>0 and every f in L2(mu;R), there exists u in D.closure.domain satisfying all conclusions below simultaneously. Write u_rep and f_rep for the standard measurable representatives of the actual scalar L2 classes, and G_rep for the standard representative of G=D.closure(u) in L2(mu;E). Abbreviate the exact scalar expression by\n  r(x)=epsilon*u_rep(x)+<gradient(W)(x),G_rep(x)>_E-f_rep(x).\n(a) For every z in D.closure.domain,\n  epsilon*<u,z>_{L2(mu;R)}+<D.closure(u),D.closure(z)>_{L2(mu;E)}=<f,z>_{L2(mu;R)}.\n(b) u_rep and G_rep are locally integrable with respect to Lebesgue volume.\n(c) For every C1 compactly supported psi:E->R and every direction a in E, both x->psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E and x->u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are Lebesgue integrable, and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\n(d) The real scalar function x->||r(x)||^2 is locally Lebesgue integrable.\n(e) For every compact set K in E, u_rep, G_rep and r each satisfy MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to volume.restrict K, including a.e. strong measurability and finite L2 norm for that actual restricted measure.\n(f) For every C2 compactly supported phi:E->R, the two functions x->u_rep(x)*Laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) and x->r(x)*phi(x) are Lebesgue integrable and\n  integral u_rep(x)*Laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) dx = integral r(x)*phi(x) dx.\n(g) For every C2 compactly supported chi:E->R, define the following actual functions, with the notation v_chi corresponding to the let-defined v in the statement:\n  v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x),\n  G_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by G_rep(x) + u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x),\n  F_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),G_rep(x)>_E+u_rep(x)*Laplacian.laplacian(chi)(x).\nThen v_chi, G_chi and F_chi each satisfy MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to the full volume measure, with actual a.e. strong measurability and finite global L2 norm. All three topological supports are contained in the topological support of chi:\n  tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi),\n  tsupport(G_chi) subset tsupport(chi),\n  tsupport(F_chi) subset tsupport(chi).\nFor every C1 compactly supported psi:E->R and every a in E, both x->psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are Lebesgue integrable, and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor every C2 compactly supported phi:E->R, both x->v_chi(x)*Laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) and x->F_chi(x)*phi(x) are Lebesgue integrable, and\n  integral v_chi(x)*Laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) dx = integral F_chi(x)*phi(x) dx.\nAll unannotated local-integrability, integrability and integral assertions use canonical Lebesgue volume. The Hilbert inner products use the actual law mu. Laplacian.laplacian on chi and phi is the actual finite-basis test-function trace; no classical Laplacian of the arbitrary representative u_rep or v_chi is asserted. The same u and G serve every test and every cutoff. chi is any real C2 compact-support function, without positivity, value-range or plateau assumptions. The localized functions are given by these three formulas, not independent existential choices; no membership of v_chi in a weighted partial-operator domain is asserted.\nThe result is a universal implication for any such supplied D; it does not add a dense-domain premise or assert existence of D. One u is selected per epsilon,f before all compact restrictions, ordinary tests and cutoffs. No solution uniqueness, H2 regularity, classical Delta u, core characterization, measurable parameter selection or quantitative bound is an explicit conclusion.",
