roducts are l1 with integral psi inner(gchi,a)=-integral v dpsi[a]. for every c2 compact phi both pde products are l1 with integral v delta phi=integral fchi phi. the same u is chosen before all cutoffs; only smooth test/cutoff functions have classical derivatives. same actual original d/u/g/r, one u before all c2 compact chi: derive actual compact support/global volume l2 of chi*u, chi*g+u*gradchi, chi*r+2<gradchi,g>+u*delta chi, all c1 compact weak-gradient and c2 compact distribution pde with every l1 term legal. no localized weighted closure-domain membership, h2, schwartz/tempered adapter, global core/bochner, bl/poincare, epsilon0, noncompact domain, measurable y-selector or either main/composition. reflected/rgo law/scale remain distinct; tv never transfers unbounded expected cost. let e be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with borel measurable structure and canonical lebesgue volume, permitting dimension zero. the approved ambient section instances are part of the contract. let w:e->r be c1 and assume exp(-w) is lebesgue integrable. define mu=volume.tilted(x->-w(x)), i.e. the measure with density exp(-w)/integral exp(-w) relative to volume; positive normalization is not built into that definition. for every real-linear partial operator d:l2(mu;r)->l2(mu;e), assume d is closable and its graph is exactly characterized as follows: for every scalar l2 class a and vector l2 class h, (a,h) belongs to graph(d) if and only if there exists a smooth compactly supported phi:e->r with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and h=gradient(phi) mu-almost everywhere. d.closure is the operator with that same topological graph closure, on its submodule domain. this d is fixed before epsilon and the forcing f. for every real epsilon>0 and every f in l2(mu;r), there exists u in d.closure.domain satisfying all conclusions below simultaneously. write u_rep and f_rep for the standard measurable representatives of the actual scalar l2 classes, and g_rep for the standard representative of g=d.closure(u) in l2(mu;e). abbreviate the exact scalar expression by r(x)=epsilon*u_rep(x)+<gradient(w)(x),g_rep(x)>_e-f_rep(x). (a) for every z in d.closure.domain, epsilon*<u,z>_{l2(mu;r)}+<d.closure(u),d.closure(z)>_{l2(mu;e)}=<f,z>_{l2(mu;r)}. (b) u_rep and g_rep are locally integrable with respect to lebesgue volume. (c) for every c1 compactly supported psi:e->r and every direction a in e, both x->psi(x)*<g_rep(x),a>_e and x->u_rep(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are lebesgue integrable, and integral psi(x)*<g_rep(x),a>_e dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. (d) the real scalar function x->||r(x)||^2 is locally lebesgue integrable. (e) for every compact set k in e, u_rep, g_rep and r each satisfy memlp at exponent 2 with respect to volume.restrict k, including a.e. strong measurability and finite l2 norm for that actual restricted measure. (f) for every c2 compactly supported phi:e->r, the two functions x->u_rep(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) and x->r(x)*phi(x) are lebesgue integrable and integral u_rep(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) dx = integral r(x)*phi(x) dx. (g) for every c2 compactly supported chi:e->r, define the following actual functions, with the notation v_chi corresponding to the let-defined v in the statement: v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x), g_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by g_rep(x) + u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x), f_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),g_rep(x)>_e+u_rep(x)*laplacian.laplacian(chi)(x). then v_chi, g_chi and f_chi each satisfy memlp at exponent 2 with respect to the full volume measure, with actual a.e. strong measurability and finite global l2 norm. all three topological supports are contained in the topological support of chi: tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(g_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(f_chi) subset tsupport(chi). for every c1 compactly supported psi:e->r and every a in e, both x->psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are lebesgue integrable, and integral psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. for every c2 compactly supported phi:e->r, both x->v_chi(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) and x->f_chi(x)*phi(x) are lebesgue integrable, and integral v_chi(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) dx = integral f_chi(x)*phi(x) dx. all unannotated local-integrability, integrability and integral assertions use canonical lebesgue volume. the hilbert inner products use the actual law mu. laplacian.laplacian on chi and phi is the actual finite-basis test-function trace; no classical laplacian of the arbitrary representative u_rep or v_chi is asserted. the same u and g serve every test and every cutoff. chi is any real c2 compact-support function, without positivity, value-range or plateau assumptions. the localized functions are given by these three formulas, not independent existential choices; no membership of v_chi in a weighted partial-operator domain is asserted. the result is a universal implication for any such supplied d; it does not add a dense-domain premise or assert existence of d. one u is selected per epsilon,f before all compact restrictions, ordinary tests and cutoffs. no solution uniqueness, h2 regularity, classical delta u, core characterization, measurable parameter selection or quantitative bound is an explicit conclusion. accepted pbps2609.06905v1 section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 and appendixc.1 omitted same-solution compact localization analytic prerequisite; sphmc2609.06906v1 section4.1 actual bl dependency only. no numbered source localization theorem is claimed. autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.functionalinequalities.localizedweakresolvent.localized_weak_resolvent autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/functionalinequalities/localizedweakresolvent.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 7be0a1a1ee2cb0049518334bd41825ce89ddc5c96fb4ba974eff02407bed5c26 accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects exact normalized gibbs from c1 w, supplied original closable compact-smooth gradi