      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a full finite real Hilbert/Borel space with its canonical full-space volume, including dimension0; its vector-space connectedness and nonzero Haar volume are used. Real u is genuinely LocallyIntegrable against volume; it need not be globally volume integrable.\nFor EVERY real C1 compactly supported test psi and EVERY direction a, u(x)*D_a psi(x) is genuinely integrable against volume and its integral is0. No classical derivative of the rough u is assumed.\nA genuine locally-volume-integrable rough real function whose every legal C1 compact directional weak derivative is zero is volume-AE ONE real constant, including0.\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0 and actual full-space volume. Genuine locally-volume-L1 u, all C1 compact directional tests with legal integrable products and zero weak derivative imply ONE real constant volume-AE. Actual normalized Gibbs W C1/exp(-W) integrable, SAME original exact compact-smooth graph D and closability give closed-gradient-zero implies weighted-AE constant. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S and original dense D_y precede ALL closure-domain u; source C2 curvature/eta cap/positive partitions retained but no additional curvature is needed by the generic kernel leaf. Only one direction; constants-domain converse, full kernel equality, centered residual/epsilon0/range/Poincare/BL/core and both main/composition remain open. No global-volume integrability of constants, classical differentiability of rough u, Nontrivial E, final kernel certificate, spectral gap or joint fiber selector. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space Lebesgue/Haar volume, including dimension zero. The approved ambient instances belong to the contract; E is a connected real vector space and the full-space volume is nonzero.\nLet u:E->R be locally integrable with respect to this volume. Assume that for every real C1 compactly supported test psi:E->R and every direction a:E, the actual function x->u(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) is volume-integrable and\n  integral u(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx = 0.\nThen there exists ONE real c such that u(x)=c for volume-almost every x in E.\nLocal integrability is ordinary volume-local L1, not a global-volume L1 requirement. The derivative is the genuine real Frechet derivative of the C1 test function, not a totalized zero derivative asserted for the rough u. The same c works on the whole space, not a separately chosen value on each neighborhood/test/direction; c may depend on u. The conclusion is an almost-everywhere equality, not pointwise constancy or classical differentiability of u. No mollifier, sequence, or derivative certificate is an input. No disconnected-domain analogue, uniqueness assertion, weighted operator-domain converse, spectral gap or additional functional inequality is an explicit conclusion.",
