      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261006-pbpsconditionalc1resolvent semantic-audit astis-rt-20261006-pbpsconditionalc1resolvent companion:pbps-conditional-c1-resolvent · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalc1resolvent.conditional_c1_resolvent. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder explicit analytic prerequisite restatement: e has the same full-space finite-dimensional real hilbert/borel structure, including dimension zero. v is c2 with true all-point/all-direction alpha i<=hess v<=beta i, alpha,beta nnreal, 0<alpha<=beta, eta>0 and beta eta<=1. the original gibbs law, genuine independent gaussian augmentation, selected r,s kernels, reflected w_y, finite positive partition and fixed original gradient d per fiber are derived by the existing actual conditional producer. neither normalization nor a convenient replacement operator is supplied. the potential is reflected, with quarter hessian scaling. the unreflected sphmc rgo potential/law is different. existence is fiberwise for every y; no joint measurable resolvent selection, unbounded cost transfer or macroscopic h1/poincare theorem is asserted. for actual c2 v with 0<alpha<=beta global hessian bounds, eta>0 and beta eta<=1, construct the actual gibbs-gaussian augmentation and common markov conditional kernels r,s, with disintegration r and s_y=(r_y)#(x->2x-y). s_y is the true normalized reflected gibbs law for w_y(u)=v((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta), with c2 regularity and positive integrable weight. for every y, retain one dense closable exact compact-smooth gradient d, fixed before epsilon/input, and derive every positive-epsilon l2 forcing weak solution, ordinary weak gradient/local integrability and all c1 compact weighted volume test equations. no measurable solution selection in y is claimed. same actual compact-gradient graph closure admits c1 compact function/gradient pairs; actual positive-epsilon weak resolvent has all c1 compact weighted volume tests and genuine ordinary weak gradient. actual pbps reflected conditional r/s law and original fixed d precede epsilon/input. no local h2, global operator-core/bochner, conditional poincare/bl, centered epsilon limit, noncompact constant/linear domains, measurable y-selection, sphmc hessian lower/full4.1, pbps hypocoercivity or either complete main/composition. tv never transfers unbounded expected cost. let e be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space, equipped with its borel measurable space and canonical lebesgue measure dx; dimension zero is allowed. let v:e->r and alpha,beta be nonnegative real scalars and eta a real scalar. assume alpha>0, alpha<=beta, v is c2, and, for every x,v in e, alpha*||v||^2 <= (fderiv r (fderiv r v) x v) v <= beta*||v||^2. assume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. define mu = volume.tilted(x -> -v(x)), j = map((x,g) -> (x,x+sqrt(eta)*g), mu.prod(stdgaussian e)), w_y(z) = v((y+z)/2) + ||z-y||^2/(8*eta). here volume.tilted(-f) is the volume measure with density exp(-f)/integral exp(-f); the gaussian/product/pushforward are the actual measures. there exist kernels r,s:e->measure e with all the following properties: r and s are markov kernels; r is a conditional kernel for j.map prod.swap, disintegrating the swapped joint (y,x); and for every y in e, s(y) is the pushforward of r(y) under x -> 2*x-y. for every y in e, s(y)=volume.tilted(z -> -w_y(z)), w_y is c2, exp(-w_y) is lebesgue integrable, and its lebesgue integral is strictly positive. moreover, for this y there exists a real-linear partial operator d:l2(s(y);r) -> l2(s(y);e) whose domain is dense in l2(s(y);r), which is closable and whose closure is closed, and whose graph is characterized exactly as follows: for every a in l2(s(y);r) and h in l2(s(y);e), (a,h) belongs to graph(d) iff there exists phi:e->r that is smooth and has compact support, with a=phi s(y)-almost everywhere and h=gradient(phi) s(y)-almost everywhere. for this same d, for every real epsilon>0 and every f in l2(s(y);r), there exists u in domain(d.closure) satisfying all the following conclusions simultaneously. write u_rep and f_rep for the usual representatives of the scalar l2 classes, and g_rep for the usual representative of g=d.closure(u) in l2(s(y);e). (1) for every v in domain(d.closure), epsilon*<u,v>_{l2(s(y);r)} + <d.closure(u),d.closure(v)>_{l2(s(y);e)} = <f,v>_{l2(s(y);r)}. (2) u_rep and g_rep are locally integrable with respect to lebesgue volume. (3) for every c1 compactly supported psi:e->r and every direction v in e, both x -> psi(x)*<g_rep(x),v>_e and x -> u_rep(x)*(fderiv r psi x v) are lebesgue integrable and integral psi(x)*<g_rep(x),v>_e dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv r psi x v) dx. (4) for every c1 compactly supported psi:e->r, all three functions x -> exp(-w_y(x))*(u_rep(x)*psi(x)), x -> exp(-w_y(x))*<g_rep(x),gradient(psi)(x)>_e, x -> exp(-w_y(x))*(f_rep(x)*psi(x)) are lebesgue integrable, and epsilon*integral exp(-w_y(x))*(u_rep(x)*psi(x)) dx + integral exp(-w_y(x))*<g_rep(x),gradient(psi)(x)>_e dx = integral exp(-w_y(x))*(f_rep(x)*psi(x)) dx. one pair of kernels r,s works for all y. for each y one d is chosen before epsilon and f, and works for all of them. for each epsilon and f the same u serves every variational test v, every directional weak-gradient test, and every weighted test psi. the hilbert inner products use s(y), whereas all local-integrability assertions, directional weak-gradient integrals, partition integrals, and the final weighted test integrals use lebesgue volume. the displayed weighted equation uses exp(-w_y) without dividing by its partition integral. the conclusions about s(y), w_y, and d hold for every y, not merely almost every y; the conditional-kernel conclusion itself has its usual disintegration meaning. accepted pbps arxiv:2609.06905v1 appendix c.1 proof of lemma b.1/lemma c.1 compact-smooth-to-weighted-h1 analytic prerequisite; section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 actual reflected conditional law. sphmc2609.06906v1 section4.1 bl actual-resolvent dependency only. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalc1resolvent.conditional_c1_resolvent autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalc1resolvent.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 b3fb5c6c0d8dda8e5b27ec35b79703f5af0966b475c45a1f30095128a297300f accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual gibbs-gaussian augmentation, common conditional r/s, reflected potential and same original gradient per fiber. mu, actual j, markov r/s, s_y=reflection#r_y=volume.tilted(-w_y), actual d_y and its actual weak solutions. equivalent full proof preserves parent witnesses and law equality then calls genuine c1 resolvent. no supplied conditional law or arbitrary chosen output. domains finite-dimensional real hilbert/borel full space incl0; reflected pbps fibers, not unreflected sphmc rgo. exactly full-space e, actual gaussian product/pushforward and scalar/vector l2(s_y); ordinary integrals volume. equivalent w_y(u)=v((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta). reflection pushforward has inverse(y+u)/2 and volume jacobian2^-d, hence quarter hessian scaling; no laws/operators identified without adapter. quantifiers one r,s for every y; for each y one d before epsilon/f; one u for every test. all y (not merely a.e.) fiber density/c2/l1/z/d conclusions; same d_y for all positive epsilon and l2 inputs; all five weak-solution groups simultaneous. equivalent whole statement and refine chain retain original r,s,d. disintegration retains its usual a.e. semantics; fiber construction is everywhere. no joint measurable y-selection of resolvents. assumptions actual c2 v with nnreal alpha,beta,0<alpha<=beta, all-point/all-vector true hessian bounds; eta>0,beta eta<=1. identical hypotheses, including the inherited source eta cap. equivalent conditionalgradient actual parent constructs kernels and dense closable exact gradient from true normalized reflected law. no normalizer, c1-domain, law, h2 or final pde certificate supplied. conclusion common kernels/disintegration/reflection, everywhere normalized reflected c2 potential with integrable positive partition, dense exact closable d with closed closure, same-d full c1 compact resolvent conclusions. all original kernel/potential/operator and all variational/local/directional/weighted conjunctions retained. equivalent proof obtains exact parent hfiber, preserves all witnesses, lowers actual c2 w to c1 and rewrites only actual s_y law equality. the final equation uses exp(-w_y) without z_y. scopes actual pbps reflected conditional analytic prerequisite with disclosed hilbert/0d extension. fiberwise fixed-d c1 compact weak tests only; no macro h1 extension, poincare or numerical/sphmc law claim. explicit-elaboration publication role prerequisite and six source-ordered lesson steps honor source section2.2/c1 boundaries. only a disclosed analytic prerequisite. no quoted numbered pbps theorem, macroscopic h1 extension, noncompact constant/linear test domain, local laplacian/h2 regularity, global operator core/bochner, poincare/bl, epsilon-zero limit, measurable fiber solution selection, sphmc hessian lower/full4.1, pbps hypocoercivity, complete main theorem, composition or work-cost claim. constant dependencies alpha,beta,eta cap as source; w_y gaussian denominator8eta, reflection2 and quarter hessian. same factors and positive-epsilon consumer, no added convergence/spectral constants. equivalent source unreflected rgo has denominator2eta and reflected hessian is one quarter(alpha+eta^-1)/(beta+eta^-1). dirichlet scaling under reflection is factor4, not an unchanged operator. dimension0 requires no unit-vector/positive-dimension assumption.",
