      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nSource V C2, NNReal0<alpha<=beta and actual allpoint/allvector alphaI<=HessV<=betaI; eta>0,beta*eta<=1. Full finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel E including0.\nActual common Gaussian J=(x,x+sqrteta*xi)#(mu*Gamma), Markov/disintegrating R and actual reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y. W_y(u)=V((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta), exact normalized reflected density and positive integrable partition. SAME original dense closable compact-smooth gradient D_y chosen BEFORE ALL meanzero L2 forcing f and epsilon sequences.\nMean-zero forcing is with respect to actual S_y; real variational solutions and scaled residual limit are constructed fiberwise. No identification of auxiliary conditional versions, jointly measurable solution selector, or normalized score derivative.\nConstruct true common Gaussian/disintegrating/reflected J/R/S and one original dense closable D_y before ALL centered forcing/epsilon sequences. Construct true same-domain variational solutions on actual S_y with strong epsilon_n*u_n zero limit, retaining source curvature/eta cap/partition/order.\nFix real complete Hilbert H,K and SAME actual closed partial linear D before forcing f, positive epsilon sequence->0 and actual variational solutions u_n. H separable explicitly; actual finite-dimensional Borel Gibbs E gives genuine scalar L2 separability by countably generated finite measure, not finite-dimensional L2. Actual energy/scaled domain, Riesz WeakDual sequential compactness, WithLp2 genuine graph double-orthogonal and forcing orthogonal to EVERY kernel give strong epsilon*u_n->0 and epsilon*D(u_n)->0 without Poincare or uniform unscaled u. True C1 Gibbs W/positive exponential normalizer/actual normalized probability and SAME exact original compact-smooth closable gradient beforeALLf; genuine mean-zero L2 forcing is integrable and kernel-orthogonal via actual AEconstant. Construct actual positive-epsilon variational solutions, retaining ordinary localL1/weakC1 test integrabilities. Actual common PBPS J/R/S/reflected law/sourceC2 alpha-beta/eta cap/positive partitions and originalD_y beforeALLf/epsilon; fiberwise only. No epsilon0 solution/range/unscaled uniform bound/extra spatial moment/supplied weak-limit or graph or residual certificate/Poincare/BL/core/adjoint/jointselector/normalized conditional-score derivative/both main/composition; TV never transfers unbounded expectedcost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances and canonical volume, including dimension zero. Let V:E->R, alpha,beta:NNReal,eta:R. Assume alpha cast>0,alpha<=beta,V C2 and for every x,a:E BOTH\n  alpha*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a <= beta*||a||^2.\nAssume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Define actual measures/potential\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  J=map((x,g)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*g),mu.prod(stdGaussian E)),\n  W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+||z-y||^2/(8*eta).\nThese are genuine normalized Gibbs tilt,independent product with standard real Hilbert Gaussian and pushforward.\nThere exist common kernels R,S:E->Measure E with R,S Markov,R a true conditional kernel for J.map Prod.swap,and for every y S(y)=(R(y)).map(x->2*x-y).\nFor EVERY y, S(y)=volume.tilted(z->-W_y(z)),W_y C2,exp(-W_y) volume-integrable with strictly positive volume integral. There exists ONE original real-linear partial gradient D:Lp R 2 (S(y))->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 (S(y)) with dense domain in scalar L2,closability,closed closure,and exact graph: for every scalar a/vector G,(a,G) is in D.graph iff exists smooth compactly supported real phi with a=phi S(y)-AE and G=gradient(phi) S(y)-AE.\nFor EVERY actual scalar L2(S(y)) forcing f with integral f(x) dS(y)(x)=0,and EVERY epsilon:N->R positive at every n and tending atTop0,there exists ONE family u:N->this SAME D.closure.domain such that for EVERY n and EVERY v:D.closure.domain,\n  epsilon_n*<u_n,v>_{L2(S(y);R)}+<D.closure(u_n),D.closure(v)>_{L2(S(y);E)}=<f,v>_{L2(S(y);R)},\nand epsilon_n scalar-multiplied by the actual scalar L2(S(y)) class u_n tends atTop strongly to the zero quotient.\nOne common R,S precedes all y,one original D per y precedes ALL centered f and ALL positive-to-zero sequences,one family follows f/epsilon before every n and variational test. All y have density/operator facts;conditional disintegration has usual version scope,not a claim about all possible versions on every y. Only the literal reflected normalized-law equality is asserted,no equality of two distinct conditional kernels.\nThe displayed sequence output is exactly a variational family and scaled-function strong-zero. It does not separately list forcing Integrable,ordinary local weak/PDE/cutoff facts or scaled-gradient convergence as output conjuncts. Forcing is actual weighted L2 with actual law mean0;no abstract orthogonality premise or centered-u assumption replaces it. Partition integrability uses volume;means,inner products and limit use S(y). No monotonicity,rate,uniform unscaled bound,joint measurable y/f/sequence selection,unscaled/range/epsilon0/further functional inequality,score variance,full adjoint/core/Hessian or main/expected-cost composition conclusion is asserted.",
