    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-PBPSConditionalCompactCoercivity",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-PBPSConditionalCompactCoercivity",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:pbps-conditional-compact-coercivity · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalCompactCoercivity.conditional_compact_coercivity.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nSame finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel structure including dimension zero. Source V is C2; alpha,beta are NNReal with 0<alpha<=beta, actual all-point/all-vector alpha I<=Hess V<=beta I, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1.\nActual augmentation J=(x,x+sqrt(eta)*xi)#(mu*standardGaussian), common probability/disintegrating R/S, S_y=(2x-y)#R_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), C2 W_y and positive integrable partition are genuine parent conclusions. The accepted curvature parent yields HessW_y >= ((alpha+eta^-1)/4)I for this same explicit W, without equating its auxiliary kernels with the resolvent kernels.\nOriginal dense closable exact compact-smooth gradient D_y and closed closure are fixed before epsilon/f. For every epsilon>0 and f in actual L2(S_y), ONE actual u precedes ALL real C2 compact cutoffs chi. Parent all-domain variational identity, original ordinary weak/local facts and actual localized v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*D.closure(u)+u*gradientchi, Fchi=chi*r+2inner(gradientchi,D.closure(u))+u*Deltachi, r=epsilon*u+inner(gradientW,D.closure(u))-f, are retained.\nConstruct genuine common R/S; for every y fix original D_y before epsilon/f, choose ONE u before ALL C2 compact chi. Retain actual R/S/reflection/positive partitions, the same original D graph/density/closability/closed closure, ONE u and all-domain variational identity, original local u/G/r square integrability, every original C1 weak-gradient test/C2 weak PDE, and every cutoff volumeL2/support/weak identity. For each cutoff produce actual weighted classes vW,AW,GW linked to v=chi*u, Gchi and Achi=inner(gradientW,Gchi)-Fchi, original (vW,GW) in D_y.closure.graph and ((alpha+eta^-1)/4)*norm(GW)^2<=norm(AW)^2.\nDerive genuine compact weighted L2/AE classes vW/GW/AW for actual v/G/(innergradWG-F), same original D.closure graph membership and lambda*normGW^2<=normAW^2 via actual same ordinary-to-weighted smooth sequence. Source fixes originalD before epsilon/f and ONEu before ALLC2chi. No supplied weighted domain/core/convergence/coercivity certificate; no rough classical Hessian or full adjoint/generator-core identity, globalcutoff/tail/Bochner,epsilon0/kernel/range/noncompactlinear/Poincare/BL/jointmeasurablechoice/main/composition. Reflected quarter/fourfold constants exact. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume; dimension zero is allowed. Let V:E->R, alpha,beta:NNReal and eta:R. Assume alpha cast to R is strictly positive, alpha<=beta, V is C2, and for all x,a in E,\n  alpha*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a <= beta*||a||^2.\nAssume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Define the actual measures and potential\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  J=map((x,g)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*g),mu.prod(stdGaussian E)),\n  W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+||z-y||^2/(8*eta).\nThe tilt has density exp(-V)/integral exp(-V) with respect to volume; prod/map/stdGaussian are the actual independent product, pushforward and standard real Hilbert Gaussian.\nThere exist kernels R,S:E->Measure E satisfying all the following: both are Markov kernels; R is a conditional kernel disintegrating the swapped actual joint J.map Prod.swap; and for every y in E, S(y)=(R(y)).map(x->2*x-y).\nFor every y in E, S(y)=volume.tilted(z->-W_y(z)), W_y is C2, exp(-W_y) is volume-integrable, and its volume integral is strictly positive. For this y there exists a real-linear partial operator D:L2(S(y);R)->L2(S(y);E) with dense domain in scalar L2(S(y)), D closable and D.closure closed. Its graph is exactly characterized by: for every scalar L2 a and vector L2 H, (a,H) is in graph(D) iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real function q with a=q S(y)-almost everywhere and H=gradient(q) S(y)-almost everywhere.\nFor this same D, for every real epsilon>0 and every f in L2(S(y);R), there exists u in D.closure.domain satisfying all conclusions below simultaneously. Write u_rep and f_rep for the standard measurable representatives of the scalar quotient classes and G_rep for the actual standard vector L2 representative of G=D.closure(u). Abbreviate the displayed residual by\n  r(x)=epsilon*u_rep(x)+<gradient(W_y)(x),G_rep(x)>_E-f_rep(x).\n(a) For every z in D.closure.domain,\n  epsilon*<u,z>_{L2(S(y);R)}+<D.closure(u),D.closure(z)>_{L2(S(y);E)}=<f,z>_{L2(S(y);R)}.\n(b) u_rep and G_rep are locally integrable with respect to ordinary Lebesgue volume.\n(c) For every real C1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:E, both x->psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E and x->u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\n(d) x->||r(x)||^2, using the real scalar norm, is locally volume-integrable.\n(e) For every compact K in E, u_rep,G_rep,r each satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to volume.restrict K.\n(f) For every real C2 compactly supported q, both x->u_rep(x)*Delta(q)(x) and x->r(x)*q(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral u_rep(x)*Delta(q)(x) dx = integral r(x)*q(x) dx.\n(g) For every real C2 compactly supported chi, define the actual functions (v_chi denotes the statement's let-defined v)\n  v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x),\n  G_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by G_rep(x)+u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x),\n  F_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),G_rep(x)>_E+u_rep(x)*Delta(chi)(x).\nThen v_chi,G_chi,F_chi each satisfy actual global MemLp 2 volume, and each has its topological support contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(G_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(F_chi) subset tsupport(chi).\nFor every real C1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:E, both x->psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable, and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor every real C2 compactly supported psi, both x->v_chi(x)*Delta(psi)(x) and x->F_chi(x)*psi(x) are volume-integrable, and\n  integral v_chi(x)*Delta(psi)(x) dx = integral F_chi(x)*psi(x) dx.\nUnder this same cutoff define the actual scalar A_chi(x)=<gradient(W_y)(x),G_chi(x)>_E-F_chi(x), with exactly the minus sign before F_chi. Then v_chi,G_chi,A_chi each satisfy actual MemLp at exponent 2 with respect to S(y). There exist scalar classes vW,AW in Lp R 2 (S(y)) and a vector class GW in Lp E 2 (S(y)) such that vW=v_chi S(y)-almost everywhere, AW=A_chi S(y)-almost everywhere and GW=G_chi S(y)-almost everywhere, and simultaneously\n  (vW,GW) belongs to this original D.closure.graph,\n  ((alpha+1/eta)/4)*||GW||_{L2(S(y);E)}^2 <= ||AW||_{L2(S(y);R)}^2.\nThe scalar alpha in the coefficient is its NNReal-to-real cast and 1/eta is the real reciprocal; the quarter factor is exact. Weighted membership and inequality are conclusions about the returned actual quotient classes, not assumptions added to their existence.\nOne common R,S pair serves every y; one D per y is selected before all epsilon and forcing f; one actual u and its G are chosen per epsilon/f before ALL C2 compact cutoffs; each cutoff's v_chi,G_chi,F_chi,A_chi are formula-defined and its returned weighted classes are chosen afterward. All y have the stated density/operator conclusions. Conditional disintegration itself retains usual version scope, not an assertion about every possible conditional version at every y. No jointly measurable y-dependent solution or class selector is asserted.\nOriginal Hilbert inner products and final quotient norms use S(y); all ordinary local integrability, compact restrictions, real weak-gradient/PDE integrals and localized global volume-L2 conclusions use canonical volume. MemLp means actual a.e. strong measurability and finite norm. AE class identities are under S(y), not pointwise/support equalities of quotient representatives. C2 compact cutoffs have no extra range, positivity or plateau assumption. Classical Laplacians act only on C2 tests/cutoffs; no classical derivative/Hessian of rough u or v_chi is asserted. The statement is cutoff-wise weighted closure membership and scalar coercivity; it does not remove cutoffs or assert a global coercivity/Bochner theorem, adjoint/core equality, epsilon=0/kernel/range theorem, further functional inequality, or complete kernel-composition result.",
