its topological support contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(g_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(f_chi) subset tsupport(chi). for every real c1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:e, both x->psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are volume-integrable, and integral psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. for every real c2 compactly supported psi, both x->v_chi(x)*delta(psi)(x) and x->f_chi(x)*psi(x) are volume-integrable, and integral v_chi(x)*delta(psi)(x) dx = integral f_chi(x)*psi(x) dx. under this same cutoff define the actual scalar a_chi(x)=<gradient(w_y)(x),g_chi(x)>_e-f_chi(x), with exactly the minus sign before f_chi. then v_chi,g_chi,a_chi each satisfy actual memlp at exponent 2 with respect to s(y). there exist scalar classes vw,aw in lp r 2 (s(y)) and a vector class gw in lp e 2 (s(y)) such that vw=v_chi s(y)-almost everywhere, aw=a_chi s(y)-almost everywhere and gw=g_chi s(y)-almost everywhere, and simultaneously (vw,gw) belongs to this original d.closure.graph, ((alpha+1/eta)/4)*||gw||_{l2(s(y);e)}^2 <= ||aw||_{l2(s(y);r)}^2. the scalar alpha in the coefficient is its nnreal-to-real cast and 1/eta is the real reciprocal; the quarter factor is exact. weighted membership and inequality are conclusions about the returned actual quotient classes, not assumptions added to their existence. one common r,s pair serves every y; one d per y is selected before all epsilon and forcing f; one actual u and its g are chosen per epsilon/f before all c2 compact cutoffs; each cutoff's v_chi,g_chi,f_chi,a_chi are formula-defined and its returned weighted classes are chosen afterward. all y have the stated density/operator conclusions. conditional disintegration itself retains usual version scope, not an assertion about every possible conditional version at every y. no jointly measurable y-dependent solution or class selector is asserted. original hilbert inner products and final quotient norms use s(y); all ordinary local integrability, compact restrictions, real weak-gradient/pde integrals and localized global volume-l2 conclusions use canonical volume. memlp means actual a.e. strong measurability and finite norm. ae class identities are under s(y), not pointwise/support equalities of quotient representatives. c2 compact cutoffs have no extra range, positivity or plateau assumption. classical laplacians act only on c2 tests/cutoffs; no classical derivative/hessian of rough u or v_chi is asserted. the statement is cutoff-wise weighted closure membership and scalar coercivity; it does not remove cutoffs or assert a global coercivity/bochner theorem, adjoint/core equality, epsilon=0/kernel/range theorem, further functional inequality, or complete kernel-composition result. accepted pbps arxiv2609.06905v1 section2.2 reflected conditional law and appendixc.1 omitted analytic gradient-domain/coercivity prerequisite; sphmc arxiv2609.06906v1 section4.1 bl covariance-upper prerequisite. authored compact weighted scalar coercivity and same original gradient-domain membership, not a numbered theorem/global core/poincare/bl. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalcompactcoercivity.conditional_compact_coercivity autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalcompactcoercivity.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 3a8e8a2f96a7ab2af3e583e3db2eb594152a3623b4c0795ae9a4982608920a46 accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual gibbs v law, gaussian augmentation j, common disintegrating r and reflected s, explicit w_y, original gradient d_y and same resolvent u; localized v/gchi/fchi and achi. same j from independent standard gaussian, r/s/reflection/law and actual formula-defined w_y/u/g/r/v/gchi/fchi/achi; actual ae-linked output classes. equivalent full107-line consumer, full128-line nonquadratic test and actual parent interfaces/proofs checked. curvature helper auxiliary r2/s2 are used only for