      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261006-pbpsconditionalcompactsmoothgraph semantic-audit astis-rt-20261006-pbpsconditionalcompactsmoothgraph companion:pbps-conditional-compact-smooth-graph · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalcompactsmoothgraph.conditional_compact_smooth_graph. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement: same finite real hilbert/borel/canonical-volume structure including dimension zero. v is c2, alpha/beta nnreal, 0<alpha<=beta, all-point/all-vector alpha i<=hess v<=beta i; eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. true augmentation j=(x,x+sqrt(eta)*xi)#(mu*standardgaussian), common actual disintegrating probability kernels r/s, s_y=(2x-y)#r_y=volume.tilted(-w_y), w_y(z)=v((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), and actual positive integrable partitions are derived from accepted parents. reflected/rgo laws/operators and quarter hessian/fourfold dirichlet scaling remain distinct. original dense closable compact-smooth gradient d_y with closed closure is fixed before epsilon/forcing. for every epsilon>0 and f in l2(s_y), choose one actual u before all c2 compact cutoffs chi. derive the actual v=chi*u, gchi=chi*d.closure(u)+u*gradientchi and fchi=chi*r+2inner(gradientchi,d.closure(u))+u*deltachi, r=epsilon*u+inner(gradientw,d.closure(u))-f; all required volumel2/support/weak equations are genuine parent conclusions. construct common r/s; for each y fix original d_y before epsilon/f, choose one u before all c2 compact chi. retain original exact d graph, dense/closable/closed properties, all-domain positive-epsilon variational identity, ordinary locally integrable u/g, all-c1 compact directional weak-gradient identities, local squared-r integrability, compact-volumel2 of u/g/r, original all-c2 pde, and all actual localized volumel2/support/first/second weak identities. the actual volumel2 properties are