ctly supported q, both x->u_rep(x)*delta(q)(x) and x->r(x)*q(x) are volume-integrable and integral u_rep(x)*delta(q)(x) dx = integral r(x)*q(x) dx. (g) for every real c2 compactly supported chi, define the following actual functions (v_chi denotes the statement's let-defined v): v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x), g_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by g_rep(x)+u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x), f_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),g_rep(x)>_e+u_rep(x)*delta(chi)(x). then v_chi,g_chi,f_chi each satisfy actual global memlp 2 volume, and their topological supports each are contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(g_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(f_chi) subset tsupport(chi). for every real c1 compactly supported psi and every direction a:e, both x->psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are volume-integrable and integral psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. for every real c2 compactly supported psi, both x->v_chi(x)*delta(psi)(x) and x->f_chi(x)*psi(x) are volume-integrable and integral v_chi(x)*delta(psi)(x) dx = integral f_chi(x)*psi(x) dx. for this chi there exist scalar classes vl,fl in lp r 2 volume and a vector class gradl in lp e 2 volume with vl=v_chi volume-almost everywhere, fl=f_chi volume-almost everywhere and gradl=g_chi volume-almost everywhere. there exist a compact kprime in e and one sequence phi:n->schwartzmap e r such that all tsupport(phi_n) are contained in kprime and (phi_n).tolp 2 volume tends attop to vl in actual scalar l2(volume) norm. there further exists a family hphig of actual memlp 2 volume witnesses for the genuine gradients gradient(phi_n), for every n, such that (hphig_n).tolp(gradient(phi_n)) tends attop to gradl in vector l2(volume) norm, and (delta(phi_n)).tolp 2 volume tends attop to fl in scalar l2(volume) norm. these are the same sequence and common outer compact for all n and all three limits. one r,s pair works for all y. for each y one d is chosen before all epsilon>0 and forcing f; for each epsilon,f one u and its actual output g are chosen before all cutoffs chi; for each chi its actual formula-defined localized functions are fixed before the ae-linked classes, common compact and single sequence. kprime and sequence may depend on y,epsilon,f,u,chi and need not be common across different cutoffs. no relation kprime containing tsupport(chi) is asserted. conditional disintegration has its standard scope, not a claim about every conditional version on every y. all density/operator conclusions hold for every y, not merely almost every y. all original hilbert inner products use s(y); ordinary local integrability, weak/pde integrals, compact restrictions, localized global l2, selected real classes and all three norm limits use volume. memlp includes actual a.e. strong measurability and finite norm; selected class identities are volume-ae, not pointwise representative/support equalities. derivatives and laplacians of the smooth approximants and c1/c2 tests are actual classical operators; no pointwise total laplacian of rough u/v_chi is asserted. the cutoff only has c2 and compact support, without range/positivity/plateau assumptions. there is no joint measurable y-dependent solution/sequence choice, weighted-domain/core certification, explicit bessel/sobolev conclusion, norm estimate, further functional inequality or kernel-composition assertion. accepted pbps arxiv:2609.06905v1 section2.2 actual reflected conditional law and appendixc.1 omitted analytic gradient-domain prerequisite; sphmc arxiv:2609.06906v1 section4.1 covariance-upper/bl prerequisite only. authored compact ordinary-volume smooth graph approximation, not a quoted numbered theorem. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalcompactsmoothgraph.conditional_compact_smooth_graph autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalcompactsmoothgraph.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 44ead7747222f0b