d by gradient(chi)(x), f_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),g_rep(x)>_e+u_rep(x)*delta(chi)(x). then v_chi,g_chi,f_chi each satisfy actual global memlp 2 volume, and each topological support is contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(g_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(f_chi) subset tsupport(chi). for every real c1 compactly supported psi and direction a:e, both x->psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are volume-integrable and integral psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. for every real c2 compactly supported q, both x->v_chi(x)*delta(q)(x) and x->f_chi(x)*q(x) are volume-integrable and integral v_chi(x)*delta(q)(x) dx = integral f_chi(x)*q(x) dx. all memlp assertions mean actual a.e. strong measurability and finite l2 norm for their displayed measure. the ordinary local, compact-restricted and test assertions use canonical volume, whereas hilbert inner products and both global inequalities use s(y). derivatives/laplacians of potentials/tests/cutoffs are actual operators; no pointwise classical derivative or total laplacian of the rough representative u is asserted. the same u/g serves all tests, all compact restrictions, both inequalities and all cutoffs. chi only has c2 and compact support; no range, positivity or plateau condition is added. the coefficient uses alpha cast to r and the exact real reciprocal 1/eta divided by 4. the global inequalities are ((alpha+1/eta)/4)*||d.closure(u)||^2 <= ||f-epsilon*u||^2 <= ||f||^2, with all norms under actual s(y). the approved reflected curvature constants are (alpha+1/eta)/4 and (beta+1/eta)/4; the output does not add a standalone hessian inequality for w_y as another conjunct. one common r,s pair works for every y, one d per y works for every positive epsilon/forcing, and one u per epsilon/f is chosen before all c2 cutoffs. all y have the stated density/operator facts, not merely almost every y; conditional disintegration retai