      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored analytic prerequisite restatement:\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0; V C2 with NNReal 0<alpha<=beta and actual all-point/all-vector alphaI<=HessV<=betaI. eta>0 and beta*eta<=1 are retained from the genuine conditional parent.\nActual common Gaussian J=(x,x+sqrteta*xi)#(mu*standardGaussian), Markov/disintegrating R and reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y. True W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), S_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), integrable/positive partition and SAME dense closable exact original gradient D_y are produced before ALL closure-domain u.\nConstruct actual common J/R/S and for each y SAME original dense/closable/exact compact-gradient D_y before ALL closure-domain elements u. Every such u with D_y.closure u=0 is S_y-AE ONE real constant. Actual laws, source hypotheses and partitions remain; no joint measurable selector or full kernel/Poincare result.\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0 and actual full-space volume. Genuine locally-volume-L1 u, all C1 compact directional tests with legal integrable products and zero weak derivative imply ONE real constant volume-AE. Actual normalized Gibbs W C1/exp(-W) integrable, SAME original exact compact-smooth graph D and closability give closed-gradient-zero implies weighted-AE constant. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S and original dense D_y precede ALL closure-domain u; source C2 curvature/eta cap/positive partitions retained but no additional curvature is needed by the generic kernel leaf. Only one direction; constants-domain converse, full kernel equality, centered residual/epsilon0/range/Poincare/BL/core and both main/composition remain open. No global-volume integrability of constants, classical differentiability of rough u, Nontrivial E, final kernel certificate, spectral gap or joint fiber selector. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel space with canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero and all approved section ambient instances. Let V:E->R, alpha,beta:NNReal and eta:R. Assume alpha cast to R is strictly positive, alpha<=beta, V is C2, and for every x,a:E both exact actual Hessian bounds hold:\n  alpha*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a <= beta*||a||^2.\nAssume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Define actual measures and reflected potential\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  J=map((x,g)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*g),mu.prod(stdGaussian E)),\n  W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+||z-y||^2/(8*eta).\nTilted means the actual exp(-potential)/partition density against volume; standard Gaussian, independent product and pushforward are genuine measures.\nThere exist kernels R,S:E->Measure E with all the following simultaneous properties: R and S are Markov kernels; R disintegrates the swapped actual joint J.map Prod.swap; and for every y:E,\n  S(y)=(R(y)).map(x->2*x-y).\nFor every y:E, S(y)=volume.tilted(z->-W_y(z)), W_y is C2, exp(-W_y) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. For this y there exists a real-linear partial operator D:L2(S(y);R)->L2(S(y);E) with dense domain in the scalar L2 space, D closable and D.closure closed. Its original graph is exactly characterized by: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H, (a,H) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real function phi with a=phi S(y)-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) S(y)-almost everywhere.\nFor every u in this SAME D.closure.domain, if D.closure(u)=0 as an actual vector L2(S(y)) class, there exists a real c such that the scalar quotient's standard representative equals c S(y)-almost everywhere.\nOne common R,S pair is chosen before all y. For each y one original D is chosen before ALL of its closure-domain u; a suitable D is not chosen afresh for each u. The constant c may depend on y and u and is selected after them. Potential/density/operator conclusions hold for every y, not only almost every y. The conditional-kernel property has its usual disintegration/version scope, not a claim that all possible conditional versions have these pointwise identities. All unannotated partition integrability/integrals use volume; graph and zero-output constancy use actual weighted quotient classes and AE under S(y). No rough classical derivative or Hessian is asserted. No joint measurable y-dependent operator/constant selector, constant-domain converse or full kernel equality, resolvent estimate, centered/epsilon-zero/range/Poincare or further inequality, core/main or expected-cost composition theorem is concluded.",
