          "reconstructed": "Exists R,S both Markov, R a conditional kernel for the swapped actual J, S y the pushforward of R y under x->2*x-y for every y. For every y, S y=volume.tilted(-W_y), W_y C2, exp(-W_y) volume-integrable with strictly positive integral; exists dense-domain closable scalar-to-vector D with closed closure and exact smooth compact gradient graph modulo S y. One selected closure-domain u satisfies the Hilbert variational equation for all closure-domain tests; volume local integrability of original u_rep/G_rep; for every C1 compact test and every direction the two L1 products and ordinary weak-gradient equation with minus sign; local volume integrability of ||r||^2; MemLp 2 (volume.restrict K) for u_rep,G_rep,r for every compact K; for every C2 compact test the two L1 products and unweighted positive-sign equation integral u_rep*Delta(phi)=integral r*phi. For every C2 compact cutoff chi, let v_chi=chi*u_rep, G_chi=chi scalar-multiplied by G_rep + u_rep scalar-multiplied by gradient chi, and F_chi=chi*r + 2*<gradient chi,G_rep> + u_rep*Delta chi. All three are actual global MemLp 2 volume and each topological support is contained in tsupport chi. For every C1 compact psi and direction a, both psi*<G_chi,a> and v_chi*Dpsi[a] are volume-integrable and integral psi*<G_chi,a>=-integral v_chi*Dpsi[a]. For every C2 compact phi both v_chi*Delta phi and F_chi*phi are volume-integrable and integral v_chi*Delta phi=integral F_chi*phi. Every integrability assertion is retained separately from the equations. Here r=epsilon*u_rep+<gradient(W_y),G_rep>-f_rep.",
