          "reconstructed": "One R,S pair serves all y. Each y has one D serving every positive epsilon/forcing; each epsilon/f yields one u serving all tests and cutoffs. True conditional-kernel property retains usual disintegration scope and does not quantify over every conditional version on every y. Scalar/vector representatives and original G come from the actual quotient/closure. Volume conclusions are ordinary unweighted integrals, distinct from S y Hilbert inner products. Localized v_chi/G_chi/F_chi use actual original representatives and fixed formulas, with global volume L2 and support inclusions. No localized weighted-domain assertion, pointwise total Laplacian u, H2, core theorem, joint measurable y selection, uniqueness, invariance or iteration result is an explicit conclusion.",
