ported chi:e->r, define the following actual functions, with the notation v_chi corresponding to the let-defined v in the statement: v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x), g_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by g_rep(x) + u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x), f_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),g_rep(x)>_e+u_rep(x)*laplacian.laplacian(chi)(x). then v_chi, g_chi and f_chi each satisfy memlp at exponent 2 with respect to the full volume measure, with actual a.e. strong measurability and finite global l2 norm. all three topological supports are contained in the topological support of chi: tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(g_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(f_chi) subset tsupport(chi). for every c1 compactly supported psi:e->r and every a in e, both x->psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) are lebesgue integrable, and integral psi(x)*<g_chi(x),a>_e dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv r psi x a) dx. for every c2 compactly supported phi:e->r, both x->v_chi(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) and x->f_chi(x)*phi(x) are lebesgue integrable, and integral v_chi(x)*laplacian.laplacian(phi)(x) dx = integral f_chi(x)*phi(x) dx. all unannotated local-integrability, integrability and integral assertions use canonical lebesgue volume. the hilbert inner products use the actual law s(y). laplacian.laplacian on chi and phi is the actual finite-basis test-function trace; no classical laplacian of the arbitrary representative u_rep or v_chi is asserted. the same u and g serve every test and every cutoff. chi is any real c2 compact-support function, without positivity, value-range or plateau assumptions. the localized functions are given by these three formulas, not independent existential choices; no membership of v_chi in a weighted partial-operator domain is asserted. one r,s pair works for all y, and every y has the potential/density identity and a suitable d; these conclusions are not limited to almost every y. conditional disintegration has its usual scope and does not assert this for every possible version of r on exceptional y. d is selected fiberwise once and works for all epsilon>0 and all scalar l2 forcing f; u is chosen before every cutoff chi. there is no joint measurable y-dependent d or u selection, uniqueness, h2 or classical-laplacian conclusion, core characterization, invariance/iteration or quantitative bound. accepted pbps2609.06905v1 section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 and appendixc.1 omitted same-solution compact localization analytic prerequisite; sphmc2609.06906v1 section4.1 actual bl dependency only. no numbered source localization theorem is claimed. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionallocalizedresolvent.conditional_localized_resolvent autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionallocalizedresolvent.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 039aa1043bde1b493efea53d026739c1b39dafee87e0f0b8e384fddd008d9973 accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actual normalized gibbs mu and independent gaussian noisy joint j, common true markov/disintegrating r and reflected s, actual w_y, produced original d_y and same u/g/r with explicit cutoff functions. c2 potential v with nnreal alpha,beta and real eta; actual normalized gibbs tilt mu; actual gaussian independent product/noisy joint j and midpoint-quadratic w_y; markov r,s with true swapped-joint conditional disintegration and reflection pushforward; fiberwise dense closable partial gradient d and closed closure on actual l2(s y); epsilon, forcing f, original solution u/g/residual r; compact restrictions, c1/c2 tests and all explicit localized cutoff objects. equivalent calls actual ordinaryweakresolvent once, retains all original conjuncts and exact same u/g/r. introduces all cutoffs only after existential u; no supplied final localization/pde/h2 certificate. entire87-line proof calls actual conditionalgradient to obtain common r/s, exact actual j/reflection/density/positive partition and original dense closab