      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalLocalizedSobolev.conditional_localized_sobolev.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE has the same finite real Hilbert/Borel/full-space structure including dimension zero. V is C2 with alpha,beta NNReal, 0<alpha<=beta, all-point/all-vector alpha I<=Hess V<=beta I; eta>0 and beta eta<=1.\nConstruct the true Gaussian/Gibbs augmentation J, common Markov/disintegrating R/S, exact reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), C2 and positive integrable partition.\nFor every fiber fix original dense closable exact compact-smooth gradient D_y with closed closure before epsilon/forcing. For each epsilon>0/f in L2(S_y), one actual u/G/r serves all C2 compact chi. Derive all local/global volume facts and PDE inputs from the accepted actual conditional localization. No measurable joint fiberwise solution/class selector, unreflected RGO identity or localized weighted-domain membership is assumed.\nConstruct genuine common R/S and original fiber D_y before epsilon/f; choose ONE actual u before ALL C2 compact cutoffs. Retain all-domain variational identity, ordinary locally integrable u/G, all C1 compact directional weak-gradient tests, locally integrable squared r=epsilon*u+inner(grad W_y,G)-f, compact-volume L2 of u/G/r and all original C2 compact distribution tests. For every C2 compact chi retain v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*G+u*grad chi, Fchi=chi*r+2 inner(grad chi,G)+u Delta chi, all three global-volume L2/support inclusions, all C1 localized weak-gradient and C2 localized PDE identities with legal products. For each cutoff, Construct actual vc,Fc in complex L2(volume), with vc=volume-a.e. ofReal(v) and Fc=volume-a.e. ofReal(Fchi). For every complex Schwartz psi, both (Delta psi)*ofReal(v) and psi*ofReal(Fchi) are L1 and their integrals equal. For T_v=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc) and T_F=Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc), derive Delta T_v=T_F and MemSobolev 2 2 T_v. The latter uses B2 T=T-(2pi)^(-2) Delta T and a genuine complex L2 witness, not a supplied regularity result. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/quarter Hessian and Dirichlet scales remain distinct.\nDerive actual all-complex-Schwartz tested PDE with both products L1, genuine complex volume-L2 classes/AE embeddings, actual TD Laplacian and MemSobolev2 using B2=I-(2pi)^-2 Delta. Genuine conditional same originalD before epsilon/f, one actualu before allC2 compactcutoffs; retain parent properties. No real mixed-second representatives/Hessian, original weighted localized-domain membership/core/Bochner, BL/Poincare/epsilon0/measurable fiber selector/full4.1/main/composition. Reflected/RGO laws/operators/scales distinct; TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances and canonical ordinary Lebesgue volume; dimension zero is allowed. Let V:E->R, alpha,beta:NNReal and eta:R. Assume alpha cast to R is strictly positive, alpha<=beta, V is C2, and for every x,a in E,\n  alpha*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a <= beta*||a||^2.\nAssume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Define the actual measures and potential\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  J=map((x,g)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*g),mu.prod(stdGaussian E)),\n  W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+||z-y||^2/(8*eta).\nThe tilted measure has density exp(-V)/integral exp(-V) against volume; the Gaussian is standard on the real Hilbert space, and prod and map are actual independent product and pushforward.\nThere exist kernels R,S:E->Measure E with the following simultaneous properties: both are Markov kernels; R is a true conditional kernel disintegrating J.map Prod.swap; for every y in E, S(y)=(R(y)).map(x->2*x-y).\nFor every y in E, S(y)=volume.tilted(z->-W_y(z)), W_y is C2, exp(-W_y) is Lebesgue integrable, and its Lebesgue integral is strictly positive. For this y there exists a real-linear partial operator D:L2(S(y);R)->L2(S(y);E), with dense domain in the actual scalar L2 space, D closable and D.closure closed. Its graph is exactly characterized by: for every scalar L2 class a and vector L2 class H, (a,H) belongs to graph(D) if and only if there exists a smooth compactly supported real function phi with a=phi S(y)-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) S(y)-almost everywhere.\nFor this same D, for every real epsilon>0 and every f in scalar L2(S(y)), there exists u in D.closure.domain satisfying all the following conclusions simultaneously. Let u_rep,f_rep be the standard representatives of the actual scalar L2 classes and G_rep the standard vector L2 representative of G=D.closure(u). Abbreviate the exact displayed scalar expression by\n  r(x)=epsilon*u_rep(x)+<gradient(W_y)(x),G_rep(x)>_E-f_rep(x).\n(a) For every z in D.closure.domain,\n  epsilon*<u,z>_{L2(S(y);R)}+<D.closure(u),D.closure(z)>_{L2(S(y);E)}=<f,z>_{L2(S(y);R)}.\n(b) u_rep and G_rep are locally integrable with respect to ordinary Lebesgue volume.\n(c) For every real C1 compactly supported psi and every direction a in E, both x->psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E and x->u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_rep(x),a>_E dx = - integral u_rep(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\n(d) x->||r(x)||^2, using the scalar real norm, is locally volume-integrable.\n(e) For every compact K contained in E, u_rep,G_rep and r each satisfy MemLp at exponent 2 for volume.restrict K, including actual a.e. strong measurability and finite norm with respect to that restricted measure.\n(f) For every real C2 compactly supported phi, both x->u_rep(x)*Delta(phi)(x) and x->r(x)*phi(x) are volume-integrable and\n  integral u_rep(x)*Delta(phi)(x) dx = integral r(x)*phi(x) dx.\n(g) For every real C2 compactly supported chi, define the following actual functions (v_chi denotes the statement's let-defined v):\n  v_chi(x)=chi(x)*u_rep(x),\n  G_chi(x)=chi(x) scalar-multiplied by G_rep(x) + u_rep(x) scalar-multiplied by gradient(chi)(x),\n  F_chi(x)=chi(x)*r(x)+2*<gradient(chi)(x),G_rep(x)>_E+u_rep(x)*Delta(chi)(x).\nThen v_chi,G_chi,F_chi each satisfy actual global MemLp 2 volume. Their topological supports each are contained in tsupport(chi): tsupport(v_chi) subset tsupport(chi), tsupport(G_chi) subset tsupport(chi), and tsupport(F_chi) subset tsupport(chi).\nFor every real C1 compactly supported psi and a in E, both x->psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E and x->v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) are volume-integrable, and\n  integral psi(x)*<G_chi(x),a>_E dx = - integral v_chi(x)*(fderiv R psi x a) dx.\nFor every real C2 compactly supported phi, both x->v_chi(x)*Delta(phi)(x) and x->F_chi(x)*phi(x) are volume-integrable, and\n  integral v_chi(x)*Delta(phi)(x) dx = integral F_chi(x)*phi(x) dx.\nFurthermore for this chi there exist vc,Fc in Lp C 2 volume with vc=(x->(v_chi(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere and Fc=(x->(F_chi(x):C)) volume-almost everywhere, such that all the following hold for these same classes:\n  For every psi in SchwartzMap E C, x->Delta(psi)(x)*(v_chi(x):C) and x->psi(x)*(F_chi(x):C) are both volume-integrable and\n    integral Delta(psi)(x)*(v_chi(x):C) dx = integral psi(x)*(F_chi(x):C) dx;\n  Delta(Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)) = Lp.toTemperedDistribution(Fc);\n  MemSobolev 2 2 (Lp.toTemperedDistribution(vc)).\nOne pair R,S works for all y; each y has one D fixed before all epsilon/forcing choices; each epsilon,f has one u fixed before all cutoffs; after each cutoff one pair vc,Fc is chosen before all Schwartz tests. All y have the stated density/operator conclusions, not merely almost every y. Conditional-kernel disintegration retains its usual scope, without claiming identities for every possible version on exceptional y. All Hilbert inner products use S(y); all unannotated local-integrability, compact restrictions, global localized L2 and distribution/Schwartz integrals use ordinary volume. The arbitrary real C2 compact cutoff has no positivity, range or plateau assumption. There is no joint measurable y-dependent D/u/class selection or localized weighted-domain/core assertion.\nLp C 2 volume is the genuine complex L2 quotient with its standard measurable representative. These volume-a.e. identities bind the chosen classes to the actual pointwise real functions cast into C; they do not assert pointwise support identities for the chosen complex representatives. Every Schwartz test is a genuine smooth rapidly decreasing complex function on the real space E, and no compact-support restriction is imposed on it. Its derivatives are real Frechet derivatives. Pairings and displayed integrals use ordinary complex multiplication with no complex conjugation. Lp.toTemperedDistribution is the genuine complex-linear distribution embedding whose value at psi is integral psi(x)*the L2 representative(x) dx. The distribution Laplacian is the true tempered-distribution operator. MemSobolev 2 2 means there exists an actual fprime in Lp C 2 volume with besselPotential E C 2 of the displayed distribution equal to Lp.toTemperedDistribution(fprime); its multiplier is (1+||xi||^2)^(2/2). The approved Fourier convention is Delta T=-(2*pi)^2 FM(||xi||^2)T. This order-2 Bessel-Sobolev assertion is not a pointwise classical Laplacian, a real Hessian representative, or a weighted-core conclusion.",
