e s(y); all unannotated local-integrability, compact restrictions, global localized l2 and distribution/schwartz integrals use ordinary volume. the arbitrary real c2 compact cutoff has no positivity, range or plateau assumption. there is no joint measurable y-dependent d/u/class selection or localized weighted-domain/core assertion. lp c 2 volume is the genuine complex l2 quotient with its standard measurable representative. these volume-a.e. identities bind the chosen classes to the actual pointwise real functions cast into c; they do not assert pointwise support identities for the chosen complex representatives. every schwartz test is a genuine smooth rapidly decreasing complex function on the real space e, and no compact-support restriction is imposed on it. its derivatives are real frechet derivatives. pairings and displayed integrals use ordinary complex multiplication with no complex conjugation. lp.totempereddistribution is the genuine complex-linear distribution embedding whose value at psi is integral psi(x)*the l2 representative(x) dx. the distribution laplacian is the true tempered-distribution operator. memsobolev 2 2 means there exists an actual fprime in lp c 2 volume with besselpotential e c 2 of the displayed distribution equal to lp.totempereddistribution(fprime); its multiplier is (1+||xi||^2)^(2/2). the approved fourier convention is delta t=-(2*pi)^2 fm(||xi||^2)t. this order-2 bessel-sobolev assertion is not a pointwise classical laplacian, a real hessian representative, or a weighted-core conclusion. accepted pbps arxiv:2609.06905v1 section2.2 actual reflected conditional law and appendixc.1 compact-gradient density/closedness analytic prerequisite; sphmc arxiv:2609.06906v1 section4.1 covariance-upper/bl dependency only. this authored compact-schwartz-sobolev prerequisite is not a quoted numbered source theorem. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionallocalizedsobolev.conditional_localized_sobolev autosamplingtheory/examplecases/