      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0; source V C2 and NNReal0<alpha<=beta with true all-point/all-vector alphaI<=HessV<=betaI, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1.\nActual common Gaussian J=(x,x+sqrteta*xi)#(mu*standardGaussian), Markov/disintegrating R and reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y; actual W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), S_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), integrable/positive partition. SAME dense closable exact original D_y precedes ALL constants/domain elements/directions.\nActual unnormalized parameter-y score s_y(u)[a]=-DV((y+u)/2)[a]/2-inner(y-u,a)/(4eta), not the negative u-gradient or already centered normalized score. Its C1/scalarL2/boundedgradient is produced by the accepted score theorem; only literal S2_y=S_y from exact density is used.\nConstruct true common conditional J/R/S, positive reflected C2 potential and SAME original D_y before ALL c/u/a. Produce actual constant domain, full kernel equality and actual noncompact unnormalized directional-y score C1/gradient bound with true scalar/vector L2 class pair in SAME D_y.closure.graph. No R2/R identity or alternate operator is assumed.\nActual finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0. Fix actual finite mu and SAME original closable exact compact-C-infinity gradient D BEFORE ALL C1 f with actual MemLp f2mu and MemLp gradientf2mu. Genuine smooth cutoff exhaustion/derivative-product/weighted L2 limits put actual class pair into SAME closure graph, without compact support or extra spatial moment. Finite mu constants are genuinely in original closure domain with outputzero. For actual C1 Gibbs W/exp(-W) integrable, combine actual constants-domain with accepted one-way implication for full zero-output iff AEconstant on SAME D. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/Sdensity/positive partitions/sourceC2 alpha beta eta cap and original D_y beforeALL constants/u/directions; real unnormalized y-score C1/L2/boundedgradient from accepted score producer transfers along ONLY explicit reflected density equality S2_y=S_y and enters SAME original closed graph. No R2=R or alternateD equality, global ordinary L1, C-infinity potential, gradient of rough representative, Nontrivial E, spatial moment, supplied domain/fullkernel/spectralgap/Poincare certificate, epsilon0/range/centering/measurablejointselector/core/BL/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be the full finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical ordinary volume, including dimension zero. All approved section instances belong to the contract. Let V:E->R, alpha,beta:NNReal and eta:R. Assume alpha cast to R is strictly positive, alpha<=beta, V is C2, and for every x,b:E both bounds hold:\n  alpha*||b||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x b) b,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x b) b <= beta*||b||^2.\nAssume eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Define the actual measures, potential and real continuous-linear-functional-valued function\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  J=map((x,g)->(x,x+sqrt(eta)*g),mu.prod(stdGaussian E)),\n  W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+||z-y||^2/(8*eta),\n  s_y(z)=-(1/2) scalar-multiplied by fderiv R V ((y+z)/2) -(1/(4*eta)) scalar-multiplied by innerSL R (y-z).\nEquivalently, for every direction a:E,\n  s_y(z)[a]=-(1/2)*(fderiv R V ((y+z)/2) a)-<y-z,a>_E/(4*eta).\nThis is the unnormalized parameter-y directional score defined by the actual formula; it is neither the negative z-gradient nor a centered normalized score. All measure operations are actual: normalized Gibbs tilt, independent product with the standard finite real Hilbert Gaussian, and pushforward.\nThere exist kernels R,S:E->Measure E such that both are Markov kernels, R is a true conditional kernel disintegrating J.map Prod.swap, and for every y, S(y)=(R(y)).map(x->2*x-y).\nFor every y:E, S(y)=volume.tilted(z->-W_y(z)), W_y is C2, exp(-W_y) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. There exists for this y one real-linear partial operator D:Lp R 2 (S(y)) ->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 (S(y)) with dense domain in the actual scalar L2 space, D closable and D.closure closed. Its graph is exactly the smooth compact-function/gradient pairs: for every scalar a and vector H, (a,H) is in D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi with a=phi S(y)-almost everywhere and H=gradient(phi) S(y)-almost everywhere.\nThis SAME D simultaneously has all the following properties:\n(1) For every c:R, there exists u in D.closure.domain such that its scalar quotient representative equals the constant function x->c S(y)-almost everywhere and D.closure(u)=0 in vector L2(S(y)).\n(2) For every u in D.closure.domain, D.closure(u)=0 if and only if there exists c:R such that its scalar representative is c S(y)-almost everywhere.\n(3) For every direction a:E, the real function z->s_y(z)[a] is C1. For every z:E its actual Riesz gradient satisfies\n  ||gradient(q->s_y(q)[a])(z)||_E <= ((1/eta-alpha)/4)*||a||_E.\nFor this same directional function there exists hp:MemLp (z->s_y(z)[a]) 2 (S(y)), and there exists hq:MemLp (gradient(z->s_y(z)[a])) 2 (S(y)), such that the actual ordered pair of scalar/vector quotient classes (hp.toLp the directional-score function,hq.toLp its actual gradient) belongs to this SAME D.closure.graph.\nOne common R,S pair precedes every y; each y has one D preceding ALL constants c, ALL closure-domain u and ALL directions a. Constant-domain witnesses and score L2 proof witnesses are produced after their respective universal inputs. Each directional gradient bound is all-point, and its coefficient is exactly (1/eta-alpha cast)/4; the eta cap together with alpha<=beta makes it nonnegative without adding a separate assumption. No alternate D is selected for a constant, u or direction. All y have the stated density/operator conclusions, while conditional disintegration retains its usual version scope. No extra equality between two conditional kernels is asserted.\nAll original/operator/score L2 classes, graph links and constant AE identities use S(y); the partition integrability and integrals use ordinary volume. Actual standard measurable representatives are used, with AE identities only rather than exact pointwise/support identities. No rough classical Hessian, covariance/centered-score statement, spectral-gap or further functional inequality, centered-residual/epsilon-zero/range theorem, complete adjoint/core, main/cost composition theorem, or jointly measurable fiber/constant/direction selection is concluded.",
