ssian, and pushforward. there exist kernels r,s:e->measure e such that both are markov kernels, r is a true conditional kernel disintegrating j.map prod.swap, and for every y, s(y)=(r(y)).map(x->2*x-y). for every y:e, s(y)=volume.tilted(z->-w_y(z)), w_y is c2, exp(-w_y) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. there exists for this y one real-linear partial operator d:lp r 2 (s(y)) ->partiallinear[r] lp e 2 (s(y)) with dense domain in the actual scalar l2 space, d closable and d.closure closed. its graph is exactly the smooth compact-function/gradient pairs: for every scalar a and vector h, (a,h) is in d.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi with a=phi s(y)-almost everywhere and h=gradient(phi) s(y)-almost everywhere. this same d simultaneously has all the following properties: (1) for every c:r, there exists u in d.closure.domain such that its scalar quotient representative equals the constant function x->c s(y)-almost everywhere and d.closure(u)=0 in vector l2(s(y)). (2) for every u in d.closure.domain, d.closure(u)=0 if and only if there exists c:r such that its scalar representative is c s(y)-almost everywhere. (3) for every direction a:e, the real function z->s_y(z)[a] is c1. for every z:e its actual riesz gradient satisfies ||gradient(q->s_y(q)[a])(z)||_e <= ((1/eta-alpha)/4)*||a||_e. for this same directional function there exists hp:memlp (z->s_y(z)[a]) 2 (s(y)), and there exists hq:memlp (gradient(z->s_y(z)[a])) 2 (s(y)), such that the actual ordered pair of scalar/vector quotient classes (hp.tolp the directional-score function,hq.tolp its actual gradient) belongs to this same d.closure.graph. one common r,s pair precedes every y; each y has one d preceding all constants c, all closure-domain u and all directions a. constant-domain witnesses and score l2 proof witnesses are produced after their respective universal inputs. each directional gradient bound is all-point, and its coefficient is exactly (1/eta-alpha cast)/4; the eta cap together with alpha<=beta makes it nonnegative without adding a separate assumption. no alternate d is selected for a constant, u or direction. all y have the stated density/operator conclusions, while conditional disintegration retains its usual version scope. no extra equality between two conditional kernels is asserted. all original/operator/score l2 classes, graph links and constant ae identities use s(y); the partition integrability and integrals use ordinary volume. actual standard measurable representatives are used, with ae identities only rather than exact pointwise/support identities. no rough classical hessian, covariance/centered-score statement, spectral-gap or further functional inequality, centered-residual/epsilon-zero/range theorem, complete adjoint/core, main/cost composition theorem, or jointly measurable fiber/constant/direction selection is concluded. accepted pbps arxiv2609.06905v1 section2.2 and appendixc.1 density/closedness at1200 and actual noncompact directional score tests1217-1226; authored original-gradient graph-domain/kernel analytic prerequisites. sphmc2609.06906v1 section4.1 rgo covariance background is a separate consumer. autosamplingtheory.examplecases.proximalbps.conditionalscorecloseddomain.conditional_score_closed_gradient_domain autosamplingtheory/examplecases/proximalbps/conditionalscorecloseddomain.lean true root-samplinglib-writer anonymous_decoder_20261006 3f90d5114cc85f0137229d65f308a76ea1682e8d14c84d8f44d605147848af1a accepted phase_source_reviewer_20261005 objects actualmu/j gaussianaugmentation/commonr/s/reflectedw and originald_y; actual unnormalizedparameter-y directionalscore. same independentgaussianproduct/pushforward/disintegration/reflection plus explicit clm scoreformula;notnegativeu-gradient orcenterednormalizedscore. equivalent whole74proof45-58 originalcommonr/s/d_y retained;auxiliaryscoreproducer48-56 onlyliterals2y=sy byexactdensity,neverr2=r. domains full finite real hilbert/borel in