    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-ScaledClosedGraphResolvent",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-ScaledClosedGraphResolvent",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:scaled-closed-graph-resolvent · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.ScaledClosedGraphResolvent.scaled_resolvent_sequence_tendsto_zero.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nReal complete Hilbert H,K; H genuinely separable, SAME actual closed partial-linear D before f and all solution data. Positive epsilon_n tending0; actual domain u_n satisfies ALL genuine variational tests epsilon_n<un,v>+<Dun,Dv>=<f,v>.\nForcing f is orthogonal to EVERY v in SAME domain with Dv=0. No supplied weak clusters/closedgraph-limit certificate, Poincare, unscaled uniform solution bound, finite-dimensional H or K, or dense/range premise.\nFor every actual variational solution sequence in SAME closed D, both epsilon_n*u_n and epsilon_n*D(u_n) tend0 strongly when genuine forcing is orthogonal to the entire kernel. Explicit Hilbert/Riesz/graph/energy hypotheses only.\nFix real complete Hilbert H,K and SAME actual closed partial linear D before forcing f, positive epsilon sequence->0 and actual variational solutions u_n. H separable explicitly; actual finite-dimensional Borel Gibbs E gives genuine scalar L2 separability by countably generated finite measure, not finite-dimensional L2. Actual energy/scaled domain, Riesz WeakDual sequential compactness, WithLp2 genuine graph double-orthogonal and forcing orthogonal to EVERY kernel give strong epsilon*u_n->0 and epsilon*D(u_n)->0 without Poincare or uniform unscaled u. True C1 Gibbs W/positive exponential normalizer/actual normalized probability and SAME exact original compact-smooth closable gradient beforeALLf; genuine mean-zero L2 forcing is integrable and kernel-orthogonal via actual AEconstant. Construct actual positive-epsilon variational solutions, retaining ordinary localL1/weakC1 test integrabilities. Actual common PBPS J/R/S/reflected law/sourceC2 alpha-beta/eta cap/positive partitions and originalD_y beforeALLf/epsilon; fiberwise only. No epsilon0 solution/range/unscaled uniform bound/extra spatial moment/supplied weak-limit or graph or residual certificate/Poincare/BL/core/adjoint/jointselector/normalized conditional-score derivative/both main/composition; TV never transfers unbounded expectedcost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let H,K be real complete Hilbert spaces and assume H is explicitly separable. Let D:H->partialLinear[R] K be a genuine real-linear partial operator on its actual submodule domain, with D.IsClosed (actual closed graph). Fix f:H. Let epsilon:N->R have epsilon_n>0 for every n and tend atTop to0 in R; monotonicity is not assumed. Let u:N->D.domain be a supplied actual solution family.\nAssume for EVERY n and EVERY v:D.domain,\n  epsilon_n*<u_n,v>_H+<D(u_n),D(v)>_K=<f,v>_H.\nAssume for EVERY v:D.domain, D(v)=0 implies <f,v>_H=0. This is forcing orthogonality to every element of the actual kernel of this SAME partial operator.\nThen BOTH limits hold simultaneously in genuine norm topologies:\n  epsilon_n scalar-multiplied by (u_n as H) tends atTop to0 in H,\n  epsilon_n scalar-multiplied by D(u_n) tends atTop to0 in K.\nD is fixed before f,epsilon and solutions; this theorem applies to every supplied family satisfying all the actual variational equations. It does not construct another family. H and K need not be finite-dimensional; K separability, dense domain, bounded operator, supplied cluster/graph/limit certificate, or uniform unscaled-solution bound is not assumed. Ordinary product maxnorm is not silently identified with a Hilbert product. There is no abstract mean-zero replacement for all-kernel orthogonality and no assumption that solutions are centered. Both scalings are epsilon_n, not sqrt(epsilon_n). No rate, unscaled convergence, epsilon=0 solution, range/spectral-gap/further inequality or jointly measurable selection is concluded.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
        {
          "slot": "objects",
          "original": "Authored abstract real complete Hilbert H,K and SAME closed partial-linear D, fixed f and actual variational u_n. Source use is a prerequisite toward genuine Gibbs-gradient background, not source printed Poincare.",
          "reconstructed": "Real complete Hilbert H,K, explicit separable H, genuine partial-linear closed D, fixed f and supplied actual solution family.",
          "relation": "equivalent",
          "evidence": "The entire141-line module implements actual Riesz/closed-graph/energy construction; packet0 reconstruction names the same objects. H/K are not assumed finite-dimensional."
        },
        {
