      "original_theorem": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nSource C2 V with beta=1 and alpha=kappa^-1; kappa>=1; actual allpoint/allvector curvature kappa^-1*norma^2<=D2V[a,a]<=norma^2; source0<eta<=1 retained.\nActual source UNNORMALIZED exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*Gaussian_eta, normalized Gibbs mu=volume.tilted(-V), unreflected R_y=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)). Finite Hilbert/Borel including0 is disclosed representation extension.\nNo partition, covariance, moment, derivative or PI certificate on this source theorem. Actual probability, posterior vectorL2, C2, U=V_eta+logZV, both true Hessian bounds and global Lipschitz are produced internally. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher derivative, numerical kernel, cost or main claim.\nFor the actual source Gaussian-smoothed unnormalized potential and true RGO posterior, produce probability and vectorL2, covariance upper norma^2/(kappa^-1+eta^-1), C2 regularity and (kappa+eta)^-1*norma^2<=D2V_eta(y)[a,a]<=(1+eta)^-1*norma^2, and true1-Lipschitz gradient. This is the analytic Lemma4.1, not an algorithm/main theorem.\nCanonical BOTH-curvature Gibbs linear covariance upper with genuine vectorL2, actual positive partition and probability normalization; not full anisotropic Brascamp-Lieb. Actual source beta=1 alpha=kappa^-1, 1<=kappa, 0<eta<=1; genuine posterior law R_y, internally produced probability/vectorL2/positive partitions/C2 and normalized-U versus unnormalized-V_eta constant shift. Derive true covariance upper and both Hessian bounds (kappa+eta)^-1 and (1+eta)^-1, then true 1-Lipschitz gradient. Finite real Hilbert/Borel including zero dimension is disclosed representation extension. No input covariance/PI/oracle/moment/normalizer certificate on source Anchor. No joint measurable posterior kernel selector, higher smoothing derivatives, algorithm/Wp/proxy-warmness/main/querycost/composition. PBPS reflected quarter law and source-score remain separate. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace and CompleteSpace instances,with canonical full-space volume;dimension zero is allowed and no Nontrivial premise is present. Let V:E->R and kappa,eta:R. Assume kappa>=1,V C2,and for EVERY x,a:E BOTH actual bounds\n  kappa^(-1)*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x a) a <= ||a||^2.\nAssume 0<eta<=1. Define the following literal measures,normalizing prefactor and potential:\n  mu=volume.tilted(x->-V(x)),\n  d=Module.finrank R E,\n  C=((sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-1))^d,\n  A(y)=C*integral exp(-V(x)-||y-x||^2/(2*eta)) dx,\n  V_eta(y)=-Real.log(A(y)),\n  R(y)=mu.tilted(x->-||x-y||^2/(2*eta)).\nA uses actual Lebesgue volume and NO division by the original Gibbs partition;V_eta is precisely the negative literal real log of that A,not a replaced normalized-mu convolution potential.R is the literal E->Measure E family of tilts against mu,not an existential or asserted Markov/disintegration kernel.\nThen ALL the following conjuncts hold:\n(1) IsProbabilityMeasure mu.\n(2) V_eta is C2.\n(3) For EVERY y:E,R(y) is an actual probability measure and MemLp id 2 (R(y)) holds:the true position vector is AE strongly measurable with finite L2 norm.\n(4) For EVERY y:E and EVERY a:E,\n  ProbabilityTheory.covarianceBilin(R(y))(a,a) <= ||a||^2/(kappa^(-1)+eta^(-1)).\nWith the genuine probability and moment outputs this is the actual integral <a,x-mean_{R(y)}>^2 dR(y),not the covariance API's outside-vector-L2 zero fallback.\n(5) For EVERY y:E and EVERY a:E,BOTH actual Hessian bounds of the literal V_eta hold:\n  (1/(kappa+eta))*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V_eta) y a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V_eta) y a) a <= (1/(1+eta))*||a||^2.\n(6) LipschitzWith (1:NNReal) (gradient V_eta):the genuine Riesz gradient globally satisfies\n  ||gradient(V_eta)(y)-gradient(V_eta)(z)|| <= ||y-z|| for all y,z:E.\nThe gradient is exactly (InnerProductSpace.toDual R E).symm(fderiv R V_eta),with actual derivatives ensured by C2.The declared global Lipschitz constant is exactly1;it is not rewritten as a stronger eta-dependent constant.\nMeasure.tilted uses withDensity ENNReal.ofReal(exp(h)/integral exp(h)),a totalized construction outside normalizable cases;denominator0 gives zero density.The explicit probability outputs are actual laws rather than reliance on that fallback.The log in the let is literal totalized Real.log;there is no separately displayed positive-A conjunct or partial-log-domain premise added to the signature.C2/Hessian statements concern this exact function.For d=0 the prefactor C is1,and all measure/moment/all-vector/global-metric conclusions remain in scope.No input exponential-integrability or position-moment certificate is added:these law/moment facts are outputs here.No source kernel identity,conditional disintegration,y-measurability assertion for R,score differentiation or entire-paper/main/composition claim is concluded.",
