      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.SS3",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed scoped source restatement:\nFor every actual input pair and every common two-vector noise value, the source exact-gradient numerical phase obeys the M_kappa norm contraction with simultaneous explicit universal constant c=1/65536 under h Lambda_J<=c/kappa. The actual averaged Hessian and remainder are supplied by the independently compiled genuine algorithm producer, never assumed as a contraction/phase certificate.\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel sigma algebra, including dimension zero. f:E->R is genuinely globally C2, kappa>=1, and (2kappa)^-1||v||²<=D²f(z)[v,v]<=||v||² for all z,v. This is the explicit normalized potential interface; actual V_eta construction is an independent producer.\nJ>=2,h>0. Actual nodes t_j=h/2(1-cos(j*pi/(J-1))), actual Lagrange cardinals ell_j, Lambda_J=sup_[0,h] sum|ell_j|, omega_ij=integral_0^{t_i}(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds, b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds and c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds. The sole step restriction is h Lambda_J<=1/(65536 kappa); h<=1 and h²Lambda<=1 are derived.\na=exp(-h/2), sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)). P0=a p+sigma zeta0; Y0_j=x+t_j P0; Y1_i=Y0_i-sum omega_ij gradient f(Y0_j); Phi=(x+hP0-sum c_j gradient f(Y1_j), a(P0-sum b_j gradient f(Y1_j))+sigma zeta1). This is the actual exact-gradient phase, shared synchronously at every input/noise pair, not only almost surely.\nQ_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||²+inner(x,p)+||p||² and norm_M=sqrt(Q). The proof uses genuine Euclidean L2 phase norms throughout; it never treats the default product max norm as Euclidean.\nActual deterministic exact-gradient numerical phase contraction at the explicit normalized C2 curvature interface. Actual f=V_eta smoothing/C2/curvature producer remains independently open. No Khat/Kbar substitution, increment/logLambda/B2, invariant law/local errors/history/query work, PBPS, either full main theorem or actual-input expected-cost composition. TV proximity does not transfer unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its measurable Borel structure, every globally C^2 f:E->R, real kappa,h and natural J, assume kappa>=1,J>=2,h>0,and for every base point z and vector v in E,\n  (1/(2kappa))||v||^2 <= D^2 f(z)[v,v] <= ||v||^2.\nFor indices in Fin(J)={0,...,J-1},define exactly\n  t_i=(h/2)(1-cos((i/(J-1))pi)),\n  ell_j=the real Lagrange cardinal polynomial at these nodes,\n  Lambda=sup{sum_j |ell_j(s)|:s in [0,h]},\n  omega_ij=integral_0^{t_i}(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds,\n  b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds,\n  c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds.\nThe node quotient uses real coercions;integrals are ordinary Lebesgue Bochner interval integrals and the supremum is real. If h Lambda<=1/(65536 kappa),define a=exp(-h/2),sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)),and for incoming z=(X,P) and supplied common vector pair zeta=(u,v),\n  P0(z,zeta)=a P+sigma u,\n  Y0_j(z,zeta)=X+t_j P0(z,zeta),\n  Y1_i(z,zeta)=Y0_i(z,zeta)-sum_j omega_ij grad f(Y0_j(z,zeta)),\n  Phi(z,zeta)=(X+h P0(z,zeta)-sum_j c_j grad f(Y1_j(z,zeta)),\n               a(P0(z,zeta)-sum_j b_j grad f(Y1_j(z,zeta)))+sigma v).\nLet Q_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||^2+<x,p>+||p||^2. Then for every z,zprime,zeta in E x E,\n  sqrt(Q_kappa(Phi(z,zeta).1-Phi(zprime,zeta).1,\n               Phi(z,zeta).2-Phi(zprime,zeta).2))\n    <= (1-h/(65536 kappa))sqrt(Q_kappa(z.1-zprime.1,z.2-zprime.2)).\nSquare roots are nonnegative real square roots. Both compared updates use the same arbitrary zeta,pointwise with no noise-law or almost-everywhere restriction. All sums use J actual nodes. The contraction is in the displayed square-root quadratic energy with its cross term,rather than in an unstated Euclidean or maximum product norm. The statement contains no probability law,kernel assertion,transport-of-measures conclusion,iteration history or query-count claim.",
