      "original_theorem": "Attributed scoped source restatement:\nFor every real kappa and phase point, define the exact source block-matrix quadratic form Q_kappa. Valid norm use is restricted to kappa>=1 by the compiled comparisons.\nArbitrary real inner-product E, with no finite-dimension or measurability premise. Kappa>=1 for the comparisons; the total definition accepts every real kappa.\nExisting source Q/API promotion with unchanged proof, no separate mathematical progress credit. Actual deterministic exact-gradient numerical phase contraction at the explicit normalized C2 curvature interface. Actual f=V_eta smoothing/C2/curvature producer remains independently open. No Khat/Kbar substitution, increment/logLambda/B2, invariant law/local errors/history/query work, PBPS, either full main theorem or actual-input expected-cost composition. TV proximity does not transfer unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For any real inner-product space E,any real kappa and any pair z=(x,p) in E x E,define the real-valued function\n  Q_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||^2+<x,p>+||p||^2.\nThis is a definition with unrestricted real kappa,not a theorem assuming kappa>=1. The norms and inner product are those of E. The cross coefficient is exactly 1. No positivity,coercivity,metric or probability property is asserted by the definition.",
