      "original_theorem": "Attributed scoped source restatement:\nThe paper's exact twisted phase transport cost controls ordinary phase transport and therefore transfers reference position/momentum moments to an incoming law.\nReal inner-product phase space.\nkappa>=1.\nExplicit reference second moments for the final adapter.\nMetric/moment adapter only; D.3, history, D.7, D.8 and main theorems remain open.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with a Borel measurable structure. For arbitrary measures nu and reference on E x E,any xstar in E and real kappa,r,Mx,Mp,assume kappa>=1. Write\n  Q_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||^2+<x,p>+||p||^2,\n  P_kappa(nu,reference)=inf_{pi coupling of nu,reference}\n                          integral^- ENNReal.ofReal(Q_kappa(s-sprime)) dpi.\nAssume the real functions (X,P)->||X-xstar||^2 and (X,P)->||P||^2 are separately Bochner integrable under reference,and\n  integral ||X-xstar||^2 dreference <= Mx,\n  integral ||P||^2 dreference <= Mp,\n  P_kappa(nu,reference) <= ENNReal.ofReal(r^2).\nThen the real function (X,P)->||X-xstar||^2+||P||^2 is Bochner integrable under nu,and\n  integral (||X-xstar||^2+||P||^2) dnu <= 2(Mx+Mp)+24r^2.\nBoth measures are arbitrary,with no probability normalization assumption. r,Mx,Mp are arbitrary real parameters without separately stated nonnegativity assumptions. xstar is any vector,not a stationary point supplied by a potential. The phase moment is the explicit sum of coordinate squared norms,not the square of the default maximum product norm. The transport input is the unrooted quadratic phase cost with specified marginals;no sampled-state or iteration-history interpretation is part of this theorem.",
