    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-SPHMCActualIncrement",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-SPHMCActualIncrement",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-actual-increment · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.ActualIncrement.source_synchronous_increment.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.SS3",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed scoped mathematical restatement with explicit remaining producer:\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including dimension zero. f:E->R is globally C2, kappa>=1, and its genuine nested second derivative satisfies (2kappa)^-1||v||^2<=D2f(z)[v,v]<=||v||^2 for every z,v. This is the explicit normalized smoothed-potential interface; the actual f=V_eta producer remains independently open.\nJ>=2,h>0. Actual Chebyshev-Lobatto nodes t_j=h/2(1-cos(j*pi/(J-1))), cardinal polynomials ell_j and ordinary Lebesgue integral weights omega_ij=integral_0^t_i(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds, b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds,c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds. Lambda=sup_[0,h] sum_j|ell_j| and h Lambda<=1/(65536 kappa). No supplied convenient weights, Hessian, phase or remainder certificate.\na=exp(-h/2),sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)); P0=a p+sigma zeta0; Y0_j=x+t_j P0; Y1_i=Y0_i-sum_j omega_ij gradient f(Y0_j); Phi=(x+hP0-sum_j c_j gradient f(Y1_j),a(P0-sum_j b_j gradient f(Y1_j))+sigma zeta1). The same two noise vectors are shared by the two inputs. The inequality is for every z,zprime,zeta, not only almost surely.\nQ_kappa(x,p)=((2kappa)^-1+1/2)||x||^2+inner(x,p)+||p||^2. The source M_kappa norm is sqrt Q. Intermediate Euclidean phase norms are the true WithLp2 product; the ordinary product max norm is not substituted.\nFor the actual full exact-gradient two-refresh two-Picard Phi, the synchronous increment difference obeys sqrt Q_kappa((Phi_z-Phi_zprime)-(z-zprime)) <=12 h sqrt Q_kappa(z-zprime), under the explicit normalized C2 curvature interface and actual h Lambda<=1/(65536 kappa). This is the source difference of increments because vector subtraction is additive. The source universal C is explicitly elaborated as12, with the same c1/65536 as the actual contraction. All compared states and common noise values are included.\nActual Lemma4.8 normalized-curvature numerical interface only. The actual f=V_eta smoothing/C2/curvature producer is a separate prerequisite before claiming the fully instantiated source lemma. No measure-level contraction, Khat/Kbar bias/variance, local discretization, invariance, history/expected query cost, Wp/proxy-warmness/initialization, PBPS or either full main/composition result is proved here. TV closeness cannot transfer unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "For every complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space E with its Borel measurable structure,consider a globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable f:E->R,real kappa,h and natural J. Assume kappa>=1,J>=2,h>0,and for all base points z and vectors v in E,\n  (1/(2kappa))||v||^2 <= D^2 f(z)[v,v] <= ||v||^2.\nFor the actual indices i,j in Fin(J)={0,...,J-1},define exactly\n  t_i=(h/2)(1-cos((i/(J-1))pi)),\n  ell_j=the real Lagrange cardinal polynomial at these nodes,\n  Lambda=sup{sum_j |ell_j(s)|:s in [0,h]},\n  omega_ij=integral_0^{t_i}(t_i-s)ell_j(s)ds,\n  b_j=integral_0^h ell_j(s)ds,\n  c_j=integral_0^h(h-s)ell_j(s)ds.\nThe node quotient uses real coercions. The supremum is real,and the interval integrals are ordinary Lebesgue Bochner integrals. If\n  h Lambda<=1/(65536kappa),\nput a=exp(-h/2),sigma=sqrt(1-exp(-h)). For an incoming phase state z=(X,P) and supplied vector pair zeta=(u,v),define\n  P0(z,zeta)=a P+sigma u,\n  Y0_j(z,zeta)=X+t_j P0(z,zeta),\n  Y1_i(z,zeta)=Y0_i(z,zeta)-sum_j omega_ij grad f(Y0_j(z,zeta)),\n  Phi(z,zeta)=(X+h P0(z,zeta)-sum_j c_j grad f(Y1_j(z,zeta)),\n               a(P0(z,zeta)-sum_j b_j grad f(Y1_j(z,zeta)))+sigma v).\nThe gradient is the actual Riesz representative of the first Frechet derivative of f. All sums range over the entire Fin(J) index set. Define the exact quadratic energy\n  Q_kappa(x,p)=(1/(2kappa)+1/2)||x||^2+<x,p>+||p||^2.\nThen for every z,zprime,zeta in E x E,letting deltaX=z.1-zprime.1 and deltaP=z.2-zprime.2,\n  sqrt(Q_kappa((Phi(z,zeta).1-Phi(zprime,zeta).1)-deltaX,\n               (Phi(z,zeta).2-Phi(zprime,zeta).2)-deltaP))\n    <=12h sqrt(Q_kappa(deltaX,deltaP)).\nEquivalently the pair inside Q on the left is the increment difference (Phi(z,zeta)-z)-(Phi(zprime,zeta)-zprime),with coordinatewise subtraction. The square roots are real nonnegative square roots;the energy has cross coefficient exactly 1. Both noise vectors are shared between the two compared updates. Quantification is pointwise over every supplied noise pair,with no probability distribution or almost-everywhere restriction.\nThe theorem asserts this exact bound on the difference of increments. It does not state a contraction factor for the full output difference,an absolute bound on an individual update increment,a probability-kernel or transport result,a sampling history,an evaluation-count bound,or a remainder-operator representation. No supplied positive-form or metric certificate is an additional hypothesis.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
