      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed source prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space equipped with its Borel measurable space, including dimension zero. V:E->R is globally C2. alpha>0, eta>0, and for every x,v, alpha norm(v)^2<=D2V(x)[v,v]. The source upper Hessian bound and eta upper cap are not required for this normalization/regularity adapter.\nZ_V=integral exp(-V(x))dx, mu=volume.tilted(-V), C_eta=(sqrt(2*pi*eta))^(-dim E), A_eta(y)=C_eta integral exp(-V(x)-norm(y-x)^2/(2eta))dx, and the SOURCE potential is V_eta(y)=-log A_eta(y). These are actual functions and measures, not supplied normalized Gibbs certificates.\nOriginal Gibbs integrability, positive Z_V, mu probability, actual Gaussian add-noise density, integrable A_eta and preserved partition are derived. The normalized probability-density potential is U_eta=-log(C_eta integral exp(-norm(y-x)^2/(2eta))dmu(x)); the exact identity U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V is a conclusion. No moments, minimizer, input law, conditional representative, smoothed regularity or smoothed Hessian certificate is passed.\nThe original Gibbs mass Z_V is strictly positive and mu is a probability measure. The actual Gaussian add-noise law equals volume.withDensity(ofReal(exp(-V_eta)/Z_V)). The source unnormalized weight A_eta is integrable with integral exactly Z_V, so this same law is volume.tilted(-V_eta). A_eta is positive everywhere, V_eta is globally C2, and at every y the normalized negative-log density U_eta(y)=V_eta(y)+log Z_V.\nActual source unnormalized smoothed potential V_eta, positive finite partition Z_V preserved by smoothing, genuine original and smoothed Gibbs probability laws, normalized U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V and source V_eta C2. No posterior score/covariance, curvature/higher derivative inequalities, exact-flow stationarity, numerical accuracy/stochastic errors/history/work, PBPS process or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure,including dimension zero. Let V:E->R be globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable,and let alpha,eta be strictly positive real numbers. Assume the genuine Hessian lower bound\n  alpha||v||^2 <= D^2 V(x)[v,v]\nfor every x,v in E. No upper Hessian bound is assumed.\nWrite volume for canonical Lebesgue measure on E,d=dim_R E,and define the actual real integral,measure,normalizer and unnormalized convolution by\n  ZV=integral_E exp(-V(x)) dvolume(x),\n  mu=volume.tilted(x -> -V(x)),\n  C=((sqrt(2 pi eta))^(-1))^d,\n  A(y)=C integral_E exp(-V(x)-||y-x||^2/(2 eta)) dvolume(x).\nThe tilt mu means the measure volume.withDensity(x -> ENNReal.ofReal(exp(-V(x))/ZV)). All real integrals are Bochner integrals. Let G be the standard centered identity-covariance Gaussian probability measure on E. Then the following nine conclusions hold simultaneously:\n  1. ZV>0.\n  2. mu is a probability measure.\n  3. The independent-noise pushforward satisfies\n       (mu x G)_*((x,g) -> x+sqrt(eta)g)\n         =volume.withDensity(y -> ENNReal.ofReal(exp(-(-log(A(y))))/ZV)).\n  4. A:E->R is Bochner integrable with respect to volume.\n  5. integral_E A(y) dvolume(y)=ZV.\n  6. The same pushforward measure also satisfies\n       (mu x G)_*((x,g) -> x+sqrt(eta)g)\n         =volume.tilted(y -> -(-log(A(y)))).\n  7. A(y)>0 for every y in E.\n  8. The actual function F(y)=-log(A(y)) is globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable.\n  9. For every y in E,\n       -log(C integral_E exp(-||y-x||^2/(2 eta)) dmu(x))\n         =-log(A(y))+log(ZV).\nThus the exact negative-log unnormalized convolution is F=-log A. The output density in conclusion 3 is exp(-F)/ZV;pointwise positivity makes exp(-F)=A. Conclusion 6 is tilt by -F,not by F;its tilt normalizer is the integral of exp(-F),which conclusion 5 identifies with ZV. The normalized negative-log convolution in conclusion 9 differs from F by the additive constant +log ZV.\nThe input mu is fixed by the defined Lebesgue tilt of -V,not an arbitrary pre-supplied probability measure. The Gaussian vector is independent under the displayed product law,with noise scale sqrt(eta). All quantities are the actual displayed functions and measures,not certificates or chosen density representatives. Positive ZV,probability normalization,convolution normalization,pointwise positivity and global C2 regularity are conclusions rather than extra hypotheses.\nNo finite-moment,integrability or normalization premise is added for exp(-V),no separate coercivity/minimizer assumption is supplied,and no positive-dimension or eta upper-bound restriction appears. The statement does not assert an upper or lower Hessian bound for F,a convexity-transfer estimate,a gradient bound,analyticity,higher smoothness,an invariant law or a numerical sampling algorithm.",
