      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Attributed Cramer-Rao half restatement:\nE is a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable space and canonical volume, including dimension zero. alpha,beta are NNReal, 0<alpha<=beta. U or V is genuinely C2; actual Hessian at every point and direction lies between alpha*norm(v)^2 and beta*norm(v)^2.\nEvery Gibbs law is the actual volume.tilted(-potential). Probability, finite second moments, score integrability, centered score pairing and covariance bounds are derived. No minimizer, finite input moments, partition constant, derivative/score/covariance or well-behaved certificate is supplied.\neta>0 is arbitrary; source eta<=1 is unnecessary for this half. C_eta=(sqrt(2 pi eta)^-1)^d is the actual Gaussian prefactor. V_eta is the literal unnormalized source convolution; U_eta=V_eta+log Z_V, and R_y is the actual selected quadratic tilt of the original Gibbs law.\nFor every observation y and direction v, the actual selected RGO posterior R_y has covarianceBilin(R_y)(v,v)>=norm(v)^2/(beta+eta^-1). The actual source unnormalized Gaussian convolution V_eta has genuine Hessian D2V_eta(y)[v,v]<=beta/(1+beta eta)*norm(v)^2. Source beta=1 gives exactly (1+eta)^-1. Brascamp-Lieb/Hessian lower and the full two-sided Lemma4.1 are not claimed.\nActual Gibbs all-direction covariance lower bound and its actual RGO/source V_eta Hessian upper consumer only. No Brascamp-Lieb covariance upper/Hessian lower, full Lemma4.1, general nonlinear Cramer-Rao, higher regularity, exact stationarity, approximate/stochastic/history work, PBPS process or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be any complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure and canonical Lebesgue volume,including dimension zero. Let V:E->R be globally twice continuously Frechet differentiable,and let alpha,beta be nonnegative real parameters with alpha>0 and alpha<=beta. Suppose,for every x,v in E,\n  (alpha:R)||v||^2<=D^2 V(x)[v,v]<=(beta:R)||v||^2.\nLet eta be any strictly positive real number. Define exactly\n  mu=volume.tilted(x -> -V(x)),\n  d=dim_R E,\n  C=((sqrt(2pi eta))^(-1))^d,\n  A(y)=C integral_E exp(-V(x)-||y-x||^2/(2eta)) dvolume(x),\n  Veta(y)=-log(A(y)),\n  R(y)=mu.tilted(x -> -||x-y||^2/(2eta)).\nThe tilt is the actual exponential-density normalization against its base measure using a real Bochner integral. In particular mu is normalized exp(-V) against volume,and R(y) is normalized exp(-||x-y||^2/(2eta)) against that actual mu. The Gaussian prefactor C is included in the unnormalized Lebesgue convolution A;A itself contains no division by the partition integral of exp(-V).\nThen the following two globally quantified conclusions hold simultaneously:\n  for every y,v in E,\n    ||v||^2/((beta:R)+eta^(-1))<=CovBilin(R(y))(v,v);\n  for every y,v in E,\n    D(D Veta)(y)[v][v]<=((beta:R)/(1+(beta:R)eta))||v||^2.\nThe nested derivative first differentiates the continuous-linear-map-valued function y->D Veta(y),then applies v to each of the two directional slots. CovBilin(R(y))(v,v) is the named true centered covariance of the scalar projection <v,X> with itself under the actual measure R(y),with the supplied covariance interpretation in its identity-L2 regime. It is a real scalar,not a pre-supplied covariance matrix or operator.\nBoth inequalities hold at every y and every v,not just almost everywhere or for unit vectors. The statement has exactly these two conclusion groups. It does not include additional IsProbabilityMeasure or MemLp conclusions for mu or R(y),nor do those appear as separately supplied premises. It also does not include normalization/pushforward identities,strict positivity of A,a separate ContDiff assertion about Veta,a lower Hessian bound for Veta,an upper covariance bound,finite-step kernels or invariance. All measures and functions in the inequalities are fixed by the exact displayed lets. No upper bound on eta or positive-dimension restriction is supplied.",
