    {
      "id": "semantic-audit:ASTIS-RT-20261006-StandardizedRGOPositionFisher",
      "kind": "semantic-audit",
      "label": "ASTIS-RT-20261006-StandardizedRGOPositionFisher",
      "status": "fidelity-exact",
      "subtitle": "companion:sphmc-standardized-rgo-position-fisher · equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "summary": "Blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher.",
      "column": 7,
      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8",
      "original_theorem": "Exact bounded statement:\nSource beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2<=D2V(x)[v,v]<=normv^2 for every x,v.\nFinite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero, and arbitrary measurable parameter space S; measurable eta/y with every0<eta(s)<=1. These coordinate-free and parameter-space extensions are disclosed.\nNo supplied proximal point, law identity, normalizer, probability, curvature, gradient or moment certificate. Actual p, mu/R/r probability, normalized affine law, C2 curvature/mode and genuine position/Fisher L2 are internally produced. The numerical-prox eta<=1/(2beta) cap is a separate computational contract.\nProduce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr<=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr<=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr<=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.\nSource realκ>=1,beta1/alphakappainv,C2/globalbothcurvature and every0<eta<=1 retained. Fullfinite real Hilbert/Borel incl0 and arbitrary measurableS are disclosed extensions. Actualp,normalizedmu/R/r,affinelaw,curvature/stationarity andtrue moments are all outputs, never certificates. Generic canonical affine transport needs only nonzero scale and proves identity of Mathlib normalized tilts; it does not assert a probability law without produced positive integrability. GaussianTalagrand/LSI/FIRSTW2 inequality4.6,bias4.2/MGF4.3/fullLemma4.2,higher/Picard/Wp/proxywarmness/initialization,posteriorjointMarkovsemantics,actualsamplers/PBPSreflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation,main/work/composition OPEN. Actualr/R distinct from Gaussiangradientoutput and HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Numericalprox sourcecapeta<=1/(2beta) remains; TV never transfers unboundedcost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a complete finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup, InnerProductSpace R, CompleteSpace, FiniteDimensional R, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace instances. Its volume is the actual full-space real Hilbert Lebesgue/Haar measure; dimension zero is allowed. Let S be an arbitrary measurable space. Let V:E->R and kappa:R satisfy kappa>=1, V is twice continuously Frechet differentiable, and for every x,v in E BOTH\n  kappa^(-1)*||v||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x v) v,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R V) x v) v <= ||v||^2.\nLet eta:S->R and y:S->E be measurable, with 0<eta(s)<=1 for every s in S. The gradient is the genuine real Hilbert Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative.\nThere exists ONE map p:S->E such that p is measurable and for every s in S,\n  p(s)+eta(s) scalar-multiplied gradient V(p(s))=y(s).\nFor that same p define the following literal objects:\n  rho(s,u)=V(p(s)+sqrt(eta(s)) scalar-multiplied u)-V(p(s))\n           -sqrt(eta(s))*inner R (gradient V(p(s))) u,\n  Q(s,u)=||u||^2/2+rho(s,u),\n  mu=volume.tilted(x -> -V(x)),\n  R(s)=mu.tilted(x -> -||x-y(s)||^2/(2*eta(s))),\n  r(s)=Measure.map(x -> (sqrt(eta(s)))^(-1) scalar-multiplied (x-p(s)))(R(s)).\nThen mu is a probability measure, and for EVERY s in S ALL the following hold simultaneously:\n(1) R(s) is a probability measure.\n(2) rho(s,-) is C2 and Q(s,-) is C2.\n(3) gradient(rho(s,-))(0)=0 and gradient(Q(s,-))(0)=0.\n(4) For every u,v in E,\n  0 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R (rho(s,-))) u v) v <= eta(s)*||v||^2.\n(5) For every u,v in E,\n  ||v||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R (Q(s,-))) u v) v <= (1+eta(s))*||v||^2.\n(6) The exact standardized law identity is\n  r(s)=volume.tilted(u -> -Q(s,u)).\n(7) r(s) is a probability measure, and MemLp id 2 (r(s)) holds, meaning true AE strong measurability and a finite vector L2 norm for the position function.\n(8) u -> ||u||^2 is integrable with respect to r(s), and\n  integral ||u||^2 dr(s)(u) <= Module.finrank R E.\n(9) MemLp (gradient(rho(s,-))) 2 (r(s)) holds, meaning a genuine vector L2 gradient.\n(10) BOTH exact real gradient-energy bounds hold:\n  integral ||gradient(rho(s,-))(u)||^2 dr(s)(u)\n    <= (eta(s))^2 * integral ||u||^2 dr(s)(u),\n  integral ||gradient(rho(s,-))(u)||^2 dr(s)(u)\n    <= (eta(s))^2 * Module.finrank R E.\nEach C2, zero-gradient and lower/upper-Hessian conjunct above is separate and retained. The two last inequalities are uncentered squared-norm integrals, with no energy factor1/2 and no substituted mean or covariance. Their measure is the SAME actual standardized r(s), not the original volume, mu, or R(s).\nEvery tilt is the actual normalized exponential withDensity construction. The theorem separately PRODUCES probability for mu,R(s),r(s), real vector L2 and norm-square integrability, so the law and moment claims are not inferred solely from a totalized measure equality or an outside-integrability fallback. No positive partition, posterior moment, score bound, or selector certificate is supplied as a hypothesis. The affine normalization is represented by the exact equality to volume.tilted(-Q); no uncancelled Jacobian factor is asserted. The scope is every positive step size at most1, including1, and the whole E including dimension zero; kappa only has the displayed real lower bound1.\nThe existential p precedes every let-defined rho,Q,mu,R,r and all their conjuncts. The probability of mu is outside the subsequent forall s and is not made vacuous if S is empty. No joint measurability of s->R(s) or s->r(s), Markov posterior kernel, measurable disintegration, uniform-in-parameter integral, unequal-step comparison, Gaussian gradient-output law, HMC transition, bias/MGF, query count, transport, algorithm or whole-paper conclusion is stated. The only selector conclusion is its measurability and the exact first-order equation; no extra minimizer/growth/uniqueness clause is inserted.",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
      "blindness": "source hidden from decoder",
      "semantic_slots": [
