      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
      "original_theorem": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE has the same finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel/full-space structure, including dimension zero. W is C1 and exp(-W) is genuinely integrable for volume. The law mu is exactly volume.tilted(-W), whose probability normalization is derived.\nD is the same closable partial gradient with exact compact smooth representative graph. epsilon is positive and forcing f is a genuine scalar L2(mu) class. No weak solution, H1 membership of a test, differentiability of u, coercivity or Poincare certificate is supplied.\nAll quantifiers/representatives/measures are retained: the weak equation tests every original closure-domain element; ordinary weak derivatives use volume and every C1 compact scalar test/direction; the weighted equation now uses every C1 compact scalar test, with all three products L1 for volume.\nFor C1 W and genuine integrability of exp(-W) volume, let mu=volume.tilted(-W). For every same closable exact compact smooth gradient D, epsilon>0 and scalar L2(mu) input f, construct u in D.closure.domain satisfying the variational equation for every domain test. Its actual closed gradient is the ordinary weak gradient, with locally volume-integrable representatives and full C1 compact directional identities. For every C1 compact psi, all three weighted volume products are integrable and epsilon integral exp(-W)u psi + integral exp(-W)<D.closure u,gradient psi> = integral exp(-W)f psi.\nSame actual compact-gradient graph closure admits C1 compact function/gradient pairs; actual positive-epsilon weak resolvent has all C1 compact weighted volume tests and genuine ordinary weak gradient. Actual PBPS reflected conditional R/S law and original fixed D precede epsilon/input. No local H2, global operator-core/Bochner, conditional Poincare/BL, centered epsilon limit, noncompact constant/linear domains, measurable y-selection, SPHMC Hessian lower/full4.1, PBPS hypocoercivity or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable structure,including dimension zero. Let W:E->R be globally C1 and suppose exp(-W) is Bochner integrable against canonical Lebesgue volume. Define the actual measure\n  mu=volume.tilted(x -> -W(x)),\nmeaning normalized density exp(-W)/integral exp(-W)dvolume relative to volume. The tilt definition alone does not include a probability or nonzero-normalization certificate.\nFor every real linear partial operator D:L2(mu;R)->L2(mu;E),assume D is closable and that,for all scalar a and vector H L2 classes,\n  (a,H) in graph(D) if and only if there exists smooth compactly supported phi:E->R\n  with a=phi mu-almost everywhere and H=grad phi mu-almost everywhere.\nThen for every real epsilon>0 and every input f in L2(mu;R),there exists u in the domain of T=closure(D) with all of the following properties. Write ubar,fbar for the usual representatives of the scalar classes u,f,and G for the representative of the actual vector class T u.\n  (a) For every v in domain(T),with its scalar class and actual vector output T v,\n        epsilon <u,v>_{L2(mu;R)}+<T u,T v>_{L2(mu;E)}\n          =<f,v>_{L2(mu;R)}.\n  (b) ubar:E->R is locally Bochner integrable with respect to volume.\n  (c) G:E->E is locally Bochner integrable with respect to volume.\n  (d) For every globally C1 compactly supported real psi:E->R and every direction e in E,\n        psi(x)<G(x),e> and ubar(x)D psi(x)[e]\n      are both integrable against volume,and\n        integral psi(x)<G(x),e> dvolume(x)\n          =-integral ubar(x)D psi(x)[e] dvolume(x).\n  (e) For every globally C1 compactly supported real psi,the following three real integrands are integrable against volume:\n        exp(-W(x))(ubar(x)psi(x)),\n        exp(-W(x))<G(x),grad psi(x)>,\n        exp(-W(x))(fbar(x)psi(x)),\n      and the exact weighted test identity holds:\n        epsilon integral exp(-W)(ubar psi)dvolume\n          +integral exp(-W)<G,grad psi>dvolume\n          =integral exp(-W)(fbar psi)dvolume.\nThe Frechet derivative and gradient of the test functions are actual derivatives. Domain and L2-class coercions use their usual representatives. The unannotated local integrability,Integrable assertions and integrals are with respect to canonical Lebesgue volume;the Hilbert inner products in (a) are instead under the actual mu. The last identity uses the unnormalized weight exp(-W),not an inserted density-normalization factor.\nThe solution u is fixed before every variational or compact-test quantifier;the same actual T u is used throughout. No uniqueness claim,solution norm bound,mean-zero restriction on f,additional C2 hypothesis on W,dense-domain premise for the supplied D,or existence of D is asserted. Probability normalization of mu is not an extra stated conjunct.",
