      "original_theorem": "Let Phi and PhiPrime be real-valued functions on the real line. Assume Phi is continuous and has exact right derivative PhiPrime(u) within [u,infinity) at every u. If r Phi(u) <= PhiPrime(u) for every real u, then for every s <= t, Phi(s) <= Phi(t) exp(-r(t-s)). No sign condition on Phi or r is required. This is only the scalar endpoint comparison; concrete semigroup and curvature identities are outside its scope.",
