      "url": "lean-foundations.html?view=semantic",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/DakeBU/Automization-Sampling-Optimisation-Geometry-Lib",
      "original_theorem": "Let eta be a progressively measurable real integrand that is square-integrable on a positive finite horizon T, let B be Brownian motion relative to a filtration satisfying the usual conditions, and let tau be a nonnegative stopping time satisfying tau(omega) <= T for every omega. Then the completed Ito integral process I_t = integral_0^t eta_s dB_s evaluated at tau is integrable. This is a bounded global-L2 statement; it asserts nothing about unbounded stopping times, local-L2 integrands before localization, vector stochastic integration, quadratic variation, or Ito's formula.",
      "reconstructed_theorem": "设 μ 是样本空间 Ω 上的有限测度，filtration 是以非负实数为时间参数的滤过，T>0 是有限时间范围，η 是该滤过和测度下、时间范围 T 内的实值渐进可测 L² 被积过程，B 是相对于 filtration 和 μ 的实 Brownian 运动。若 filtration 满足通常条件，τ:Ω→ℝ≥0 是相对于 filtration 的停止时间，并且对每个 ω 都有 τ(ω)≤T，则随机变量 ω↦∫₀^{τ(ω)}η_s dB_s，即构造的 Ito 积分过程在随机时间 τ(ω) 处的取值，是关于 μ 的 Bochner 可积函数。",
      "fidelity_verdict": "equivalent-after-elaboration",
