      "search": "semantic-audit:astis-rt-20261004-bounded-stopped-ito-mean-zero semantic-audit astis-rt-20261004-bounded-stopped-ito-mean-zero bounded-stopped-ito-mean:mean-zero · equivalent-after-elaboration blind reconstruction and seven-slot semantic comparison for autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.stochasticprocesses.boundedstoppeditomean.integral_itointegralprocess_at_boundedstopping_eq_zero. equivalent-after-elaboration source hidden from decoder let eta be a progressively measurable real integrand that is square-integrable on a positive finite horizon t, let b be brownian motion relative to a filtration satisfying the usual conditions, and let tau be a nonnegative stopping time satisfying tau(omega) <= t for every omega. then the expectation of the completed ito integral i_tau = integral_0^tau eta_s db_s is zero. this is the centered value of the constructed real global-l2 ito process at a bounded stopping time; it is not a general optional-sampling theorem and asserts nothing about unbounded stopping times, local martingales before localization, vector stochastic integration, quadratic variation, or ito's formula. 在相同设定下，设 t>0，η 是时间范围 t 内的实值渐进可测 l² 被积过程，b 是相对于 filtration 和有限测度 μ 的实 brownian 运动，且 filtration 满足通常条件。若 τ:ω→ℝ≥0 是相对于 filtration 的停止时间并逐点满足 τ≤t，则停止的 ito 积分具有零均值：∫ω(∫₀^{τ(ω)}η_s db_s)dμ(ω)=0。 accepted standard bounded stopping consequence for a square-integrable real ito integral; samplinglib completed-process formulation autosamplingtheory.technicallemmas.stochasticprocesses.boundedstoppeditomean.integral_itointegralprocess_at_boundedstopping_eq_zero autosamplingtheory/technicallemmas/stochasticprocesses/boundedstoppeditomean.lean true sphere_second_order_proof_auditor source_blind_lean_statement_decoder 68ce9425165e85966b0b67dafb767c0bb5657a1c7b641e0edfb362406f38eff3 accepted sphere_second_order_source_reviewer objects 样本空间、有限测度、非负实时间滤过、正有限范围、渐进 l2 被积过程、brownian 运动、停止时间和完成的实 ito 积分过程。 样本空间 ω、有限测度 μ、滤过 filtration、时间范围 t、渐进 l² 被积过程 η、非负停止时间 τ、实 brown