      "original_theorem": "Let E be a real inner-product space and I a nonempty finite type. Let x_i:E be a deterministic sample, let B≥0 with ||x_i||≤B for every i, and let Σ:E→E be a continuous linear operator that is symmetric and satisfies ||Σ||≤B^2. With Σhat=|I|^{-1}sum_i x_i tensor x_i, one has Σhat-Σ=|I|^{-1}sum_i(x_i tensor x_i-Σ). Every centered summand x_i tensor x_i-Σ is symmetric and has operator norm at most 2B^2. This is only the deterministic preprocessing for matrix concentration: it does not assert independence, an expectation identity, a variance proxy, matrix Bernstein, a probability tail, or a sample-complexity bound.",
