ct space and i is a finite type; completeness and nonemptiness are not required. the lean context is [normedaddcommgroup e] [innerproductspace ℝ e] and [fintype κ]. the lesson consistently says real inner-product space and finite sample index. same no completespace e or nonempty κ instance appears on empiricalsecondmoment. the publication lesson and its lean-description field now match this exact domain. quantifiers for every real inner-product space e, every finite type i, and every sample x : i → e, including i empty. e and κ are implicit universally quantified variables and sample is an arbitrary explicit argument. κ has only a fintype instance. same the definition contains no restriction on sample and no nonempty κ premise, so the empty finite type remains in scope. assumptions only real inner-product-space structure and finiteness; no probability law, independence, centering, or boundedness. the target definition uses only normedaddcommgroup e, innerproductspace ℝ e, and fintype κ. the lesson explicitly denies stochastic, centering, and boundedness premises. same the later preconcentration theorem has additional local hypotheses, but they are not arguments, instances, or premises of empiricalsecondmoment; the binding targets only the definition obligation. conclusion σhat = |i|⁻¹ ∑ i (x_i ⊗ x_i), with (x_i ⊗ x_i)(y) = inner(x_i,y) x_i. empiricalsecondmoment sample = (fintype.card κ : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ i, innerproductspace.rankone ℝ (sample i) (sample i). same mathlib's self rank-one operator is exactly the continuous linear map y ↦ ⟪sample i,y⟫ sample i, so both the summands and normalized finite sum coincide. scopes a deterministic definition valid for all finite samples, with the empty-sample convention; it does not assert concentration. the module exposes a transparent definition for all finite κ. the lesson separates it from later concentration consumers, which use a nonempty index type. same the target declaration is a def with no theorem-level probabilistic conclusion. extra assumptions in the separately declared preconcentration theorem do not change the definition's scope. constant dependencies the normalization is exactly the inverse real cardinality |i|⁻¹; the empty sample yields zero. the scalar is exactly (fintype.card κ : ℝ)⁻¹ and each summand is innerproductspace.rankone. if κ is empty, the inverse cardinality and empty sum evaluate to zero. same the source, blind reconstruction, exact lean expression, formula, lesson dependencies, and module docstring agree on the sole normalization and the empty-index convention.",
