      "original_theorem": "Let E be a continuous real-valued energy curve with an exact one-sided derivative E'(u)=-qD(u) at every time. Let r>0 and suppose rE(u)<=qD(u)+b for every real u. Then for every s<=t, E(t)<=E(s) exp(-r(t-s))+(b/r)(1-exp(-r(t-s))). This scalar comparison does not construct a semigroup or establish the derivative identity or coercivity estimate for a concrete model.",
