      "original_theorem": "The order-r derivative expression weights u^(j-r) by the descending factorial j^(r) and the original coefficient. Formula: P_r(u)=\\sum_{j\\in S}j^{\\underline r}a_j u^{j-r} Assumptions: r and j are natural numbers. Natural subtraction is truncated. When j<r, the descending factorial is zero. Boundary: This definition alone does not assert differentiability.",
