        },
        {
          "label": "Mechanism",
          "value": "Optimization selects a minimum; an RGO draws from a normalized exponential of the same energy. This is a span through a common energy, not an equivalence of outputs."
        },
        {
          "label": "Hypothesis Map",
          "value": "Require existence (and, when claimed, uniqueness) of the minimizer; separately require 0 < partition function < infinity. Fix temperature and quadratic scaling."
        },
        {
          "label": "Conclusion Map",
          "value": "Quadratic regularization, convexity and some perturbation lemmas are shared; kernel simulation and target invariance are extra."
        },
        {
          "label": "Failure Boundary",
          "value": "An RGO is not itself the full proximal sampler, not automatically a JKO step, and not an exact deterministic proximal map."
        },
        {
