          "value": "Embed a measurable update map as a deterministic probability kernel. The product denotes first T, then S."
        },
        {
          "label": "Hypothesis Map",
          "value": "Updates must be measurable; pin kernel composition orientation and the measurable-space contracts."
        },
        {
          "label": "Conclusion Map",
          "value": "Transport deterministic iteration into a special case of Markov evolution; this does not manufacture Gibbs invariance."
        },
        {
          "label": "Failure Boundary",
          "value": "Continuity is not a substitute for checking the actual measurable structures. Stochastic kernels are not generally deterministic maps."
        },
        {
          "label": "Category objects",
