      "search": "transport:metric-pl concept-bridge metric gradient flow: pl controls dissipation shared dissipation template the common proof skeleton is metric gradient flow plus a gap-versus-squared-gradient coercivity inequality. the scalar differential inequality then gives exponential energy-gap decay. literature/structural correspondence; no lean-certified functor or theorem transfer. family:metric-gradient-flow, family:gap-gradient the common proof skeleton is metric gradient flow plus a gap-versus-squared-gradient coercivity inequality. the scalar differential inequality then gives exponential energy-gap decay. identify the actual metric gradient, a valid chain rule/energy-dissipation identity, a lower energy level e_*, and flow existence. discrete algorithms need an additional descent/local-error argument. the final gronwall step is shared across euclidean pl, riemannian pl and wasserstein pl; only the metric, energy and proof of the coercivity premise change. this template does not identify the underlying spaces or prove that a formal wasserstein gradient exists. w2/otto geometry requires rigorous first-variation and edi/evi hypotheses in infinite-dimensional settings. metric energy problems (x,g,e,e_*) carrying a justified gradient-flow/dissipation structure. translations that preserve the energy/dissipation inequality and explicitly map constants; no total morphism class is defined. the scalar dissipation template is reusable, but no category-level identity law is certified. metric and regularity side conditions must be recomputed after each transport; no composition certificate is claimed. calculus, manifold, transport, flow log-concave-sampling optimisation riemannian-optimization statistical-optimal-transport conceptual incidence scope, not compiled cross-domain use",
