      "search": "transport:pi-chi2 concept-bridge poincaré ↔ χ²: l² pl-shaped coercivity functional-inequality mirror poincaré is a quadratic l2 coercivity inequality. for the reversible semigroup it controls the dirichlet dissipation of the density fluctuation and yields exponential chi-square decay by the same scalar pl/gronwall pattern. literature/structural correspondence; no lean-certified functor or theorem transfer. family:l2-coercivity poincaré is a quadratic l2 coercivity inequality. for the reversible semigroup it controls the dirichlet dissipation of the density fluctuation and yields exponential chi-square decay by the same scalar pl/gronwall pattern. use the exact reversible markov-semigroup/dirichlet-form domain and density hypotheses from the sampling source. on the optimization side the analogy is to a quadratic gap controlled by its gradient/dissipation, not an identification of objectives. poincaré occupies the pl-shaped coercivity slot for the chi-square/l2 gap, while lsi occupies it for kl. this gives a clean family-level comparison of convergence mechanisms. poincaré and lsi are different functional inequalities; chi-square and kl are different gaps. pi is generally weaker than lsi, and the reversible/domain hypotheses cannot be erased by the analogy. a reversible semigroup together with its invariant measure, density gap and dirichlet dissipation. a conceptual slot correspondence with quadratic optimization coercivity; no direct theorem transport is claimed. not established; this is a functional-inequality mirror. do not compose pi/chi-square with lsi/kl edges by label similarity; exact comparison theorems must be cited separately. semigroup, flow log-concave-sampling optimisation conceptual incidence scope, not compiled cross-domain use",
      "library_scope": [
        "log-concave-sampling",
        "optimisation"
      ],
