        },
        {
          "label": "Conceptual families",
          "value": "family:conditional-dependence"
        },
        {
          "label": "Mechanism",
          "value": "Matrix and covariance inequalities recur, but the useful discrete property is uniform spectral control of conditional influences. This is a structural comparison, not strong convexity on a spin cube."
        },
        {
          "label": "Hypothesis Map",
          "value": "Binary spins with nonzero conditional single-site variances; off-diagonal convention, diagonal and frozen-site handling explicit. Normalize/symmetrize in the correct weighted inner product and check every required pinning."
        },
        {
          "label": "Conclusion Map",
          "value": "Reuse covariance/PSD algebra. A model-specific pinning bound then feeds a separately proved local-to-global mixing theorem."
        },
        {
          "label": "Failure Boundary",
          "value": "An unconditional covariance bound is not uniform spectral independence. Generating-polynomial log-concavity is not density log-concavity; no Euclidean Hessian lower bound or universal rapid mixing follows."
        },
        {
          "label": "Category objects",
          "value": "Typed (state space, probability law, operator, discrepancy, metric, clock) presentations."
        },
        {
          "label": "Category morphisms",
          "value": "Only the explicitly scoped mechanism/adapter; no total morphism map constructed."
        },
